{"parentUuid":"5e2f3467-86e5-4043-b9bf-bdb5e448e586","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KgoEMNwgkJ4jcFwJLQS5aa","type":"tool_result","content":"      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"R9\",\n        \"severity\": \"high\",\n        \"path\": \"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md — Task 6, aios-audit-cron.sh\",\n        \"evidence\": \"The unattended wrapper commits using the shared working tree's index. If the user already staged unrelated files, git commit includes those files and git push publishes them. Git failures are then masked by the final successful echo because the script lacks failure propagation. Scheduling at 09:30 also does not exclude a backup race: data/jobs.json permits daily-backup to run for 240 minutes.\",\n        \"fix\": \"Avoid unattended commits in the user's working tree, or use an isolated checkout and scoped publication. Add locking, explicit failure propagation, and a durable completion record; do not rely on start-time spacing.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"R10\",\n        \"severity\": \"medium\",\n        \"path\": \"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md — Task 5, audit workflow\",\n        \"evidence\": \"The harness owns Agents and Rules in rot.md, but the direct audit only specifies skill checks and a directory count; it supplies no actual rules or agent audit. Nevertheless Step 4 updates Last audited for audited layers. brain-audit and doctor-plus are advertised as delegates but have no ownership row that schedules them. Initializing all layers as audited today also skips work without corresponding evidence.\",\n        \"fix\": \"Define concrete checks and delegation for each layer, initialize unknown audit dates as unknown, and advance dates only after the relevant checks complete successfully.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"coverage\": [\n      \"Verified the plan file SHA256