{"parentUuid":"d087ef63-19a6-4229-9264-b2eb632657f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceyvn7MHUEneJXb26GvYD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan rewritten. Now the dispositions file and round 2 of the Codex review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32157,"cache_read_input_tokens":132388,"output_tokens":2131,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":203},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32157,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2131,"cache_read_input_tokens":132388,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32157},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ceyvn6JmybKedP3amENtF","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"53cc3d14-33eb-4210-b52f-441f632563df","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:19:31.830Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"53cc3d14-33eb-4210-b52f-441f632563df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceyvn7MHUEneJXb26GvYD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UB7roKNMnycXzAm61ac5Tu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/aios-dispositions.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 1 dispositions — all ten ACCEPTED\n\nThree findings were verified directly on disk before rewriting. Two of them\ninverted the plan's architecture.\n\n## Verified on disk\n\n- R3: `git -C ~/.claude/skills remote -v` -> `erash11/claude-skills`.\n  `git log --oneline -5` -> `3ab4467 chore: apply global skill audit`, in sync\n  with origin. The earlier \"skills are gitignored\" note was about the `dotclaude`\n  repo and hid that this directory is its own versioned repo.\n- R1: `sync-to-codex.sh` confirmed to contain `rm -rf \"$dst/$s\"; cp -R \"$SRC/$s\"`.\n- R2: `~/.claude/skills/_shared/` confirmed to hold `config.json` + `Inference/`\n  and to be referenced by 10+ skills.\n\n## Disposition table\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed in the plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | ACCEPTED | New **Task 3** hardens both sync scripts BEFORE anything moves. A refuse-if-`$SRC/$s`-is-a-symlink guard exits 2 with no writes. Task 3 Step 4 proves it with a canary file that must survive. The `.ps1` twin gets a ReparsePoint guard. |\n| R2 | ACCEPTED | Every \"rm -rf any directory without a SKILL.md\" instruction is deleted. Task 2 adds guard B refusing to prune support dirs. Task 4's script reports `NO-SKILL ... left alone`. Task 4 Step 5 asserts `meeting-sync/scripts/sync.py` still resolves `parents[2]/_shared/config.json`. |\n| R3 | ACCEPTED — **architecture inverted** | Canonical is now `~/.claude/skills/` (the git repo). `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views. Canonical holds real dirs only. Task 4 Step 4 asserts `git ls-files -s` stages no mode-120000 entry, so no Mac symlink can reach Windows. Task 1 records git revert as the real undo for this repo. |\n| R4 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 Step 5 uses the documented exported factory + `pi.on('tool_call', ...)` + `event.input`. Regex fixed to `/(^\\|[\\s\"'=:])~?\\/?DEV(\\/\\|$\\|[\\s\"'])/` so a bare `~/DEV` matches. Note added that the installed version wins over the research note if they disagree. |\n| R5 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 runs Pi as a separate macOS user `piuser` with no read access to the operator home; Step 1 proves the boundary with two Permission-denied checks and stops if either succeeds. Pi gets a COPY of the pool. The unguarded `ls ~/DEV` probe is deleted. The guard is labelled defence-in-depth, not a boundary. **ADOPT is removed as a possible verdict**; only COST-MEASURED or BLOCKED. |\n| R6 | ACCEPTED | `aios-metrics.py` dedupes by `os.path.realpath`, so a link and its target count once. Session glob is explicitly `recursive=True`. Expected counts derived from post-migration invariants, not Task 2 directory totals. Added `symlinks_in_canonical`, `real_dirs_in_pool_view`, `real_dirs_in_codex_view` as layout assertions. |\n| R7 | ACCEPTED | Checker parses the flat YAML subset including `>-`/`\\|` block scalars, requires a positive AND a distinct negative clause (overlap is a failure), and **exits 2 on a missing or empty inventory**. Task 5 Step 2 proves the empty case cannot report success. Naming decided explicitly: the rule is `name` equals the directory name; TitleCase is legal (`CreateSkill`, `Harvest`). |\n| R8 | ACCEPTED | All optional actions use explicit `if ...; fi`. Functions and scripts `return 0` / `exit 0` explicitly. Same pattern applied to the cron wrapper. |\n| R9 | ACCEPTED | The cron **no longer commits or pushes at all**. It writes a trend row and a nudge; the human commits during the audit. Added an atomic `mkdir` lock, explicit failure propagation (metrics failure exits 1 and writes no row), a `MISSING` sentinel that blocks a partial row, and moved the schedule to 14:00. Task 7 Step 3 proves both failure paths. |\n| R10 | ACCEPTED | `rot.md` initializes every layer's `Last audited` to `unknown` except Skills (2026-09-12, genuinely audited). Each layer gains a concrete check column; Agents reads \"0 exist, report and skip\". `brain-audit` and `doctor-plus` now have ownership rows. Dates advance only for layers whose check ran and produced output; Task 6 Step 6 verifies the `unknown` count drops by exactly that many, not to zero. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\nEOF\nwc -l \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/aios-dispositions.md\"","description":"Write review dispositions file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32157,"cache_read_input_tokens":132388,"output_tokens":2131,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":203},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32157,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2131,"cache_read_input_tokens":132388,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32157},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ceyvn6JmybKedP3amENtF","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f092325-0f08-40c5-bbcb-90b152025480","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:19:54.081Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
