o for this repo. |\n| R4 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 Step 5 uses the documented exported factory + `pi.on('tool_call', ...)` + `event.input`. Regex fixed to `/(^\\|[\\s\\\"'=:])~?\\/?DEV(\\/\\|$\\|[\\s\\\"'])/` so a bare `~/DEV` matches. Note added that the installed version wins over the research note if they disagree. |\n| R5 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 runs Pi as a separate macOS user `piuser` with no read access to the operator home; Step 1 proves the boundary with two Permission-denied checks and stops if either succeeds. Pi gets a COPY of the pool. The unguarded `ls ~/DEV` probe is deleted. The guard is labelled defence-in-depth, not a boundary. **ADOPT is removed as a possible verdict**; only COST-MEASURED or BLOCKED. |\n| R6 | ACCEPTED | `aios-metrics.py` dedupes by `os.path.realpath`, so a link and its target count once. Session glob is explicitly `recursive=True`. Expected counts derived from post-migration invariants, not Task 2 directory totals. Added `symlinks_in_canonical`, `real_dirs_in_pool_view`, `real_dirs_in_codex_view` as layout assertions. |\n| R7 | ACCEPTED | Checker parses the flat YAML subset including `>-`/`\\|` block scalars, requires a positive AND a distinct negative clause (overlap is a failure), and **exits 2 on a missing or empty inventory**. Task 5 Step 2 proves the empty case cannot report success. Naming decided explicitly: the rule is `name` equals the directory name; TitleCase is legal (`CreateSkill`, `Harvest`). |\n| R8 | ACCEPTED | All optional actions use explicit `if ...; fi`. Functions and scripts `return 0` / `exit 0` explicitly. Same pattern applied to the cron wrapper. |\n| R9 | ACCEPTED | The cron **no longer commits or pushes at all**. It writes a trend row and a nudge; the human commits during the audit. Added an atomic `mkdir` lock, explicit failure propagation (metrics failure exits 1 and writes no row), a `MISSING` sentinel that blocks a partial row, and moved the schedule to 14:00. Task 7 Step 3 proves both failure paths. |\n| R10 | ACCEPTED | `rot.md` initializes every layer's `Last audited` to `unknown` except Skills (2026-09-12, genuinely audited). Each layer gains a concrete check column; Agents reads \\\"0 exist, report and skip\\\". `brain-audit` and `doctor-plus` now have ownership rows. Dates advance only for layers whose check ran and produced output; Task 6 Step 6 verifies the `unknown` count drops by exactly that many, not to zero. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\nEOF\nwc -l \\\"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/aios-dispositions.md\\\"\"\n\nReason: shell redirect to a dynamic or escaped path may truncate a sensitive file and requires human approval.\n\nExplanation: The redirect target is expanded by the shell at runtime, so dcg cannot prove where it points before the file is opened with O_TRUNC.\n             \n             Safer alternatives:\n             - Resolve and inspect the target path first.\n             - Use a literal `/tmp/<subdir>/scratch` path for disposable output.\n             - Use append (`>>`) when preserving existing content is acceptable.\n\nRule: core.filesystem:redirect-truncate-dynamic-path\n\nIf this operation is truly needed, ask the user for explicit permission and have them run the command manually.","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UB7roKNMnycXzAm61ac5Tu"}]},"uuid":"2750f5ca-71fe-44e7-93b2-e1b679c0f484","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:19:54.563Z","toolUseResult":"Error: BLOCKED by dcg\n\nTip: dcg explain \"cat > \\\"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/aios-dispositions.md\\\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 1 dispositions — all ten ACCEPTED\n\nThree findings were verified directly on disk before rewriting. Two of them\ninverted the plan's architecture.\n\n## Verified on disk\n\n- R3: `git -C ~/.claude/skills remote -v` -> `erash11/claude-skills`.\n  `git log --oneline -5` -> `3ab4467 chore: apply global skill audit`, in sync\n  with origin. The earlier \\\"skills are gitignored\\\" note was about the `dotclaude`\n  repo and hid that this directory is its own versioned repo.\n- R1: `sync-to-codex.sh