{"parentUuid":"c707f3a8-23c4-4abe-b454-e03b60eb8ca1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0138BUhmJ91ggZAbJbEd7tTE","type":"tool_result","content":"status: completed exit: 0\nVERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: The revised architecture resolves the original migration direction and several prior defects, but incomplete view generation, ineffective validation, and broken execution gates remain. The on-disk SHA256 matches the supplied revision.\n\n[HIGH] R2-01  Tasks 3–5\n  E: The sync scripts still publish only seven SHARED names, and canonicalization only inverts existing outward links. Neither migrates the remaining duplicate pool directories nor publishes missing canonical skills. On disk, pool copies of memory-write and meeting-sync differ from their canonical counterparts, and backup is absent from the pool. Task 5 edits only canonical frontmatter, leaving Pi with stale or missing skills.\n  F: Generate both views from an explicit complete canonical-skill manifest. Reconcile existing duplicates with archived backups, publish missing entries, and verify per-skill content parity and discovery across harnesses.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-02  Task 6 layout invariants\n  E: Task 2 explicitly preserves approximately 150 third-party pool entries as real directories, but Task 6 requires real_dirs_in_pool_view=0 and classifies every real skill directory as an erroneous edit. The planned preserved state therefore necessarily fails the mandatory audit gate. Windows copy views also legitimately contain real directories.\n  F: Track ownership and platform in the view manifest. Validate generated entries against their expected representation, while reporting third-party installations separately.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-03  Task 3 Step 6 and Task 4 Step 4\n  E: Task 3 demands a clean git status before committing the two script edits, so its prerequisite cannot pass as written. Task 4 checks git ls-files before staging replacements and expects no mode-120000 entries. The current index contains tracked symlinks including anti-sleep and claudex-loop; changing the working tree does not change those index entries until git add.\n  F: Allow precisely the expected script modifications at the Task 3 gate. In Task 4, stage the intended replacements before inspecting index modes, then inspect the staged diff and reject unexpected changes.\n\n[HIGH] R2-04  Task 1 rollback block\n  E: The command labelled as restoring only unversioned folders extracts the entire archive, which also contains .claude/skills and its .git directory. After migration commits, this overlays old repository metadata and working-tree files onto the current canonical repository without removing newly introduced files. The subsequent git-revert procedure is no longer operating on the untouched current repository.\n  F: Extract only .agents/skills and .codex/skills for view rollback. Keep canonical rollback entirely separate and specify how its content and restored view targets remain consistent.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-05  Task 5 checker\n  E: R7's negative-only defect remains: for 'Do not use when auditing', 'use when' starts at offset 7 and 'do not use' at offset 0, so comparing their starting offsets does not detect overlap. The alleged YAML subset parser also accepts malformed quoted scalars and duplicate keys rather than rejecting unsupported syntax.\n  F: Exclude positive matches contained within negative-clause spans. Define and strictly validate the supported YAML grammar, including quoting and duplicate keys, or use a proper parser. Add explicit negative-only and malformed-frontmatter verification cases.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-06  Task 7 cron wrapper\n  E: A killed process or reboot leaves the mkdir lock behind. Every subsequent monthly invocation exits 0 without metrics or a nudge; the proposed stale-lock verification removes the lock manually and does not establish recovery. Separately, failed writes to the trend file or error log are ignored because the script lacks errexit or explicit checks and ends with exit 0.\n  F: Implement recoverable lock ownership and stale-lock handling. Check every required write and propagate failures, recording success only after the row and notification are durably written.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-07  Task 8 Steps 5–6\n  E: The revised regex matches bare ~/DEV, but the actual revised probe is 'ls /Users/piuser/DEV | head -3'. The character before DEV is '/', which is absent from the allowed leading boundary, and the expression cannot consume /Users/piuser. Consequently this exact probe does not match the guard.\n  F: Use a disposable fixture and ensure the precise probe matches the intended path policy. Verify handler invocation and require an explicit guard-block result, distinguishing it from a missing-directory error.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-08  Task 8 Step 2\n  E: The newly created standard user runs npm install -g against the existing Homebrew installation. /opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules is owned by kristinarash:admin with mode 755, so piuser cannot install there. No user-owned prefix or alternate executable path is configured, making the prescribed install path fail before the cost measurement.\n  F: Install into a piuser-owned prefix or local project directory and invoke that explicit executable. Keep installation and teardown confined to that prefix.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-09  Task 6 delegation\n  E: The Memory row delegates auditing ~/.claude/projects/*/memory and global-memory to improve-system. Its actual body scans SecondBrain Notes, Knowledge, and Projects instead. Its Step 0 also applies previously approved proposals and writes a pending ledger, conflicting with the compound audit's report-and-date-only write boundary. A successful delegate invocation would not establish that the named memory stores were audited.\n  F: Define a scoped, read-only delegation contract and explicitly inspect the named memory stores. Suppress delegate mutation steps and advance each receipt only when its specified scope was actually checked.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fcf19327-f9d1-43bc-8d2b-eef8d9283420","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:21:54.748Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"status: completed exit: 0\nVERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: The revised architecture resolves the original migration direction and several prior defects, but incomplete view generation, ineffective validation, and broken execution gates remain. The on-disk SHA256 matches the supplied revision.\n\n[HIGH] R2-01  Tasks 3–5\n  E: The sync scripts still publish only seven SHARED names, and canonicalization only inverts existing outward links. Neither migrates the remaining duplicate pool directories nor publishes missing canonical skills. On disk, pool copies of memory-write and meeting-sync differ from their canonical counterparts, and backup is absent from the pool. Task 5 edits only canonical frontmatter, leaving Pi with stale or missing skills.\n  F: Generate both views from an explicit complete canonical-skill manifest. Reconcile existing duplicates with archived backups, publish missing entries, and verify per-skill content parity and discovery across harnesses.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-02  Task 6 layout invariants\n  E: Task 2 explicitly preserves approximately 150 third-party pool entries as real directories, but Task 6 requires real_dirs_in_pool_view=0 and classifies every real skill directory as an erroneous edit. The planned preserved state therefore necessarily fails the mandatory audit gate. Windows copy views also legitimately contain real directories.\n  F: Track ownership and platform in the view manifest. Validate generated entries against their expected representation, while reporting third-party installations separately.\n\n[MEDIUM] R2-03  Task 3 Step 6 and Task 4 Step 4\n  E: Task 3 demands a clean git status before committing the two script edits, so its prerequisite cannot pass as written. Task 4 checks git ls-files before staging replacements and expects no mode-1200