{"parentUuid":"44f7d932-3562-432a-b7c3-5a1cf940c108","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceyw5HELGydbkPTnfB799","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3198,"cache_read_input_tokens":179419,"output_tokens":2338,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3198,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2338,"cache_read_input_tokens":179419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3198},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ceyw5GsVgdMDiC9GHXQsh","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"bc335784-8ac3-425b-8fb9-aad4ea3f4b7e","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:23:23.429Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"bc335784-8ac3-425b-8fb9-aad4ea3f4b7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceyw5HELGydbkPTnfB799","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NSZwrpTPvmpfbVpAF64Ey4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"- [ ] **Step 5: Prove the normal path still works**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\nls -la ~/.codex/skills | grep -E 'startup|closeout'\n```\n\nExpected: dry run lists `would sync` lines and `exit=0`; the real run reports `synced …` and `exit=0`; the listing shows symlinks into `~/.claude/skills`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink**\n\n```bash\ngrep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short\n```\n\nExpected: `git status` is **clean**. The views live outside the repo, so the backup's `git add -A` has nothing machine-specific to pick up. If `git status` lists a symlink inside `~/.claude/skills`, stop — that is exactly R3 and it must not be committed.","new_string":"- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**\n\nBefore the views are regenerated, the existing pool copies must be checked — regenerating overwrites them, and two of them contain edits that exist nowhere else. Verified on disk today: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **differ** between canonical and pool; `backup` and 7 others are **absent** from the pool entirely.\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12\necho \"=== canonical skills whose pool copy DIFFERS ===\"\nfor d in ~/.claude/skills/*/; do\n  s=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"\n  [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ] || continue\n  b=~/.agents/skills/\"$s\"\n  if [ -e \"$b\" ] && [ ! -L \"$b\" ] && ! diff -rq \"$d\" \"$b\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    echo \"DIVERGED $s\"\n  fi\ndone\necho \"=== canonical skills ABSENT from the pool ===\"\ncomm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)\n```\n\nExpected: at least `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` under DIVERGED, and 8 names under ABSENT.\n\nFor **each** DIVERGED name, look at the actual difference and decide which side wins — then back up the pool copy before it is overwritten:\n\n```bash\nfor s in memory-write meeting-sync; do\n  echo \"===== $s =====\"\n  diff -ru ~/.claude/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" | head -40\n  cp -R ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/\"$s\"\ndone\nls ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/\n```\n\nRead each diff. If the pool copy is newer or better, copy that content **into canonical** (`cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/`) and commit it there. If canonical wins, do nothing — the sync will overwrite the pool. **Do not skip reading the diffs**; regenerating discards whatever you did not move. The `pre-sync-2026-09-12/` backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong.\n\nThe ABSENT names need no action: the new complete-manifest sync publishes them automatically. That is the bug the manifest fixes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the normal path publishes everything**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh | grep -c 'would sync'\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\necho \"--- every canonical skill must now be in the pool (must be empty) ---\"\ncomm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)\necho \"--- manifest ---\"\nwc -l < ~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\nls -la ~/.codex/skills | grep -E 'startup|backup' | head -4\n```\n\nExpected: `exit=0` both times; the `would sync` count is **122** (61 skills × 2 views) or higher with support dirs; the ABSENT list is now **empty**; the manifest holds 62 lines; the listing shows symlinks into `~/.claude/skills`. An ABSENT name still printing means the manifest loop did not pick it up.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n\n```bash\ngrep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20\necho \"--- staged/modified in canonical ---\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short\necho \"--- symlinks in the working tree (must be 0 until Task 4) ---\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\n```\n\nExpected: `git status` shows **exactly** `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` as modified — plus any skill content moved in Step 5 — **and nothing else**. Round 2 caught the earlier wording here, which demanded a clean tree at a point where this task has deliberately just edited two tracked files; a clean tree would have been impossible. What matters is that no *unexpected* path appears, especially not a symlink inside the repo.\n\n> The `find` count is still non-zero at this point (19 outward links remain until Task 4). That is expected here. It must read `0` after Task 4, and `git ls-files` must never stage one — that check lives in Task 4 Step 4, after staging."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3198,"cache_read_input_tokens":179419,"output_tokens":2338,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3198,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2338,"cache_read_input_tokens":179419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3198},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockInde