{"parentUuid":"762d0164-0c46-4eda-b26a-cda23073d0ab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceyw7ojSEyrdoVgvu5QzN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RKC4pkBUG8ue8qmube2JEC","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"```bash\necho \"--- symlinks in canonical (must be 0) ---\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\necho \"--- SKILL.md count (must be 61) ---\"\nfind -L ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\necho \"--- dangling pool links (must be empty) ---\"\nfind ~/.agents/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print\necho \"--- git sees real files, not links ---\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short | head -20\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"' | head\n```\n\nExpected: `0`; `61`; no dangling output; `git status` lists new real files; the `ls-files` line prints **nothing** (mode `120000` is a symlink — none may be staged). If any symlink is staged, unstage it and stop; that is R3.","new_string":"```bash\necho \"--- symlinks in canonical working tree (must be 0) ---\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\necho \"--- SKILL.md count (must be 61) ---\"\nfind -L ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\necho \"--- dangling pool links (must be empty) ---\"\nfind ~/.agents/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print\n```\n\nExpected: `0`; `61`; no dangling output.\n\n**Now stage, then inspect the index (R2-03).** Round 2 caught the earlier ordering: `git ls-files` reads the *index*, and the index still held the 19 old symlink entries (`anti-sleep`, `claudex-loop`, …) until a `git add` replaced them. Checking before staging proved nothing.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\necho \"--- staged symlinks (mode 120000) - MUST be empty ---\"\ngit ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"'\necho \"--- staged summary ---\"\ngit diff --cached --stat | tail -5\necho \"--- staged type changes (link -> real file) ---\"\ngit diff --cached --summary | grep -E 'mode change|delete mode 120000' | head -20\n```\n\nExpected: the `120000` list prints **nothing**; the summary shows the 19 inversions as `delete mode 120000` paired with new real files. If any `120000` entry is still staged, run `git reset` and stop — committing it would send an absolute Mac symlink to Windows, which is R3."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":185444,"output_tokens":1075,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":340,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":185444,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":340},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ceyw7o22Dgd8czxYgt5aL","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"273eb99e-e8c8-4989-a706-40c3cfb0db82","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:24:06.235Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
