{"parentUuid":"8d5b7852-8e3b-4ab3-b268-2681a21e3458","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywHQp5FPpESXuXW1spn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018s4dZfdcoeyM8Saz8w4kEL","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"```bash\nsudo -u piuser mkdir -p /Users/piuser/pi-trial\nsudo -u piuser npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent 2>&1 | tail -5\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc 'which -a pi && pi --version'\n```\n\nExpected: a path and a version string. `--ignore-scripts` is deliberate — no postinstall scripts run.","new_string":"`npm install -g` would target `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules`, which is `drwxr-xr-x kristinarash:admin` — `piuser` cannot write there and the install fails before any measurement happens (R2-08). Install into a prefix `piuser` owns, and call that executable by absolute path:\n\n```bash\nsudo -u piuser mkdir -p /Users/piuser/pi-trial /Users/piuser/.npm-global\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc 'npm config set prefix /Users/piuser/.npm-global'\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc 'npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent' 2>&1 | tail -5\nPI=/Users/piuser/.npm-global/bin/pi\nsudo -u piuser \"$PI\" --version\n```\n\nExpected: an install summary and a version string. `--ignore-scripts` is deliberate — no postinstall scripts run. Everything lands under `/Users/piuser/.npm-global`, so teardown is one `rm -rf` and Eric's Homebrew tree is never touched.\n\n> Use the absolute `$PI` path in every later step. `piuser`'s login PATH does not include the new prefix, and `which pi` would silently find nothing or, worse, Eric's copy."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1206,"cache_read_input_tokens":197932,"output_token