lently find nothing or, worse, Eric's copy.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1643,"oldLines":14,"newStart":1643,"newLines":20,"lines":[" "," - [ ] **Step 2: Install Pi as that user**"," ","+`npm install -g` would target `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules`, which is `drwxr-xr-x kristinarash:admin` — `piuser` cannot write there and the install fails before any measurement happens (R2-08). Install into a prefix `piuser` owns, and call that executable by absolute path:","+"," ```bash","-sudo -u piuser mkdir -p /Users/piuser/pi-trial","-sudo -u piuser npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent 2>&1 | tail -5","-sudo -u piuser bash -lc 'which -a pi && pi --version'","+sudo -u piuser mkdir -p /Users/piuser/pi-trial /Users/piuser/.npm-global","+sudo -u piuser bash -lc 'npm config set prefix /Users/piuser/.npm-global'","+sudo -u piuser bash -lc 'npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent' 2>&1 | tail -5","+PI=/Users/piuser/.npm-global/bin/pi","+sudo -u piuser \"$PI\" --version"," ```"," ","-Expected: a path and a version string. `--ignore-scripts` is deliberate — no postinstall scripts run.","+Expected: an install summary and a version string. `--ignore-scripts` is deliberate — no postinstall scripts run. Everything lands under `/Users/piuser/.npm-global`, so teardown is one `rm -rf` and Eric's Homebrew tree is never touched."," ","+> Use the absolute `$PI` path in every later step. `piuser`'s login PATH does not include the new prefix, and `which pi` would silently find nothing or, worse, Eric's copy.","+"," - [ ] **Step 3: Give it a copy of the pruned pool, not the real one**"," "," ```bash"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ece4fd8d-114b-4478-be49-c0ceabd41acd","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.