{"parentUuid":"4656ec6b-632f-4f95-be36-934925fa834c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"01a262fe-9e88-4bdc-a539-3a3192e814a4","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:26:21.035Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"01a262fe-9e88-4bdc-a539-3a3192e814a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywJcJuUBtX8GE6ALSg5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q1uhBRwNHTPoNXEBHRAPT7","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"```typescript\n// Minimal port of the dcg guard. Proves the hook -> extension mapping.\n// Defence in depth only: the real boundary is the piuser file permissions.\nconst DENY: RegExp[] = [\n  /\\brm\\s+-rf\\s+\\/(?!tmp)/,\n  /DexaProject/i,\n  /GoogleDrive-/,\n  /(^|[\\s\"'=:])~?\\/?DEV(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,        // R4: bare ~/DEV must match\n  /(^|[\\s\"'=:])~?\\/?SecondBrain(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,\n];\n\nexport default function guard(pi: any) {\n  pi.on(\"tool_call\", (event: any) => {\n    const blob = JSON.stringify(event?.input ?? {});   // R4: input, not args\n    for (const re of DENY) {\n      if (re.test(blob)) {\n        return { block: true, reason: `guard: blocked by ${re}` };\n      }\n    }\n    return { block: false };\n  });\n}\n```\n\nPrint mode may require explicitly trusting a project extension; if Pi asks, grant it for this project only and note the step in the report.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the guard blocks — and that it does not block everything**\n\n```bash\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc 'cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && pi --print \"Run: ls /Users/piuser/DEV | head -3\" 2>&1 | tail -10'\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc 'cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && pi --print \"Run: echo hello\" 2>&1 | tail -5'\n```\n\nExpected: the first is **blocked** with the guard reason; the second **succeeds**. A guard that blocks everything is not a guard. The probe targets a path inside `piuser`'s own home, so the guard — not the OS — is what must stop it. If the first is not blocked after two attempts at the extension path or event name, stop per the stop conditions.","new_string":"```typescript\n// Minimal port of the dcg guard. Proves the hook -> extension mapping.\n// Defence in depth only: the real boundary is the piuser file permissions.\n//\n// R2-07: match the protected NAME anywhere a path separator or string edge\n// precedes it, so /Users/piuser/DEV, ~/DEV, ./DEV and a bare DEV/ all hit.\n// The earlier expression required a whitespace/quote boundary and therefore\n// missed the very probe used to test it.\nconst DENY: RegExp[] = [\n  /\\brm\\s+-rf\\s+\\/(?!tmp)/,\n  /DexaProject/i,\n  /GoogleDrive-/,\n  /(^|[\\s\"'=:/])DEV(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,\n  /(^|[\\s\"'=:/])SecondBrain(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,\n];\n\nexport default function guard(pi: any) {\n  pi.on(\"tool_call\", (event: any) => {\n    const blob = JSON.stringify(event?.input ?? {});   // R4: input, not args\n    console.log(`[guard] saw tool_call: ${blob.slice(0, 200)}`);\n    for (const re of DENY) {\n      if (re.test(blob)) {\n        return { block: true, reason: `guard: blocked by ${re}` };\n      }\n    }\n    return { block: false };\n  });\n}\n```\n\nThe `console.log` is deliberate: Step 6 must distinguish \"the guard blocked it\" from \"the handler never ran.\" Print mode may require explicitly trusting a project extension; if Pi asks, grant it for this project only and note the step in the report.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the guard blocks — on a fixture that really exists**\n\nCreate a disposable fixture first, so a block cannot be confused with a missing-directory error (R2-07):\n\n```bash\nsudo -u piuser mkdir -p /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc 'echo canary > /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV/file.txt'\nsudo -u piuser ls /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV        # proves it exists and is readable\n```\n\nThen run the three probes:\n\n```bash\nPI=/Users/piuser/.npm-global/bin/pi\n# A: must be BLOCKED by the guard, not by a missing path.\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: ls /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV' 2>&1 | tail -12\"\n# B: must SUCCEED - a guard that blocks everything is not a guard.\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: echo hello' 2>&1 | tail -6\"\n# C: must SUCCEED - a sibling path that is not protected.\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: ls /Users/piuser/fixture' 2>&1 | tail -6\"\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n- **A** — `[guard] saw tool_call:` appears (the handler ran) **and** the result carries `guard: blocked by`. The fixture exists and is readable, so a \"no such directory\" message would mean the guard did **not** fire.\n- **B** — prints `hello`, no block.\n- **C** — lists `DEV`, no block. This is the false-positive check: the guard must key on the path segment, not on any string containing those letters.\n\nIf A is not blocked, or the `[guard]` line never appears, after two attempts at the extension path or event name, stop per the stop conditions and record which of the two failed — \"handler never registered\" and \"regex did not match\" are different costs to report."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":647,"cache_read_input_tokens":200116,"output_tokens":2097,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":647,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2097,"cache_read_input_tokens":200116,"cache_creation_input_tokens":647,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":647},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeywJbcEKoFPkFemdMEb4","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"58d1a487-40f4-4463-8bc1-8abf2cffeb80","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:26:43.548Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
