locks everything is not a guard. The probe targets a path inside `piuser`'s own home, so the guard — not the OS — is what must stop it. If the first is not blocked after two attempts at the extension path or event name, stop per the stop conditions.","newString":"```typescript\n// Minimal port of the dcg guard. Proves the hook -> extension mapping.\n// Defence in depth only: the real boundary is the piuser file permissions.\n//\n// R2-07: match the protected NAME anywhere a path separator or string edge\n// precedes it, so /Users/piuser/DEV, ~/DEV, ./DEV and a bare DEV/ all hit.\n// The earlier expression required a whitespace/quote boundary and therefore\n// missed the very probe used to test it.\nconst DENY: RegExp[] = [\n  /\\brm\\s+-rf\\s+\\/(?!tmp)/,\n  /DexaProject/i,\n  /GoogleDrive-/,\n  /(^|[\\s\"'=:/])DEV(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,\n  /(^|[\\s\"'=:/])SecondBrain(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,\n];\n\nexport default function guard(pi: any) {\n  pi.on(\"tool_call\", (event: any) => {\n    const blob = JSON.stringify(event?.input ?? {});   // R4: input, not args\n    console.log(`[guard] saw tool_call: ${blob.slice(0, 200)}`);\n    for (const re of DENY) {\n      if (re.test(blob)) {\n        return { block: true, reason: `guard: blocked by ${re}` };\n      }\n    }\n    return { block: false };\n  });\n}\n```\n\nThe `console.log` is deliberate: Step 6 must distinguish \"the guard blocked it\" from \"the handler never ran.\" Print mode may require explicitly trusting a project extension; if Pi asks, grant it for this project only and note the step in the report.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the guard blocks — on a fixture that really exists**\n\nCreate a disposable fixture first, so a block cannot be confused with a missing-directory error (R2-07):\n\n```bash\nsudo -u piuser mkdir -p /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc 'echo canary > /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV/file.txt'\nsudo -u piuser ls /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV        # proves it exists and is readable\n```\n\nThen run the three probes:\n\n```bash\nPI=/Users/piuser/.npm-global/bin/pi\n# A: must be BLOCKED by the guard, not by a missing path.\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: ls /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV' 2>&1 | tail -12\"\n# B: must SUCCEED - a guard that blocks everything is not a guard.\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: echo hello' 2>&1 | tail -6\"\n# C: must SUCCEED - a sibling path that is not protected.\nsudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: ls /Users/piuser/fixture' 2>&1 | tail -6\"\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n- **A** — `[guard] saw tool_call:` appears (the handler ran) **and** the result carries `guard: blocked by`. The fixture exists and is readable, so a \"no such directory\" message would mean the guard did **not** fire.\n- **B** — prints `hello`, no block.\n- **C** — lists `DEV`, no block. This is the false-positive check: the guard must key on the path segment, not on any string containing those letters.\n\nIf A is not blocked, or the `[guard]` line never appears, after two attempts at the extension path or event name, stop per the stop conditions and record which of the two failed — \"handler never registered\" and \"regex did not match\" are different costs to report.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1698,"oldLines":17,"newStart":1698,"newLines":23,"lines":[" ```typescript"," // Minimal port of the dcg guard. Proves the hook -> extension mapping."," // Defence in depth only: the real boundary is the piuser file permissions.","+//","+// R2-07: match the protected NAME anywhere a path separator or string edge","+// precedes it, so /Users/piuser/DEV, ~/DEV, ./DEV and a bare DEV/ all hit.","+// The earlier expression required a whitespace/quote boundary and therefore","+// missed the very probe used to test it."," const DENY: RegExp[] = [","   /\\brm\\s+-rf\\s+\\/(?!tmp)/,","   /DexaProject/i,","   /GoogleDrive-/,","-  /(^|[\\s\"'=:])~?\\/?DEV(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,        // R4: bare ~/DEV must match","-  /(^|[\\s\"'=:])~?\\/?SecondBrain(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,","+  /(^|[\\s\"'=:/])DEV(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,","+  /(^|[\\s\"'=:/])SecondBrain(\\/|$|[\\s\"'])/,"," ];"," "," export default function guard(pi: any) {","   pi.on(\"tool_call\", (event: any) => {","     const blob = JSON.stringify(event?.input ?? {});   // R4: input, not args","+    console.log(`[guard] saw tool_call: ${blob.slice(0, 200)}`);","     for (const re of DENY) {","       if (re.test(blob)) {","         return { block: true, reason: `guard: blocked by ${re}` };"]},{"oldStart":1719,"oldLines":17,"newStart":1725,"newLines":38,"lines":[" }"," ```"," ","-Print mode may require explicitly trusting a project extension; if Pi asks, grant it for this project only and note the step in the report.","+The `console.log` is deliberate: Step 6 must distinguish \"the guard blocked it\" from \"the handler never ran.\" Print mode may require explicitly trusting a project extension; if Pi asks, grant it for this project only and note the step in the report."," ","-- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the guard blocks — and that it does not block everything**","+- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the guard blocks — on a fixture that really exists**"," ","+Create a disposable fixture first, so a block cannot be confused with a missing-directory error (R2-07):","+"," ```bash","-sudo -u piuser bash -lc 'cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && pi --print \"Run: ls /Users/piuser/DEV | head -3\" 2>&1 | tail -10'","-sudo -u piuser bash -lc 'cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && pi --print \"Run: echo hello\" 2>&1 | tail -5'","+sudo -u piuser mkdir -p /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV","+sudo -u piuser bash -lc 'echo canary > /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV/file.txt'","+sudo -u piuser ls /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV        # proves it exists and is readable"," ```"," ","-Expected: the first is **blocked** with the guard reason; the second **succeeds**. A guard that blocks everything is not a guard. The probe targets a path inside `piuser`'s own home, so the guard — not the OS — is what must stop it. If the first is not blocked after two attempts at the extension path or event name, stop per the stop conditions.","+Then run the three probes:"," ","+```bash","+PI=/Users/piuser/.npm-global/bin/pi","+# A: must be BLOCKED by the guard, not by a missing path.","+sudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: ls /Users/piuser/fixture/DEV' 2>&1 | tail -12\"","+# B: must SUCCEED - a guard that blocks everything is not a guard.","+sudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: echo hello' 2>&1 | tail -6\"","+# C: must SUCCEED - a sibling path that is not protected.","+sudo -u piuser bash -lc \"cd /Users/piuser/pi-trial && $PI --print 'Run: ls /Users/piuser/fixture' 2>&1 | tail -6\"","+```","+","+Expected:","+","+- **A** — `[guard] saw tool_call:` appears (the handler ran) **and** the result carries `guard: blocked by`. The fixture exists and is readable, so a \"no such directory\" message would mean the guard did **not** fire.","+- **B** — prints `hello`, no block.","+- **C** — lists `DEV`, no block. This is the false-positive check: the guard must key on the path segment, not on any string containing those letters.","+","+If A is not blocked, or the `[guard]` line never appears, after two attempts at the extension path or event name, stop per the stop conditions and record which of the two failed — \"handler never registered\" and \"regex did not match\" are different costs to report.","+"," - [ ] **Step 7: Write the cost measurement**"," "," ```bash"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"58d1a487-40f4-4463-8bc1-8abf2cffeb80","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
