{"parentUuid":"908dc4b4-6cbb-4468-a82e-451882c24de5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fe666289-41c8-4fed-8ae5-a4f3e3203752","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:26:59.002Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"fe666289-41c8-4fed-8ae5-a4f3e3203752","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywMQdmqKy1Nzm8SFvuN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012e5TqL7YaHocBfSjjaT9oM","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"---\n\n### Task 1: Snapshot and freeze the current state","new_string":"### Round 2 findings — disposition\n\nThree claims were re-verified on disk before accepting: pool copies of `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **do** differ from canonical; **8** canonical skills are absent from the pool; `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules` is `drwxr-xr-x kristinarash:admin`, so `piuser` genuinely cannot install there.\n\n| ID | Sev | Codex's finding | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R2-01 | high | The sync scripts publish only 7 `SHARED` names and canonicalization only inverts existing links — so the views never carry the other 54 skills. Pool copies of `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` differ from canonical; `backup` is absent. Pi would see stale and missing skills. | **ACCEPTED.** Verified. `sync-to-codex.sh` now builds a **complete manifest** — every canonical directory with a SKILL.md, plus declared support dirs — and writes `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` recording what it owns. It also retires entries dropped from canonical. New **Task 3 Step 5** reconciles the two diverged copies by reading the diffs and backing them up before the regenerate overwrites them. Task 3 Step 6 asserts the absent list is empty afterwards. |\n| R2-02 | med | Task 2 deliberately preserves ~150 third-party pool entries as real directories, but Task 6 required `real_dirs_in_pool_view=0` — so the intended state fails the mandatory gate. Windows copy-views legitimately hold real dirs too. | **ACCEPTED.** The metric is replaced by `pool_view_drift` / `codex_view_drift`, which check **only manifest-owned entries** and are platform-aware (symlink on Mac, copy on Windows). Third-party entries are counted separately as `pool_third_party` and reported as information, never as an error. |\n| R2-03 | med | Task 3 Step 6 demanded a clean `git status` right after editing two tracked files — impossible. Task 4 checked `git ls-files` **before** staging, so it read the old index entries and proved nothing. | **ACCEPTED.** Task 3's gate now expects exactly the two script edits plus any content moved in Step 5, and rejects anything else. Task 4 now runs `git add -A` **first**, then inspects staged modes and the staged summary. |\n| R2-04 | high | The rollback labelled \"un-versioned folders\" extracted the whole archive, including `.claude/skills` and its `.git` — overlaying stale repo metadata onto a migrated repo without removing new files, so the later `git revert` no longer operates on a coherent history. | **ACCEPTED.** Task 1 now takes **two separate tarballs**: a VIEWS archive (the only tarball rollback) and a CANONICAL archive marked reference-only. Step 3 asserts the VIEWS archive contains no `.claude` directory. The rollback block states the two paths must never be combined, and that git — not the tarball — is the canonical undo, followed by regenerating the views. |\n| R2-05 | med | The overlap test compared start offsets, so `\"Do not use when auditing\"` still passed: `use when` is at offset 7, `do not use` at 0. The parser also accepted malformed quotes and duplicate keys. | **ACCEPTED.** Clause detection now uses **span containment** — a positive phrase inside a negative phrase does not count. Added duplicate-key and unbalanced-quote rejection. Task 5 Step 2 adds three explicit fixtures (`negonly`, `dupekey`, `badquote`) that must all fail, so the checker's own failure modes are proven rather than assumed. |\n| R2-06 | med | A killed process or reboot leaves the `mkdir` lock behind, silencing every future run; the proposed test removed the lock by hand and proved nothing about recovery. Failed writes to the trend file and error log were ignored. | **ACCEPTED.** The lock now records its owner PID and is **reclaimed** when the owner is not running (or the lock is over a day old with no pid). Every required write is checked, with the trend row read back to confirm. Task 7 Step 3 now tests three cases — dead metrics script, **live** lock, **stale** lock — and asserts the stale case actually adds a row. |\n| R2-07 | med | The revised regex matched `~/DEV`, but the actual probe was `ls /Users/piuser/DEV`: the preceding character is `/`, which the leading boundary did not allow — so the exact test probe would not have matched the guard. | **ACCEPTED.** `/` added to the leading boundary class. The probe now runs against a **disposable fixture that really exists** (`/Users/piuser/fixture/DEV`), so a block cannot be confused with a missing-directory error. The handler logs on entry, distinguishing \"guard blocked it\" from \"handler never ran\", and a third probe checks the guard does not fire on a sibling path. |\n| R2-08 | med | `piuser` running `npm install -g` targets `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules`, owned by `kristinarash:admin` mode 755 — the install fails before any measurement happens. | **ACCEPTED.** Verified. Task 8 sets a `piuser`-owned prefix (`/Users/piuser/.npm-global`) and calls the absolute executable in every step, since that prefix is not on `piuser`'s PATH. Teardown is a single `rm -rf` of that prefix; Homebrew is never touched. |\n| R2-09 | med | The Memory row delegates `~/.claude/projects/*/memory` and `global-memory` to `improve-system`, but that skill actually scans SecondBrain. Its Step 0 also applies approved proposals and writes a ledger, conflicting with a report-only audit. A clean exit would not establish the named stores were audited. | **ACCEPTED.** The row is split: **Memory (agent)** is audited by `aios-audit` directly with a concrete check; **Memory (vault notes)** delegates to `improve-system`. A new **delegation contract** in `rot.md` requires read-only invocation with mutation steps suppressed, requires verifying a delegate's real scope rather than its claimed one, and forbids stamping a date because a delegate exited cleanly. |\n\n**Rejected:** none.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Snapshot and freeze the current state"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":203650,"output_tokens":2346,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2346,"cache_read_input_tokens":203650,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeywMPypm9d1PXccZFJ9k","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf4a68e9-46d7-4026-a45e-9dfe85eeee7c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:27:26.853Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
