conflicting with a report-only audit. A clean exit would not establish the named stores were audited. | **ACCEPTED.** The row is split: **Memory (agent)** is audited by `aios-audit` directly with a concrete check; **Memory (vault notes)** delegates to `improve-system`. A new **delegation contract** in `rot.md` requires read-only invocation with mutation steps suppressed, requires verifying a delegate's real scope rather than its claimed one, and forbids stamping a date because a delegate exited cleanly. |\n\n**Rejected:** none.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Snapshot and freeze the current state","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":86,"oldLines":6,"newStart":86,"newLines":24,"lines":[" | R9 | high | The cron wrapper commits from the shared working tree — a staged unrelated file gets published — and masks git failures. 09:30 does not dodge a backup that may run 240 minutes. | **ACCEPTED.** Task 6's cron **no longer commits or pushes at all.** It writes the trend row and a nudge; the human commits during the audit. That removes the leak, the race, and the masked failure together. |"," | R10 | med | Agents and Rules have no actual check, yet `Last audited` is stamped for them; `brain-audit`/`doctor-plus` are named as delegates with no ownership row. | **ACCEPTED.** `rot.md` initializes every layer to `unknown` except Skills (genuinely audited 2026-09-12). Each layer gets a concrete check or an explicit \"no check yet.\" Dates advance only after that layer's check runs. |"," ","+### Round 2 findings — disposition","+","+Three claims were re-verified on disk before accepting: pool copies of `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **do** differ from canonical; **8** canonical skills are absent from the pool; `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules` is `drwxr-xr-x kristinarash:admin`, so `piuser` genuinely cannot install there.","+","+| ID | Sev | Codex's finding | Disposition |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| R2-01 | high | The sync scripts publish only 7 `SHARED` names and canonicalization only inverts existing links — so the views never carry the other 54 skills. Pool copies of `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` differ from canonical; `backup` is absent. Pi would see stale and missing skills. | **ACCEPTED.** Verified. `sync-to-codex.sh` now builds a **complete manifest** — every canonical directory with a SKILL.md, plus declared support dirs — and writes `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` recording what it owns. It also retires entries dropped from canonical. New **Task 3 Step 5** reconciles the two diverged copies by reading the diffs and backing them up before the regenerate overwrites them. Task 3 Step 6 asserts the absent list is empty afterwards. |","+| R2-02 | med | Task 2 deliberately preserves ~150 third-party pool entries as real directories, but Task 6 required `real_dirs_in_pool_view=0` — so the intended state fails the mandatory gate. Windows copy-views legitimately hold real dirs too. | **ACCEPTED.** The metric is replaced by `pool_view_drift` / `codex_view_drift`, which check **only manifest-owned entries** and are platform-aware (symlink on Mac, copy on Windows). Third-party entries are counted separately as `pool_third_party` and reported as information, never as an error. |","+| R2-03 | med | Task 3 Step 6 demanded a clean `git status` right after editing two tracked files — impossible. Task 4 checked `git ls-files` **before** staging, so it read the old index entries and proved nothing. | **ACCEPTED.** Task 3's gate now expects exactly the two script edits plus any content moved in Step 5, and rejects anything else. Task 4 now runs `git add -A` **first**, then inspects staged modes and the staged summary. |","+| R2-04 | high | The rollback labelled \"un-versioned folders\" extracted the whole archive, including `.claude/skills` and its `.git` — overlaying stale repo metadata onto a migrated repo without removing new files, so the later `git revert` no longer operates on a coherent history. | **ACCEPTED.** Task 1 now takes **two separate tarballs**: a VIEWS archive (the only tarball rollback) and a CANONICAL archive marked reference-only. Step 3 asserts the VIEWS archive contains no `.claude` directory. The rollback block states the two paths must never be combined, and that git — not the tarball — is the canonical undo, followed by regenerating the views. |","+| R2-05 | med | The overlap test compared start offsets, so `\"Do not use when auditing\"` still passed: `use when` is at offset 7, `do not use` at 0. The parser also accepted malformed quotes and duplicate keys. | **ACCEPTED.** Clause detection now uses **span containment** — a positive phrase inside a negative phrase does not count. Added duplicate-key and unbalanced-quote rejection. Task 5 Step 2 adds three explicit fixtures (`negonly`, `dupekey`, `badquote`) that must all fail, so the checker's own failure modes are proven rather than assumed. |","+| R2-06 | med | A killed process or reboot leaves the `mkdir` lock behind, silencing every future run; the proposed test removed the lock by hand and proved nothing about recovery. Failed writes to the trend file and error log were ignored. | **ACCEPTED.** The lock now records its owner PID and is **reclaimed** when the owner is not running (or the lock is over a day old with no pid). Every required write is checked, with the trend row read back to confirm. Task 7 Step 3 now tests three cases — dead metrics script, **live** lock, **stale** lock — and asserts the stale case actually adds a row. |","+| R2-07 | med | The revised regex matched `~/DEV`, but the actual probe was `ls /Users/piuser/DEV`: the preceding character is `/`, which the leading boundary did not allow — so the exact test probe would not have matched the guard. | **ACCEPTED.** `/` added to the leading boundary class. The probe now runs against a **disposable fixture that really exists** (`/Users/piuser/fixture/DEV`), so a block cannot be confused with a missing-directory error. The handler logs on entry, distinguishing \"guard blocked it\" from \"handler never ran\", and a third probe checks the guard does not fire on a sibling path. |","+| R2-08 | med | `piuser` running `npm install -g` targets `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules`, owned by `kristinarash:admin` mode 755 — the install fails before any measurement happens. | **ACCEPTED.** Verified. Task 8 sets a `piuser`-owned prefix (`/Users/piuser/.npm-global`) and calls the absolute executable in every step, since that prefix is not on `piuser`'s PATH. Teardown is a single `rm -rf` of that prefix; Homebrew is never touched. |","+| R2-09 | med | The Memory row delegates `~/.claude/projects/*/memory` and `global-memory` to `improve-system`, but that skill actually scans SecondBrain. Its Step 0 also applies approved proposals and writes a ledger, conflicting with a report-only audit. A clean exit would not establish the named stores were audited. | **ACCEPTED.** The row is split: **Memory (agent)** is audited by `aios-audit` directly with a concrete check; **Memory (vault notes)** delegates to `improve-system`. A new **delegation contract** in `rot.md` requires read-only invocation with mutation steps suppressed, requires verifying a delegate's real scope rather than its claimed one, and forbids stamping a date because a delegate exited cleanly. |","+","+**Rejected:** none.","+"," ---"," "," ### Task 1: Snapshot and freeze the current state"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cf4a68e9-46d7-4026-a45e-9dfe85eeee7c","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
