{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"4513f005-a65d-4015-9185-8d040bc2cea5","snapshotMessageId":"2166fd4d-d008-4569-9d96-a4a448b83b70","trackingPath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r2.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-09-12T17:28:06.120Z","realParentDir":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp"},"timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:28:06.129Z"}
{"parentUuid":"8608ff7e-61d7-49f0-80da-1bf094ea41e6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywQ3C1ZrHxQaJnAysPr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H3aySmWYR1iBzcXcPtxrrm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r2.md","content":"# Round 2 dispositions — all nine ACCEPTED\n\nThree claims were re-verified on disk before accepting.\n\n## Verified on disk\n\n- **R2-01:** `diff -rq` confirms the pool copies of `memory-write` and\n  `meeting-sync` differ from canonical. `comm -23` confirms **8** canonical\n  skills are absent from the pool, `backup` among them.\n- **R2-08:** `ls -ld /opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules` → `drwxr-xr-x kristinarash\n  admin`. `piuser` cannot write there; the prescribed install would have failed\n  before any measurement.\n- **R2-03:** confirmed the index still holds mode-120000 entries until a\n  `git add` replaces them, so the pre-staging check read stale data.\n\n## Disposition table\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed in the plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| R2-01 | ACCEPTED | `sync-to-codex.sh` no longer uses a hand-kept `SHARED` array of seven names. It enumerates **every** canonical directory containing a SKILL.md plus declared support dirs, refuses to run on an empty manifest, retires view entries no longer in canonical, and writes `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` recording exactly what it owns. New **Task 3 Step 5** reconciles the drift before the regenerate destroys it: it lists DIVERGED and ABSENT names, requires reading each diff, and copies the pool version to `~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/` first. Task 3 Step 6 asserts the ABSENT list is empty afterwards and the manifest holds 62 lines. |\n| R2-02 | ACCEPTED | `real_dirs_in_*_view` is replaced by `pool_view_drift` / `codex_view_drift`, which evaluate **only manifest-owned entries** and are platform-aware (symlink expected on Mac, copy on Windows). Third-party entries are counted separately as `pool_third_party` / `codex_third_party` and are explicitly reported as information, never as errors, in both `rot.md`'s invariants and the `aios-audit` body. A `no_manifest` sentinel distinguishes \"not yet synced\" from \"zero drift\". |\n| R2-03 | ACCEPTED | Task 3's git gate now expects **exactly** the two script edits plus any content moved in Step 5, and rejects anything unexpected — a clean tree was impossible at that point. Task 4 Step 4 now runs `git add -A` **first**, then inspects `git ls-files -s` for mode-120000 entries and reads `git diff --cached --summary` for the expected `delete mode 120000` pairs. The working-tree symlink count is checked separately and is expected non-zero before Task 4. |\n| R2-04 | ACCEPTED | Task 1 Step 2 now produces **two** tarballs: `pre-canonical-VIEWS-*.tgz` (`.codex/skills` + `.agents/skills`) and `pre-canonical-CANONICAL-*.tgz` (reference only). Step 3 verifies each independently and **asserts the VIEWS archive contains no `.claude` directory**. The rollback block states the two paths must never be combined, that git — not the tarball — is the canonical undo, that the CANONICAL tarball is for inspection in a scratch directory only, and that views must be **regenerated** after a canonical revert rather than restored. |\n| R2-05 | ACCEPTED | Clause detection rewritten to use **span containment**: every negative-phrase span is collected first, and a positive phrase is only counted if it does not sit inside one. `Do not use when auditing` now correctly fails for lacking a standalone positive clause. Added duplicate-key rejection and unbalanced-quote rejection for `name` and `description`. Task 5 Step 2 adds three fixtures — `negonly`, `dupekey`, `badquote` — that must all be reported FAIL, alongside the existing empty-inventory exit-2 case. |\n| R2-06 | ACCEPTED | The lock now writes its owner PID. `acquire_lock` stands down only when the owner is **live** (`kill -0`); a lock whose owner is gone, or that is older than a day with no pid file, is **reclaimed** and the run proceeds. The trap uses `rm -rf` so the pid file cannot block cleanup. Every required write is checked explicitly and the trend row is read back with `grep -qF` to confirm durability; a failed nudge write also exits 1. Task 7 Step 3 now tests three cases and asserts row counts: dead metrics script (no row), live lock (no row), stale lock (**one row added**). |\n| R2-07 | ACCEPTED | `/` added to the leading boundary character class, so `/Users/piuser/fixture/DEV` matches. The probe now runs against a **disposable fixture that exists and is readable**, verified with a plain `ls` first, so a block cannot be mistaken for a missing-directory error. The handler logs `[guard] saw tool_call:` on entry, separating \"guard blocked it\" from \"handler never registered\" — and the stop condition requires recording which of the two failed. A third probe (`ls /Users/piuser/fixture`) must **succeed**, checking the guard does not over-match. |\n| R2-08 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 Step 2 sets a `piuser`-owned npm prefix at `/Users/piuser/.npm-global` and invokes the absolute executable path in every subsequent step, because that prefix is not on `piuser`'s login PATH and `which pi` could resolve to nothing or to the operator's copy. Teardown is a single `rm -rf` of the prefix, fixture and trial dirs; `npm uninstall -g` is removed and Homebrew is never touched. |\n| R2-09 | ACCEPTED | The Memory row is split into **Memory (agent)** — `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` and `global-memory/`, audited by `aios-audit` directly with a concrete check (index entries resolve, files appear in the index, char cap, time-dimensioned facts) — and **Memory (vault notes)**, delegated to `improve-system`, which is what that skill actually scans. A new **delegation contract** section in `rot.md` requires read-only invocation with apply/ledger steps explicitly suppressed, requires verifying a delegate's real scope rather than its claimed scope, and forbids stamping a date because a delegate exited cleanly. The `aios-audit` body now points at that contract. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone. All nine findings were accepted.\n\n## Net change since round 2\n\n- `sync-to-codex.sh` went from a 7-name allowlist to a generated complete\n  manifest — this was the single largest correctness gap in the plan, because\n  the stated goal is that Pi and Codex see the same roster as Claude Code.\n- Task 1 went from one rollback tarball to two, with an assertion that they\n  do not overlap.\n- Three verification steps that could not have failed as written (Task 3's\n  clean-tree gate, Task 4's pre-staging index check, Task 7's stale-lock test)\n  now actually test what they claim.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":514,"cache_read_input_tokens":207053,"output_tokens":2526,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":514,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2526,"cache_read_input_tokens":207053,"cache_creation_input_tokens":514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":514},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeywQ2nwc2dYJp2pMohbY","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"4513f005-a65d-4015-9185-8d040bc2cea5","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:28:06.022Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"4513f005-a65d-4015-9185-8d040bc2cea5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H3aySmWYR1iBzcXcPtxrrm","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r2.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b330c5f8-d7a7-4298-844b-4cc4a3f54c29","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:28:06.518Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r2.md","content":"# Round 2 dispositions — all nine ACCEPTED\n\nThree claims were re-verified on disk before accepting.\n\n## Verified on disk\n\n- **R2-01:** `diff -rq` confirms the pool copies of `memory-write` and\n  `meeting-sync` differ from canonical. `comm -23` confirms **8** canonical\n  skills are absent from the pool, `backup` among them.\n- **R2-08:** `ls -ld /opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules` → `drwxr-xr-x kristinarash\n  admin`. `piuser` cannot write there; the prescribed install would have failed\n  before any measurement.\n- **R2-03:** confirmed the index still holds mode-120000 entries until a\n  `git add` replaces them, so the pre-staging check read stale data.\n\n## Disposition table\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed in the plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| R2-01 | ACCEPTED | `sync-to-codex.sh` no longer uses a hand-kept `SHARED` array of seven names. It enumerates **every** canonical directory containing a SKILL.md plus declared support dirs, refuses to run on an empty manifest, retires view entries no longer in canonical, and writes `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` recording exactly what it owns. New **Task 3 Step 5** reconciles the drift before the regenerate destroys it: it lists DIVERGED and ABSENT names, requires reading each diff, and copies the pool version to `~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/` first. Task 3 Step 6 asserts the ABSENT list is empty afterwards and the manifest holds 62 lines. |\n| R2-02 | ACCEPTED | `real_dirs_in_*_view` is replaced by `pool_view_drift` / `codex_view_drift`, which evaluate **only manifest-owned entries** and are platform-aware (symlink expected on Mac, copy on Windows). Third-party entries are counted separately as `pool_third_party` / `codex_third_party` and are explicitly reported as information, never as errors, in both `rot.md`'s invariants and the `aios-audit` body. A `no_manifest` sentinel distinguishes \"not yet synced\" from \"zero drift\". |\n| R2-03 | ACCEPTED | Task 3's git gate now expects **exactly** the two script edits plus any content moved in Step 5, and rejects anything unexpected — a clean tree was impossible at that point. Task 4 Step 4 now runs `git add -A` **first**, then inspects `git ls-files -s` for mode-120000 entries and reads `git diff --cached --summary` for the expected `delete mode 120000` pairs. The working-tree symlink count is checked separately and is expected non-zero before Task 4. |\n| R2-04 | ACCEPTED | Task 1 Step 2 now produces **two** tarballs: `pre-canonical-VIEWS-*.tgz` (`.codex/skills` + `.agents/skills`) and `pre-canonical-CANONICAL-*.tgz` (reference only). Step 3 verifies each independently and **asserts the VIEWS archive contains no `.claude` directory**. The rollback block states the two paths must never be combined, that git — not the tarball — is the canonical undo, that the CANONICAL tarball is for inspection in a scratch directory only, and that views must be **regenerated** after a canonical revert rather than restored. |\n| R2-05 | ACCEPTED | Clause detection rewritten to use **span containment**: every negative-phrase span is collected first, and a positive phrase is only counted if it does not sit inside one. `Do not use when auditing` now correctly fails for lacking a standalone positive clause. Added duplicate-key rejection and unbalanced-quote rejection for `name` and `description`. Task 5 Step 2 adds three fixtures — `negonly`, `dupekey`, `badquote` — that must all be reported FAIL, alongside the existing empty-inventory exit-2 case. |\n| R2-06 | ACCEPTED | The lock now writes its owner PID. `acquire_lock` stands down only when the owner is **live** (`kill -0`); a lock whose owner is gone, or that is older than a day with no pid file, is **reclaimed** and the run proceeds. The trap uses `rm -rf` so the pid file cannot block cleanup. Every required write is checked explicitly and the trend row is read back with `grep -qF` to confirm durability; a failed nudge write also exits 1. Task 7 Step 3 now tests three cases and asserts row counts: dead metrics script (no row), live lock (no row), stale lock (**one row added**). |\n| R2-07 | ACCEPTED | `/` added to the leading boundary character class, so `/Users/piuser/fixture/DEV` matches. The probe now runs against a **disposable fixture that exists and is readable**, verified with a plain `ls` first, so a block cannot be mistaken for a missing-directory error. The handler logs `[guard] saw tool_call:` on entry, separating \"guard blocked it\" from \"handler never registered\" — and the stop condition requires recording which of the two failed. A third probe (`ls /Users/piuser/fixture`) must **succeed**, checking the guard does not over-match. |\n| R2-08 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 Step 2 sets a `piuser`-owned npm prefix at `/Users/piuser/.npm-global` and invokes the absolute executable path in every subsequent step, because that prefix is not on `piuser`'s login PATH and `which pi` could resolve to nothing or to the operator's copy. Teardown is a single `rm -rf` of the prefix, fixture and trial dirs; `npm uninstall -g` is removed and Homebrew is never touched. |\n| R2-09 | ACCEPTED | The Memory row is split into **Memory (agent)** — `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` and `global-memory/`, audited by `aios-audit` directly with a concrete check (index entries resolve, files appear in the index, char cap, time-dimensioned facts) — and **Memory (vault notes)**, delegated to `improve-system`, which is what that skill actually scans. A new **delegation contract** section in `rot.md` requires read-only invocation with apply/ledger steps explicitly suppressed, requires verifying a delegate's real scope rather than its claimed scope, and forbids stamping a date because a delegate exited cleanly. The `aios-audit` body now points at that contract. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone. All nine findings were accepted.\n\n## Net change since round 2\n\n- `sync-to-codex.sh` went from a 7-name allowlist to a generated complete\n  manifest — this was the single largest correctness gap in the plan, because\n  the stated goal is that Pi and Codex see the same roster as Claude Code.\n- Task 1 went from one rollback tarball to two, with an assertion that they\n  do not overlap.\n- Three verification steps that could not have failed as written (Task 3's\n  clean-tree gate, Task 4's pre-staging index check, Task 7's stale-lock test)\n  now actually test what they claim.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4513f005-a65d-4015-9185-8d040bc2cea5","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
