{"parentUuid":"3705b18a-8ccd-4fd8-8482-a9f28f73eb63","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywXMW2P2w4EgdawGnNd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017s9tiQAXezy1fy1SxqVNh2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json,glob\nf=sorted(glob.glob('/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r3/**/result.json',recursive=True))\nd=json.load(open(f[0])); r=d['response']\nprint('VERDICT:',r.get('verdict'))\nprint('SUMMARY:',r.get('summary'))\nprint()\nfor x in r.get('findings',[]):\n    print('['+x['severity'].upper()+'] '+x['id']+'  '+x['path'].split(chr(8212))[-1].strip())\n    print('  E:',x['evidence'])\n    print('  F:',x['fix'])\n    print()\n\"","description":"Read round 3 verdict"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_read_input_tokens":210214,"output_tokens":307,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":492,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":307,"cache_read_input_tokens":210214,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":492},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeywXLtKdkGNkaUJpCvnd","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2f4d466-2898-4f6e-b755-942589bc3eb8","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:29:17.540Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c2f4d466-2898-4f6e-b755-942589bc3eb8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017s9tiQAXezy1fy1SxqVNh2","type":"tool_result","content":"VERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: The supplied SHA256 matches the on-disk plan. Several prior fixes are resolved, but the revision introduces an execution deadlock and unsafe manifest deletion; the negative-only checker defect also remains.\n\n[HIGH] R3-01  Task 3 Step 6 / Task 4 prerequisites\n  E: The complete-manifest guard now rejects every outward canonical symlink, including the existing anti-sleep and claudex-loop links. Task 3 Step 6 nevertheless requires successful dry and real sync before Task 4 may run. Only Task 4 removes those links. The mandatory prerequisites therefore form a deadlock. Task 4 subsequently runs only a dry sync, so simply bypassing the earlier gate would still leave views unpublished.\n  F: Install and verify the rejecting guard first, then canonicalize, then perform reconciliation and the full real sync. Move the successful-publication gate after canonicalization.\n\n[HIGH] R3-02  Task 3 sync retirement loop\n  E: The new writable view manifest supplies unchecked path components directly to rm -rf. A line '../../.claude/skills' in ~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex resolves outside the view and deletes the canonical repository on the next dev-sync. The nonempty-variable checks do not prevent traversal.\n  F: Validate every manifest entry as a single permitted basename before any mutation, reject separators and dot components, verify containment, and use literal matching rather than grep regular expressions. Archive retired entries before removal.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-03  Task 3 Step 3\n  E: The PowerShell modification still adds only a reparse-point guard to the existing seven-name SHARED loop. The inspected script has no complete enumeration, support-directory publication, ownership manifest, or retirement behavior. dev-sync explicitly invokes this twin on Windows, so the promised complete generated views and manifest-based audit remain unavailable there.\n  F: Implement the same manifest and ownership semantics in the PowerShell twin, using copies for Windows. Update its failure handling and specify equivalent verification before publishing the scripts.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-04  Task 5 clause_problems\n  E: The negative-only fixture still passes clause detection. In 'do not use when auditing', the negative span for 'do not use' is [0,10), while the positive span for 'use when' is [7,15). The positive span is not fully contained, so inside_negative returns false and pos_found becomes true. This directly contradicts the required fixture result.\n  F: Reject positive matches overlapping the governing negative phrase, or parse complete negative constructions including 'when' and 'for'. Preserve the explicit negative-only fixture as a required check.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-05  Task 1 archive verification and rollback\n  E: The canonical archive preserves relative links such as anti-sleep -> ../../.agents/skills/anti-sleep. Extracting it under /tmp/tartest/canon while extracting the pool under /tmp/tartest/views leaves those links dangling, so the canonical SKILL.md count cannot reach the expected 61. Separately, reverting the inversion commit while current pool entries point back into canonical creates reciprocal symlink cycles; the hardened sync then refuses to regenerate them.\n  F: Verify the two archives in a compatible isolated directory layout without overlaying a live repository. Define rollback by migration phase, including restoring real pool targets before reverting canonical entries back to outward symlinks.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-06  Task 3 Step 6\n  E: The ABSENT assertion compares all top-level canonical entries against the pool, but the sync publishes only SKILL.md directories and _shared. Existing canonical entries include CLAUDE.md, docs, sync-to-codex.sh, and sync-to-codex.ps1. These legitimately remain absent after successful publication, so the required empty output cannot establish success.\n  F: Compare the generated managed manifest against actual view entries, excluding repository scripts and documentation. Derive expected counts from that same manifest.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-07  Task 6 view_drift\n  E: The audit trusts the view's own manifest without comparing it to canonical inventory. An empty manifest reports zero drift despite missing every canonical skill. A managed Mac symlink pointing at the wrong existing directory also reports zero drift, and Windows copies with stale contents pass because only representation is checked.\n  F: Compare manifest membership against canonical expected entries, verify each Mac link resolves to its exact canonical target, and compare Windows copy contents. Report missing, extra, misdirected, and stale managed entries separately.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"be46397d-00c7-442e-88c9-1e26a05da274","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:29:18.918Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"VERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: The supplied SHA256 matches the on-disk plan. Several prior fixes are resolved, but the revision introduces an execution deadlock and unsafe manifest deletion; the negative-only checker defect also remains.\n\n[HIGH] R3-01  Task 3 Step 6 / Task 4 prerequisites\n  E: The complete-manifest guard now rejects every outward canonical symlink, including the existing anti-sleep and claudex-loop links. Task 3 Step 6 nevertheless requires successful dry and real sync before Task 4 may run. Only Task 4 removes those links. The mandatory prerequisites therefore form a deadlock. Task 4 subsequently runs only a dry sync, so simply bypassing the earlier gate would still leave views unpublished.\n  F: Install and verify the rejecting guard first, then canonicalize, then perform reconciliation and the full real sync. Move the successful-publication gate after canonicalization.\n\n[HIGH] R3-02  Task 3 sync retirement loop\n  E: The new writable view manifest supplies unchecked path components directly to rm -rf. A line '../../.claude/skills' in ~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex resolves outside the view and deletes the canonical repository on the next dev-sync. The nonempty-variable checks do not prevent traversal.\n  F: Validate every manifest entry as a single permitted basename before any mutation, reject separators and dot components, verify containment, and use literal matching rather than grep regular expressions. Archive retired entries before removal.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-03  Task 3 Step 3\n  E: The PowerShell modification still adds only a reparse-point guard to the existing seven-name SHARED loop. The inspected script has no complete enumeration, support-directory publication, ownership manifest, or retirement behavior. dev-sync explicitly invokes this twin on Windows, so the promised complete generated views and manifest-based audit remain unavailable there.\n  F: Implement the same manifest and ownership semantics in the PowerShell twin, using copies for Windows. Update its failure handling and specify equivalent verification before publishing the scripts.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-04  Task 5 clause_problems\n  E: The negative-only fixture still passes clause detection. In 'do not use when auditing', the negative span for 'do not use' is [0,10), while the positive span for 'use when' is [7,15). The positive span is not fully contained, so inside_negative returns false and pos_found becomes true. This directly contradicts the required fixture result.\n  F: Reject positive matches overlapping the governing negative phrase, or parse complete negative constructions including 'when' and 'for'. Preserve the explicit negative-only fixture as a required check.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-05  Task 1 archive verification and rollback\n  E: The canonical archive preserves relative links such as anti-sleep -> ../../.agents/skills/anti-sleep. Extracting it under /tmp/tartest/canon while extracting the pool under /tmp/tartest/views leaves those links dangling, so the canonical SKILL.md count cannot reach the expected 61. Separately, reverting the inversion commit while current pool entries point back into canonical creates reciprocal symlink cycles; the hardened sync then refuses to regenerate them.\n  F: Verify the two archives in a compatible isolated directory layout without overlaying a live repository. Define rollback by migration phase, including restoring real pool targets before reverting canonical entries back to outward symlinks.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-06  Task 3 Step 6\n  E: The ABSENT assertion compares all top-level canonical entries against the pool, but the sync publishes only SKILL.md directories and _shared. Existing canonical entries include CLAUDE.md, docs, sync-to-codex.sh, and sync-to-codex.ps1. These legitimately remain absent after successful publication, so the required empty output cannot establish success.\n  F: Compare the generated managed manifest against actual view entries, excluding repository scripts and documentation. Derive expected counts from that same manifest.\n\n[MEDIUM] R3-07  Task 6 view_drift\n  E: The audit trusts the view's own manifest without comparing it to canonical inventory. An empty manifest reports zero drift despite missing every canonical skill. A managed Mac symlink pointing at the wrong existing directory also reports zero drift, and Windows copies with stale contents pass because only representation is checked.\n  F: Compare manifest membership against canonical expected entries, verify each Mac link resolves to its exact canonical target, and compare Windows copy contents. Report missing, extra, misdirected, and stale managed entries separately.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2f4d466-2898-4f6e-b755-942589bc3eb8","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristi