{"parentUuid":"cff504dd-42ea-4cf2-a5ff-411450cfd0cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywbBCmV9MZsrAUzyfze","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the deadlock — Task 3 required a sync that its own new guard correctly refuses until Task 4 runs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1564,"cache_read_input_tokens":215163,"output_tokens":2044,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":314},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2044,"cache_read_input_tokens":215163,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeywbAW6nAASTcKxCqKHE","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"d61c3d16-7dad-4494-95c2-684d2fd01cce","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:30:11.849Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d61c3d16-7dad-4494-95c2-684d2fd01cce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywbBCmV9MZsrAUzyfze","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UU1fVfdYBCFBnDsnz9aadV","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**\n\nBefore the views are regenerated, the existing pool copies must be checked — regenerating overwrites them, and two of them contain edits that exist nowhere else. Verified on disk today: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **differ** between canonical and pool; `backup` and 7 others are **absent** from the pool entirely.","new_string":"- [ ] **Step 5: Confirm the guard refuses the CURRENT layout — and that this is correct**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 2)\"\n```\n\nExpected: a list of `FATAL ... is a symlink` lines naming the 19 outward links (`anti-sleep`, `claudex-loop`, …) and `exit=2`.\n\n**This is the correct result, not a failure.** Round 3 caught a deadlock here: an earlier draft demanded a *successful* sync at this point, but the guard this task installs deliberately rejects outward canonical symlinks, and only Task 4 removes them. Requiring both made the two tasks impossible to run in either order.\n\nThe order is now: **install and prove the guard (Task 3) → canonicalize (Task 4) → reconcile and publish (Task 4, Steps 8–10).** No real sync runs until the layout the guard demands actually exists.\n\n> If this prints `exit=0` instead, the manifest loop is not seeing the outward links — that means the guard would not have protected anything. Stop and fix.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n\n```bash\ngrep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20\necho \"--- staged/modified in canonical ---\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short\n```\n\nExpected: `git status` shows **exactly** `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` as modified, **and nothing else**. Round 2 caught the earlier wording, which demanded a clean tree at a point where this task has deliberately just edited two tracked files. What matters is that no *unexpected* path appears, especially not a symlink inside the repo.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit both copies**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add sync-to-codex.sh sync-to-codex.ps1\ngit commit -m \"fix: generate complete views from canonical; refuse symlinked sources\n\nDelete-then-copy destroyed the link target when ~/.claude/skills/<name>\npointed into ~/.agents/skills (R1). Views are now generated from the full\ncanonical manifest rather than a 7-name allowlist (R2-01), with manifest\nentries validated as plain basenames before any removal (R3-02).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Invert the outward symlinks, then publish the views\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `~/.claude/skills/` (19 symlinks become real dirs)\n- Modify: `~/.agents/skills/`, `~/.codex/skills/` (regenerated from the manifest)\n- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: the hardened, guard-proven sync script from Task 3.\n- Produces: a canonical repo with **zero symlinks**, and two views carrying every canonical skill. Task 5 then edits one file per skill and all three harnesses see it.\n\n**Direction, restated because round 1 had it backwards.** 19 entries in `~/.claude/skills/` are symlinks pointing *out* to `~/.agents/skills/`. Their real content therefore sits outside the git repo — unversioned, not on Windows, not in the backup. This task pulls each real directory **into** the repo, leaves a link behind at the pool, and only then publishes the views.\n\n**PLACEHOLDER-TASK4-STEPS**\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**\n\nBefore the views are regenerated, the existing pool copies must be checked — regenerating overwrites them, and two of them contain edits that exist nowhere else. Verified on disk today: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **differ** between canonical and pool; `backup` and 7 others are **absent** from the pool entirely."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1564,"cache_read_input_tokens":215163,"output_tokens":2044,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":314},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2044,"cache_read_input_tokens":215163,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CeywbAW6nAASTcKxCqKHE","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"210cf281-95f9-47b2-a405-7077866d335e","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:30:30.131Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
