{"parentUuid":"558bd66f-69ae-4845-a0fb-7a7f52f968c7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G9acc8ZXdHDWG7zKEm7CSn","type":"tool_result","content":"610\tRead each diff. If the pool copy is newer or better, copy that content **into canonical** (`cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/`) and commit it there. If canonical wins, do nothing — the sync will overwrite the pool. **Do not skip reading the diffs**; regenerating discards whatever you did not move. The `pre-sync-2026-09-12/` backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong.\n611\t\n612\tThe ABSENT names need no action: the new complete-manifest sync publishes them automatically. That is the bug the manifest fixes.\n613\t\n614\t- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the normal path publishes everything**\n615\t\n616\t```bash\n617\tDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n618\tDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh | grep -c 'would sync'\n619\tbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n620\techo \"--- every canonical skill must now be in the pool (must be empty) ---\"\n621\tcomm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)\n622\techo \"--- manifest ---\"\n623\twc -l < ~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\n624\tls -la ~/.codex/skills | grep -E 'startup|backup' | head -4\n625\t```\n626\t\n627\tExpected: `exit=0` both times; the `would sync` count is **122** (61 skills × 2 views) or higher with support dirs; the ABSENT list is now **empty**; the manifest holds 62 lines; the listing shows symlinks into `~/.claude/skills`. An ABSENT name still printing means the manifest loop did not pick it up.\n628\t\n629\t- [ ] **Step 7: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n630\t\n631\t```bash\n632\tgrep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20\n633\techo \"--- staged/modified in canonical ---\"\n634\tgit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short\n635\techo \"--- symlinks in the working tree (must be 0 until Task 4) ---\"\n636\tfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\n637\t```\n638\t\n639\tExpected: `git status` shows **exactly** `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` as modified — plus any skill content moved in Step 5 — **and nothing else**. Round 2 caught the earlier wording here, which demanded a clean tree at a point where this task has deliberately just edited two tracked files; a clean tree would have been impossible. What matters is that no *unexpected* path appears, especially not a symlink inside the repo.\n640\t\n641\t> The `find` count is still non-zero at this point (19 outward links remain until Task 4). That is expected here. It must read `0` after Task 4, and `git ls-files` must never stage one — that check lives in Task 4 Step 4, after staging.\n642\t\n643\t- [ ] **Step 8: Commit both copies**\n644\t\n645\t```bash\n646\tcd ~/.claude/skills\n647\tgit add sync-to-codex.sh sync-to-codex.ps1\n648\tgit commit -m \"fix: refuse to sync when canonical source is a symlink (R1)\n649\t\n650\tDelete-then-copy destroyed the link target when ~/.claude/skills/<name>\n651\tpointed into ~/.agents/skills. Views are now generated from a proven-real\n652\tcanonical source; symlink on Mac, copy on Windows.\n653\t\n654\tCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n655\tgit push\n656\tcd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS\n657\tprintf '# Sync hardening 2026-09-12\\n\\nR1 fix. Guard test output:\\n\\n```\\n%s\\n```\\n' \\\n658\t  \"$(HOME=/tmp/syncguard bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\")\" \\\n659\t  > docs/audits/2026-09-12-sync-hardening.md\n660\tgit add docs/audits/2026-09-12-sync-hardening.md\n661\tgit commit -m \"docs: record the sync guard test\n662\t\n663\tCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n664\t```\n665\t\n666\t---\n667\t\n668\t### Task 4: Invert the 19 outward symlinks into the canonical repo\n669\t\n670\t**Files:**\n671\t- Modify: `~/.claude/skills/` (19 symlinks become real dirs)\n672\t- Modify: `~/.agents/skills/` (19 real dirs become links back)\n673\t- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`\n674\t\n675\t**Interfaces:**\n676\t- Consumes: the hardened sync script from Task 3.\n677\t- Produces: a canonical repo with **zero symlinks**, so Task 5 edits one file per skill and every harness sees it.\n678\t\n679\t**Direction, restated because round 1 had it backwards.** 19 entries in `~/.claude/skills/` are symlinks pointing *out* to `~/.agents/skills/`. Their real content therefore sits outside the git repo — unversioned, not on Windows, not in the backup. This task pulls each real directory **into** the repo and leaves a link behind at the pool.\n680\t\n681\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**\n682\t\n683\tCreate `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`:\n684\t\n685\t```bash\n686\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n687\t# Invert outward symlinks so ~/.claude/skills holds real directories only.\n688\t#   before: ~/.claude/skills/X -> ~/.agents/skills/X   (real content outside git)\n689\t#   after:  ~/.claude/skills/X is real; ~/.agents/skills/X -> it"}]},"uuid":"013ed8d2-1cca-4a41-ab67-226ffe31d14c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:30:55.814Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","content":"Read each diff. If the pool copy is newer or better, copy that content **into canonical** (`cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/`) and commit it there. If canonical wins, do nothing — the sync will overwrite the pool. **Do not skip reading the diffs**; regenerating discards whatever you did not move. The `pre-sync-2026-09-12/` backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong.\n\nThe ABSENT names need no action: the new complete-manifest sync publishes them automatically. That is the bug the manifest fixes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the normal path publishes everything**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh | grep -c 'would sync'\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\necho \"--- every canonical skill must now be in the pool (must be empty) ---\"\ncomm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)\necho \"--- manifest ---\"\nwc -l < ~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\nls -la ~/.codex/skills | grep -E 'startup|backup' | head -4\n```\n\nExpected: `exit=0` both times; the `would sync` count is **122** (61 skills × 2 views) or higher with support dirs; the ABSENT list is now **empty**; the manifest holds 62 lines; the listing shows symlinks into `~/.claude/skills`. An ABSENT name still printing means the manifest loop did not pick it up.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n\n```bash\ngrep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20\necho \"--- staged/modified in canonical ---\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short\necho \"--- symlinks in the working tree (must be 0 until Task 4) ---\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\n```\n\nExpected: `git status` shows **exactly** `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` as modified — plus any skill content moved in Step 5 — **and nothing else**. Round 2 caught the earlier wording here, which demanded a clean tree at a point where this task has deliberately just edited two tracked files; a clean tree would have been impossible. What matters is that no *unexpected* path appears, especially not a symlink inside the repo.\n\n> The `find` count is still non-zero at this point (19 outward links remain until Task 4). That is expected here. It must read `0` after Task 4, and `git ls-files` must never stage one — that check lives in Task 4 Step 4, after staging.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Commit both copies**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add sync-to-codex.sh sync-to-codex.ps1\ngit commit -m \"fix: refuse to sync when canonical source is a symlink (R1)\n\nDelete-then-copy destroyed the link target when ~/.claude/skills/<name>\npointed into ~/.agents/skills. Views are now generated from a proven-real\ncanonical source; symlink on Mac, copy on Windows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\ncd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS\nprintf '# Sync hardening 2026-09-12\\n\\nR1 fix. Guard test output:\\n\\n```\\n%s\\n```\\n' \\\n  \"$(HOME=/tmp/syncguard bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\")\" \\\n  > docs/audits/2026-09-12-sync-hardening.md\ngit add docs/audits/2026-09-12-sync-hardening.md\ngit commit -m \"docs: record the sync guard test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Invert the 19 outward symlinks into the canonical repo\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `~/.claude/skills/` (19 symlinks become real dirs)\n- Modify: `~/.agents/skills/` (19 real dirs become links back)\n- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: the hardened sync script from Task 3.\n- Produces: a canonical repo with **zero symlinks**, so Task 5 edits one file per skill and every harness sees it.\n\n**Direction, restated because round 1 had it backwards.** 19 entries in `~/.claude/skills/` are symlinks pointing *out* to `~/.agents/skills/`. Their real content therefore sits outside the git repo — unversioned, not on Windows, not in the backup. This task pulls each real directory **into** the repo and leaves a link behind at the pool.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**\n\nCreate `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Invert outward symlinks so ~/.claude/skills holds real directories only.\n#   before: ~/.claude/skills/X -> ~/.agents/skills/X   (real content outside git)\n#   after:  ~/.claude/skills/X is real; ~/.agents/skills/X -> it","numLines":80,"startLine":61