{"parentUuid":"013ed8d2-1cca-4a41-ab67-226ffe31d14c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/CLAUDE.md","content":{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"# KeystoneOS Claude Adapter\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` — it is the canonical router and operating policy for this repo. Everything below is Claude-specific only.\n\n- The Claude memory pipeline at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\claude-memory-compiler` is valuable and must remain in place. KeystoneOS makes that memory visible to other harnesses by reference, never by rewriting it.\n- Claude global working memory lives at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\global-memory` (USER.md, MEMORY.md, transcripts/). It is enumerated in `data/memory-sources.json` like every other source.\n- Commits to this repo are artifacts, not reviewed code: autonomous commit and push are authorized (decision 2026-06-11, memory `feedback-auto-commit-push`).\n\n## Agent skills\n\n### Issue tracker\n\nIssues live as local markdown files under `.scratch/<feature>/` in this repo. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n\n### Domain docs\n\n**This repo's decision record is `decisions/log.md`** — append-only, one section per decision, current. Read it before proposing architectural changes, and append to it rather than starting a parallel store.\n\n`docs/agents/domain.md` describes the generic `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/` convention used by the engineering skills. Neither exists here and neither is required — that doc says to proceed silently when they're absent. If `/domain-modeling` ever creates them lazily, `decisions/log.md` still wins on any conflict (see the precedence rule in `AGENTS.md`).\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false},"displayPath":"CLAUDE.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d054d1f2-9040-4ffe-b16a-a1559c56d5c7","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:30:55.827Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/CLAUDE.md:\n\n# KeystoneOS Claude Adapter\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` — it is the canonical router and operating policy for this repo. Everything below is Claude-specific only.\n\n- The Claude memory pipeline at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\claude-memory-compiler` is valuable and must remain in place. KeystoneOS makes that memory visible to other harnesses by reference, never by rewriting it.\n- Claude global working memory lives at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\global-memory` (USER.md, MEMORY.md, transcripts/). It is enumerated in `data/memory-sources.json` like every other source.\n- Commits to this repo are artifacts, not reviewed code: autonomous commit and push are authorized (decision 2026-06-11, memory `feedback-auto-commit-push`).\n\n## Agent skills\n\n### Issue tracker\n\nIssues live as local markdown files under `.scratch/<feature>/` in this repo. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n\n### Domain docs\n\n**This repo's decision record is `decisions/log.md`** — append-only, one section per decision, current. Read it before proposing architectural changes, and append to it rather than starting a parallel store.\n\n`docs/agents/domain.md` describes the generic `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/` convention used by the engineering skills. Neither exists here and neither is required — that doc says to proceed silently when they're absent. If `/domain-modeling` ever creates them lazily, `decisions/log.md` still wins on any conflict (see the precedence rule in `AGENTS.md`).\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
