{"parentUuid":"fdf1cfa5-4dc3-4239-9656-f2aea1d6a652","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywesBvNhctA6i48fuBj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4331,"cache_read_input_tokens":219684,"output_tokens":3006,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":231},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4331,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3006,"cache_read_input_tokens":219684,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4331,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4331},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeywerWysY1d7jkjAYoKr","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"bc9a017e-a444-44ea-a012-fb50545d5f33","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:31:00.790Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"bc9a017e-a444-44ea-a012-fb50545d5f33","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywesBvNhctA6i48fuBj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SWdvNTwCQ1yLz7Rwne8FqD","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the normal path publishes everything**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh | grep -c 'would sync'\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\necho \"--- every canonical skill must now be in the pool (must be empty) ---\"\ncomm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)\necho \"--- manifest ---\"\nwc -l < ~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\nls -la ~/.codex/skills | grep -E 'startup|backup' | head -4\n```\n\nExpected: `exit=0` both times; the `would sync` count is **122** (61 skills × 2 views) or higher with support dirs; the ABSENT list is now **empty**; the manifest holds 62 lines; the listing shows symlinks into `~/.claude/skills`. An ABSENT name still printing means the manifest loop did not pick it up.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n\n```bash\ngrep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20\necho \"--- staged/modified in canonical ---\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short\necho \"--- symlinks in the working tree (must be 0 until Task 4) ---\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\n```\n\nExpected: `git status` shows **exactly** `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` as modified — plus any skill content moved in Step 5 — **and nothing else**. Round 2 caught the earlier wording here, which demanded a clean tree at a point where this task has deliberately just edited two tracked files; a clean tree would have been impossible. What matters is that no *unexpected* path appears, especially not a symlink inside the repo.\n\n> The `find` count is still non-zero at this point (19 outward links remain until Task 4). That is expected here. It must read `0` after Task 4, and `git ls-files` must never stage one — that check lives in Task 4 Step 4, after staging.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Commit both copies**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add sync-to-codex.sh sync-to-codex.ps1\ngit commit -m \"fix: refuse to sync when canonical source is a symlink (R1)\n\nDelete-then-copy destroyed the link target when ~/.claude/skills/<name>\npointed into ~/.agents/skills. Views are now generated from a proven-real\ncanonical source; symlink on Mac, copy on Windows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\ncd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS\nprintf '# Sync hardening 2026-09-12\\n\\nR1 fix. Guard test output:\\n\\n```\\n%s\\n```\\n' \\\n  \"$(HOME=/tmp/syncguard bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\")\" \\\n  > docs/audits/2026-09-12-sync-hardening.md\ngit add docs/audits/2026-09-12-sync-hardening.md\ngit commit -m \"docs: record the sync guard test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Invert the 19 outward symlinks into the canonical repo\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `~/.claude/skills/` (19 symlinks become real dirs)\n- Modify: `~/.agents/skills/` (19 real dirs become links back)\n- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: the hardened sync script from Task 3.\n- Produces: a canonical repo with **zero symlinks**, so Task 5 edits one file per skill and every harness sees it.\n\n**Direction, restated because round 1 had it backwards.** 19 entries in `~/.claude/skills/` are symlinks pointing *out* to `~/.agents/skills/`. Their real content therefore sits outside the git repo — unversioned, not on Windows, not in the backup. This task pulls each real directory **into** the repo and leaves a link behind at the pool.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**","new_string":"- [ ] **Step 9: Publish the views and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"dry exit=$?\"\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real exit=$?\"\n\nMAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\necho \"--- manifest size ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"\n\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\n\necho \"--- managed links that do not resolve to canonical (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do\n  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"\ndone < \"$MAN\"\n```\n\nExpected: both `exit=0`; the manifest holds **62** lines (61 skills + `_shared`); all three MISSING/WRONG-TARGET lists are **empty**.\n\n> **R3-06:** success is measured against the **manifest**, not against `ls ~/.claude/skills`. The repo legitimately also contains `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view. Comparing raw directory listings would report those as permanent failures.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n\nRun `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61). If it dropped, roll back per Task 1 Path 1.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\ngit status --short | head\ngit commit -m \"refactor: canonical repo holds real directories, no symlinks\n\n19 skills whose content lived in ~/.agents/skills are now inside the repo,\nso they version and reach Windows. The views link back to them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\ncd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS && git add scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh && git commit -m \"feat: symlink inversion script\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### PLACEHOLDER-TASK5-MARKER\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4331,"cache_read_input_tokens":219684,"output_tokens":3006,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":231},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4331,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3006,"cache_read_input_tokens":219684,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4331,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4331},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeywerWysY1d7jkjAYoKr","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0d30862-1efa-45fe-8b82-d6ca63c5e08b","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:31:27.408Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
