tated because round 1 had it backwards.** 19 entries in `~/.claude/skills/` are symlinks pointing *out* to `~/.agents/skills/`. Their real content therefore sits outside the git repo — unversioned, not on Windows, not in the backup. This task pulls each real directory **into** the repo and leaves a link behind at the pool.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**","newString":"- [ ] **Step 9: Publish the views and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"dry exit=$?\"\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real exit=$?\"\n\nMAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\necho \"--- manifest size ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"\n\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\n\necho \"--- managed links that do not resolve to canonical (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do\n  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"\ndone < \"$MAN\"\n```\n\nExpected: both `exit=0`; the manifest holds **62** lines (61 skills + `_shared`); all three MISSING/WRONG-TARGET lists are **empty**.\n\n> **R3-06:** success is measured against the **manifest**, not against `ls ~/.claude/skills`. The repo legitimately also contains `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view. Comparing raw directory listings would report those as permanent failures.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n\nRun `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61). If it dropped, roll back per Task 1 Path 1.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\ngit status --short | head\ngit commit -m \"refactor: canonical repo holds real directories, no symlinks\n\n19 skills whose content lived in ~/.agents/skills are now inside the repo,\nso they version and reach Windows. The views link back to them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\ncd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS && git add scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh && git commit -m \"feat: symlink inversion script\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### PLACEHOLDER-TASK5-MARKER\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":611,"oldLines":73,"newStart":611,"newLines":55,"lines":[" "," The ABSENT names need no action: the new complete-manifest sync publishes them automatically. That is the bug the manifest fixes."," ","-- [ ] **Step 6: Prove the normal path publishes everything**","+- [ ] **Step 9: Publish the views and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**"," "," ```bash","-DRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"","-DRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh | grep -c 'would sync'","-bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"","-echo \"--- every canonical skill must now be in the pool (must be empty) ---\"","-comm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)","-echo \"--- manifest ---\"","-wc -l < ~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex","-ls -la ~/.codex/skills | grep -E 'startup|backup' | head -4","-```","+DRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"dry exit=$?\"","+bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real exit=$?\""," ","-Expected: `exit=0` both times; the `would sync` count is **122** (61 skills × 2 views) or higher with support dirs; the ABSENT list is now **empty**; the manifest holds 62 lines; the listing shows symlinks into `~/.claude/skills`. An ABSENT name still printing means the manifest loop did not pick it up.","+MAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex","+echo \"--- manifest size ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\""," ","-- [ ] **Step 7: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**","+echo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"","+while IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"","+echo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"","+while IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\""," ","-```bash","-grep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20","-echo \"--- staged/modified in canonical ---\"","-git -C ~/.claude/skills status --short","-echo \"--- symlinks in the working tree (must be 0 until Task 4) ---\"","-find ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l","+echo \"--- managed links that do not resolve to canonical (must be empty) ---\"","+while IFS= read -r s; do","+  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"","+  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"","+done < \"$MAN\""," ```"," ","-Expected: `git status` shows **exactly** `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` as modified — plus any skill content moved in Step 5 — **and nothing else**. Round 2 caught the earlier wording here, which demanded a clean tree at a point where this task has deliberately just edited two tracked files; a clean tree would have been impossible. What matters is that no *unexpected* path appears, especially not a symlink inside the repo.","+Expected: both `exit=0`; the manifest holds **62** lines (61 skills + `_shared`); all three MISSING/WRONG-TARGET lists are **empty**."," ","-> The `find` count is still non-zero at this point (19 outward links remain until Task 4). That is expected here. It must read `0` after Task 4, and `git ls-files` must never stage one — that check lives in Task 4 Step 4, after