{"parentUuid":"71b71b0f-e884-4181-a815-aa62f61a546c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywhgR75rNxiKcgb9tuc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L9VbsukQun5JMETqg1UpJv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = \"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md\"\nt = open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\n\nA = \"**PLACEHOLDER-TASK4-STEPS**\\n\\n\"\nB = \"### PLACEHOLDER-TASK5-MARKER\\n\\n\"\nassert A in t and B in t, \"markers missing\"\n\ni = t.index(A)\nj = t.index(B)\ngroup = t[i + len(A): j]            # reconcile(8) + publish(9) + confirm(10)\nassert \"Step 8: Reconcile\" in group and \"Step 10: Confirm\" in group\n\n# Remove the group and both markers; invert steps now follow the Task 4 intro.\nt = t[:i] + t[j + len(B):]\n\n# The invert block ends at its own old Step 7 (confirm + commit) - replace that\n# with the moved group, renumbered 7/8/9.\nold7 = \"- [ ] **Step 7: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\"\nk = t.index(old7)\nend = t.index(\"\\n### Task 5:\", k)\n\ngroup = (group.replace(\"Step 8: Reconcile\", \"Step 7: Reconcile\")\n              .replace(\"Step 9: Publish\",   \"Step 8: Publish\")\n              .replace(\"Step 10: Confirm\",  \"Step 9: Confirm\")\n              .rstrip() + \"\\n\\n---\\n\")\n\nt = t[:k] + group + t[end + 1:]\nopen(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(t)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPYEOF\necho \"--- Task 4 step order now ---\"\ngrep -n '^### Task \\|^- \\[ \\] \\*\\*Step' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md | sed -n '/Task 3/,/Task 5/p'","description":"Reorder Task 4 steps and verify"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1185,"cache_read_input_tokens":227157,"output_tokens":2207,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1441},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1185,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2207,"cache_read_input_tokens":227157,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1185},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CeywhenNMBVVXHt15oaq5","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"b5972998-f735-44b2-9b47-a07742227c3f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:32:03.843Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b5972998-f735-44b2-9b47-a07742227c3f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L9VbsukQun5JMETqg1UpJv","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\n--- Task 4 step order now ---\n318:### Task 3: Harden the sync writers — before anything moves\n337:- [ ] **Step 1: Read both current scripts and record the baseline**\n347:- [ ] **Step 2: Rewrite the bash script**\n490:- [ ] **Step 3: Apply the same guard to the PowerShell twin**\n507:- [ ] **Step 4: Prove the guard fires — the whole point of this task**\n521:- [ ] **Step 5: Confirm the guard refuses the CURRENT layout — and that this is correct**\n535:- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n545:- [ ] **Step 7: Commit both copies**\n563:### Task 4: Invert the outward symlinks, then publish the views\n576:- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**\n633:- [ ] **Step 2: Dry run and read every line**\n641:- [ ] **Step 3: Apply**\n649:- [ ] **Step 4: Verify the canonical repo is symlink-free and complete**\n677:- [ ] **Step 5: Verify `_shared` consumers still resolve (the R2 check)**\n694:- [ ] **Step 6: Re-run the sync guard now that the layout changed**\n702:- [ ] **Step 7: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**\n738:- [ ] **Step 8: Publish the views and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**\n763:- [ ] **Step 9: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n786:### Task 5: Normalize every skill to portable frontmatter","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cac5a1a8-6cdb-4bc3-9e53-fc2e9ca869a7","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:32:05.332Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok\n--- Task 4 step order now ---\n318:### Task 3: Harden the sync writers — before anything moves\n337:- [ ] **Step 1: Read both current scripts and record the baseline**\n347:- [ ] **Step 2: Rewrite the bash script**\n490:- [ ] **Step 3: Apply the same guard to the PowerShell twin**\n507:- [ ] **Step 4: Prove the guard fires — the whole point of this task**\n521:- [ ] **Step 5: Confirm the guard refuses the CURRENT layout — and that this is correct**\n535:- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n545:- [ ] **Step 7: Commit both copies**\n563:### Task 4: Invert the outward symlinks, then publish the views\n576:- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**\n633:- [ ] **Step 2: Dry run and read every line**\n641:- [ ] **Step 3: Apply**\n649:- [ ] **Step 4: Verify the canonical repo is symlink-free and complete**\n677:- [ ] **Step 5: Verify `_shared` consumers still resolve (the R2 check)**\n694:- [ ] **Step 6: Re-run the sync guard now that the layout changed**\n702:- [ ] **Step 7: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**\n738:- [ ] **Step 8: Publish the views and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**\n763:- [ ] **Step 9: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n786:### Task 5: Normalize every skill to portable frontmatter","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":573,"oldLines":93,"newStart":573,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," **Direction, restated because round 1 had it backwards.** 19 entries in `~/.claude/skills/` are symlinks pointing *out* to `~/.agents/skills/`. Their real content therefore sits outside the git repo — unversioned, not on Windows, not in the backup. This task pulls each real directory **into** the repo, leaves a link behind at the pool, and only then publishes the views."," ","-**PLACEHOLDER-TASK4-STEPS**","-","-- [ ] **Step 8: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**","-","-Before the views are regenerated, the existing pool copies must be checked — regenerating overwrites them, and two of them contain edits that exist nowhere else. Verified on disk today: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **differ** between canonical and pool; `backup` and 7 others are **absent** from the pool entirely.","-","-```bash","-mkdir -p ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12","-echo \"=== canonical skills whose pool copy DIFFERS ===\"","-for d in ~/.claude/skills/*/; do","-  s=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"","-  [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ] || continue","-  b=~/.agents/skills/\"$s\"","-  if [ -e \"$b\" ] && [ ! -L \"$b\" ] && ! diff -rq \"$d\" \"$b\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then","-    echo \"DIVERGED $s\"","-  fi","-done","-echo \"=== canonical skills ABSENT from the pool ===\"","-comm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)","-```","-","-Expected: at least `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` under DIVERGED, and 8 names under ABSENT.","-","-For **each** DIVERGED name, look at the actual difference and decide which side wins — then back up the pool copy before it is overwritten:","-","-```bash","-for s in memory-write meeting-sync; do","-  echo \"===== $s =====\"","-  diff -ru ~/.claude/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" | head -40","-  cp -R ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/\"$s\"","-done","-ls ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/","-```","-","-Read each diff. If the pool copy is newer or better, copy that content **into canonical** (`cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/`) and commit it there. If canonical wins, do nothing — the sync will overwrite the pool. **Do not skip reading the diffs**; regenerating discards whatever you did not move. The `pre-sync-2026-09-12/` backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong.","-","-The ABSENT names need no action: the new complete-manifest sync publishes them automatically. That is the bug the manifest fixes.","-","-- [ ] **Step 9: Publish the views and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**","-","-```bash","-DRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"dry exit=$?\"","-bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real exit=$?\"","-","-MAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex","-echo \"--- manifest size ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"","-","-echo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"","-while IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"","-echo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"","-while IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"","-","-echo \"--- managed links that do not resolve to canonical (must be empty) ---\"","-while IFS= read -r s; do","-  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"","-  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"","-done < \"$MAN\"","-```","-","-Expected: both `exit=0`; the manifest holds **62** lines (61 skills + `_shared`); all three MISSING/WRONG-TARGET lists are **empty**.","-","-> **R3-06:** success is measured against the **manifest**, not against `ls ~/.claude/skills`. The repo legitimately also contains `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view. Comparing raw directory listings would report those as permanent failures.","-","-- [ ] **Step 10: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**","-","-Run `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61). If it dropped, roll back per Task 1 Path 1.","-","-```bash","-cd ~/.claude/skills","-git add -A","-git status --short | head","-git commit -m \"refactor: canonical repo holds real directories, no symlinks","-","-19 skills whose content lived in ~/.agents/skills are now inside the repo,","-so they version and reach Windows. The views link back to them.","-","-Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"","-git push","-cd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS && git add scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh && git commit -m \"feat: symlink inversion script","-","-Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"","-```","-","----","-","-### PLACEHOLDER-TASK5-MARKER","-"," - [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**"," "," Create `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`:"]},{"oldStart":786,"oldLines":9,"newStart":699,"newLines":70,"lines":[" "," Expected: `would sync` lines and `exit=0` — **not** `FATAL`. A FATAL here means a `SHARED` entry is still a symlink and Step 3 did not finish."," ","-- [ ] **Step 7: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**","+- [ ] **Step 7: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**","+","+Before the views are regenerated, the existing pool copies must be checked — regenerating overwrites them, and two of them contain edits that exist nowhere else. Verified on disk today: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **differ** between canonical and pool; `backup` and 7 others are **absent** from the pool entirely.","+","+```bash","+mkdir -p ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12","+echo \"=== canonical skills whose pool copy DIFFERS ===\"","+for d in ~/.claude/skills/*/; do","+  s=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"","+  [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ] || continue","+  b=~/.agents/skills/\"$s\"","+  if [ -e \"$b\" ] && [ ! -L \"$b\" ] && ! diff -rq \"$d\" \"$b\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then","+    echo \"DIVERGED $s\"","+  fi","+done","+echo \"=== canonical skills ABSENT from the pool ===\"","+comm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)","+```","+","+Expected: at least `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` under DIVERGED, and 8 names under ABSENT.","+","+For **each** DIVERGED name, look at the actual difference and decide which side wins — then back up the pool copy before it is overwritten:","+","+```bash","+for s in memory-write meeting-sync; do","+  echo \"===== $s =====\"","+  diff -ru ~/.claude/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" | head -40","+  cp -R ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/\"$s\"","+done","+ls ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/","+```","+","+Read each diff. If the pool copy is newer or better, copy that content **into canonical** (`cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/`) and commit it there. If canonical wins, do nothing — the sync will overwrite the pool. **Do not skip reading the diffs**; regenerating discards whatever you did not move. The `pre-sync-2026-09-12/` backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong.","+","+The ABSENT names need no action: the new complete-manifest sync publishes them automatically. That is the bug the manifest fixes.","+","+- [ ] **Step 8: Publish the views and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**","+","+```bash","+DRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"dry exit=$?\"","+bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real exit=$?\"","+","+MAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex","+echo \"--- manifest size ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"","+","+echo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"","+while IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"","+echo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"","+while IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"","+","+echo \"--- managed links that do not resolve to canonical (must be empty) ---\"","+while IFS= read -r s; do","+  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"","+  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"","+done < \"$MAN\"","+```","+","+Expected: both `exit=0`; the manifest holds **62** lines (61 skills + `_shared`); all three MISSING/WRONG-TARGET lists are **empty**.","+","+> **R3-06:** success is measured against the **manifest**, not against `ls ~/.claude/skills`. The repo legitimately also contains `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view. Comparing raw directory listings would report those as permanent failures."," ","-Run `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61). If it dropped, roll back per Task 1.","+- [ ] **Step 9: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**","+","+Run `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61). If it dropped, roll back per Task 1 Path 1."," "," ```bash"," cd ~/.claude/skills"]},{"oldStart":797,"oldLines":7,"newStart":771,"newLines":7,"lines":[" git commit -m \"refactor: canonical repo holds real directories, no symlinks"," "," 19 skills whose content lived in ~/.agents/skills are now inside the repo,","-so they version and reach Windows. The pool links back to them.","+so they version and reach Windows. The views link back to them."," "," Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\""," git push"]},{"oldStart":808,"oldLines":6,"newStart":782,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ---"," ","+---"," ### Task 5: Normalize every skill to portable frontmatter"," "," **Files:**"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5972998-f735-44b2-9b47-a07742227c3f","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
