{"parentUuid":"4bc422d1-d694-4cd1-b714-349cafc454be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywmLAouiMdBzsL8fjgz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the PowerShell twin — Windows would have kept the old 7-name behaviour."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1674,"cache_read_input_tokens":231174,"output_tokens":2833,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":84},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1674,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2833,"cache_read_input_tokens":231174,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1674},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeywmKV8BctP7b69MAQLM","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"537ac515-7dab-4a28-ba18-59a2b3cc8557","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:32:26.505Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"537ac515-7dab-4a28-ba18-59a2b3cc8557","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywmLAouiMdBzsL8fjgz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T3N33SKE7FuVMVRSXZDRJw","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"- [ ] **Step 3: Apply the same guard to the PowerShell twin**\n\nEdit `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1`. Before its copy loop, add:\n\n```powershell\n# R1 GUARD: canonical must be a real directory, never a reparse point.\nforeach ($s in $SHARED) {\n  $p = Join-Path $SRC $s\n  if ((Test-Path $p) -and ((Get-Item $p -Force).Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint)) {\n    Write-Error \"FATAL $p is a link. Canonical must be a real directory. Refusing to sync.\"\n    exit 2\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWindows keeps `Copy-Item` (mode `copy`); it does not create symlinks without elevation.","new_string":"- [ ] **Step 3: Give the PowerShell twin the same semantics, not just the guard**\n\n`dev-sync` invokes this script on Windows. An earlier draft bolted a reparse-point guard onto the untouched seven-name loop — which would have left Windows with the old partial views and no manifest, so the audit's drift check could never run there (R3-03). The twin needs the **same** complete enumeration, manifest, validated retirement and ownership semantics. Windows copies rather than links (symlinks need elevation).\n\nReplace the body of `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1` with:\n\n```powershell\n# sync-to-codex.ps1 -- Windows twin of sync-to-codex.sh.\n# Rebuilds the Codex and agent-pool VIEWS from the canonical repo by COPY.\n# Same contract as the bash version: complete manifest, ownership file,\n# validated retirement, refuse-on-link guard.\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\n$SRC          = Join-Path $HOME '.claude\\skills'\n$SUPPORT      = @('_shared')\n$MANIFESTNAME = '.generated-by-sync-to-codex'\n$DRY          = $env:DRY_RUN -eq '1'\n$ARCHIVE      = Join-Path $HOME (\".agents\\skills-archive\\retired-\" + (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd'))\n\nfunction Test-IsLink($p) {\n  (Test-Path $p) -and ((Get-Item $p -Force).Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint)\n}\n\n# Complete manifest: every canonical dir with a SKILL.md, plus support dirs.\n$MANAGED = @()\nGet-ChildItem -Path $SRC -Directory -Force | ForEach-Object {\n  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }\n  if (Test-Path (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md')) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }\n}\nforeach ($s in $SUPPORT) {\n  if (Test-Path (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $MANAGED += $s }\n}\n\nif ($MANAGED.Count -eq 0) {\n  Write-Error \"FATAL no skills found under $SRC - refusing to wipe the views.\"\n  exit 2\n}\n\n# R1 GUARD: canonical must be real directories, never reparse points.\n$bad = @()\nforeach ($s in $MANAGED) {\n  if (Test-IsLink (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $bad += $s }\n}\nif ($bad.Count -gt 0) {\n  foreach ($s in $bad) { Write-Error \"FATAL $SRC\\$s is a link. Canonical must be a real directory.\" }\n  Write-Error \"Refusing to sync; this would delete the link targets. No changes made.\"\n  exit 2\n}\n\nWrite-Host \"canonical manifest: $($MANAGED.Count) entries\"\n\nforeach ($dst in @((Join-Path $HOME '.agents\\skills'), (Join-Path $HOME '.codex\\skills'))) {\n  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $dst | Out-Null\n  $manifestPath = Join-Path $dst $MANIFESTNAME\n\n  # Retire entries no longer managed. R3-02: validate each line is a plain\n  # name before it reaches Remove-Item, and archive before removing.\n  if (Test-Path $manifestPath) {\n    foreach ($old in (Get-Content $manifestPath)) {\n      $old = $old.Trim()\n      if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($old)) { continue }\n      if ($old -match '[\\\\/]' -or $old.StartsWith('.') -or $old -eq '..') {\n        Write-Warning \"REFUSE manifest entry '$old' is not a plain name - ignored\"; continue\n      }\n      if ($MANAGED -contains $old) { continue }\n      $target = Join-Path $dst $old\n      $resolvedParent = (Get-Item $dst).FullName\n      if (-not $target.StartsWith($resolvedParent)) {\n        Write-Warning \"REFUSE '$old' resolves outside $dst - ignored\"; continue\n      }\n      Write-Host \"retire $old from $dst (no longer in canonical)\"\n      if (-not $DRY -and (Test-Path $target)) {\n        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $ARCHIVE | Out-Null\n        if (-not (Test-Path (Join-Path $ARCHIVE $old))) {\n          Copy-Item $target (Join-Path $ARCHIVE $old) -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n        }\n        Remove-Item $target -Recurse -Force\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  foreach ($s in $MANAGED) {\n    if ($DRY) { Write-Host \"would sync $s -> $dst (copy)\"; continue }\n    $target = Join-Path $dst $s\n    if (Test-Path $target) { Remove-Item $target -Recurse -Force }\n    Copy-Item (Join-Path $SRC $s) $target -Recurse -Force\n  }\n\n  if (-not $DRY) {\n    Set-Content -Path $manifestPath -Value $MANAGED\n    Write-Host \"synced $($MANAGED.Count) entries -> $dst (copy); manifest written\"\n  }\n}\n\nif ($DRY) { Write-Host \"(DRY RUN - set DRY_RUN=1 cleared to apply)\" }\nexit 0\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3b: Syntax-check the twin on this Mac**\n\n`pwsh` is installed (`/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) specifically to run KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs, so the parse can be checked here even though the script is for Windows:\n\n```bash\npwsh -NoProfile -Command '\n  $ErrorActionPreference=\"Stop\"\n  $t = Get-Content -Raw ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1\n  $errs = $null\n  [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseInput($t, [ref]$null, [ref]$errs) | Out-Null\n  if ($errs.Count) { $errs | ForEach-Object { $_.Message }; exit 1 } else { \"parse OK\"; exit 0 }\n'; echo \"exit=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `parse OK` and `exit=0`. Do **not** run the script itself on the Mac — it would overwrite the Mac views with copies instead of links. Its behaviour is verified on Windows when Tasks 2–5 are repeated there."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1674,"cache_read_input_tokens":231174,"output_tokens":2833,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":84},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1674,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2833,"cache_read_input_tokens":231174,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1674},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CeywmKV8BctP7b69MAQLM","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"a691bfb0-0cd2-4ec3-8328-f3653ce344da","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:32:52.669Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a691bfb0-0cd2-4ec3-8328-f3653ce344da","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T3N33SKE7FuVMVRSXZDRJw","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"73e6f13c-e82b-4736-b861-1f63f7e32947","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:32:52.881Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","oldString":"- [ ] **Step 3: Apply the same guard to the PowerShell twin**\n\nEdit `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1`. Before its copy loop, add:\n\n```powershell\n# R1 GUARD: canonical must be a real directory, never a reparse point.\nforeach ($s in $SHARED) {\n  $p = Join-Path $SRC $s\n  if ((Test-Path $p) -and ((Get-Item $p -Force).Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint)) {\n    Write-Error \"FATAL $p is a link. Canonical must be a real directory. Refusing to sync.\"\n    exit 2\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWindows keeps `Copy-Item` (mode `copy`); it does not create symlinks without elevation.","newString":"- [ ] **Step 3: Give the PowerShell twin the same semantics, not just the guard**\n\n`dev-sync` invokes this script on Windows. An earlier draft bolted a reparse-point guard onto the untouched seven-name loop — which would have left Windows with the old partial views and no manifest, so the audit's drift check could never run there (R3-03). The twin needs the **same** complete enumeration, manifest, validated retirement and ownership semantics. Windows copies rather than links (symlinks need elevation).\n\nReplace the body of `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1` with:\n\n```powershell\n# sync-to-codex.ps1 -- Windows twin of sync-to-codex.sh.\n# Rebuilds the Codex and agent-pool VIEWS from the canonical repo by COPY.\n# Same contract as the bash version: complete manifest, ownership file,\n# validated retirement, refuse-on-link guard.\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\n$SRC          = Join-Path $HOME '.claude\\skills'\n$SUPPORT      = @('_shared')\n$MANIFESTNAME = '.generated-by-sync-to-codex'\n$DRY          = $env:DRY_RUN -eq '1'\n$ARCHIVE      = Join-Path $HOME (\".agents\\skills-archive\\retired-\" + (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd'))\n\nfunction Test-IsLink($p) {\n  (Test-Path $p) -and ((Get-Item $p -Force).Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint)\n}\n\n# Complete manifest: every canonical dir with a SKILL.md, plus support dirs.\n$MANAGED = @()\nGet-ChildItem -Path $SRC -Directory -Force | ForEach-Object {\n  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }\n  if (Test-Path (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md')) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }\n}\nforeach ($s in $SUPPORT) {\n  if (Test-Path (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $MANAGED += $s }\n}\n\nif ($MANAGED.Count -eq 0) {\n  Write-Error \"FATAL no skills found under $SRC - refusing to wipe the views.\"\n  exit 2\n}\n\n# R1 GUARD: canonical must be real directories, never reparse points.\n$bad = @()\nforeach ($s in $MANAGED) {\n  if (Test-IsLink (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $bad += $s }\n}\nif ($bad.Count -gt 0) {\n  foreach ($s in $bad) { Write-Error \"FATAL $SRC\\$s is a link. Canonical must be a real directory.\" }\n  Write-Error \"Refusing to sync; this would delete the link targets. No changes made.\"\n  exit 2\n}\n\nWrite-Host \"canonical manifest: $($MANAGED.Count) entries\"\n\nforeach ($dst in @((Join-Path $HOME '.agents\\skills'), (Join-Path $HOME '.codex\\skills'))) {\n  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $dst | Out-Null\n  $manifestPath = Join-Path $dst $MANIFESTNAME\n\n  # Retire entries no longer managed. R3-02: validate each line is a plain\n  # name before it reaches Remove-Item, and archive before removing.\n  if (Test-Path $manifestPath) {\n    foreach ($old in (Get-Content $manifestPath)) {\n      $old = $old.Trim()\n      if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($old)) { continue }\n      if ($old -match '[\\\\/]' -or $old.StartsWith('.') -or $old -eq '..') {\n        Write-Warning \"REFUSE manifest entry '$old' is not a plain name - ignored\"; continue\n      }\n      if ($MANAGED -contains $old) { continue }\n      $target = Join-Path $dst $old\n      $resolvedParent = (Get-Item $dst).FullName\n      if (-not $target.StartsWith($resolvedParent)) {\n        Write-Warning \"REFUSE '$old' resolves outside $dst - ignored\"; continue\n      }\n      Write-Host \"retire $old from $dst (no longer in canonical)\"\n      if (-not $DRY -and (Test-Path $target)) {\n        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $ARCHIVE | Out-Null\n        if (-not (Test-Path (Join-Path $ARCHIVE $old))) {\n          Copy-Item $target (Join-Path $ARCHIVE $old) -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n        }\n        Remove-Item $target -Recurse -Force\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  foreach ($s in $MANAGED) {\n    if ($DRY) { Write-Host \"would sync $s -> $dst (copy)\"; continue }\n    $target = Join-Path $dst $s\n    if (Test-Path $target) { Remove-Item $target -Recurse -Force }\n    Copy-Item (Join-Path $SRC $s) $target -Recurse -Force\n  }\n\n  if (-not $DRY) {\n    Set-Content -Path $manifestPath -Value $MANAGED\n    Write-Host \"synced $($MANAGED.Count) entries -> $dst (copy); manifest written\"\n  }\n}\n\nif ($DRY) { Write-Host \"(DRY RUN - set DRY_RUN=1 cleared to apply)\" }\nexit 0\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3b: Syntax-check the twin on this Mac**\n\n`pwsh` is installed (`/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) specifically to run KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs, so the parse can be checked here even though the script is for Windows:\n\n```bash\npwsh -NoProfile -Command '\n  $ErrorActionPreference=\"Stop\"\n  $t = Get-Content -Raw ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1\n  $errs = $null\n  [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseInput($t, [ref]$null, [ref]$errs) | Out-Null\n  if ($errs.Count) { $errs | ForEach-Object { $_.Message }; exit 1 } else { \"parse OK\"; exit 0 }\n'; echo \"exit=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `parse OK` and `exit=0`. Do **not** run the script itself on the Mac — it would overwrite the Mac views with copies instead of links. Its behaviour is verified on Windows when Tasks 2–5 are repeated there.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":487,"oldLines":23,"newStart":487,"newLines":120,"lines":[" "," The manifest file is the answer to R2-02. A view entry listed in `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` is owned by this script and must be a symlink on Mac (a copy on Windows). Anything else in the view is a third-party install, and the audit reports it separately instead of flagging it as an error."," ","-- [ ] **Step 3: Apply the same guard to the PowerShell twin**","+- [ ] **Step 3: Give the PowerShell twin the same semantics, not just the guard**"," ","-Edit `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1`. Before its copy loop, add:","+`dev-sync` invokes this script on Windows. An earlier draft bolted a reparse-point guard onto the untouched seven-name loop — which would have left Windows with the old partial views and no manifest, so the audit's drift check could never run there (R3-03). The twin needs the **same** complete enumeration, manifest, validated retirement and ownership semantics. Windows copies rather than links (symlinks need elevation)."," ","+Replace the body of `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1` with:","+"," ```powershell","-# R1 GUARD: canonical must be a real directory, never a reparse point.","-foreach ($s in $SHARED) {","-  $p = Join-Path $SRC $s","-  if ((Test-Path $p) -and ((Get-Item $p -Force).Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint)) {","-    Write-Error \"FATAL $p is a link. Canonical must be a real directory. Refusing to sync.\"","-    exit 2","+# sync-to-codex.ps1 -- Windows twin of sync-to-codex.sh.","+# Rebuilds the Codex and agent-pool VIEWS from the canonical repo by COPY.","+# Same contract as the bash version: complete manifest, ownership file,","+# validated retirement, refuse-on-link guard.","+$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'","+","+$SRC          = Join-Path $HOME '.claude\\skills'","+$SUPPORT      = @('_shared')","+$MANIFESTNAME = '.generated-by-sync-to-codex'","+$DRY          = $env:DRY_RUN -eq '1'","+$ARCHIVE      = Join-Path $HOME (\".agents\\skills-archive\\retired-\" + (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd'))","+","+function Test-IsLink($p) {","+  (Test-Path $p) -and ((Get-Item $p -Force).Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint)","+}","+","+# Complete manifest: every canonical dir with a SKILL.md, plus support dirs.","+$MANAGED = @()","+Get-ChildItem -Path $SRC -Directory -Force | ForEach-Object {","+  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }","+  if (Test-Path (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md')) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }","+}","+foreach ($s in $SUPPORT) {","+  if (Test-Path (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $MANAGED += $s }","+}","+","+if ($MANAGED.Count -eq 0) {","+  Write-Error \"FATAL no skills found under $SRC - refusing to wipe the views.\"","+  exit 2","+}","+","+# R1 GUARD: canonical must be real directories, never reparse points.","+$bad = @()","+foreach ($s in $MANAGED) {","+  if (Test-IsLink (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $bad += $s }","+}","+if ($bad.Count -gt 0) {","+  foreach ($s in $bad) { Write-Error \"FATAL $SRC\\$s is a link. Canonical must be a real directory.\" }","+  Write-Error \"Refusing to sync; this would delete the link targets. No changes made.\"","+  exit 2","+}","+","+Write-Host \"canonical manifest: $($MANAGED.Count) entries\"","+","+foreach ($dst in @((Join-Path $HOME '.agents\\skills'), (Join-Path $HOME '.codex\\skills'))) {","+  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $dst | Out-Null","+  $manifestPath = Join-Path $dst $MANIFESTNAME","+","+  # Retire entries no longer managed. R3-02: validate each line is a plain","+  # name before it reaches Remove-Item, and archive before removing.","+  if (Test-Path $manifestPath) {","+    foreach ($old in (Get-Content $manifestPath)) {","+      $old = $old.Trim()","+      if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($old)) { continue }","+      if ($old -match '[\\\\/]' -or $old.StartsWith('.') -or $old -eq '..') {","+        Write-Warning \"REFUSE manifest entry '$old' is not a plain name - ignored\"; continue","+      }","+      if ($MANAGED -contains $old) { continue }","+      $target = Join-Path $dst $old","+      $resolvedParent = (Get-Item $dst).FullName","+      if (-not $target.StartsWith($resolvedParent)) {","+        Write-Warning \"REFUSE '$old' resolves outside $dst - ignored\"; continue","+      }","+      Write-Host \"retire $old from $dst (no longer in canonical)\"","+      if (-not $DRY -and (Test-Path $target)) {","+        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $ARCHIVE | Out-Null","+        if (-not (Test-Path (Join-Path $ARCHIVE $old))) {","+          Copy-Item $target (Join-Path $ARCHIVE $old) -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue","+        }","+        Remove-Item $target -Recurse -Force","+      }","+    }","   }","+","+  foreach ($s in $MANAGED) {","+    if ($DRY) { Write-Host \"would sync $s -> $dst (copy)\"; continue }","+    $target = Join-Path $dst $s","+    if (Test-Path $target) { Remove-Item $target -Recurse -Force }","+    Copy-Item (Join-Path $SRC $s) $target -Recurse -Force","+  }","+","+  if (-not $DRY) {","+    Set-Content -Path $manifestPath -Value $MANAGED","+    Write-Host \"synced $($MANAGED.Count) entries -> $dst (copy); manifest written\"","+  }"," }","+","+if ($DRY) { Write-Host \"(DRY RUN - set DRY_RUN=1 cleared to apply)\" }","+exit 0"," ```"," ","-Windows keeps `Copy-Item` (mode `copy`); it does not create symlinks without elevation.","+- [ ] **Step 3b: Syntax-check the twin on this Mac**"," ","+`pwsh` is installed (`/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) specifically to run KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs, so the parse can be checked here even though the script is for Windows:","+","+```bash","+pwsh -NoProfile -Command '","+  $ErrorActionPreference=\"Stop\"","+  $t = Get-Content -Raw ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1","+  $errs = $null","+  [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseInput($t, [ref]$null, [ref]$errs) | Out-Null","+  if ($errs.Count) { $errs | ForEach-Object { $_.Message }; exit 1 } else { \"parse OK\"; exit 0 }","+'; echo \"exit=$?\"","+```","+","+Expected: `parse OK` and `exit=0`. Do **not** run the script itself on the Mac — it would overwrite the Mac views with copies instead of links. Its behaviour is verified on Windows when Tasks 2–5 are repeated there.","+"," - [ ] **Step 4: Prove the guard fires — the whole point of this task**"," "," ```bash"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a691bfb0-0cd2-4ec3-8328-f3653ce344da","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
