mp/tartest && mkdir -p /tmp/tartest\n\n# Both archives into ONE scratch root, so the relative links resolve.\ntar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz     -C /tmp/tartest\ntar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-CANONICAL-2026-09-12.tgz -C /tmp/tartest\n\necho \"--- views ---\"\nls /tmp/tartest/.agents/skills | wc -l\nls /tmp/tartest/.codex/skills  | wc -l\necho \"--- canonical, with links resolving against the extracted pool ---\"\nfind -L /tmp/tartest/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\ntest -f /tmp/tartest/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared OK\"\ngit -C /tmp/tartest/.claude/skills log --oneline -1\n\n# Separation check: the VIEWS archive alone must carry no .claude content.\nrm -rf /tmp/viewsonly && mkdir -p /tmp/viewsonly\ntar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz -C /tmp/viewsonly\necho \"--- must be empty ---\"\nls -d /tmp/viewsonly/.claude 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nExpected: `306`, `32`, `61`, `_shared OK`, `3ab4467 chore: apply global skill audit`, and **no output** from the separation check. If the views archive contains `.claude`, the separation failed — STOP, no later task may run.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":167,"oldLines":22,"newStart":167,"newLines":31,"lines":[" "," - [ ] **Step 3: Verify each tarball independently**"," ","+The two archives must be **separate on disk but extracted into ONE compatible tree** (R3-05). The 19 canonical symlinks are relative (`../../.agents/skills/anti-sleep`), so extracting the canonical archive alone leaves them dangling and the `find -L` count can never reach 61. Extract both into the same scratch root — and never over the live repo:","+"," ```bash","-rm -rf /tmp/tartest && mkdir -p /tmp/tartest/{views,canon}","+rm -rf /tmp/tartest && mkdir -p /tmp/tartest"," ","-tar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz -C /tmp/tartest/views","-ls /tmp/tartest/views/.agents/skills | wc -l","-ls /tmp/tartest/views/.codex/skills | wc -l","-echo \"--- views archive must NOT contain .claude (must be empty) ---\"","-ls -d /tmp/tartest/views/.claude 2>/dev/null","+# Both archives into ONE scratch root, so the relative links resolve.","+tar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz     -C /tmp/tartest","+tar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-CANONICAL-2026-09-12.tgz -C /tmp/tartest"," ","-tar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-CANONICAL-2026-09-12.tgz -C /tmp/tartest/canon","-find -L /tmp/tartest/canon/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l","-test -f /tmp/tartest/canon/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared OK\"","-git -C /tmp/tartest/canon/.claude/skills log --oneline -1","+echo \"--- views ---\"","+ls /tmp/tartest/.agents/skills | wc -l","+ls /tmp/tartest/.codex/skills  | wc -l","+echo \"--- canonical, with links resolving against the extracted pool ---\"","+find -L /tmp/tartest/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l","+test -f /tmp/tartest/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared OK\"","+git -C /tmp/tartest/.claude/skills log --oneline -1","+","+# Separation check: the VIEWS archive alone must carry no .claude content.","+rm -rf /tmp/viewsonly && mkdir -p /tmp/viewsonly","+tar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz -C /tmp/viewsonly","+echo \"--- must be empty ---\"","+ls -d /tmp/viewsonly/.claude 2>/dev/null"," ```"," ","-Expected: `306`, `32`, **no `.claude` directory in the views archive**, then `61`, `_shared OK`, and `3ab4467 chore: apply global skill audit`. If the views archive contains `.claude`, the separation failed — STOP, no later task may run.","+Expected: `306`, `32`, `61`, `_shared OK`, `3ab4467 chore: apply global skill audit`, and **no output** from the separation check. If the views archive contains `.claude`, the separation failed — STOP, no later task may run."," "," - [ ] **Step 4: Record the two rollback paths, kept strictly apart**