{"parentUuid":"f845523a-67b4-49d3-8b1b-b1d766bc8f84","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A9RxDXwooorkKH8MFXWZpH","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"27e2cdd7-2453-423b-9320-7928a4a21c45","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:33:34.268Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","oldString":"- **Round 2** — Codex: **REVISE**, 2 high / 7 medium (R2-01 – R2-09). All accepted. Round 2 caught that the views published only 7 of 61 skills, and that the single rollback tarball would corrupt the canonical repo.\n\nBoth disposition tables are below. Artifacts: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r{1,2}/`.","newString":"- **Round 2** — Codex: **REVISE**, 2 high / 7 medium (R2-01 – R2-09). All accepted. Round 2 caught that the views published only 7 of 61 skills, and that the single rollback tarball would corrupt the canonical repo.\n- **Round 3** — Codex: **REVISE**, 2 high / 5 medium (R3-01 – R3-07). All accepted. Round 3 caught a task-ordering deadlock and a path-traversal `rm -rf` introduced by round 2's own manifest fix.\n\nAll three disposition tables are below. Artifacts: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r{1,2,3}/`.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":8,"newStart":14,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," - **Round 1** — Codex: **REVISE**, 6 high / 4 medium (R1–R10). All accepted. **The architecture above is the inverse of round 1's** — round 1 made `~/.agents/skills/` canonical, which R1/R3 showed would cause data loss."," - **Round 2** — Codex: **REVISE**, 2 high / 7 medium (R2-01 – R2-09). All accepted. Round 2 caught that the views published only 7 of 61 skills, and that the single rollback tarball would corrupt the canonical repo.","+- **Round 3** — Codex: **REVISE**, 2 high / 5 medium (R3-01 – R3-07). All accepted. Round 3 caught a task-ordering deadlock and a path-traversal `rm -rf` introduced by round 2's own manifest fix."," ","-Both disposition tables are below. Artifacts: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r{1,2}/`.","+All three disposition tables are below. Artifacts: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r{1,2,3}/`."," "," ---"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f845523a-67b4-49d3-8b1b-b1d766bc8f84","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"27e2cdd7-2453-423b-9320-7928a4a21c45","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14738698 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"024573ea-5986-4852-b799-67bebfe53306","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:33:34.271Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14738698 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"024573ea-5986-4852-b799-67bebfe53306","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0bc61cd5-1ee6-42f7-ad4f-aace03f3c5e9","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:33:34.271Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0bc61cd5-1ee6-42f7-ad4f-aace03f3c5e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeywrYHwZc2CeTiAqiknq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UdxaouTvRHPT52jeCrkDxr","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"**Rejected:** none.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Snapshot and freeze the current state","new_string":"**Rejected:** none.\n\n### Round 3 findings — disposition\n\nTwo of the seven were defects **introduced by round 2's own fixes** — the complete-manifest guard created a task-ordering deadlock, and the manifest retirement loop fed unchecked strings to `rm -rf`. That is the argument for the review gates existing at all.\n\n| ID | Sev | Codex's finding | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R3-01 | high | The new complete-manifest guard rejects every outward canonical symlink, yet Task 3 still required a *successful* sync before Task 4 could run — and only Task 4 removes those links. The prerequisites deadlocked. | **ACCEPTED.** Task 3's Step 5 now expects the guard to **refuse** (`exit=2`) on the pre-inversion layout, and says explicitly that this is the correct result. Reconciliation and the real publish moved out of Task 3 into **Task 4 Steps 7–9**, after inversion. The order is now: install and prove the guard → canonicalize → reconcile → publish. |\n| R3-02 | high | The retirement loop feeds unvalidated manifest lines straight to `rm -rf`. A line reading `../../.claude/skills` in the writable `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` would delete the canonical repository on the next `dev-sync`. The `${var:?}` checks do not stop traversal. | **ACCEPTED — this was a defect I introduced in round 2.** Added `valid_entry()`, which refuses empties, `.`/`..`, any path separator, and dotfiles. Membership testing uses `grep -qxF --` (literal, whole-line) instead of `grep -qx`, which treated the entry as a regex. Containment is proven by resolving the parent and requiring it to equal the view root. Retired entries are **archived** to `~/.agents/skills-archive/retired-<date>/` before removal — a retirement is never a silent delete. The PowerShell twin carries the same validation. |\n| R3-03 | med | The PowerShell edit added only a reparse-point guard to the untouched seven-name loop. It has no complete enumeration, no support-directory publication, no ownership manifest and no retirement — and `dev-sync` invokes it on Windows, so the promised views and manifest-based audit would not exist there. | **ACCEPTED.** Task 3 Step 3 now replaces the twin's whole body with the same contract in PowerShell: complete enumeration, manifest, validated retirement with archiving, refuse-on-link guard — copying rather than linking, since Windows symlinks need elevation. New **Step 3b** parse-checks it with the installed `pwsh` without running it, since running it on the Mac would replace the link views with copies. |\n| R3-04 | med | The negative-only fixture still passes. In `do not use when auditing`, the negative span is [0,10) and `use when` is [7,15) — the positive **overlaps** but is not **contained**, so `inside_negative` returns false. | **ACCEPTED — a repeat miss on my part.** Containment was the wrong relation. Negative spans are now extended through a trailing `when`/`for` so `do not use when` is one governing construction, and any positive match **overlapping** a negative span is discarded. The `negonly` fixture stays a required check. |\n| R3-05 | med | The canonical archive preserves relative links like `anti-sleep -> ../../.agents/skills/anti-sleep`. Extracting it under `canon/` while the pool goes under `views/` leaves them dangling, so the expected count of 61 is unreachable. Separately, reverting the inversion while pool entries point back into canonical creates reciprocal symlink cycles the hardened sync then refuses to regenerate. | **ACCEPTED.** Step 3 now extracts **both** archives into one scratch root so the relative links resolve, with a separate views-only extraction to prove the separation. The rollback block is rewritten **by migration phase** (A: views only; B: after inversion; C: after frontmatter), and Phase B states the order explicitly — restore real pool targets **first**, then revert canonical — with a cycle check that must print nothing. |\n| R3-06 | med | The ABSENT assertion compares all top-level canonical entries against the pool, but the sync publishes only SKILL.md directories and `_shared`. `CLAUDE.md`, `docs`, and the two sync scripts legitimately remain absent, so the required empty output is unachievable. | **ACCEPTED.** The check now iterates the **generated manifest** and asserts each entry exists in both views, rather than diffing raw directory listings. Expected counts derive from the manifest (62 = 61 skills + `_shared`). A note records why repository scripts and docs must never appear in a view. |\n| R3-07 | med | `view_drift` trusts the view's own manifest. An empty manifest reports zero drift despite every skill being missing; a managed Mac symlink pointing at the wrong directory also reports zero; Windows copies with stale contents pass because only representation is checked. | **ACCEPTED.** Drift is now measured against a `canonical_expected()` set computed from the canonical repo, not from the manifest. It counts manifest/canonical disagreement in **both** directions, missing entries, wrong representation for the platform, **link targets that do not resolve to the matching canonical directory**, and — in copy mode — stale trees via a relative-path-and-size comparison. |\n\n**Rejected:** none.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Snapshot and freeze the current state"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":683,"cache_read_input_tokens":239513,"output_tokens":2