{"parentUuid":"ba3062d0-b8c6-4cdb-bc2c-ef8972f014c1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WrRTrAWF4eHBfjwEqaLzM8","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r3.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"9761702c-be9c-4698-baf8-207db260e5c6","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:34:45.924Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r3.md","content":"# Round 3 dispositions — all seven ACCEPTED\n\nTwo of the seven (R3-01, R3-02) were defects **introduced by round 2's own\nfixes**. Both are corrected below.\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed in the plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| R3-01 | ACCEPTED | The deadlock is removed by reordering, not by weakening the guard. Task 3 Step 5 now expects the guard to **refuse** (`exit=2`) on the pre-inversion layout and states that this is the correct result, with a note explaining that requiring a successful sync there made the two tasks impossible to run in either order. Reconciliation and the real publish moved out of Task 3 into **Task 4 Steps 7, 8 and 9**, after inversion. Task 3's remaining steps are: rewrite bash → rewrite PowerShell → parse-check PowerShell → prove the guard fires on a canary → confirm it refuses the current layout → git gate → commit. Task 4 is: write the inverter → dry run → apply → verify symlink-free and inspect the **staged** index → verify `_shared` consumers → re-run the guard (now expected to pass) → reconcile → publish → confirm and commit. |\n| R3-02 | ACCEPTED | Added `valid_entry()`, which refuses empty lines, `.`, `..`, any `/` or `\\`, and dotfiles. Membership testing changed from `grep -qx` to `grep -qxF --` so a manifest entry is matched literally rather than as a regex. Containment is proven independently: the entry's parent directory is resolved and must equal the view root, otherwise the entry is refused with a message. Retired entries are **copied to `~/.agents/skills-archive/retired-<date>/` before removal**, so a retirement is never a silent delete. The PowerShell twin carries the same three protections. |\n| R3-03 | ACCEPTED | Task 3 Step 3 no longer bolts a guard onto the old seven-name loop; it replaces the twin's entire body with the same contract expressed in PowerShell — complete enumeration of canonical directories holding a SKILL.md plus declared support dirs, refusal on an empty manifest, reparse-point guard, validated and archived retirement, and the ownership manifest — using `Copy-Item` because Windows symlinks require elevation. New **Step 3b** parse-checks it using the installed `pwsh` via `Parser::ParseInput`, with an explicit instruction **not** to execute it on the Mac, since that would replace the link-based views with copies. |\n| R3-04 | ACCEPTED | Containment was the wrong relation; the fix is overlap plus span extension. Each negative span is now extended through an immediately following `\" when\"` or `\" for\"`, so `do not use when` is one governing construction rather than `do not use` followed by a claimable `use when`. Any positive match whose span **overlaps** a negative span is discarded. Verified by executing the corrected function against three inputs before committing: `\"do not use when auditing anything at all.\"` → `['no positive']`; `\"use when x happens. do not use when y.\"` → `[]`; `\"use when x happens.\"` → `['no negative']`. The `negonly` fixture remains a required check in Task 5 Step 2. |\n| R3-05 | ACCEPTED | Task 1 Step 3 now extracts **both** archives into a single scratch root (`/tmp/tartest`) so the relative canonical links resolve against the extracted pool and the count can reach 61, plus a separate views-only extraction into `/tmp/viewsonly` that must contain no `.claude` directory — preserving the separation assertion without breaking link resolution. The rollback block is rewritten **by migration phase**: Phase A (views only, before inversion), Phase B (after inversion), Phase C (after frontmatter edits). Phase B states the ordering constraint explicitly — restore real pool targets **first**, then revert canonical, because reverting first leaves canonical links and pool links pointing at each other — and ends with a cycle check (`find ... -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print`) that must print nothing. |\n| R3-06 | ACCEPTED | The publication assertion no longer diffs raw directory listings. It iterates the **generated manifest** and checks each entry exists in both views, plus a third check that every managed Mac link resolves to `$HOME/.claude/skills/<name>`. Expected counts derive from the manifest (62 = 61 skills + `_shared`). A note records that `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` legitimately live in the repo and must never appear in a view, which is why the old comparison could never pass. |\n| R3-07 | ACCEPTED | `view_drift` no longer trusts the view's own manifest. A new `canonical_expected()` computes the expected set from the canonical repo. Drift now counts: manifest-vs-canonical disagreement in **both** directions (so an empty or stale manifest is itself drift), entries missing from the view, wrong representation for the platform, **Mac links whose `realpath` does not equal the matching canonical directory**, and — in copy mode — stale trees compared by relative path set and file sizes via `_same_tree`. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n\n## Verification run before this round was submitted\n\n- All embedded `python` blocks compile (`compile()`, 2/2 OK).\n- All embedded `bash` script blocks pass `bash -n` (0 syntax errors).\n- The corrected `clause_problems` was executed against the three fixtures and\n  produced the required results, including the previously-failing negative-only\n  case.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":fal