{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"2b6ec9c1-529f-4837-abaa-60258e4f2631","snapshotMessageId":"2166fd4d-d008-4569-9d96-a4a448b83b70","trackingPath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r4.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-09-12T17:38:01.856Z","realParentDir":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp"},"timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:38:01.877Z"}
{"parentUuid":"90e786b7-237f-4bb5-97ac-635d348c060c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeyxAx4hErArF2CwDiHfZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Urv7VC8wA3i3sjxtUjrAS","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r4.md","content":"# Round 4 dispositions — all four ACCEPTED\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed in the plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| R4-01 | ACCEPTED | Two changes. (a) `valid_entry()` in bash and the equivalent regex in PowerShell now refuse glob metacharacters `* ? [ ]` and a leading `-`, in addition to the existing empty/`.`/`..`/separator/dotfile refusals. (b) **Every** manifest-derived filesystem call in the PowerShell twin now uses `-LiteralPath` — `Get-Content`, `Test-Path`, `Get-Item`, `Get-ChildItem`, `Copy-Item`, `Remove-Item`, `Set-Content` — so nothing can wildcard-expand even if validation were bypassed. Containment is additionally proven by requiring `$item.Parent.FullName` to equal the view root, which constrains the operation to exactly one immediate child. Verified by executing the bash guard against `* ? [a-z] ../../.claude/skills .hidden '' . .. -rf` (all refused) and `backup memory-write _shared` (all allowed). |\n| R4-02 | ACCEPTED | Archival is now a precondition for deletion, not a best-effort side effect. `\\|\\| true` and `-ErrorAction SilentlyContinue` are removed. Each view gets its **own** archive subdirectory (`retired-<date>/.agents/` and `retired-<date>/.codex/`), so the second view's copy can never be deleted because the first view already archived a same-named entry. A pre-existing destination is now a hard error rather than a skip. The sequence is: create the archive dir (abort on failure) → refuse on collision → copy (abort on failure) → read the copy back (abort if absent) → only then `rm -rf`. Both scripts exit 3 on any of those. |\n| R4-03 | ACCEPTED | The unconditional \"regenerate after any revert\" footer is removed. A new section states the incompatibility plainly — the hardened sync refuses outward symlinks by design, and Phases B and C restore exactly that layout, so regenerating exits 2 and every later `dev-sync` does too. Two explicit options replace it: **Option 1 (default)** revert the sync-hardening commit as well, so the installed script matches the restored layout, with no regeneration; **Option 2** do not revert the inversion at all, fix forward and regenerate. Expected post-rollback `dev-sync` behaviour is stated for each, including that `aios-audit` will report `no_manifest` under Option 1 and that this is correct. A closing line names hardened-script-plus-legacy-layout as the one combination that must never be left in place. |\n| R4-04 | ACCEPTED | `_same_tree` now compares **SHA-256 content hashes** per relative path instead of file sizes, so a same-length edit to a trigger phrase, command or config value is detected. Read errors are no longer suppressed: an unreadable file is recorded as `UNREADABLE:<errno>` and any such entry makes the comparison return `False`, so a permission or I/O problem counts as drift rather than silently passing. `hashlib` added to the imports. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n\n## Verification run before this round was submitted\n\n- Both embedded `python` blocks compile cleanly.\n- All embedded `bash` script blocks pass `bash -n`.\n- The `valid_entry` guard was executed against 12 inputs; all nine attack\n  shapes refused, all three real skill names allowed.\n- The PowerShell twin was grepped for non-`-LiteralPath` filesystem calls:\n  none remain (the only matches are comment lines).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":466,"cache_read_input_tokens":261792,"output_tokens":1340,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":466,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1340,"cache_read_input_tokens":261792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":466,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":466},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeyxAwXSoA8PS1paMZZP1","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"2b6ec9c1-529f-4837-abaa-60258e4f2631","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:38:01.838Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"2b6ec9c1-529f-4837-abaa-60258e4f2631","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Urv7VC8wA3i3sjxtUjrAS","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r4.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"d5570dfc-34b9-43ed-a70d-601b012577f7","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:38:01.994Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r4.md","content":"# Round 4 dispositions — all four ACCEPTED\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed in the plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| R4-01 | ACCEPTED | Two changes. (a) `valid_entry()` in bash and the equivalent regex in PowerShell now refuse glob metacharacters `* ? [ ]` and a leading `-`, in addition to the existing empty/`.`/`..`/separator/dotfile refusals. (b) **Every** manifest-derived filesystem call in the PowerShell twin now uses `-LiteralPath` — `Get-Content`, `Test-Path`, `Get-Item`, `Get-ChildItem`, `Copy-Item`, `Remove-Item`, `Set-Content` — so nothing can wildcard-expand even if validation were bypassed. Containment is additionally proven by requiring `$item.Parent.FullName` to equal the view root, which constrains the operation to exactly one immediate child. Verified by executing the bash guard against `* ? [a-z] ../../.claude/skills .hidden '' . .. -rf` (all refused) and `backup memory-write _shared` (all allowed). |\n| R4-02 | ACCEPTED | Archival is now a precondition for deletion, not a best-effort side effect. `\\|\\| true` and `-ErrorAction SilentlyContinue` are removed. Each view gets its **own** archive subdirectory (`retired-<date>/.agents/` and `retired-<date>/.codex/`), so the second view's copy can never be deleted because the first view already archived a same-named entry. A pre-existing destination is now a hard error rather than a skip. The sequence is: create the archive dir (abort on failure) → refuse on collision → copy (abort on failure) → read the copy back (abort if absent) → only then `rm -rf`. Both scripts exit 3 on any of those. |\n| R4-03 | ACCEPTED | The unconditional \"regenerate after any revert\" footer is removed. A new section states the incompatibility plainly — the hardened sync refuses outward symlinks by design, and Phases B and C restore exactly that layout, so regenerating exits 2 and every later `dev-sync` does too. Two explicit options replace it: **Option 1 (default)** revert the sync-hardening commit as well, so the installed script matches the restored layout, with no regeneration; **Option 2** do not revert the inversion at all, fix forward and regenerate. Expected post-rollback `dev-sync` behaviour is stated for each, including that `aios-audit` will report `no_manifest` under Option 1 and that this is correct. A closing line names hardened-script-plus-legacy-layout as the one combination that must never be left in place. |\n| R4-04 | ACCEPTED | `_same_tree` now compares **SHA-256 content hashes** per relative path instead of file sizes, so a same-length edit to a trigger phrase, command or config value is detected. Read errors are no longer suppressed: an unreadable file is recorded as `UNREADABLE:<errno>` and any such entry makes the comparison return `False`, so a permission or I/O problem counts as drift rather than silently passing. `hashlib` added to the imports. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n\n## Verification run before this round was submitted\n\n- Both embedded `python` blocks compile cleanly.\n- All embedded `bash` script blocks pass `bash -n`.\n- The `valid_entry` guard was executed against 12 inputs; all nine attack\n  shapes refused, all three real skill names allowed.\n- The PowerShell twin was grepped for non-`-LiteralPath` filesystem calls:\n  none remain (the only matches are comment lines).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2b6ec9c1-529f-4837-abaa-60258e4f2631","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
