{"parentUuid":"648c78a2-db25-41b4-8ae6-72a3faac1eb0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06e7d3ba-222f-4650-8a25-521650a48509","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RNZf7WvtZxJ1Kw5T3Joiza","type":"tool_result","content":"VERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: The plan hash matches, and the four previous findings are addressed. One retirement edge case remains: removing a canonical skill leaves an unmanaged dangling link that the audit overlooks.\n\n[MEDIUM] R5-01  Task 3 Bash retirement loop and Task 6 view_drift\n  E: After dev-sync pulls a canonical skill deletion, its generated Mac symlink becomes dangling. Retirement requires `[ -e \"$dst/$old\" ]`, which is false for dangling symlinks, so the link remains. The script then removes the name from the ownership manifest. view_drift checks only current canonical names and manifest membership, while third_party_in_view requires a readable SKILL.md; neither reports the abandoned link. Thus the normal deletion workflow leaves permanent, untracked view debris while reporting zero drift.\n  F: Detect directory entries with `-e || -L`, handle dangling-link retirement explicitly, and preserve ownership until retirement succeeds. Archive the link itself without requiring its target to exist. Add an audit check for dangling view links and a verification case covering canonical deletion followed by sync.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"afc4ddf7-d4de-4662-bfd6-0807a11a375c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:38:43.118Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"VERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: The plan hash matches, and the four previous findings are addressed. One retirement edge case remains: removing a canonical skill leaves an unmanaged dangling link that the audit overlooks.\n\n[MEDIUM] R5-01  Task 3 Bash retirement loop and Task 6 view_drift\n  E: After dev-sync pulls a canonical skill deletion, its generated Mac symlink becomes dangling. Retirement requires `[ -e \"$dst/$old\" ]`, which is false for dangling symlinks, so the link remains. The script then removes the name from the ownership manifest. view_drift checks only current canonical names and manifest membership, while third_party_in_view requires a readable SKILL.md; neither reports the abandoned link. Thus the normal deletion workflow leaves permanent, untracked view debris while reporting zero drift.\n  F: Detect directory entries with `-e || -L`, handle dangling-link retirement explicitly, and preserve ownership until retirement succeeds. Archive the link itself without requiring its target to exist. Add an audit check for dangling view links and a verification case covering canonical deletion followed by sync.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"648c78a2-db25-41b4-8ae6-72a3faac1eb0","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
