{"parentUuid":"5d5777f0-e87e-4ddc-b2de-0f5ebc7b9b5c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeyxTV3xb77SCTTnuXfu1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0161a21AkeUdizQRDvjNXBFv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r5.md","content":"# Round 5 disposition — ACCEPTED\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed in the plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| R5-01 | ACCEPTED | Four coordinated changes, then verified by execution. **(a) Detection:** the bash retirement guard is now `[ -e \"$dst/$old\" ] \\|\\| [ -L \"$dst/$old\" ]`, so a dangling link is still seen. The PowerShell twin falls back to a `Get-Item -Force` lookup, since `Test-Path` is likewise false for a dangling reparse point. **(b) Archiving:** `cp -R` became `cp -RP`, which copies a symlink *as a link*, so a dangling one archives without needing its target to exist; the read-back check accepts `-e` **or** `-L`, and the collision check likewise. **(c) Ownership:** a new `KEEP_OWNED` array retains refused entries in the manifest, so an entry we declined to retire stays tracked rather than becoming untracked debris — the run also warns which names were retained. **(d) Audit:** new `dangling_in_view()` walks the view with `os.listdir` + `os.path.islink`/`os.path.exists` and reports abandoned links; `pool_dangling` and `codex_dangling` are added to the metrics, listed in the expected-values table as `0`, and named in the `aios-audit` invariant step as RED conditions. A new **Task 3 Step 4b** adds the required verification case: publish two skills, delete one upstream, sync again, assert zero dangling links and a per-view archive entry. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n\n## Executed verification (not a claim — this was run)\n\nThe bash sync script was extracted from the plan and the R5-01 scenario run\nagainst it end to end:\n\n```\nexit=0\ndangling: 0  (expect 0)\narchive dirs:\nagents\ncodex\nlrwxr-xr-x  goner -> /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/goner     (retired-<date>/agents/)\nlrwxr-xr-x  goner -> /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/goner     (retired-<date>/codex/)\nmanifest goner count: 0  (expect 0)\nkeeper -> /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/keeper\n```\n\nBoth views archived the link independently — the R4-02 per-view archive fix\nworking — the manifest released `goner`, and the surviving skill stayed\ncorrectly linked.\n\nOne incidental improvement while testing: the per-view archive subdirectories\nwere named `.agents` / `.codex`, i.e. hidden, so a human looking for a retired\nskill would not have found them. The leading dot is now stripped in both\nscripts (`agents` / `codex`), and the verification step's expected paths were\nupdated to match.\n\nAlso re-confirmed this round: both embedded `python` blocks compile, all\nembedded `bash` script blocks pass `bash -n`, and the PowerShell twin contains\nno non-`-LiteralPath` filesystem calls.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":283663,"output_tokens":1105,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1105,"cache_read_input_tokens":283663,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeyxTUFb324KYvdnBHimv","attributionSkill":"codex-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"5abb99ad-af8d-4382-9bcc-9667f14f73b5","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:41:42.751Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEf