d.","+- **Round 6** — Codex: **APPROVED**, 0 findings. *\"No material unresolved defects identified within the reviewed scope.\"*"," ","-All three disposition tables are below. Artifacts: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r{1,2,3}/`.","+**Gate A is satisfied. Task 1 may begin.**"," ","+Findings by round: 10 → 9 → 7 → 4 → 1 → 0. High-severity: 6 → 2 → 2 → 2 → 0 → 0. Two defects (R3-01, R3-02) were introduced by an earlier round's own fix and caught by the next — which is the argument for the gates existing.","+","+Disposition tables for rounds 1–3 are below; rounds 4 and 5 are recorded in `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r{4,5}.md`. Artifacts: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r{1..6}/`.","+","+> **Reviewer's stated limitations, carried forward as execution risk.** The review was read-only and static: no files were edited, no tests executed, no Windows filesystem behaviour exercised, and no Pi runtime isolation verified. The host independently ran the embedded-script parse checks, the clause-detection fixtures, the `valid_entry` guard cases and the full canonical-deletion scenario — those results are real. Everything else is an approved *plan*, not proven behaviour. Gates B, C and D still apply.","+"," ---"," "," ## Global Constraints"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"376a8948-3945-41ac-b807-3cd8838ed8f8","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
