d into all three trees. Same rule as plugins: not ours to rewrite, vendor into the repo, or publish to views. **Windows consequence, stated rather than hidden:** they were *already* broken there — tracked as mode-120000 links to a path that does not exist on that box. Untracking them means the next `dev-sync` pull deletes the dead links. To have them on Windows, install the package separately (see the `vendored-skill-install` skill). Nothing regresses; the breakage stops being silent."," - Pruning the ~150 pool entries that are third-party installs. Task 2 touches only the 98 that match yesterday's archive. The rest need a human decision via `aios-audit`."," - Migrating all 61 hooks to Pi. Task 8 ports exactly one to measure cost."," - **Adopting Pi.** Task 8 produces a cost number only. Adoption needs a boundary design that is its own project."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2ab1027-1a1b-4006-b449-43b69f4c8e92","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
