{"parentUuid":"36984abf-ba2b-4ac8-bbc9-c07bc8080e9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez3a4EjuQvZaKVnEHkfA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017Hbar3v9K5VE1iSZbhK6RS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt <<'EOF'\n\n=== AMEND-01 (found while verifying the snapshot) ===\nFour canonical entries are a TWO-HOP chain into a vendored third-party package:\n  ~/.claude/skills/<X> -> ~/.agents/skills/<X> -> ~/.agents/vendor-review/claudex-loop/skills/<X>\n  X in: claudex-loop, claudex-route, codex-build, codex-review\nThey were ALREADY committed to erash11/claude-skills as mode-120000 symlinks and\npushed - dead on Windows. They are untracked + gitignored in Task 4, not vendored\ninto the repo. The VIEWS tarball now includes .agents/vendor-review.\nWithout it the canonical SKILL.md count restores as 57, not 61.\n\n=== ROLLBACK - BY MIGRATION PHASE. Find where you are, then follow that row. ===\n\nPHASE A - before Task 4 ran (canonical still holds the outward symlinks).\n  Only views changed. Restore them and stop:\n    rm -rf ~/.codex/skills ~/.agents/skills ~/.agents/vendor-review\n    tar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz -C ~\n\nPHASE B - Task 4 inverted the links and committed.\n  ORDER MATTERS. Reverting canonical first creates reciprocal symlink cycles:\n  canonical entries become outward links again while the pool entries still\n  point back into canonical - each a link to the other, resolving to nothing.\n  Restore the pool to REAL directories FIRST, then revert canonical:\n\n    # 1. Real pool targets back (includes vendor-review).\n    rm -rf ~/.agents/skills ~/.codex/skills ~/.agents/vendor-review\n    tar xzf ~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz -C ~\n\n    # 2. Now revert the inversion commit.\n    git -C ~/.claude/skills log --oneline\n    git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <inversion-sha>\n    git -C ~/.claude/skills push\n\n    # 3. Verify no cycles: every canonical link must resolve.\n    find ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print\n    #    Must print nothing.\n\nPHASE C - Task 5 also rewrote frontmatter. Revert those commits too, newest\n  first, then do PHASE B.\n\n# NEVER extract the CANONICAL tarball over ~/.claude/skills. It would overlay\n# stale .git metadata onto new files without removing them, corrupting the very\n# history the revert needs. Extract it to a scratch dir ALONGSIDE the VIEWS\n# archive (so relative links resolve) and read it there.\n\n=== AFTER A ROLLBACK: WHICH SYNC SCRIPT IS INSTALLED? ===\nThe hardened sync REFUSES outward canonical symlinks by design; Phases B and C\nrestore exactly that layout. Do NOT regenerate after a legacy rollback. Choose:\n\n  OPTION 1 (default) - roll back the sync script too:\n    git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <sync-hardening-sha> && git push\n    # dev-sync behaves as before this plan. aios-audit reports no_manifest.\n\n  OPTION 2 - keep the new architecture: do NOT revert the inversion, fix\n    forward, then: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh\n\nNever leave hardened-script + legacy-layout: dev-sync fails permanently.\nEOF\ntail -8 /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt\necho \"--- total lines ---\"; wc -l < /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt","description":"Task 1 Step 4 — record the phase-aware rollback paths"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":320402,"output_tokens":1541,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63