{"parentUuid":"73bac176-988f-4aaf-81eb-45f9d1f3cd88","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4266cc80-8a62-4f8f-9349-96ce9551674d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NCMbHjtLjbZaswLnRe9Pqx","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r6.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"e2773ff8-b95e-46af-b97d-46481df8740f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:49:24.385Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r6.md","content":"# Round 7 — plan amended during execution. Re-review requested.\n\nRound 6 APPROVED the plan. **Task 1 then executed and found something the plan\ndid not know about**, so the approval no longer binds this hash. One amendment,\n`AMEND-01`, applied in seven places.\n\n## What execution found\n\nTask 1 Step 3 (verify the archives restore) produced **57** canonical\n`SKILL.md`, not the expected 61. Investigation:\n\n```\n.claude/skills/claudex-loop  -> ../../.agents/skills/claudex-loop\n.agents/skills/claudex-loop  -> ../vendor-review/claudex-loop/skills/claudex-loop\n```\n\nA **two-hop chain** into `~/.agents/vendor-review/claudex-loop/`, a vendored\nthird-party package. Four skills affected — `claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`,\n`codex-build`, `codex-review` — linked identically from all three trees\n(`.claude`, `.agents`, `.codex`). A sweep for links resolving outside the three\nskill trees found these twelve entries and nothing else; no danglers.\n\n`vendor-review/` was outside the VIEWS tarball, so the restored canonical links\ncould not resolve. Second, and worse:\n\n```\n$ git -C ~/.claude/skills ls-files -s claudex-loop\n120000 ... claudex-loop\n```\n\n**All four are already tracked as mode-120000 symlinks and pushed** to\n`erash11/claude-skills`. That is precisely the R3 breakage this plan exists to\nprevent, already live: Windows pulls four links to a path that does not exist\non that box.\n\n## AMEND-01 — disposition\n\nDecision: **do not vendor them into the repo. Untrack and gitignore.** They are\none third-party package, so the plan's existing rule for plugin skills applies —\nnot ours to rewrite, vendor, or publish. Copying the vendor's directories into\n`erash11/claude-skills` would fork and freeze their package.\n\nApplied in seven places:\n\n| # | Where | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Task 1 Step 2/3 | VIEWS tarball now includes `.agents/vendor-review` and `.agents/.skill-lock.json`. New `vendor-review OK` assertion, and an explicit note that a count of 57 means the tarball is missing it. **Already re-taken and re-verified: 306 / 32 / 61 / `_shared OK` / `vendor-review OK`.** |\n| 2 | Task 3 sync script | `MANAGED` enumeration now skips `[ -L \"${d%/}\" ]`. Without this the four land in `MANAGED`, the R1 guard sees a symlinked source and exits 2 **on every run**, permanently breaking `dev-sync` — the R3-01 deadlock shape again. |\n| 3 | Task 4 canonicalize script | New `[ -L \"$abs\" ]` test before the `-d` check. `-d`/`-f` follow links, so without it the script would `mv` the *pool symlink* into canonical and link the pool back at it: canonical still a symlink, still tracked, nothing fixed. Now reports `VENDORED ... left alone`. |\n| 4 | Task 4 Step 4 | New sub-step runs `git rm --cached` on the four and appends four `/name/` lines to `.gitignore` with a comment pointing at `vendor-review`. Working tree untouched; they keep working on this Mac. Expected counts corrected to `inverted: 15  skipped: 4`, `symlinks left in canonical: 4`. |\n| 5 | Task 5 checker | `main()` skips `SKILL.md` whose parent directory is a symlink. Their frontmatter belongs to a third-party package we do not edit, so demanding the clause contract of them would make \"0 failing\" unreachable. |\n| 6 | Task 6 metrics | `symlinks_in_canonical` replaced by `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` (reads `git ls-files -s`, must be 0) plus informational `vendored_links_in_canonical` (expected 4). `canonical_expected()` skips symlinks. Expected-value table and the `aios-audit` invariant step updated; `rot.md`'s invariant now says \"no TRACKED symlinks\". |\n| 7 | Out of Scope | The four named, with the Windows consequence stated rather than hidden: they were already broken there; untracking means the next `dev-sync` pull deletes the dead links; installing the package separately is the fix. |\n\n## Task 1 status: COMPLETE\n\n- Inventory: 593 lines, `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt`\n- VIEWS tarball 4.1M, CANONICAL tarball 42M\n- Restore verified: `306 / 32 / 61 / _shared OK / vendor-review OK / 3ab4467`\n- Separation verified: VIEWS archive alone contains no `.claude`\n- Phase-aware rollback (A/B/C) recorded, including the vendor-review paths\n- Embedded scripts re-checked after the amendments: all python blocks compile,\n  all bash script blocks pass `bash -n`\n- Committed `d2e4a3b`\n\n## Question for this round\n\nDoes AMEND-01 hold across all seven sites, and does anything else in Tasks 2–8\nstill assume the four vendored skills are ordinary canonical content?\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"73bac176-988f-4aaf-81eb-45f9d1f3cd88","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
