{"parentUuid":"c706eb6d-85e8-435f-8071-44b2cdc87b6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez3nKzcBqBWP8TKwUXTS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019tzzTw42hpyXHbJq496YDy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json,glob\nf=sorted(glob.glob('/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r7/**/result.json',recursive=True))\nd=json.load(open(f[0])); r=d['response']\nprint('VERDICT:',r.get('verdict'))\nprint('SUMMARY:',r.get('summary'))\nprint('findings:',len(r.get('findings',[])))\nprint()\nfor x in r.get('findings',[]):\n    print('['+x['severity'].upper()+'] '+x['id']+'  '+x['path'].split(chr(8212))[-1].strip())\n    print('  E:',x['evidence'])\n    print('  F:',x['fix'])\n    print()\n\"","description":"Read round 7 verdict"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":434,"cache_read_input_tokens":325992,"output_tokens":326,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":434,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":326,"cache_read_input_tokens":325992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":434},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cez3nJDCTdAXMYk8RNdCv","type":"assistant","uuid":"82a05437-e16a-4ae4-b888-2c5c924f755d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:51:21.723Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"82a05437-e16a-4ae4-b888-2c5c924f755d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4266cc80-8a62-4f8f-9349-96ce9551674d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019tzzTw42hpyXHbJq496YDy","type":"tool_result","content":"VERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: AMEND-01 is incomplete: it bypasses the source guard, fails to ignore the vendored symlinks, and leaves incompatible sync, metrics, and normalization consumers.\nfindings: 5\n\n[HIGH] R7-01  Task 3 Step 2\n  E: MANAGED now excludes every canonical symlink before the R1 guard inspects it. The current 15 ordinary outward links therefore also escape validation, contradicting Step 5's required refusal. If a previously managed skill becomes an outward link into its pool directory, its omission makes the retirement loop archive and remove that target, breaking the canonical skill.\n  F: Exclude only explicitly declared vendored names whose targets have been verified. Refuse all other canonical symlinks before any mutation. Use that same ownership definition in the checker and metrics.\n\n[HIGH] R7-02  Task 4 Step 4\n  E: The proposed ignore patterns end in '/', which matches directories, not symlinks. After git rm --cached, the following git add -A will re-add the four mode-120000 entries. Their current tracked symlink modes were confirmed. The other writer, ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1, also runs git add -A through Sync-Repo on this repository.\n  F: Use anchored patterns without trailing slashes, such as /claudex-loop. Require verification that all four links are ignored and absent from the index after staging.\n\n[MEDIUM] R7-03  Task 3 Step 3\n  E: The PowerShell twin still enumerates vendored directories with SKILL.md and rejects their reparse points. Installing the package separately on Windows, as the amended out-of-scope section prescribes, can therefore make every subsequent dev-sync fail. The actual dev-sync skill invokes this twin after pulling the skills repository.\n  F: Implement the explicit vendored-name and target policy in PowerShell too, while continuing to reject unexpected source links.\n\n[MEDIUM] R7-04  Task 7 Step 1\n  E: The metrics producer renamed symlinks_in_canonical to tracked_symlinks_in_canonical, but ROW still calls get symlinks_in_canonical. Every successful metrics invocation consequently produces MISSING and the wrapper exits 1 before appending the trend row or writing the nudge.\n  F: Update the wrapper's lookup and table heading to the new tracked-symlink metric, and align the manual audit's trend-row schema.\n\n[MEDIUM] R7-05  Tasks 4–6\n  E: Several consumers still treat the four vendors as owned content. Task 5 explicitly includes codex-review in the frontmatter rewrite list despite excluding it from the checker. Task 4 expects a 62-entry manifest although the amended publisher produces 58; Task 5 expects 61 checked skills although its filter produces 57. Conversely, canonical_skills still calls skills_in(CANON), which follows the four links and reports 61 against the new expected 57. names_in and roster_tokens likewise retain vendors in owned-roster analysis.\n  F: Propagate a single explicit owned/vendor inventory through normalization, metrics, and verification. Remove vendor skills from editing and owned-roster recommendations; distinguish 57 owned skills, four vendor links, and 58 published entries. Replace the remaining contradictory inversion and count expectations.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"57d1b380-59cb-4a36-a811-a97f10bf0119","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:51:23.087Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"VERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: AMEND-01 is incomplete: it bypasses the source guard, fails to ignore the vendored symlinks, and leaves incompatible sync, metrics, and normalization consumers.\nfindings: 5\n\n[HIGH] R7-01  Task 3 Step 2\n  E: MANAGED now excludes every canonical symlink before the R1 guard inspects it. The current 15 ordinary outward links therefore also escape validation, contradicting Step 5's required refusal. If a previously managed skill becomes an outward link into its pool directory, its omission makes the retirement loop archive and remove that target, breaking the canonical skill.\n  F: Exclude only explicitly declared vendored names whose targets have been verified. Refuse all other canonical symlinks before any mutation. Use that same ownership definition in the checker and metrics.\n\n[HIGH] R7-02  Task 4 Step 4\n  E: The proposed ignore patterns end in '/', which matches directories, not symlinks. After git rm --cached, the following git add -A will re-add the four mode-120000 entries. Their current tracked symlink modes were confirmed. The other writer, ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1, also runs git add -A through Sync-Repo on this repository.\n  F: Use anchored patterns without trailing slashes, such as /claudex-loop. Require verification that all four links are ignored and absent from the index after staging.\n\n[MEDIUM] R7-03  Task 3 Step 3\n  E: The PowerShell twin still enumerates vendored directories with SKILL.md and rejects their reparse points. Installing the package separately on Windows, as the amended out-of-scope section prescribes, can therefore make every subsequent dev-sync fail. The actual dev-sync skill invokes this twin after pulling the skills repository.\n  F: Implement the explicit vendored-name and target policy in PowerShell too, while continuing to reject unexpected source links.\n\n[MEDIUM] R7-04  Task 7 Step 1\n  E: The metrics producer renamed symlinks_in_canonical to tracked_symlinks_in_canonical, but ROW still calls get symlinks_in_canonical. Every successful metrics invocation consequently produces MISSING and the wrapper exits 1 before appending the trend row or writing the nudge.\n  F: Update the wrapper's lookup and table heading to the new tracked-symlink metric, and align the manual audit's trend-row schema.\n\n[MEDIUM] R7-05  Tasks 4–6\n  E: Several consumers still treat the four vendors as owned content. Task 5 explicitly includes codex-review in the frontmatter rewrite list despite excluding it from the checker. Task 4 expects a 62-entry manifest although the amended publisher produces 58; Task 5 expects 61 checked skills although its filter produces 57. Conversely, canonical_skills still calls skills_in(CANON), which follows the four links and reports 61 against the new expected 57. names_in and roster_tokens likewise retain vendors in owned-roster analysis.\n  F: Propagate a single explicit owned/vendor inventory through normalization, metrics, and verification. Remove vendor skills from editing and owned-roster recommendations; distinguish 57 owned skills, four vendor links, and 58 published entries. Replace the remaining contradictory inversion and count expectations.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"82a05437-e16a-4ae4-b888-2c5c924f755d","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
