{"parentUuid":"acdb2d52-0cdc-4d62-875e-bc96566027f8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"acb21d47-94ae-44c3-b265-1a5abcc26e6c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:53:50.928Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"acb21d47-94ae-44c3-b265-1a5abcc26e6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez3ycKC7NSohYwJGJEro","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V95rNsUqkdxEyzYrtCsXZs","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r7.md","content":"# Round 7 dispositions — all five ACCEPTED\n\nAMEND-01 was incomplete. The root cause was using \"is a symlink\" as the vendor\ntest instead of a declared inventory. There is now **one `VENDORED` list**\n(`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review`) declared in\nfour places that must stay identical: `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1`,\n`aios-metrics.py`, `skill-portability-check.py`.\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R7-01 | ACCEPTED | The blanket `[ -L ]` skip is replaced by `is_vendored()`, an explicit allowlist. Only declared names are skipped, and only after verifying the link resolves under `$VENDOR_ROOT` — a vendored name pointing elsewhere is `FATAL`, as is a declared vendored name that is a *real* directory (meaning it was vendored into the repo by mistake, or the list is stale). Every other canonical symlink now enters `MANAGED` and faces the R1 guard, so the 15 ordinary outward links can no longer escape validation, and a skill that silently became a link into its own pool entry can no longer be archived and deleted by the retirement loop. |\n| R7-02 | ACCEPTED | Patterns changed from `/claudex-loop/` to `/claudex-loop` (all four). A trailing slash matches directories only and git does not treat a symlink as a directory, so the originals would have matched nothing and the next `git add -A` would have silently re-added all four mode-120000 entries — and this repo has **two** such writers: Task 4 itself and `daily-backup.ps1` via `Sync-Repo`. Added a verification block running `git check-ignore -q` on each, then `git add -A`, then asserting none of the four reappear in `git ls-files -s`. A comment in `.gitignore` records why the slash must not come back. |\n| R7-03 | ACCEPTED | The PowerShell twin gets `$VENDORED` and `$VENDORROOT` and the same three-way policy: skip declared names, `FATAL` if a declared name is a real directory, `FATAL` if its target is outside the vendor root, and continue to reject every *other* reparse point. Without this, installing the package on Windows per the amended Out-of-Scope note would have made every subsequent `dev-sync` fail. |\n| R7-04 | ACCEPTED | `ROW` now reads `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` and the new `vendored_skills`, matching the producer; the table heading gained `vendored` and `tracked links`. Because a key mismatch aborts the run **before** any row or nudge is written — one rename silently killing the monthly job — Step 2 now also diffs the producer's emitted keys against the wrapper's `get` calls and requires \"every wrapper key is emitted by the metrics script\". |\n| R7-05 | ACCEPTED | Three numbers now stated once and used consistently: **57 owned**, **4 vendored**, **58 published** (57 + `_shared`). Changed: manifest expectation 62 → 58; checker expectation \"61 skills\" → \"57 skills\"; `canonical_skills` now `len(owned(CANON))` instead of `skills_in(CANON)` (which followed the four links and reported 61); new `vendored_skills` metric; `owned()` helper added and used for `canon_names`, so `never_used` no longer counts vendors; `roster_tokens()` skips vendors; `canonical_expected()` filters on `VENDORED` rather than `islink`; the checker filters on `VENDORED` rather than `islink`. `codex-review` removed from the Task 5 frontmatter edit list with a note saying why (vendored, excluded from the checker, would be overwritten by the next vendor install). |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n\n## Verification run before submitting this round\n\n- Both embedded `python` blocks compile; all embedded `bash` script blocks pass\n  `bash -n`.\n- Stale-string sweep returns 0 for `checked 61 skills`, `manifest holds 62`,\n  `symlinks_in_canonical`, and `61 skills × 2`.\n- Committed `bb19c06`.\n\n## Question for this round\n\nIs the owned/vendor split now consistent across the sync scripts, the checker,\nthe metrics, the cron wrapper and every stated expected count — and does any\nstep in Tasks 2–8 still assume the four vendored skills are owned content?\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":342148,"output_tokens":1620,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1620,"cache_read_input_tokens":342148,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":565},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cez3ybVpivhXTtcYHJttF","type":"assistant","uuid":"c552d725-479d-46fd-9690-3b4fffead53e","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:54:11.512Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
