, would be overwritten by the next vendor install). |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n\n## Verification run before submitting this round\n\n- Both embedded `python` blocks compile; all embedded `bash` script blocks pass\n  `bash -n`.\n- Stale-string sweep returns 0 for `checked 61 skills`, `manifest holds 62`,\n  `symlinks_in_canonical`, and `61 skills × 2`.\n- Committed `bb19c06`.\n\n## Question for this round\n\nIs the owned/vendor split now consistent across the sync scripts, the checker,\nthe metrics, the cron wrapper and every stated expected count — and does any\nstep in Tasks 2–8 still assume the four vendored skills are owned content?\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c552d725-479d-46fd-9690-3b4fffead53e","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
