{"parentUuid":"36cdb631-65df-4d85-972a-c3413021b0ab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez4AoauF4mPtB6BesC51","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_read_input_tokens":357975,"output_tokens":1834,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":911},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":257,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1834,"cache_read_input_tokens":357975,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":257},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cez4AnnXg9pcHKTau12xS","type":"assistant","uuid":"80e30a85-3ce2-4889-b828-3417c1cd5223","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:56:38.610Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"80e30a85-3ce2-4889-b828-3417c1cd5223","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez4AoauF4mPtB6BesC51","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task 2 done and pushed. I'm now blocked, so here's where things stand.\n\n## Done and safe\n\n**Task 1 — snapshot.** Two separate backups taken and *verified by actually restoring them*. That verification caught a real problem (below).\n\n**Task 2 — the big one.** Pruned the stale pool: **306 → 208**. The 98 skills you thought you archived yesterday are now actually gone from the folder Pi reads. Your ~150 third-party installs were not touched. All 61 skills still resolve, nothing is dangling.\n\nBoth are committed and pushed. Fully reversible.\n\n## What verifying the backup found\n\nThe restore gave **57** skills, not 61. Four were missing. Cause:\n\n```\n~/.claude/skills/claudex-loop → ~/.agents/skills/claudex-loop → ~/.agents/vendor-review/...\n```\n\nA **two-hop chain** into a vendored package — `claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review`. That vendor folder wasn't in my backup. Fixed, re-verified, 61/61.\n\nWorse: those four are **already committed to your `claude-skills` repo as symlinks and pushed**. On Windows they're dead links pointing at a path that doesn't exist. That's the exact failure this whole plan exists to prevent — already live, silently.\n\nDecision: they stay out of the repo, same rule as plugins. Windows needs a separate install of that package. It was already broken there; now it's explicit.\n\n## Why I stopped\n\nI amended the plan for that discovery, then re-ran your Codex gate. **Codex found 5 more bugs in my amendment** — including that my `.gitignore` lines ended in `/`, which matches folders but **not symlinks**, so the next backup run would have silently re-added all four dead links.\n\nI fixed all five. Then Codex hit its usage limit:\n\n> *You've hit your usage limit... try again at 4:46 PM*\n\nTask 3 is where the rewritten sync scripts land. Codex has now caught serious bugs in that exact code **twice**. You asked for Codex to review generated code, and I can't get that review until **4:46 PM**.\n\n## Your call\n\n- **Wait for Codex** — I resume at 4:46 PM, run the gate, then continue Tasks 3–8. Your constraint respected.\n- **Continue unreviewed now** — I run Task 3 onward on my own checks only. Faster, but that code has failed review twice already.\n\nI'd wait. The sync script is the one piece that can destroy real skills, and Codex caught a genuine data-loss bug in it on the first pass.\n\nneeds input: Codex quota is exhausted until 4:46 PM. Tell me to wait and resume then, or to continue Tasks 3–8 without the Codex review gate."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_read_input_tokens":357975,"output_tokens":1834,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":911},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":257,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1834,"cache_read_input_tokens":357975,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":257},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cez4AnnXg9pcHKTau12xS","type":"assistant","uuid":"def5a93b-8da4-40e8-8a5f-5266339f1f21","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:56:51.768Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
