{"parentUuid":"c6d71b86-5ec2-482f-8ed3-5a397a2b33e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez5jmHY8BbjCu1M3Ao9E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rhozbd1JosMLhaNyb9ApMG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/task4-new.md","content":"### Task 4: Untrack the third-party links, then publish the views\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `~/.claude/skills/.gitignore` (generated block)\n- Modify: `~/.claude/skills` git index (untrack 19 symlinks)\n- Modify: `~/.agents/skills/`, `~/.codex/skills/` (regenerated from the manifest)\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: the hardened sync script from Task 3.\n- Produces: a canonical repo whose *index* holds only content Eric wrote, and two views carrying all 43 published entries. Task 5 then edits one file per skill and all three harnesses see it.\n\n**This task used to invert 19 symlinks into the repo. That script is deleted.** Round 8 established why: **all 19 outward links are third-party.** 14 are `skills` CLI installs recorded in `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` — five of them from `mattpocock-skills`, which this plan puts explicitly out of scope — four are the `vendor-review/claudex-loop` package, and `persistent-localhost` is a hand-install. Inverting them would have copied fourteen other people's packages into `erash11/claude-skills` and frozen them there.\n\n**Ownership is structural, and that is the whole simplification:**\n\n| Shape in `~/.claude/skills/` | Meaning | Count |\n|---|---|---|\n| real directory | Eric wrote it | **42** (+`_shared`) |\n| symlink | installed by the `skills` CLI, or vendored | **19** |\n\nSo: **42 owned skills, 43 published entries** (42 + `_shared`), **19 third-party links**. Nothing needs inverting. The links stay exactly where they are, keep working on this Mac, and simply stop being tracked by git.\n\nAll 19 are currently tracked as mode-120000 and **already pushed** — dead links on Windows. That is the R3 breakage this plan exists to prevent, live today.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Untrack all 19, keeping them on disk**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"{print $4}' > /tmp/tracked-links.txt\nwc -l < /tmp/tracked-links.txt\ncat /tmp/tracked-links.txt\n```\n\nExpected: `19`, then the names. Every one must be a symlink on disk — if a real directory appears here, stop: that is an owned skill and it belongs in the index.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\nxargs -a /tmp/tracked-links.txt git rm --cached --\ngit status --short | head -25\n```\n\nExpected: 19 `D` lines. The directories must **still exist** — `ls -la ~/.claude/skills/anti-sleep` still shows a link.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Let the sync script write the ignore block, then prove it holds**\n\nThe `.gitignore` block is generated by `sync-to-codex.sh`, not hand-maintained, so a future `npx skills add` is covered automatically (R8-02):\n\n```bash\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\nsed -n '/BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex/,/END generated-by-sync-to-codex/p' ~/.claude/skills/.gitignore\n```\n\nExpected: `exit=0`, and a block listing all 19 names, each with a **leading slash and no trailing slash**.\n\n> A trailing slash matches directories only, and git does not treat a symlink as a directory — `/anti-sleep/` would match nothing, and the next `git add -A` would silently re-add all 19. This repo has two such writers: Step 3 below, and `daily-backup.ps1` via `Sync-Repo`.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do\n  printf '%-28s ignored=%s ondisk=%s\\n' \"$s\" \\\n    \"$(git check-ignore -q \"$s\" && echo yes || echo NO)\" \\\n    \"$(ls -ld \"$s\" | cut -c1)\"\ndone < /tmp/tracked-links.txt\n```\n\nExpected: `ignored=yes` and `ondisk=l` for all 19. A single `NO` means the pattern is wrong — fix before staging.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Stage, then inspect the index (R2-03)**\n\n`git ls-files` reads the *index*, so it must be checked **after** staging, not before:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\necho \"--- staged symlinks (mode 120000) - MUST be empty ---\"\ngit ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"'\necho \"--- staged summary ---\"\ngit diff --cached --stat | tail -3\n```\n\nExpected: the `120000` list prints **nothing**; the summary shows 19 deletions plus the `.gitignore` change. If any `120000` entry survives, run `git reset` and stop — committing one sends a Mac symlink to Windows.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Verify the owned roster is intact and `_shared` still resolves**\n\n```bash\necho \"owned real dirs with SKILL.md (expect 42):\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type d ! -path ~/.claude/skills -exec test -f {}/SKILL.md \\; -print | wc -l\necho \"third-party links (expect 19):\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\necho \"total resolvable SKILL.md (expect 61):\"\nfind -L ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\necho \"--- dangling links (must be empty) ---\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print\ntest -f ~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared OK\"\npython3 -c \"\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path.home()/'.claude/skills/meeting-sync/scripts/sync.py'\ncfg = p.resolve().parents[2]/'_shared/config.json'\nprint('meeting-sync resolves _shared:', cfg.exists())\n\"\n```\n\nExpected: `42`, `19`, `61`, no dangling output, `_shared OK`, and `True`. The `True` is the R2 check: 10+ skills reach `_shared` through `parents[2]`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**\n\nTwo owned skills have pool copies that differ from canonical, and the publish in Step 6 overwrites them. Verified on disk: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **differ**; `backup` and 7 others are **absent** from the pool.\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12\necho \"=== owned skills whose pool copy DIFFERS ===\"\nfor d in ~/.claude/skills/*/; do\n  s=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"\n  [ -L \"${d%/}\" ] && continue\n  [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ] || continue\n  b=~/.agents/skills/\"$s\"\n  if [ -e \"$b\" ] && [ ! -L \"$b\" ] && ! diff -rq \"$d\" \"$b\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    echo \"DIVERGED $s\"\n  fi\ndone\n```\n\nFor each DIVERGED name, read the diff and decide which side wins, backing up the pool copy first:\n\n```bash\nfor s in memory-write meeting-sync; do\n  echo \"===== $s =====\"\n  diff -ru ~/.claude/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" | head -40\n  cp -R ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/\"$s\"\ndone\nls ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/\n```\n\nIf the pool copy is better, `cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/` and commit it in canonical. If canonical wins, do nothing. **Do not skip reading the diffs** — the publish discards whatever you did not move. The backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong.\n\nThe ABSENT names need no action: the complete-manifest publish covers them automatically.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Publish, and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"dry exit=$?\"\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real exit=$?\"\n\nMAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\necho \"--- manifest size (expect 43) ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"\n\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed links not resolving to canonical (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do\n  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"\ndone < \"$MAN\"\n```\n\nExpected: both `exit=0`; the script reports `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`; the manifest holds **43** lines; all three lists **empty**.\n\n> **The numbers, kept straight.** 61 resolvable `SKILL.md` in canonical = **42 owned** + **19 third-party links**. Published = **43** (42 owned + `_shared`). Pool after publish = 208 pruned entries reconciled with the 43 managed. Any step expecting 57, 58, 61 or 62 is stale.\n\nSuccess is measured against the **manifest**, never against `ls ~/.claude/skills`: the repo also holds `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1` and `CLAUDE.md`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n\nRun `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61 — untracking changes git, not what the harness reads from disk). If it dropped, roll back per **Task 1, PHASE A**.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\ngit status --short | head\ngit commit -m \"chore: stop tracking third-party skill symlinks\n\nAll 19 outward links in this repo are third-party: 14 skills-CLI installs\nrecorded in ~/.agents/.skill-lock.json (five of them mattpocock-skills),\n4 from the vendor-review/claudex-loop package, plus persistent-localhost.\nThey were tracked as mode-120000 and pushed, i.e. dead links on Windows.\n\nThey stay on disk and keep working here; the repo now holds only skills\nwritten here. sync-to-codex.sh regenerates the ignore block on every run,\nso a future \\`npx skills add\\` cannot get its link committed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":376169,"output_tokens":4073,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4073,"cache_read_input_tokens":376169,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cez5jkVezbAyyxA2TYf31","type":"assistant","uuid":"00ee8dc0-40c1-43ad-9965-20c6f489cb3b","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:17:40.448Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
