read -r s; do\n  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"\ndone < \"$MAN\"\n```\n\nExpected: both `exit=0`; the script reports `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`; the manifest holds **43** lines; all three lists **empty**.\n\n> **The numbers, kept straight.** 61 resolvable `SKILL.md` in canonical = **42 owned** + **19 third-party links**. Published = **43** (42 owned + `_shared`). Pool after publish = 208 pruned entries reconciled with the 43 managed. Any step expecting 57, 58, 61 or 62 is stale.\n\nSuccess is measured against the **manifest**, never against `ls ~/.claude/skills`: the repo also holds `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1` and `CLAUDE.md`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n\nRun `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61 — untracking changes git, not what the harness reads from disk). If it dropped, roll back per **Task 1, PHASE A**.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\ngit status --short | head\ngit commit -m \"chore: stop tracking third-party skill symlinks\n\nAll 19 outward links in this repo are third-party: 14 skills-CLI installs\nrecorded in ~/.agents/.skill-lock.json (five of them mattpocock-skills),\n4 from the vendor-review/claudex-loop package, plus persistent-localhost.\nThey were tracked as mode-120000 and pushed, i.e. dead links on Windows.\n\nThey stay on disk and keep working here; the repo now holds only skills\nwritten here. sync-to-codex.sh regenerates the ignore block on every run,\nso a future \\`npx skills add\\` cannot get its link committed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\n```\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"00ee8dc0-40c1-43ad-9965-20c6f489cb3b","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
