{"parentUuid":"bdb50d28-e81b-4a73-a120-95f5e5b68ac4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d90457fc-55a4-4c91-beb9-bfaecc9c0aa3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YTcRznfBAdeXJEvZsJi7Wq","type":"tool_result","content":"replaced Task 4: old 279 lines -> new 185 lines\n135:### Task 1: Snapshot and freeze the current state\n321:### Task 2: Prune the stale pool mirror\n410:### Task 3: Harden the sync writers — before anything moves\n927:### Task 4: Untrack the third-party links, then publish the views\n1115:### Task 5: Normalize every skill to portable frontmatter\n1427:### Task 6: `rot.md` and the `aios-audit` compound skill\n1890:### Task 7: Put the metrics on a monthly clock\n2166:### Task 8: Pi trial under a real boundary\n2390:- [ ] **Gate B — after Task 5.** `codex-review` on `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1`, `skills-canonicalize.sh`, `skill-portability-check.py`, and ten rewritten frontmatter blocks. Codex is the right reviewer here specifically because it is the harness whose triggering the rewrite claims to fix.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fa61e91e-5d61-4a55-a901-ebc9ef28af2d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:17:49.577Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"replaced Task 4: old 279 lines -> new 185 lines\n135:### Task 1: Snapshot and freeze the current state\n321:### Task 2: Prune the stale pool mirror\n410:### Task 3: Harden the sync writers — before anything moves\n927:### Task 4: Untrack the third-party links, then publish the views\n1115:### Task 5: Normalize every skill to portable frontmatter\n1427:### Task 6: `rot.md` and the `aios-audit` compound skill\n1890:### Task 7: Put the metrics on a monthly clock\n2166:### Task 8: Pi trial under a real boundary\n2390:- [ ] **Gate B — after Task 5.** `codex-review` on `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1`, `skills-canonicalize.sh`, `skill-portability-check.py`, and ten rewritten frontmatter blocks. Codex is the right reviewer here specifically because it is the harness whose triggering the rewrite claims to fix.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":924,"oldLines":158,"newStart":924,"newLines":76,"lines":[" "," ---"," ","-### Task 4: Invert the outward symlinks, then publish the views","+### Task 4: Untrack the third-party links, then publish the views"," "," **Files:**","-- Modify: `~/.claude/skills/` (19 symlinks become real dirs)","+- Modify: `~/.claude/skills/.gitignore` (generated block)","+- Modify: `~/.claude/skills` git index (untrack 19 symlinks)"," - Modify: `~/.agents/skills/`, `~/.codex/skills/` (regenerated from the manifest)","-- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`"," "," **Interfaces:**","-- Consumes: the hardened, guard-proven sync script from Task 3.","-- Produces: a canonical repo with **zero symlinks**, and two views carrying every canonical skill. Task 5 then edits one file per skill and all three harnesses see it.","+- Consumes: the hardened sync script from Task 3.","+- Produces: a canonical repo whose *index* holds only content Eric wrote, and two views carrying all 43 published entries. Task 5 then edits one file per skill and all three harnesses see it."," ","-**Direction, restated because round 1 had it backwards.** 19 entries in `~/.claude/skills/` are symlinks pointing *out* to `~/.agents/skills/`. Their real content therefore sits outside the git repo — unversioned, not on Windows, not in the backup. This task pulls each real directory **into** the repo, leaves a link behind at the pool, and only then publishes the views.","+**This task used to invert 19 symlinks into the repo. That script is deleted.** Round 8 established why: **all 19 outward links are third-party.** 14 are `skills` CLI installs recorded in `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` — five of them from `mattpocock-skills`, which this plan puts explicitly out of scope — four are the `vendor-review/claudex-loop` package, and `persistent-localhost` is a hand-install. Inverting them would have copied fourteen other people's packages into `erash11/claude-skills` and frozen them there."," ","-- [ ] **Step 1: Write the script**","+**Ownership is structural, and that is the whole simplification:**"," ","-Create `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh`:","-","-```bash","-#!/usr/bin/env bash","-# Invert outward symlinks so ~/.claude/skills holds real directories only.","-#   before: ~/.claude/skills/X -> ~/.agents/skills/X   (real content outside git)","-#   after:  ~/.claude/skills/X is real; ~/.agents/skills/X -> it","-# Idempotent. DRY_RUN=1 by default.","-set -euo pipefail","+| Shape in `~/.claude/skills/` | Meaning | Count |","+|---|---|---|","+| real directory | Eric wrote it | **42** (+`_shared`) |","+| symlink | installed by the `skills` CLI, or vendored | **19** |"," ","-SRC=\"$HOME/.claude/skills\"","-POOL=\"$HOME/.agents/skills\"","-DRY=\"${DRY_RUN:-1}\"","-moved=0; skipped=0","+So: **42 owned skills, 43 published entries** (42 + `_shared`), **19 third-party links**. Nothing needs inverting. The links stay exactly where they are, keep working on this Mac, and simply stop being tracked by git."," ","-for link in \"$SRC\"/*; do","-  name=\"$(basename \"$link\")\"","-  case \"$name\" in .*) continue ;; esac","-  if [ ! -L \"$link\" ]; then","-    continue","-  fi","-  target=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$link\")\" && readlink \"$link\")\"","-  abs=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$link\")\" && cd \"$(dirname \"$target\")\" 2>/dev/null && pwd)/$(basename \"$target\")\"","-  # AMEND-01: if the POOL entry is itself a link, this is a two-hop chain into","-  # a vendored package (~/.agents/vendor-review/). -d and -f follow links, so","-  # without this test the script would move the pool SYMLINK into canonical and","-  # link the pool back at it - canonical would still hold a symlink, still","-  # tracked, and nothing would be fixed.","-  if [ -L \"$abs\" ]; then","-    echo \"VENDORED  $name (pool entry is itself a link -> $(readlink \"$abs\")) - left alone\"","-    skipped=$((skipped+1))","-    continue","-  fi","-  if [ ! -d \"$abs\" ]; then","-    echo \"DANGLING $name -> $target (left alone)\"","-    skipped=$((skipped+1))","-    continue","-  fi","-  if [ ! -f \"$abs/SKILL.md\" ]; then","-    echo \"NO-SKILL  $name -> $target (support dir, left alone)\"","-    skipped=$((skipped+1))","-    continue","-  fi","-  echo \"INVERT    $name  ($abs -> $SRC/$name, link back at pool)\"","-  if [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ]; then","-    rm \"$link\"","-    mv \"$abs\" \"$SRC/$name\"","-    ln -s \"$SRC/$name\" \"$abs\"","-  fi","-  moved=$((moved+1))","-done","+All 19 are currently tracked as mode-120000 and **already pushed** — dead links on Windows. That is the R3 breakage this plan exists to prevent, live today."," ","-echo","-echo \"inverted: $moved   skipped: $skipped\"","-echo \"symlinks left in canonical: $(find \"$SRC\" -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\"","-if [ \"$DRY\" = \"1\" ]; then","-  echo \"(DRY RUN - set DRY_RUN=0 to apply)\"","-fi","-exit 0","-```","+- [ ] **Step 1: Untrack all 19, keeping them on disk**"," "," ```bash","-chmod +x ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh","+cd ~/.claude/skills","+git ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"{print $4}' > /tmp/tracked-links.txt","+wc -l < /tmp/tracked-links.txt","+cat /tmp/tracked-links.txt"," ```"," ","-- [ ] **Step 2: Dry run and read every line**","+Expected: `19`, then the names. Every one must be a symlink on disk — if a real directory appears here, stop: that is an owned skill and it belongs in the index."," "," ```bash","-~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh","+cd ~/.claude/skills","+xargs -a /tmp/tracked-links.txt git rm --cached --","+git status --short | head -25"," ```"," ","-Expected: **15** `INVERT` lines, **4** `VENDORED ... left alone` lines, `inverted: 15   skipped: 4`, and the DRY footer. Any `DANGLING` line is a broken skill — investigate before applying. `NO-SKILL` lines are support directories and are correctly left alone (this is the R2 fix; there is **no** instruction anywhere in this plan to delete a directory for lacking a SKILL.md).","-","-- [ ] **Step 3: Apply**","-","-```bash","-DRY_RUN=0 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh","-```","+Expected: 19 `D` lines. The directories must **still exist** — `ls -la ~/.claude/skills/anti-sleep` still shows a link."," ","-Expected: the same lines, then `symlinks left in canonical: 4` — the four vendored links, which stay as working links on this Mac and are made invisible to git in Step 4. **Not 0.**","+- [ ] **Step 2: Let the sync script write the ignore block, then prove it holds**"," ","-- [ ] **Step 4: Verify the canonical repo is symlink-free and complete**","+The `.gitignore` block is generated by `sync-to-codex.sh`, not hand-maintained, so a future `npx skills add` is covered automatically (R8-02):"," "," ```bash","-echo \"--- symlinks in canonical working tree (expect 4, the vendored package) ---\"","-find ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l -exec basename {} \\;","-echo \"--- SKILL.md count (must be 61) ---\"","-find -L ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l","-echo \"--- dangling pool links (must be empty) ---\"","-find ~/.agents/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print","+bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"","+sed -n '/BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex/,/END generated-by-sync-to-codex/p' ~/.claude/skills/.gitignore"," ```"," ","-Expected: exactly the four vendored names (`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review`); `61`; no dangling output. Any **other** name in that link list means an inversion did not complete.","+Expected: `exit=0`, and a block listing all 19 names, each with a **leading slash and no trailing slash**."," ","-**First, untrack the vendored package (AMEND-01).** Four skills — `claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review` — are one third-party package in `~/.agents/vendor-review/claudex-loop/`, linked into all three trees. They are **already committed to this repo as mode-120000 symlinks and pushed**, which is the exact R3 breakage the plan exists to prevent, already live: Windows pulls four links pointing at a path that does not exist there.","-","-They are not ours to vendor — same rule as plugin skills. Untrack them and ignore them; the working tree is untouched and they keep working on this Mac.","+> A trailing slash matches directories only, and git does not treat a symlink as a directory — `/anti-sleep/` would match nothing, and the next `git add -A` would silently re-add all 19. This repo has two such writers: Step 3 below, and `daily-backup.ps1` via `Sync-Repo`."," "," ```bash"," cd ~/.claude/skills","-git rm --cached claudex-loop claudex-route codex-build codex-review","-cat >> .gitignore <<'EOF'","-","-# Vendored third-party package: ~/.agents/vendor-review/claudex-loop/","-# These four are SYMLINKS into it, linked into .claude/.agents/.codex alike.","-# Committing them published mode-120000 entries that are dead on Windows.","-# NOTE: no trailing slash. A trailing slash matches directories ONLY, and","-# git does not treat a symlink as a directory - `/claudex-loop/` would not","-# match, and the next `git add -A` (this repo has two: Task 4 below, and","-# daily-backup.ps1 via Sync-Repo) would silently re-add all four.","-# Install them per skill `vendored-skill-install`; do not track them here.","-/claudex-loop","-/claudex-route","-/codex-build","-/codex-review","-EOF","-git status --short | head","+while IFS= read -r s; do","+  printf '%-28s ignored=%s ondisk=%s\\n' \"$s\" \\","+    \"$(git check-ignore -q \"$s\" && echo yes || echo NO)\" \\","+    \"$(ls -ld \"$s\" | cut -c1)\"","+done < /tmp/tracked-links.txt"," ```"," ","-Expected: four `D` (deleted-from-index) lines and a modified `.gitignore`. The four must **still exist** on disk — `ls -la ~/.claude/skills/claudex-loop` still shows a link.","-","-**Prove the ignore actually holds (R7-02).** This is the step that catches the trailing-slash trap:","+Expected: `ignored=yes` and `ondisk=l` for all 19. A single `NO` means the pattern is wrong — fix before staging."," ","-```bash","-cd ~/.claude/skills","-for s in claudex-loop claudex-route codex-build codex-review; do","-  printf '%-16s ignored=%s  ' \"$s\" \"$(git check-ignore -q \"$s\" && echo yes || echo NO)\"","-  ls -ld \"$s\" | awk '{print \"ondisk=\" substr($1,1,1)}'","-done","-git add -A","-echo \"--- vendored entries back in the index? (must be empty) ---\"","-git ls-files -s | grep -E 'claudex-loop|claudex-route|codex-build|codex-review'","-```","-","-Expected: `ignored=yes` and `ondisk=l` for all four, and the final list **empty**. An `ignored=NO`, or any entry reappearing after `git add -A`, means the pattern is wrong — fix it before committing, or `daily-backup` will re-publish the dead links on its next run.","+- [ ] **Step 3: Stage, then inspect the index (R2-03)**"," ","-**Now stage, then inspect the index (R2-03).** Round 2 caught the earlier ordering: `git ls-files` reads the *index*, and the index still held the old symlink entries until a `git add` replaced them. Checking before staging proved nothing.","+`git ls-files` reads the *index*, so it must be checked **after** staging, not before:"," "," ```bash"," cd ~/.claude/skills"]},{"oldStart":1083,"oldLines":62,"newStart":1001,"newLines":52,"lines":[" echo \"--- staged symlinks (mode 120000) - MUST be empty ---\""," git ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"'"," echo \"--- staged summary ---\"","-git diff --cached --stat | tail -5","-echo \"--- staged type changes (link -> real file) ---\"","-git diff --cached --summary | grep -E 'mode change|delete mode 120000' | head -20","+git diff --cached --stat | tail -3"," ```"," ","-Expected: the `120000` list prints **nothing**; the summary shows the inversions as `delete mode 120000` paired with new real files, plus the four vendored removals. If any `120000` entry is still staged, run `git reset` and stop — committing it would send a Mac symlink to Windows, which is R3.","-","-> **15 inverted, not 19.** Of the 19 outward links, four (`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review`) are the vendored package and are reported `VENDORED ... left alone` by the script, then untracked above. So expect `inverted: 15  skipped: 4` and `symlinks left in canonical: 4` — those four remain as working links on this Mac, now correctly invisible to git.","+Expected: the `120000` list prints **nothing**; the summary shows 19 deletions plus the `.gitignore` change. If any `120000` entry survives, run `git reset` and stop — committing one sends a Mac symlink to Windows."," ","-- [ ] **Step 5: Verify `_shared` consumers still resolve (the R2 check)**","+- [ ] **Step 4: Verify the owned roster is intact and `_shared` still resolves**"," "," ```bash","-test -f ~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared in canonical OK\"","+echo \"owned real dirs with SKILL.md (expect 42):\"","+find ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type d ! -path ~/.claude/skills -exec test -f {}/SKILL.md \\; -print | wc -l","+echo \"third-party links (expect 19):\"","+find ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l","+echo \"total resolvable SKILL.md (expect 61):\"","+find -L ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l","+echo \"--- dangling links (must be empty) ---\"","+find ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print","+test -f ~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared OK\""," python3 -c \""," import pathlib"," p = pathlib.Path.home()/'.claude/skills/meeting-sync/scripts/sync.py'","-if not p.exists():","-    print('meeting-sync/scripts/sync.py not found - check path'); raise SystemExit"," cfg = p.resolve().parents[2]/'_shared/config.json'","-print('resolves to:', cfg)","-print('exists:', cfg.exists())","+print('meeting-sync resolves _shared:', cfg.exists())"," \""," ```"," ","-Expected: `_shared in canonical OK`, and `exists: True`. If `False`, the `parents[2]` hop no longer lands on `_shared` — fix the path in `sync.py` before committing.","-","-- [ ] **Step 6: Re-run the sync guard now that the layout changed**","-","-```bash","-DRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"","-```","-","-Expected: `would sync` lines and `exit=0` — **not** `FATAL`. A FATAL here means a `SHARED` entry is still a symlink and Step 3 did not finish.","+Expected: `42`, `19`, `61`, no dangling output, `_shared OK`, and `True`. The `True` is the R2 check: 10+ skills reach `_shared` through `parents[2]`."," ","-- [ ] **Step 7: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**","+- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile the pool copies that already drifted (R2-01)**"," ","-Before the views are regenerated, the existing pool copies must be checked — regenerating overwrites them, and two of them contain edits that exist nowhere else. Verified on disk today: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **differ** between canonical and pool; `backup` and 7 others are **absent** from the pool entirely.","+Two owned skills have pool copies that differ from canonical, and the publish in Step 6 overwrites them. Verified on disk: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` **differ**; `backup` and 7 others are **absent** from the pool."," "," ```bash"," mkdir -p ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12","-echo \"=== canonical skills whose pool copy DIFFERS ===\"","+echo \"=== owned skills whose pool copy DIFFERS ===\""," for d in ~/.claude/skills/*/; do","   s=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"","+  [ -L \"${d%/}\" ] && continue","   [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ] || continue","   b=~/.agents/skills/\"$s\"","   if [ -e \"$b\" ] && [ ! -L \"$b\" ] && ! diff -rq \"$d\" \"$b\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then","     echo \"DIVERGED $s\"","   fi"," done","-echo \"=== canonical skills ABSENT from the pool ===\"","-comm -23 <(ls ~/.claude/skills | sort) <(ls ~/.agents/skills | sort)"," ```"," ","-Expected: at least `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` under DIVERGED, and 8 names under ABSENT.","-","-For **each** DIVERGED name, look at the actual difference and decide which side wins — then back up the pool copy before it is overwritten:","+For each DIVERGED name, read the diff and decide which side wins, backing up the pool copy first:"," "," ```bash"," for s in memory-write meeting-sync; do"]},{"oldStart":1149,"oldLines":60,"newStart":1057,"newLines":61,"lines":[" ls ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/"," ```"," ","-Read each diff. If the pool copy is newer or better, copy that content **into canonical** (`cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/`) and commit it there. If canonical wins, do nothing — the sync will overwrite the pool. **Do not skip reading the diffs**; regenerating discards whatever you did not move. The `pre-sync-2026-09-12/` backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong.","+If the pool copy is better, `cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/` and commit it in canonical. If canonical wins, do nothing. **Do not skip reading the diffs** — the publish discards whatever you did not move. The backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong."," ","-The ABSENT names need no action: the new complete-manifest sync publishes them automatically. That is the bug the manifest fixes.","+The ABSENT names need no action: the complete-manifest publish covers them automatically."," ","-- [ ] **Step 8: Publish the views and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**","+- [ ] **Step 6: Publish, and prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**"," "," ```bash"," DRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"dry exit=$?\""," bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real exit=$?\""," "," MAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex","-echo \"--- manifest size ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"","+echo \"--- manifest size (expect 43) ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\""," "," echo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\""," while IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\""," echo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\""," while IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"","-","-echo \"--- managed links that do not resolve to canonical (must be empty) ---\"","+echo \"--- managed links not resolving to canonical (must be empty) ---\""," while IFS= read -r s; do","   t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"","   [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\""," done < \"$MAN\""," ```"," ","-Expected: both `exit=0`; the manifest holds **58** lines; all three MISSING/WRONG-TARGET lists are **empty**.","+Expected: both `exit=0`; the script reports `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`; the manifest holds **43** lines; all three lists **empty**."," ","-> **The three numbers, kept straight (R7-05).** 61 canonical entries hold a `SKILL.md`. Four are the vendored `claudex-loop` package. So: **57 owned skills**, **4 vendored links**, **58 published entries** (57 owned + `_shared`). Every count in Tasks 4, 5 and 6 uses one of those three — if a step expects 61 or 62, it is stale.","+> **The numbers, kept straight.** 61 resolvable `SKILL.md` in canonical = **42 owned** + **19 third-party links**. Published = **43** (42 owned + `_shared`). Pool after publish = 208 pruned entries reconciled with the 43 managed. Any step expecting 57, 58, 61 or 62 is stale."," ","-> **R3-06:** success is measured against the **manifest**, not against `ls ~/.claude/skills`. The repo legitimately also contains `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view. Comparing raw directory listings would report those as permanent failures.","+Success is measured against the **manifest**, never against `ls ~/.claude/skills`: the repo also holds `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1` and `CLAUDE.md`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view."," ","-- [ ] **Step 9: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**","+- [ ] **Step 7: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**"," ","-Run `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61). If it dropped, roll back per Task 1 Path 1.","+Run `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61 — untracking changes git, not what the harness reads from disk). If it dropped, roll back per **Task 1, PHASE A**."," "," ```bash"," cd ~/.claude/skills"," git add -A"," git status --short | head","-git commit -m \"refactor: canonical repo holds real directories, no symlinks","+git commit -m \"chore: stop tracking third-party skill symlinks"," ","-19 skills whose content lived in ~/.agents/skills are now inside the repo,","-so they version and reach Windows. The views link back to them.","+All 19 outward links in this repo are third-party: 14 skills-CLI installs","+recorded in ~/.agents/.skill-lock.json (five of them mattpocock-skills),","+4 from the vendor-review/claudex-loop package, plus persistent-localhost.","+They were tracked as mode-120000 and pushed, i.e. dead links on Windows."," ","-Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"","-git push","-cd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS && git add scripts/skills-canonicalize.sh && git commit -m \"feat: symlink inversion script","+They stay on disk and keep working here; the repo now holds only skills","+written here. sync-to-codex.sh regenerates the ignore block on every run,","+so a future \\`npx skills add\\` cannot get its link committed."," "," Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"","+git push"," ```"," "," ---"," ","----"," ### Task 5: Normalize every skill to portable frontmatter"," "," **Files:**"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bdb50d28-e81b-4a73-a120-95f5e5b68ac4","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
