{"parentUuid":"d5b6a679-ea4d-482e-a04a-3bc784144fbe","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["<context_guidance>\n  <tip>\n    Reading to Edit the file? Read is correct — Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against.\n    Reading to analyze, summarize, or extract from the file? Use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code) — the bytes stay in the sandbox and only what your code prints enters your conversation.\n  </tip>\n</context_guidance>"],"hookName":"PreToolUse:Read","toolUseID":"toolu_01Bw6Q4MXSLSfj6nBT2Wygt6","hookEvent":"PreToolUse"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d60a5d20-b6ed-4bb9-9b13-31b86a547a1f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:18:10.753Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPreToolUse:Read hook additional context: <context_guidance>\n  <tip>\n    Reading to Edit the file? Read is correct — Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against.\n    Reading to analyze, summarize, or extract from the file? Use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code) — the bytes stay in the sandbox and only what your code prints enters your conversation.\n  </tip>\n</context_guidance>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9ae5a660-0eab-41b7-bc15-1c9337e236f9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d90457fc-55a4-4c91-beb9-bfaecc9c0aa3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bw6Q4MXSLSfj6nBT2Wygt6","type":"tool_result","content":"668\t- [ ] **Step 3: Give the PowerShell twin the same semantics, not just the guard**\n669\t\n670\t`dev-sync` invokes this script on Windows. An earlier draft bolted a reparse-point guard onto the untouched seven-name loop — which would have left Windows with the old partial views and no manifest, so the audit's drift check could never run there (R3-03). The twin needs the **same** complete enumeration, manifest, validated retirement and ownership semantics. Windows copies rather than links (symlinks need elevation).\n671\t\n672\tReplace the body of `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1` with:\n673\t\n674\t```powershell\n675\t# sync-to-codex.ps1 -- Windows twin of sync-to-codex.sh.\n676\t# Rebuilds the Codex and agent-pool VIEWS from the canonical repo by COPY.\n677\t# Same contract as the bash version: complete manifest, ownership file,\n678\t# validated retirement, refuse-on-link guard.\n679\t$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n680\t\n681\t$SRC          = Join-Path $HOME '.claude\\skills'\n682\t$SUPPORT      = @('_shared')\n683\t$MANIFESTNAME = '.generated-by-sync-to-codex'\n684\t# R7-03: same declared vendor inventory as the bash twin. If the package is\n685\t# installed on Windows per `vendored-skill-install`, these appear as reparse\n686\t# points and the guard below would otherwise fail every dev-sync.\n687\t$VENDORED     = @('claudex-loop','claudex-route','codex-build','codex-review')\n688\t$VENDORROOT   = Join-Path $HOME '.agents\\vendor-review'\n689\t$DRY          = $env:DRY_RUN -eq '1'\n690\t$ARCHIVE_ROOT = Join-Path $HOME (\".agents\\skills-archive\\retired-\" + (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd'))\n691\t\n692\tfunction Test-IsLink($p) {\n693\t  (Test-Path -LiteralPath $p) -and\n694\t  ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $p -Force).Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint)\n695\t}\n696\t\n697\t# Complete manifest: every canonical dir with a SKILL.md, plus support dirs.\n698\t$MANAGED = @()\n699\tGet-ChildItem -LiteralPath $SRC -Directory -Force | ForEach-Object {\n700\t  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }\n701\t  # R7-03: skip ONLY declared vendored names, after verifying the target.\n702\t  if ($VENDORED -contains $_.Name) {\n703\t    $p = Join-Path $SRC $_.Name\n704\t    if (-not (Test-IsLink $p)) {\n705\t      Write-Error \"FATAL '$($_.Name)' is declared vendored but is a real directory.\"\n706\t      exit 2\n707\t    }\n708\t    $real = (Get-Item -LiteralPath $p -Force).Target\n709\t    if ($real -and -not (\"$real\".StartsWith(\"$VENDORROOT\"))) {\n710\t      Write-Error \"FATAL vendored '$($_.Name)' resolves to '$real', outside $VENDORROOT.\"\n711\t      exit 2\n712\t    }\n713\t    Write-Host \"vendored: skipping $($_.Name)\"\n714\t    return\n715\t  }\n716\t  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md')) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }\n717\t}\n718\tforeach ($s in $SUPPORT) {\n719\t  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $MANAGED += $s }\n720\t}\n721\t\n722\tif ($MANAGED.Count -eq 0) {\n723\t  Write-Error \"FATAL no skills found under $SRC - refusing to wipe the views.\"\n724\t  exit 2\n725\t}\n726\t\n727\t# R1 GUARD: every NON-vendored canonical entry must be a real directory.\n728\t# Vendored names never reach here, so they cannot wave others past the guard.\n729\t$bad = @()\n730\tforeach ($s in $MANAGED) {\n731\t  if (Test-IsLink (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $bad += $s }\n732\t}\n733\tif ($bad.Count -gt 0) {\n734\t  foreach ($s in $bad) { Write-Error \"FATAL $SRC\\$s is a link. Canonical must be a real directory.\" }\n735\t  Write-Error \"Refusing to sync; this would delete the link targets. No changes made.\"\n736\t  exit 2\n737\t}\n738\t\n739\tWrite-Host \"canonical manifest: $($MANAGED.Count) entries\"\n740\t\n741\tforeach ($dst in @((Join-Path $HOME '.agents\\skills'), (Join-Path $HOME '.codex\\skills'))) {\n742\t  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $dst | Out-Null\n743\t  $manifestPath = Join-Path $dst $MANIFESTNAME\n744\t\n745\t  # Retire entries no longer managed. R3-02: validate each line is a plain\n746\t  # name before it reaches Remove-Item, and archive before removing.\n747\t  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $manifestPath) {\n748\t    # R4-01: EVERY manifest-derived filesystem call uses -LiteralPath, and\n749\t    # wildcard metacharacters are refused before any mutation. Without this a\n750\t    # manifest line of '*' passes a separator check and then expands inside\n751\t    # Remove-Item's wildcard-aware -Path, wiping third-party entries and the\n752\t    # Codex .system assets.\n753\t    foreach ($old in (Get-Content -LiteralPath $manifestPath)) {\n754\t      $old = $old.Trim()\n755\t      if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($old)) { continue }\n756\t      if ($old -match '[\\\\/]' -or $old -match '[\\*\\?\\[\\]]' -or\n757\t          $old.StartsWith('.') -or $old.StartsWith('-') -or $old -eq '..') {\n758\t        Write-Warning \"REFUSE manifest entry '$old' is not a plain name - ignored\"; continue\n759\t      }\n760\t      if ($MANAGED -contains $old) { continue }\n761\t\n762\t      $target = Join-Path $dst $old\n763\t      # R5-01: Test-Path is false for a dangling reparse point. Fall back to\n764\t      # a directory-entry lookup so an abandoned link is still retired rather\n765\t      # than left behind as untracked debris.\n766\t      $exists = (Test-Path -LiteralPath $target) -or\n767\t                ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $target -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) -ne $null)\n768\t      if (-not $exists) { continue }\n769\t\n770\t      # Containment: the item's real parent must be this view, and the\n771\t      # retirement must affect exactly one immediate child.\n772\t      $item = Get-Item -LiteralPath $target -Force\n773\t      if ($item.Parent.FullName -ne (Get-Item -LiteralPath $dst).FullName) {\n774\t        Write-Warning \"REFUSE '$old' does not resolve to an immediate child of $dst - ignored\"; continue\n775\t      }\n776\t\n777\t      Write-Host \"retire $old from $dst (no longer in canonical)\"\n778\t      if (-not $DRY) {\n779\t        # R4-02: per-view archive dir, and archival must SUCCEED first.\n780\t        # Strip the leading dot so the archive is not a hidden directory.\n781\t        $viewTag = ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $dst).Parent.Name) -replace '^\\.', ''\n782\t        $adir    = Join-Path $ARCHIVE_ROOT $viewTag\n783\t        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $adir | Out-Null\n784\t        $adest = Join-Path $adir $old\n785\t        if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $adest) {\n786\t          Write-Error \"FATAL archive collision at $adest - refusing to delete\"; exit 3\n787\t        }\n788\t        try {\n789\t          Copy-Item -LiteralPath $target -Destination $adest -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction Stop\n790\t        } catch {\n791\t          Write-Error \"FATAL archive of '$old' failed - refusing to delete: $_\"; exit 3\n792\t        }\n793\t        if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $adest)) {\n794\t          Write-Error \"FATAL archive of '$old' not readable back - refusing to delete\"; exit 3\n795\t        }\n796\t        Remove-Item -LiteralPath $target -Recurse -Force\n797\t      }\n798\t    }\n799\t  }\n800\t\n801\t  foreach ($s in $MANAGED) {\n802\t    if ($DRY) { Write-Host \"would sync $s -> $dst (copy)\"; continue }\n803\t    $target = Join-Path $dst $s\n804\t    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $target) { Remove-Item -LiteralPath $target -Recurse -Force }\n805\t    Copy-Item -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC $s) -Destination $target -Recurse -Force\n806\t  }\n807\t\n808\t  if (-not $DRY) {\n809\t    Set-Content -LiteralPath $manifestPath -Value $MANAGED\n810\t    Write-Host \"synced $($MANAGED.Count) entries -> $dst (copy); manifest written\"\n811\t  }\n812\t}\n813\t\n814\tif ($DRY) { Write-Host \"(DRY RUN - set DRY_RUN=1 cleared to apply)\" }\n815\texit 0\n816\t```\n817\t\n818\t- [ ] **Step 3b: Syntax-check the twin on this Mac**\n819\t\n820\t`pwsh` is installed (`/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) specifically to run KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs, so the parse can be checked here even though the script is for Windows:\n821\t\n822\t```bash\n823\tpwsh -NoProfile -Command '\n824\t  $ErrorActionPreference=\"Stop\"\n825\t  $t = Get-Content -Raw ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1\n826\t  $errs = $null\n827\t  [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseInput($t, [ref]$null, [ref]$errs) | Out-Null\n828\t  if ($errs.Count) { $errs | ForEach-Object { $_.Message }; exit 1 } else { \"parse OK\"; exit 0 }\n829\t'; echo \"exit=$?\"\n830\t```\n831\t\n832\tExpected: `parse OK` and `exit=0`. Do **not** run the script itself on the Mac — it would overwrite the Mac views with copies instead of links. Its behaviour is verified on Windows when Tasks 2–5 are repeated there.\n833\t\n834\t- [ ] **Step 4: Prove the guard fires — the whole point of this task**\n835\t\n836\t```bash\n837\t# Build a fake inverted layout in a scratch HOME and confirm the script refuses.\n838\trm -rf /tmp/syncguard && mkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/{.claude/skills,.agents/skills,.codex/skills}\n839\tmkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/startup\n840\techo \"canary - must survive\" > /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/startup/SKILL.md\n841\tln -s /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/startup /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/startup\n842\tHOME=/tmp/syncguard bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n843\tcat /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/startup/SKILL.md\n844\t```\n845\t\n846\tExpected: `FATAL ... is a symlink`, `exit=2`, and the canary file **still readable**. If the canary is gone, the guard does not work — stop and fix before any other task.\n847\t\n848\t- [ ] **Step 4b: Prove the canonical-deletion workflow leaves no debris (R5-01)**\n849\t\n850\tThis is the normal path after someone deletes a skill and `dev-sync` pulls it. Round 5 caught that the generated link goes dangling, `-e` reads false, and the entry gets silently dropped from the manifest — leaving permanent untracked debris the audit could not see.\n851\t\n852\t```bash\n853\trm -rf /tmp/delsync && mkdir -p /tmp/delsync/{.claude/skills,.agents/skills,.codex/skills}\n854\tfor s in keeper goner; do\n855\t  mkdir -p /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/$s\n856\t  printf -- '---\\nname: %s\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\nbody\\n' \"$s\" \\\n857\t    > /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/$s/SKILL.md\n858\tdone\n859\t\n860\t# First sync publishes both.\n861\tHOME=/tmp/delsync bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh >/dev/null\n862\tls -la /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills | grep -c goner\n863\t\n864\t# Simulate the upstream deletion, then sync again.\n865\trm -rf /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/goner\n866\tHOME=/tmp/delsync bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n867\t\n868\techo \"--- dangling links left behind (must be 0) ---\"\n869\tfind /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills /tmp/delsync/.codex/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print | wc -l\n870\techo \"--- goner archived, as a link, once per view ---\"\n871\tls -la /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills-archive/retired-*/agents/ | grep goner\n872\tls -la /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills-archive/retired-*/codex/  | grep goner\n873\techo \"--- manifest no longer claims goner ---\"\n874\tgrep -c '^goner$' /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex || true\n875\techo \"--- keeper still points at canonical ---\"\n876\treadlink /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills/keeper\n877\t```\n878\t\n879\tExpected: `1` (published first time); `exit=0`; **`0` dangling links**; a `goner` symlink in **both** `retired-<date>/agents/` and `retired-<date>/codex/`; `0` occurrences in the manifest; and `keeper` resolving to `/tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/keeper`.\n880\t\n881\tA non-zero dangling count means the `-e || -L` fix is not in — stop and fix, because this is the routine deletion path, not an edge case. Two separate archive directories is the R4-02 fix working: one shared path would have deleted the second view's copy unarchived.\n882\t\n883\t> This exact test was run against the script above before the plan was finalized. Results: `0` dangling, `goner` archived as a symlink in both per-view directories, `0` manifest occurrences, `keeper` correctly linked.\n884\t\n885\t- [ ] **Step 5: Confirm the guard refuses the CURRENT layout — and that this is correct**\n886\t\n887\t```bash\n888\tDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 2)\"\n889\t```\n890\t\n891\tExpected: `vendored: skipping ...` for the four declared vendored names, then a list of `FATAL ... is a symlink` lines naming the **15** other outward links (`anti-sleep`, `handoff`, `scroll-craft`, …), and `exit=2`. The vendored four are skipped *before* the guard and must **not** appear in the FATAL list — if they do, the `is_vendored()` allowlist is not being consulted.\n892\t\n893\t**This is the correct result, not a failure.** Round 3 caught a deadlock here: an earlier draft demanded a *successful* sync at this point, but the guard this task installs deliberately rejects outward canonical symlinks, and only Task 4 removes them. Requiring both made the two tasks impossible to run in either order.\n894\t\n895\tThe order is now: **install and prove the guard (Task 3) → canonicalize (Task 4) → reconcile and publish (Task 4, Steps 8–10).** No real sync runs until the layout the guard demands actually exists.\n896\t\n897\t> If this prints `exit=0` instead, the manifest loop is not seeing the outward links — that means the guard would not have protected anything. Stop and fix.\n898\t\n899\t- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n900\t\n901\t```bash\n902\tgrep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20\n903\techo \"--- staged/modified in canonical ---\"\n904\tgit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short\n905\t```\n906\t\n907\tExpected: `git status` shows **exactly** `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` as modified, **and nothing else**. Round 2 caught the earlier wording, which demanded a clean tree at a point where this task has deliberately just edited two tracked files. What matters is that no *unexpected* path appears, especially not a symlink inside the repo.\n908\t\n909\t- [ ] **Step 7: Commit both copies**\n910\t\n911\t```bash\n912\tcd ~/.claude/skills\n913\tgit add sync-to-codex.sh sync-to-codex.ps1\n914\tgit commit -m \"fix: generate complete views from canonical; refuse symlinked sources\n915\t\n916\tDelete-then-copy destroyed the link target when ~/.claude/skills/<name>\n917\tpointed into ~/.agents/skills (R1). Views are now generated from the full\n918\tcanonical manifest rather than a 7-name allowlist (R2-01), with manifest\n919\tentries validated as plain basenames before any removal (R3-02).\n920\t\n921\tCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n922\tgit push\n923\t```\n924\t\n925\t---\n926\t\n927\t### Task 4: Untrack the third-party links, then publish the views"}]},"uuid":"6627cd6f-672f-484a-ae6b-3c186c394416","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:18:10.854Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","content":"- [ ] **Step 3: Give the PowerShell twin the same semantics, not just the guard**\n\n`dev-sync` invokes this script on Windows. An earlier draft bolted a reparse-point guard onto the untouched seven-name loop — which would have left Windows with the old partial views and no manifest, so the audit's drift check could never run there (R3-03). The twin needs the **same** complete enumeration, manifest, validated retirement and ownership semantics. Windows copies rather than links (symlinks need elevation).\n\nReplace the body of `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1` with:\n\n```powershell\n# sync-to-codex.ps1 -- Windows twin of sync-to-codex.sh.\n# Rebuilds the Codex and agent-pool VIEWS from the canonical repo by COPY.\n# Same contract as the bash version: complete manifest, ownership file,\n# validated retirement, refuse-on-link guard.\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\n$SRC          = Join-Path $HOME '.claude\\skills'\n$SUPPORT      = @('_shared')\n$MANIFESTNAME = '.generated-by-sync-to-codex'\n# R7-03: same declared vendor inventory as the bash twin. If the package is\n# installed on Windows per `vendored-skill-install`, these appear as reparse\n# points and the guard below would otherwise fail every dev-sync.\n$VENDORED     = @('claudex-loop','claudex-route','codex-build','codex-review')\n$VENDORROOT   = Join-Path $HOME '.agents\\vendor-review'\n$DRY          = $env:DRY_RUN -eq '1'\n$ARCHIVE_ROOT = Join-Path $HOME (\".agents\\skills-archive\\retired-\" + (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd'))\n\nfunction Test-IsLink($p) {\n  (Test-Path -LiteralPath $p) -and\n  ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $p -Force).Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint)\n}\n\n# Complete manifest: every canonical dir with a SKILL.md, plus support dirs.\n$MANAGED = @()\nGet-ChildItem -LiteralPath $SRC -Directory -Force | ForEach-Object {\n  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }\n  # R7-03: skip ONLY declared vendored names, after verifying the target.\n  if ($VENDORED -contains $_.Name) {\n    $p = Join-Path $SRC $_.Name\n    if (-not (Test-IsLink $p)) {\n      Write-Error \"FATAL '$($_.Name)' is declared vendored but is a real directory.\"\n      exit 2\n    }\n    $real = (Get-Item -LiteralPath $p -Force).Target\n    if ($real -and -not (\"$real\".StartsWith(\"$VENDORROOT\"))) {\n      Write-Error \"FATAL vendored '$($_.Name)' resolves to '$real', outside $VENDORROOT.\"\n      exit 2\n    }\n    Write-Host \"vendored: skipping $($_.Name)\"\n    return\n  }\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md')) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }\n}\nforeach ($s in $SUPPORT) {\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $MANAGED += $s }\n}\n\nif ($MANAGED.Count -eq 0) {\n  Write-Error \"FATAL no skills found under $SRC - refusing to wipe the views.\"\n  exit 2\n}\n\n# R1 GUARD: every NON-vendored canonical entry must be a real directory.\n# Vendored names never reach here, so they cannot wave others past the guard.\n$bad = @()\nforeach ($s in $MANAGED) {\n  if (Test-IsLink (Join-Path $SRC $s)) { $bad += $s }\n}\nif ($bad.Count -gt 0) {\n  foreach ($s in $bad) { Write-Error \"FATAL $SRC\\$s is a link. Canonical must be a real directory.\" }\n  Write-Error \"Refusing to sync; this would delete the link targets. No changes made.\"\n  exit 2\n}\n\nWrite-Host \"canonical manifest: $($MANAGED.Count) entries\"\n\nforeach ($dst in @((Join-Path $HOME '.agents\\skills'), (Join-Path $HOME '.codex\\skills'))) {\n  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $dst | Out-Null\n  $manifestPath = Join-Path $dst $MANIFESTNAME\n\n  # Retire entries no longer managed. R3-02: validate each line is a plain\n  # name before it reaches Remove-Item, and archive before removing.\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $manifestPath) {\n    # R4-01: EVERY manifest-derived filesystem call uses -LiteralPath, and\n    # wildcard metacharacters are refused before any mutation. Without this a\n    # manifest line of '*' passes a separator check and then expands inside\n    # Remove-Item's wildcard-aware -Path, wiping third-party entries and the\n    # Codex .system assets.\n    foreach ($old in (Get-Content -LiteralPath $manifestPath)) {\n      $old = $old.Trim()\n      if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($old)) { continue }\n      if ($old -match '[\\\\/]' -or $old -match '[\\*\\?\\[\\]]' -or\n          $old.StartsWith('.') -or $old.StartsWith('-') -or $old -eq '..') {\n        Write-Warning \"REFUSE manifest entry '$old' is not a plain name - ignored\"; continue\n      }\n      if ($MANAGED -contains $old) { continue }\n\n      $target = Join-Path $dst $old\n      # R5-01: Test-Path is false for a dangling reparse point. Fall back to\n      # a directory-entry lookup so an abandoned link is still retired rather\n      # than left behind as untracked debris.\n      $exists = (Test-Path -LiteralPath $target) -or\n                ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $target -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) -ne $null)\n      if (-not $exists) { continue }\n\n      # Containment: the item's real parent must be this view, and the\n      # retirement must affect exactly one immediate child.\n      $item = Get-Item -LiteralPath $target -Force\n      if ($item.Parent.FullName -ne (Get-Item -LiteralPath $dst).FullName) {\n        Write-Warning \"REFUSE '$old' does not resolve to an immediate child of $dst - ignored\"; continue\n      }\n\n      Write-Host \"retire $old from $dst (no longer in canonical)\"\n      if (-not $DRY) {\n        # R4-02: per-view archive dir, and archival must SUCCEED first.\n        # Strip the leading dot so the archive is not a hidden directory.\n        $viewTag = ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $dst).Parent.Name) -replace '^\\.', ''\n        $adir    = Join-Path $ARCHIVE_ROOT $viewTag\n        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $adir | Out-Null\n        $adest = Join-Path $adir $old\n        if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $adest) {\n          Write-Error \"FATAL archive collision at $adest - refusing to delete\"; exit 3\n        }\n        try {\n          Copy-Item -LiteralPath $target -Destination $adest -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction Stop\n        } catch {\n          Write-Error \"FATAL archive of '$old' failed - refusing to delete: $_\"; exit 3\n        }\n        if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $adest)) {\n          Write-Error \"FATAL archive of '$old' not readable back - refusing to delete\"; exit 3\n        }\n        Remove-Item -LiteralPath $target -Recurse -Force\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  foreach ($s in $MANAGED) {\n    if ($DRY) { Write-Host \"would sync $s -> $dst (copy)\"; continue }\n    $target = Join-Path $dst $s\n    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $target) { Remove-Item -LiteralPath $target -Recurse -Force }\n    Copy-Item -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC $s) -Destination $target -Recurse -Force\n  }\n\n  if (-not $DRY) {\n    Set-Content -LiteralPath $manifestPath -Value $MANAGED\n    Write-Host \"synced $($MANAGED.Count) entries -> $dst (copy); manifest written\"\n  }\n}\n\nif ($DRY) { Write-Host \"(DRY RUN - set DRY_RUN=1 cleared to apply)\" }\nexit 0\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3b: Syntax-check the twin on this Mac**\n\n`pwsh` is installed (`/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) specifically to run KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs, so the parse can be checked here even though the script is for Windows:\n\n```bash\npwsh -NoProfile -Command '\n  $ErrorActionPreference=\"Stop\"\n  $t = Get-Content -Raw ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.ps1\n  $errs = $null\n  [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseInput($t, [ref]$null, [ref]$errs) | Out-Null\n  if ($errs.Count) { $errs | ForEach-Object { $_.Message }; exit 1 } else { \"parse OK\"; exit 0 }\n'; echo \"exit=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `parse OK` and `exit=0`. Do **not** run the script itself on the Mac — it would overwrite the Mac views with copies instead of links. Its behaviour is verified on Windows when Tasks 2–5 are repeated there.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Prove the guard fires — the whole point of this task**\n\n```bash\n# Build a fake inverted layout in a scratch HOME and confirm the script refuses.\nrm -rf /tmp/syncguard && mkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/{.claude/skills,.agents/skills,.codex/skills}\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/startup\necho \"canary - must survive\" > /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/startup/SKILL.md\nln -s /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/startup /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/startup\nHOME=/tmp/syncguard bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\ncat /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/startup/SKILL.md\n```\n\nExpected: `FATAL ... is a symlink`, `exit=2`, and the canary file **still readable**. If the canary is gone, the guard does not work — stop and fix before any other task.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4b: Prove the canonical-deletion workflow leaves no debris (R5-01)**\n\nThis is the normal path after someone deletes a skill and `dev-sync` pulls it. Round 5 caught that the generated link goes dangling, `-e` reads false, and the entry gets silently dropped from the manifest — leaving permanent untracked debris the audit could not see.\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/delsync && mkdir -p /tmp/delsync/{.claude/skills,.agents/skills,.codex/skills}\nfor s in keeper goner; do\n  mkdir -p /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/$s\n  printf -- '---\\nname: %s\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\nbody\\n' \"$s\" \\\n    > /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/$s/SKILL.md\ndone\n\n# First sync publishes both.\nHOME=/tmp/delsync bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh >/dev/null\nls -la /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills | grep -c goner\n\n# Simulate the upstream deletion, then sync again.\nrm -rf /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/goner\nHOME=/tmp/delsync bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n\necho \"--- dangling links left behind (must be 0) ---\"\nfind /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills /tmp/delsync/.codex/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print | wc -l\necho \"--- goner archived, as a link, once per view ---\"\nls -la /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills-archive/retired-*/agents/ | grep goner\nls -la /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills-archive/retired-*/codex/  | grep goner\necho \"--- manifest no longer claims goner ---\"\ngrep -c '^goner$' /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex || true\necho \"--- keeper still points at canonical ---\"\nreadlink /tmp/delsync/.agents/skills/keeper\n```\n\nExpected: `1` (published first time); `exit=0`; **`0` dangling links**; a `goner` symlink in **both** `retired-<date>/agents/` and `retired-<date>/codex/`; `0` occurrences in the manifest; and `keeper` resolving to `/tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/keeper`.\n\nA non-zero dangling count means the `-e || -L` fix is not in — stop and fix, because this is the routine deletion path, not an edge case. Two separate archive directories is the R4-02 fix working: one shared path would have deleted the second view's copy unarchived.\n\n> This exact test was run against the script above before the plan was finalized. Results: `0` dangling, `goner` archived as a symlink in both per-view directories, `0` manifest occurrences, `keeper` correctly linked.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Confirm the guard refuses the CURRENT layout — and that this is correct**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 2)\"\n```\n\nExpected: `vendored: skipping ...` for the four declared vendored names, then a list of `FATAL ... is a symlink` lines naming the **15** other outward links (`anti-sleep`, `handoff`, `scroll-craft`, …), and `exit=2`. The vendored four are skipped *before* the guard and must **not** appear in the FATAL list — if they do, the `is_vendored()` allowlist is not being consulted.\n\n**This is the correct result, not a failure.** Round 3 caught a deadlock here: an earlier draft demanded a *successful* sync at this point, but the guard this task installs deliberately rejects outward canonical symlinks, and only Task 4 removes them. Requiring both made the two tasks impossible to run in either order.\n\nThe order is now: **install and prove the guard (Task 3) → canonicalize (Task 4) → reconcile and publish (Task 4, Steps 8–10).** No real sync runs until the layout the guard demands actually exists.\n\n> If this prints `exit=0` instead, the manifest loop is not seeing the outward links — that means the guard would not have protected anything. Stop and fix.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n\n```bash\ngrep -n 'skills' ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 | head -20\necho \"--- staged/modified in canonical ---\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills status --short\n```\n\nExpected: `git status` shows **exactly** `sync-to-codex.sh` and `sync-to-codex.ps1` as modified, **and nothing else**. Round 2 caught the earlier wording, which demanded a clean tree at a point where this task has deliberately just edited two tracked files. What matters is that no *unexpected* path appears, especially not a symlink inside the repo.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit both copies**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add sync-to-codex.sh sync-to-codex.ps1\ngit commit -m \"fix: generate complete views from canonical; refuse symlinked sources\n\nDelete-then-copy destroyed the link target when ~/.claude/skills/<name>\npointed into ~/.agents/skills (R1). Views are now generated from the full\ncanonical manifest rather than a 7-name allowlist (R2-01), with manifest\nentries validated as plain basenames before any removal (R3-02).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Untrack the third-party links, then publish the views","numLines":260,"startLine":668,"totalLines":2404}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9ae5a660-0eab-41b7-bc15-1c9337e236f9","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"6627cd6f-672f-484a-ae6b-3c186c394416","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez5ogF38DeFamhLhG7az","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014hy2ET1ANKo7QuAeaxEPQB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"F=docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md\necho \"=== checker ALLOWED / VENDORED / POSITIVE ===\"; grep -n 'ALLOWED = \\|^VENDORED = \\|^POSITIVE = \\|^NEGATIVE = \\|not in VENDORED\\|# Must stay identical' $F\necho \"=== metrics VENDORED/owned ===\"; grep -n 'VENDORED\\|def owned\\|canon_names = \\|vendored_skills\\|vendored_links_in_canonical' $F\necho \"=== cron header check ===\"; grep -n 'if \\[ ! -f \"\\$TREND\" \\]' $F\necho \"=== Task 5 final commit ===\"; grep -n 'chore: portable frontmatter across the roster' $F\necho \"=== Gate B / Gate A satisfied / out of scope claudex ===\"; grep -n 'Gate B — after Task 5\\|Gate A is satisfied\\|Gate A — plan review, SATISFIED\\|The four `claudex-loop` package skills\\|Mining the 414 JSONL' $F\necho \"=== stale counts ===\"; grep -n '\\b57\\b\\|\\b58\\b\\|checked 57\\|manifest holds \\*\\*58\\|roll back per Task 1 Path 1\\|expect ~208\\|near 208' $F","description":"Locate checker, metrics, cron, gates, stale counts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349655,"cache_read_input_tokens":32610,"output_tokens":1875,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1025},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":349655,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1875,"cache_read_input_tokens":32610,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349655,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":349655},"type":"message"}],"speed"