** from `rot.md`. `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical`, `pool_view_drift`, `codex_view_drift`, `pool_dangling` and `codex_dangling` must all be `0`. `vendored_links_in_canonical` is expected to be `4` and is **information, not a finding**. Drift means someone edited a generated view instead of the canonical repo; a dangling count means a deleted canonical skill left an abandoned link behind — both are RED. Report `pool_third_party` and `codex_third_party` as **information**, never as errors — those are deliberately preserved installs.\n1990:  \"$(get date)\" \"$(get canonical_skills)\" \"$(get vendored_skills)\" \\\n=== cron header check ===\n1974:if [ ! -f \"$TREND\" ]; then\n=== Task 5 final commit ===\n1418:cd ~/.claude/skills && git add -A && git commit -m \"chore: portable frontmatter across the roster\n=== Gate B / Gate A satisfied / out of scope claudex ===\n22:**Gate A is satisfied. Task 1 may begin.**\n2377:- [x] **Gate A — plan review, SATISFIED 2026-09-12.** Six rounds, same resumed Codex reviewer session each time so every new plan hash was recorded against it. Final verdict **APPROVED**, 0 findings, artifact `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/codex-review-r6/`. The pattern used each round, for reference when re-reviewing after edits:\n2390:- [ ] **Gate B — after Task 5.** `codex-review` on `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1`, `skills-canonicalize.sh`, `skill-portability-check.py`, and ten rewritten frontmatter blocks. Codex is the right reviewer here specifically because it is the harness whose triggering the rewrite claims to fix.\n2397:- **The four `claudex-loop` package skills** — `claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review`. One vendored third-party package in `~/.agents/vendor-review/claudex-loop/`, linked into all three trees. Same rule as plugins: not ours to rewrite, vendor into the repo, or publish to views. **Windows consequence, stated rather than hidden:** they were *already* broken there — tracked as mode-120000 links to a path that does not exist on that box. Untracking them means the next `dev-sync` pull deletes the dead links. To have them on Windows, install the package separately (see the `vendored-skill-install` skill). Nothing regresses; the breakage stops being silent.\n2403:- Mining the 414 JSONL sessions to reverse-engineer harness behaviour (video gap #9). Real, but its own project.\n=== stale counts ===\n220:Also assert the vendored package is captured. Four canonical links are a **two-hop chain** — `~/.claude/skills/claudex-loop` → `~/.agents/skills/claudex-loop` → `~/.agents/vendor-review/claudex-loop/skills/claudex-loop`. That vendor directory sits outside `.agents/skills` and the first draft of this step missed it, producing a count of 57:\n233:Expected: `306`, `32`, `61`, `_shared OK`, `vendor-review OK`, `3ab4467 chore: apply global skill audit`, and **no output** from the separation check. **A count of `57` means `vendor-review` is missing from the tarball** — rebuild it before continuing. If the views archive contains `.claude`, the separation failed — STOP, no later task may run.\n1086:> **The numbers, kept straight.** 61 resolvable `SKILL.md` in canonical = **42 owned** + **19 third-party links**. Published = **43** (42 owned + `_shared`). Pool after publish = 208 pruned entries reconciled with the 43 managed. Any step expecting 57, 58, 61 or 62 is stale.\n1388:Expected: `checked 57 skills, 0 failing, 57 portable` and `exit=0`. **57, not 61** — the checker skips the four vendored skills (R7-05).\n1800:| `canonical_skills` | `57` | the roster we own (61 minus the 4 vendored) |\n2242:Expected: a count near 208, not 306. **If it reads ~306, Task 2 did not take — stop and re-run it.** This step is the proof that pruning the pool was the right fix.\n2333:| skills auto-discovered | FILL IN (expect ~208, not 306) |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"64d49c2a-312f-4e55-be56-8e4039cf8409","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:18:17.784Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== checker ALLOWED / VENDORED