{"parentUuid":"c00878c2-e5a0-4de6-89a7-b93859f2c8ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez5qkR7GFCKmefESFS5Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CU9S2AbuW9A3KMfMEnkdfY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r8.md","content":"# Round 8 dispositions — all eleven ACCEPTED\n\n**R8-01 inverted the Task 4 design. The inversion script (`skills-canonicalize.sh`) is deleted.**\n\nVerified on disk before rewriting: `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` holds 45 entries; 14 of the 19 outward links in `~/.claude/skills` are ledger installs (`davidondrej/skills` ×4, `mattpocock-skills` ×5, `Leonxlnx/taste-skill` ×2, `HKUDS/CLI-Anything`, `nateherkai/scroll-craft`, `bradautomates/claude-video`); the other five are the four `vendor-review/claudex-loop` skills and `persistent-localhost`. `lastSelectedAgents` includes `claude-code`, `codex` and `pi`. `git ls-files -s` shows all 19 tracked as mode 120000. So **none** of the 19 is Eric's own, and Task 4 would have copied fourteen third-party packages into `erash11/claude-skills`.\n\nThe response removes code rather than adding it: ownership became **structural** — a real directory is owned, a symlink is third-party — replacing the `VENDORED` name list in all four places it lived.\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R8-01 | ACCEPTED — design inverted | Task 4 rewritten from \"invert 19 links\" to \"untrack 19 links, then publish\". `skills-canonicalize.sh` deleted from the plan and from Gate B. The `VENDORED` list removed from `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1`, `aios-metrics.py` and `skill-portability-check.py`; each now treats `islink` as third-party. Counts restated once: **42 owned, 43 published (42 + `_shared`), 19 third-party**. Task 4 Step 1 untracks via `git ls-files -s \\| awk '$1==\"120000\"'` so the list is measured, not typed. |\n| R8-02 | ACCEPTED | Two parts. (a) The FATAL-on-any-canonical-symlink guard is gone: a symlink can never enter `MANAGED`, so the R1 danger is impossible by construction and a fresh `npx skills add` no longer breaks `dev-sync`. The one guard kept is precise: a name **in a previous manifest** that is now a link means an owned skill was turned into a link by hand, which is FATAL. (b) The sync script regenerates a marked `.gitignore` block listing every current canonical link on each non-dry run, so new installs are ignored automatically. Residual window (install after the last sync, before a 09:00 backup) recorded in Out of Scope with the `pre-commit` hook as the next step if `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` ever goes non-zero; verified `daily-backup.ps1` does not pass `--no-verify`. |\n| R8-03 | ACCEPTED | Measured keys in use across all 61 `SKILL.md`: `name` 61, `description` 61, `argument-hint` 21, `allowed-tools` 7, `license` 6, `disable-model-invocation` 5, `author` 5, `metadata` 4, `effort` 4, `version` 2, `user-invocable` 2, `repository` 1, `homepage` 1. `effort`, `user-invocable`, `repository`, `homepage` added to `ALLOWED`, with the measuring command in a comment. |\n| R8-04 | ACCEPTED | The `.Target` first-hop comparison no longer exists (vendor-root check deleted with the name list). Both removal sites in the PowerShell twin — retirement and the copy loop — now test `Test-IsLink` first and delete only the link itself via `.Delete()`, never `Remove-Item -Recurse` through a junction. |\n| R8-05 | ACCEPTED as documentation | Not a script. Out of Scope now states that ~30 Task-2-archived names still have ledger entries, that the ledger belongs to the `skills` CLI, and that Eric runs `npx skills remove <name>` or accepts them. No new metric was added: the advisor's instruction this round was to prefer deleting over adding, and a ledger reader would reintroduce the third-party-inventory coupling R8-01 just removed. |\n| R8-06 | ACCEPTED | Line 22 and the Gate A checkbox now say **RE-OPENED**. Review history gains rounds 7 and 8. States that Tasks 1–2 ran under the round-6 approval and that their text is unchanged since (verified: `git diff 09e77f5..HEAD` shows no hunk touching Task 2), and that Task 3 onward waits for a fresh APPROVED. |\n| R8-07 | ACCEPTED | New **Task 3 Step 0** unloads `com.keystone.dailybackup` before any change and says to reload it by hand if the migration is abandoned. New **Task 5 Step 7** reloads it, after asserting `git status` on the skills repo is empty. |\n| R8-08 | ACCEPTED — by deletion | One writer. The `aios-audit` skill body no longer appends to `aios-trend.md`; `aios-audit-cron.sh` is the only writer and keeps its header-on-missing-file logic, which is now correct because nothing else creates the file. The skill commits the cron's waiting row instead. |\n| R8-09 | ACCEPTED | Task 4 Step 5 now lists only DIVERGED owned skills (no raw directory comparison). Rollback reference is \"Task 1, PHASE A\". Task 8's pool expectations read the post-Task-4 `pool_skills` value instead of hard-coding 208. `chmod 700 ~` replaced by a read-only `ls -ld ~` that stops if home is world-readable rather than silently changing permissions. The unverifiable \"`backup` and 7 others\" and \"208 reconciled with 43\" phrasings replaced with non-numeric statements. |\n| R8-10 | ACCEPTED | Clause matching uses `re.finditer` with `\\b` boundaries for both positive and negative phrases; the `when`/`for` span extension also requires a word boundary. New fixture `fragments` (`\"Formats output because formatting matters; output is not formatted twice.\"`) must FAIL for both clauses. |\n| R8-11 | ACCEPTED | PowerShell: new `Stop-Fatal` helper writes to stderr and exits with the intended code; every `Write-Error ...; exit N` replaced, since under `ErrorActionPreference='Stop'` `Write-Error` terminates with exit 1 first. `$KEEP_OWNED` ported — refused retirements stay in the manifest, as in bash. Cron: the nudge directory `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts` is created up front. |\n\n## Additional defect found while applying these\n\nmacOS `/bin/bash` is 3.2, where `\"${arr[@]}\"` on an **empty** array under `set -u` aborts with \"unbound variable\". The new `THIRD_PARTY` loops would crash on any machine or scratch test with zero third-party links. Both loops now use `${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}`.\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11595,"cache_read_input_tokens":382265,"output_tokens":40644,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22608},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11595,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":40644,"cache_read_input_tokens":382265,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11595},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cez5qjCgNSbv7EpphZY2F","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa827f20-dfc0-4f0d-8b2b-996cd4c94ba7","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:24:57.550Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
