{"parentUuid":"e25eda5a-39e8-4484-9eb8-dc129daf1260","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez6RRj9vf8edhB6PTt5P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Three of four checks passed, but I found a test gap (case 2's single-skill fixture masked the real guard) and a blocker (inline `-Command` tripped `dcg` in the PowerShell check). I'll fix the plan's test, re-run case 2 with two owned skills, and rewrite the PowerShell check as a file.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6979,"cache_read_input_tokens":435167,"output_tokens":7029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3537},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":7029,"cache_read_input_tokens":435167,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6979},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cez6RQT1f6UU3jxArgb1y","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e1e296c-b455-4715-b3ec-1b14f4dbf9b4","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:26:36.248Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"4e1e296c-b455-4715-b3ec-1b14f4dbf9b4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez6RRj9vf8edhB6PTt5P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016tW82v9tqhUMQLT8BTTUXH","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","old_string":"# One owned skill, one third-party install.\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/mine\nprintf -- '---\\nname: mine\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/mine/SKILL.md\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/theirs\necho \"canary - must survive\" > /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/theirs/SKILL.md\nln -s ../../.agents/skills/theirs /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/theirs\n\n# CASE 1: the link is skipped, its target survives, .gitignore covers it.\nHOME=/tmp/syncguard bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"case1 exit=$?\"\ncat /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/theirs/SKILL.md\ngit -C /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills check-ignore -q theirs && echo \"theirs ignored\" || echo \"theirs NOT ignored\"\ngit -C /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills check-ignore -q mine   && echo \"mine WRONGLY ignored\" || echo \"mine tracked\"\n\n# CASE 2: an owned, published skill turned into a link must be refused.\nrm -rf /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/mine\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/elsewhere/mine\nln -s /tmp/syncguard/elsewhere/mine /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/mine\nHOME=/tmp/syncguard bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"case2 exit=$? (expect 2)\"\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n- **case 1** — `canonical manifest: 1 entries; third-party links: 1`, `case1 exit=0`, the canary **still readable**, `theirs ignored`, `mine tracked`.\n- **case 2** — `FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill and is now a symlink ...` and `case2 exit=2`.","new_string":"# TWO owned skills and one third-party install. Two, not one: with a single\n# owned skill, CASE 2 empties MANAGED and trips \"no skills found\" first -\n# the right exit code for the wrong reason, with the guard never reached.\n# (Found by actually running this step.)\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/mine /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/other\nprintf -- '---\\nname: mine\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/mine/SKILL.md\nprintf -- '---\\nname: other\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/other/SKILL.md\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/theirs\necho \"canary - must survive\" > /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/theirs/SKILL.md\nln -s ../../.agents/skills/theirs /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/theirs\n\n# CASE 1: the link is skipped, its target survives, .gitignore covers it.\nHOME=/tmp/syncguard /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"case1 exit=$?\"\ncat /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/theirs/SKILL.md\ngit -C /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills check-ignore -q theirs && echo \"theirs ignored\" || echo \"theirs NOT ignored\"\ngit -C /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills check-ignore -q mine   && echo \"mine WRONGLY ignored\" || echo \"mine tracked\"\n\n# CASE 2: an owned, published skill turned into a link must be refused.\nrm -rf /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/mine\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/elsewhere/mine\nln -s /tmp/syncguard/elsewhere/mine /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/mine\nHOME=/tmp/syncguard /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"case2 exit=$? (expect 2)\"\n```\n\nRun with `/bin/bash` on purpose: macOS ships bash 3.2, where an empty array under `set -u` aborts. Homebrew's bash 5 would hide that.\n\nExpected:\n\n- **case 1** — `canonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 1`, `case1 exit=0`, the canary **still readable**, `theirs ignored`, `mine tracked`.\n- **case 2** — `FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill and is now a symlink ...` and `case2 exit=2`. It must be **this** message. `FATAL no skills found` also exits 2, but it means the fixture lost its last owned skill and the guard was never exercised."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6979,"cache_read_input_tokens":435167,"output_tokens":7029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3537},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":7029,"cache_read_input_tokens":435167,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6979},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cez6RQT1f6UU3jxArgb1y","type":"assistant","uuid":"e35a0647-4d59-4156-ba2f-1ab88e5f3ebe","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:26:50.581Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
