published entries** (42 + `_shared`), **19 third-party links**. Nothing needs inverting. The links stay where they are, keep working on this Mac, and stop being tracked by git.\n\nAll 19 are currently tracked as mode-120000 and **already pushed** — dead links on Windows. That is the R3 breakage this plan exists to prevent, live today.\n\n**Order matters (R9-01).** No non-dry sync may run until Step 2 has reconciled the drifted pool copies. A real sync replaces every owned skill's pool entry with a link — `rm -rf` then `ln -s` — so a pool copy holding edits that exist nowhere else is destroyed, and afterwards the divergence check finds only links and reports nothing. Verified on disk before this task: `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` pool copies are real directories that **still differ** from canonical.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Untrack all 19, keeping them on disk**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"{print $4}' > /tmp/tracked-links.txt\nwc -l < /tmp/tracked-links.txt\ncat /tmp/tracked-links.txt\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -L \"$s\" ] || echo \"NOT A LINK: $s\"; done < /tmp/tracked-links.txt\n```\n\nExpected: `19`, the names, and **no** `NOT A LINK` line. A real directory here would be an owned skill that belongs in the index — stop.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit rm --cached --quiet --pathspec-from-file=/tmp/tracked-links.txt\ngit status --short | head -25\n```\n\n`--pathspec-from-file` needs git ≥ 2.26 (this Mac has 2.55). It replaces the earlier `xargs -a`, which is GNU-only and fails on macOS's BSD `xargs` with `illegal option -- a` (R9-05).\n\nExpected: 19 `D` lines. The directories must **still exist** — `ls -la ~/.claude/skills/anti-sleep` still shows a link.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Reconcile the drifted pool copies — BEFORE any real sync (R9-01, R2-01)**\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12\necho \"=== owned skills whose pool copy is a REAL dir that DIFFERS ===\"\nfor d in ~/.claude/skills/*/; do\n  s=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"\n  [ -L \"${d%/}\" ] && continue\n  [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ] || continue\n  b=~/.agents/skills/\"$s\"\n  if [ -d \"$b\" ] && [ ! -L \"$b\" ] && ! diff -rq \"$d\" \"$b\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    echo \"DIVERGED $s\"\n  fi\ndone\n```\n\nExpected: at least `DIVERGED memory-write` and `DIVERGED meeting-sync`. **If this prints nothing, check whether a real sync already ran** (`ls -la ~/.agents/skills/memory-write` showing a link means it did, and the pool-only edits must be recovered from `~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz`).\n\nFor **each** DIVERGED name, back up the pool copy, then read the diff and decide which side wins:\n\n```bash\nfor s in memory-write meeting-sync; do\n  cp -R ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/\"$s\"\n  echo \"===== $s  (-: canonical  +: pool) =====\"\n  diff -ru ~/.claude/skills/\"$s\" ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" | head -60\ndone\nls ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/\n```\n\nIf the pool copy holds edits worth keeping, copy them **into canonical** (`cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/`) — they are then committed with this task. If canonical wins, do nothing. **Do not skip reading the diffs**: Step 3 discards whatever is left only in the pool. The backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: First real sync — publish the views and write the per-machine exclude block**\n\n```bash\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\nsed -n '/BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex/,/END generated-by-sync-to-codex/p' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude\necho \"--- lines outside the block preserved? ---\"\ngrep -v -e 'generated-by-sync-to-codex' -e '^/' -e '^# ' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude || true\ngrep -qx '/.claude/RESUME.md' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude && echo \"pre-existing /.claude/RESUME.md kept\" || echo \"RESUME.md line LOST\"\necho \"--- tracked .gitignore untouched by the sync? ---\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills diff --quiet -- .gitignore && echo \".gitignore unchanged\" || echo \".gitignore MODIFIED\"\n```\n\nExpected: `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, `exit=0`; a block listing all 19 names with a **leading slash and no trailing slash**; `pre-existing /.claude/RESUME.md kept`; `.gitignore unchanged`.\n\n> **Why `.git/info/exclude` and not `.gitignore` (R9-02).** The set of links is per-machine, but `.gitignore` is tracked and shared through `erash11/claude-skills`. Windows' sync would rewrite the block with *its* links — none — the backup would push that, and on the next pull the Mac's 19 links would stop being ignored and get committed again. `info/exclude` is never committed, so each machine keeps its own list.\n>\n> **Why no trailing slash.** A trailing slash matches directories only, and git does not treat a symlink as a directory, so `/anti-sleep/` would match nothing.\n\nProve every link is actually ignored:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do\n  printf '%-28s ignored=%s ondisk=%s\\n' \"$s\" \\\n    \"$(git check-ignore -q \"$s\" && echo yes || echo NO)\" \\\n    \"$(ls -ld \"$s\" | cut -c1)\"\ndone < /tmp/tracked-links.txt\n```\n\nExpected: `ignored=yes` and `ondisk=l` for all 19. A single `NO` means the pattern is wrong — fix before staging.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Stage, then inspect the index (R2-03)**\n\n`git ls-files` reads the *index*, so it is checked **after** staging:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\necho \"--- staged symlinks (mode 120000) - MUST be empty ---\"\ngit ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"'\necho \"--- staged summary ---\"\ngit diff --cached --stat | tail -3\n```\n\nExpected: the `120000` list prints **nothing**; the summary shows 19 deletions plus any content moved into canonical in Step 2 — and **no** `.gitignore` change. If any `120000` entry survives, `git reset` and stop. (The Task 3 pre-commit hook would refuse the commit anyway; this check is so you find out now, not at commit time.)\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Verify the owned roster is intact and `_shared` still resolves**\n\n```bash\necho \"owned real dirs with SKILL.md (expect 42):\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type d ! -path ~/.claude/skills -exec test -f {}/SKILL.md \\; -print | wc -l\necho \"third-party links (expect 19):\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\necho \"total resolvable SKILL.md (expect 61):\"\nfind -L ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\necho \"--- dangling links (must be empty) ---\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print\ntest -f ~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared OK\"\npython3 -c \"\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path.home()/'.claude/skills/meeting-sync/scripts/sync.py'\ncfg = p.resolve().parents[2]/'_shared/config.json'\nprint('meeting-sync resolves _shared:', cfg.exists())\n\"\n```\n\nExpected: `42`, `19`, `61`, no dangling output, `_shared OK`, and `True`. The `True` is the R2 check: 10+ skills reach `_shared` through `parents[2]`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh >/dev/null; echo \"idempotent dry exit=$?\"\nMAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\necho \"--- manifest size (expect 43) ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed links not resolving to canonical (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do\n  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"\ndone < \"$MAN\"\npython3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py 2>/dev/null | grep '^pool_skills=' || echo \"(metrics script not written until Task 6 - count by hand:)\"\nfind -L ~/.agents/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\n```\n\nExpected: `idempotent dry exit=0`; manifest **43** lines; all three lists **empty**. **Record the pool skill count printed last** — Task 8 compares against it.\n\nSuccess is measured against the **manifest**, never against `ls ~/.claude/skills`: the repo also holds `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1` and `CLAUDE.md`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n\nRun `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61 — untracking changes git, not what the harness reads from disk). If it dropped, roll back using **\"TASK 4\" under \"ROLLBACK BY TASK\"** in `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt` — not PHASE A, which predates Task 2 and would restore the 98 pruned skills (R9-04).\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\ngit status --short | head\ngit commit -m \"chore: stop tracking third-party skill symlinks\n\nAll 19 outward links in this repo are third-party: 14 skills-CLI installs\nrecorded in ~/.agents/.skill-lock.json (five of them mattpocock-skills),\n4 from the vendor-review/claudex-loop package, plus persistent-localhost.\nThey were tracked as mode-120000 and pushed, i.e. dead links on Windows.\n\nThey stay on disk and keep working here. Git ignores them through the\nper-machine .git/info/exclude, which sync-to-codex.sh regenerates; the\npre-commit hook refuses any future symlink commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\n```\n\nExpected: the commit succeeds — the hook allows deletions — and the push succeeds.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"62a4fb6a-b76b-447f-8d87-7a93137c8e27","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"6333c759-87cb-48f6-a0e8-0ce9c136c132","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez6z4YrybGEfdUxvqfpA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MaE4XxBJHcMThk8cnKBKRv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/r9-fixes.txt","content":"%%%%OLD%%%%\nMANAGED=()\nTHIRD_PARTY=()\nfor d in \"$SRC\"/*/; do\n  name=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"\n  case \"$name\" in .*) continue ;; esac\n  # A symlink can NEVER enter MANAGED. That makes the original R1 danger\n  # (delete-then-copy destroying a link target) structurally impossible -\n  # no guard needed, because the unsafe case cannot be constructed.\n  if [ -L \"${d%/}\" ]; then\n    THIRD_PARTY+=(\"$name\")\n    continue\n  fi\n  if [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ]; then\n    MANAGED+=(\"$name\")\n  fi\ndone\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nMANAGED=()\nTHIRD_PARTY=()\n# R9-06: glob \"$SRC\"/* with NO trailing slash. \"$SRC\"/*/ matches only links\n# that RESOLVE to directories, so a dangling third-party link was silently\n# left out of the exclude list and the next `git add -A` would commit it.\nfor d in \"$SRC\"/*; do\n  name=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"\n  case \"$name\" in .*) continue ;; esac\n  # A symlink can NEVER enter MANAGED - dangling or not. That makes the\n  # original R1 danger (delete-then-copy destroying a link target)\n  # structurally impossible.\n  if [ -L \"$d\" ]; then\n    THIRD_PARTY+=(\"$name\")\n    [ -e \"$d\" ] || echo \"WARN third-party link '$name' is dangling\" >&2\n    continue\n  fi\n  if [ -d \"$d\" ] && [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ]; then\n    MANAGED+=(\"$name\")\n  fi\ndone\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R8-02: keep .gitignore covering EVERY current canonical symlink, so the\n# next `npx skills add -a claude-code` cannot get its link committed by the\n# daily backup's `git add -A`. Managed as a marked block, rewritten in place.\nGI=\"$SRC/.gitignore\"\nBEGIN=\"# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex: third-party symlinks\"\nEND=\"# END generated-by-sync-to-codex\"\nif [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ]; then\n  tmp=\"$(mktemp)\"\n  if [ -f \"$GI\" ]; then\n    awk -v b=\"$BEGIN\" -v e=\"$END\" '\n      $0==b {skip=1} !skip {print} $0==e {skip=0}' \"$GI\" > \"$tmp\"\n  fi\n  {\n    echo \"$BEGIN\"\n    echo \"# Rewritten on every sync. Do not edit by hand.\"\n    echo \"# No trailing slash: that matches directories only, and git does not\"\n    echo \"# treat a symlink as a directory - the pattern would never match.\"\n    for name in ${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}; do echo \"/$name\"; done\n    echo \"$END\"\n  } >> \"$tmp\"\n  if ! cmp -s \"$tmp\" \"$GI\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    cp \"$tmp\" \"$GI\"\n    echo \"updated $GI (${#THIRD_PARTY[@]} third-party links ignored)\"\n  fi\n  rm -f \"$tmp\"\nfi\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R8-02 + R9-02: keep git from ever seeing the current canonical links, so the\n# daily backup's `git add -A` cannot commit an `npx skills add` link.\n#\n# Written to .git/info/exclude, NOT the tracked .gitignore. The set of links is\n# per-machine, while .gitignore is shared through erash11/claude-skills: each\n# machine's sync would rewrite the other's list, the backup would push it, and\n# the Mac's links would stop being ignored - R3 again. info/exclude is never\n# committed. Lines outside the marked block (e.g. /.claude/RESUME.md) are kept.\n# The pre-commit hook from Task 3 is the backstop for a link installed after\n# the last sync.\nEXCL=\"$SRC/.git/info/exclude\"\nBEGIN=\"# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex: third-party symlinks\"\nEND=\"# END generated-by-sync-to-codex\"\nif [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ] && [ -d \"$SRC/.git\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$SRC/.git/info\"\n  tmp=\"$(mktemp)\"\n  if [ -f \"$EXCL\" ]; then\n    awk -v b=\"$BEGIN\" -v e=\"$END\" '\n      $0==b {skip=1} !skip {print} $0==e {skip=0}' \"$EXCL\" > \"$tmp\"\n  fi\n  {\n    echo \"$BEGIN\"\n    echo \"# Rewritten on every sync. Per-machine. Do not edit by hand.\"\n    echo \"# No trailing slash: that matches directories only, and git does not\"\n    echo \"# treat a symlink as a directory - the pattern would never match.\"\n    for name in ${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}; do echo \"/$name\"; done\n    echo \"$END\"\n  } >> \"$tmp\"\n  if ! cmp -s \"$tmp\" \"$EXCL\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    cp \"$tmp\" \"$EXCL\"\n    echo \"updated $EXCL (${#THIRD_PARTY[@]} third-party links excluded)\"\n  fi\n  rm -f \"$tmp\"\nfi\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nGet-ChildItem -LiteralPath $SRC -Directory -Force | ForEach-Object {\n  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }\n  if (Test-IsLink $_.FullName) { $THIRD_PARTY += $_.Name; return }\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md')) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }\n}\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R9-06: enumerate EVERY entry, not -Directory - a dangling reparse point may\n# not report as a directory and would be missed. Classify on the ReparsePoint\n# attribute itself: Test-Path is false for a dangling link.\nGet-ChildItem -LiteralPath $SRC -Force | ForEach-Object {\n  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }\n  if ($_.Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint) { $THIRD_PARTY += $_.Name; return }\n  if ($_.PSIsContainer -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md'))) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }\n}\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R8-02: keep .gitignore covering every current canonical link.\n$GI    = Join-Path $SRC '.gitignore'\n$BEGIN = '# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex: third-party symlinks'\n$END   = '# END generated-by-sync-to-codex'\nif (-not $DRY) {\n  $kept = @()\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $GI) {\n    $skip = $false\n    foreach ($line in (Get-Content -LiteralPath $GI)) {\n      if ($line -eq $BEGIN) { $skip = $true; continue }\n      if ($line -eq $END)   { $skip = $false; continue }\n      if (-not $skip) { $kept += $line }\n    }\n  }\n  $block  = @($BEGIN, '# Rewritten on every sync. Do not edit by hand.',\n              '# No trailing slash: a trailing slash never matches a symlink.')\n  $block += ($THIRD_PARTY | ForEach-Object { \"/$_\" })\n  $block += $END\n  Set-Content -LiteralPath $GI -Value ($kept + $block)\n}\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R8-02 + R9-02: per-machine exclude list in .git/info/exclude - never the\n# tracked .gitignore, which both machines share. Written only when the content\n# changed, with LF endings, so a no-op sync never dirties anything.\n$EXCL  = Join-Path $SRC '.git\\info\\exclude'\n$BEGIN = '# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex: third-party symlinks'\n$END   = '# END generated-by-sync-to-codex'\nif ((-not $DRY) -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC '.git') -PathType Container)) {\n  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path (Join-Path $SRC '.git\\info') | Out-Null\n  $kept = @()\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $EXCL) {\n    $skip = $false\n    foreach ($line in (Get-Content -LiteralPath $EXCL)) {\n      if ($line -eq $BEGIN) { $skip = $true; continue }\n      if ($line -eq $END)   { $skip = $false; continue }\n      if (-not $skip) { $kept += $line }\n    }\n  }\n  $block  = @($BEGIN, '# Rewritten on every sync. Per-machine. Do not edit by hand.',\n              '# No trailing slash: a trailing slash never matches a symlink.')\n  $block += @($THIRD_PARTY | ForEach-Object { \"/$_\" })\n  $block += $END\n  $newText = (($kept + $block) -join \"`n\") + \"`n\"\n  $oldText = if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $EXCL) { [IO.File]::ReadAllText($EXCL) } else { '' }\n  if ($newText -ne $oldText) {\n    [IO.File]::WriteAllText($EXCL, $newText)\n    Write-Host \"updated $EXCL ($($THIRD_PARTY.Count) third-party links excluded)\"\n  }\n}\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 5b: Install the pre-commit hook that refuses symlink commits (R9-03)**\n\nThe exclude list only covers links that existed at the last sync, and the sync runs only inside `dev-sync` while the backup commits every day. So a fresh `npx skills add` is routinely in the tree before any sync has excluded it — the normal case, not an edge case. This hook is the real guarantee: it refuses any commit that **adds or changes** a mode-120000 entry, while still allowing Task 4's **removal** of the 19 tracked links (a deletion's new mode is `000000`). `daily-backup.ps1` does not pass `--no-verify`, so it holds there too. The failure is visible, not silent: that day's backup commit fails and surfaces at session start through `.errors.log`; running the sync clears it.\n\nHooks live in `.git/hooks`, are per-clone, and are never pushed — Windows needs its own copy when this task is repeated there.\n\n```bash\ntest -e ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit && echo \"EXISTS - stop and merge by hand\" || echo \"no existing hook\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills config --get core.hooksPath || echo \"core.hooksPath unset - .git/hooks is live\"\n```\n\nExpected: `no existing hook` and `core.hooksPath unset`. If a hook already exists, **stop** — do not overwrite it.\n\nCreate `~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit`:\n\n```sh\n#!/bin/sh\n# pre-commit: refuse to commit any NEW or CHANGED symlink (git mode 120000).\n# Deleting a tracked link is allowed: its new mode is 000000.\nbad=$(git diff --cached --raw --no-renames --diff-filter=ACMRT \\\n      | awk -F'\\t' '{ split($1, m, \" \"); if (m[2] == \"120000\") print $2 }')\nif [ -n \"$bad\" ]; then\n  echo \"pre-commit: refusing to commit symlinks (mode 120000):\" >&2\n  echo \"$bad\" | sed 's/^/  /' >&2\n  echo \"These are third-party skill links - dead on Windows, which pulls this repo.\" >&2\n  echo \"Fix: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh   (adds them to .git/info/exclude)\" >&2\n  echo \"then: git reset -q -- <path>\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\nexit 0\n```\n\n```bash\nchmod +x ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit\n```\n\nProve it in a scratch repo before trusting it:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/hooktest && mkdir -p /tmp/hooktest/target\necho x > /tmp/hooktest/target/SKILL.md && echo y > /tmp/hooktest/owned.md\ncd /tmp/hooktest && git init -q . && git config user.email t@t && git config user.name t\nln -s target tracked-link && git add owned.md tracked-link && git commit -q -m baseline\ncp ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit\ngit rm -q --cached tracked-link && git commit -q -m untrack;                     echo \"T1 untrack exit=$? (expect 0)\"\nln -s target newlink && git add newlink && git commit -q -m add;                  echo \"T2 new link exit=$? (expect 1)\"\ngit reset -q -- newlink\necho more >> owned.md && git add owned.md && git commit -q -m edit;                echo \"T3 normal exit=$? (expect 0)\"\nrm owned.md && ln -s target owned.md && git add owned.md && git commit -q -m f2l;   echo \"T4 file-to-link exit=$? (expect 1)\"\n```\n\nExpected: T1 `0`, T2 `1`, T3 `0`, T4 `1`. This exact sequence was run while writing the plan and produced those results. The baseline commit happens **before** the hook is copied in, exactly as the real repo already tracks 19 links today.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- **The install procedure itself (R8-02, residual).** `npx skills add ... -a claude-code` keeps creating links in `~/.claude/skills/`. That is now handled — the sync treats them as third-party and adds them to the ignore block on its next run. One window remains: an install made after the last sync and before a 09:00 backup could still be committed. If `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` ever reads non-zero, add a `pre-commit` hook in `~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/` that rejects staged mode-120000 entries (`daily-backup.ps1` does not pass `--no-verify`, so it would hold).\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- **The install procedure itself (R8-02, R9-03).** `npx skills add ... -a claude-code` keeps creating links in `~/.claude/skills/`, and the procedure is left unchanged. Two layers handle it: the sync adds every current link to the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` on its next run, and — because the sync runs only inside `dev-sync` while the backup commits daily — the **pre-commit hook installed in Task 3 Step 5b** is the actual guarantee. Cost: on a day a new install lands before a sync, the skills repo's backup commit fails visibly (surfaced at session start); running the sync clears it. **Windows** needs the same hook installed in its own clone, since hooks are never pulled.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nls -ld ~                         # must NOT be world-readable. If it is, STOP: changing home permissions is a decision for Eric, not a side effect of this plan (R8-09)\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R9-07: sysadminctl gives piuser the primary group `staff` (20), and a macOS\n# home is normally user:staff with group r-x. \"Not world-readable\" is therefore\n# the wrong test - piuser would read ~ through the GROUP bits. Default chosen\n# here: give piuser its own primary group. (Tightening ~ to drwx------ is the\n# alternative; that is Eric's call - record which was used in the report.)\ndscl . -list /Groups PrimaryGroupID | awk '$2==4242'   # must print nothing (GID unused)\nsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial\nsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial PrimaryGroupID 4242\nsudo dscl . -create /Users/piuser PrimaryGroupID 4242\nid piuser                        # must NOT list staff(20)\nls -ld ~                         # record owner, group and the group bits\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). A few gitignored on-disk links to vendored\n  packages are expected; what must never happen is committing one, because Windows\n  pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). On-disk links to third-party skills are\n  expected; they are listed in the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` (never the tracked\n  `.gitignore`), and a pre-commit hook refuses to commit one. What must never happen is\n  committing a link, because Windows pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n    # What must be zero is TRACKED symlinks. The third-party links legitimately\n    # remain on disk; they are gitignored, so they can never reach Windows.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n    # What must be zero is TRACKED symlinks. The third-party links legitimately\n    # remain on disk; they are excluded per-machine and the pre-commit hook\n    # refuses to commit one, so they can never reach Windows.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n| `third_party_links_in_canonical` | `19` | skills-CLI installs and vendored links — gitignored, expected, **not** an error; moves with every install |\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n| `third_party_links_in_canonical` | `19` | skills-CLI installs and vendored links — excluded per-machine, expected, **not** an error; moves with every install |\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nIt is the first fix in eight rounds that removed code rather than adding a guard.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nIt is the first fix in eight rounds that removed code rather than adding a guard.\n- **Round 9** — Claude (resumed session): **REVISE**, 2 high / 2 medium / 3 low (R9-01 – R9-07). All accepted. Both highs came from the round-8 redesign itself: a real sync ran *before* reconciliation and would have overwritten the two pool copies holding the only copy of their edits, and the generated ignore list lived in the tracked `.gitignore` shared by both machines, so each machine would have erased the other's entries and brought the committed-symlink bug back. Fixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee.\n%%%%END%%%%\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6327,"cache_read_input_tokens":465476,"output_tokens":26695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11935},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6327,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":26695,"cache_read_input_tokens":465476,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6327},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cez6z3GiPeWqqWL66FngX","type":"assistant","uuid":"dbdac6fc-ce8d-4b10-9bda-9cc311afb7fa","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:37:14.755Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"dbdac6fc-ce8d-4b10-9bda-9cc311afb7fa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d90457fc-55a4-4c91-beb9-bfaecc9c0aa3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MaE4XxBJHcMThk8cnKBKRv","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/r9-fixes.txt (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"d624692a-5010-4379-b55b-54bd9d9ba2c0","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:37:14.997Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/r9-fixes.txt","content":"%%%%OLD%%%%\nMANAGED=()\nTHIRD_PARTY=()\nfor d in \"$SRC\"/*/; do\n  name=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"\n  case \"$name\" in .*) continue ;; esac\n  # A symlink can NEVER enter MANAGED. That makes the original R1 danger\n  # (delete-then-copy destroying a link target) structurally impossible -\n  # no guard needed, because the unsafe case cannot be constructed.\n  if [ -L \"${d%/}\" ]; then\n    THIRD_PARTY+=(\"$name\")\n    continue\n  fi\n  if [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ]; then\n    MANAGED+=(\"$name\")\n  fi\ndone\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nMANAGED=()\nTHIRD_PARTY=()\n# R9-06: glob \"$SRC\"/* with NO trailing slash. \"$SRC\"/*/ matches only links\n# that RESOLVE to directories, so a dangling third-party link was silently\n# left out of the exclude list and the next `git add -A` would commit it.\nfor d in \"$SRC\"/*; do\n  name=\"$(basename \"$d\")\"\n  case \"$name\" in .*) continue ;; esac\n  # A symlink can NEVER enter MANAGED - dangling or not. That makes the\n  # original R1 danger (delete-then-copy destroying a link target)\n  # structurally impossible.\n  if [ -L \"$d\" ]; then\n    THIRD_PARTY+=(\"$name\")\n    [ -e \"$d\" ] || echo \"WARN third-party link '$name' is dangling\" >&2\n    continue\n  fi\n  if [ -d \"$d\" ] && [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ]; then\n    MANAGED+=(\"$name\")\n  fi\ndone\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R8-02: keep .gitignore covering EVERY current canonical symlink, so the\n# next `npx skills add -a claude-code` cannot get its link committed by the\n# daily backup's `git add -A`. Managed as a marked block, rewritten in place.\nGI=\"$SRC/.gitignore\"\nBEGIN=\"# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex: third-party symlinks\"\nEND=\"# END generated-by-sync-to-codex\"\nif [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ]; then\n  tmp=\"$(mktemp)\"\n  if [ -f \"$GI\" ]; then\n    awk -v b=\"$BEGIN\" -v e=\"$END\" '\n      $0==b {skip=1} !skip {print} $0==e {skip=0}' \"$GI\" > \"$tmp\"\n  fi\n  {\n    echo \"$BEGIN\"\n    echo \"# Rewritten on every sync. Do not edit by hand.\"\n    echo \"# No trailing slash: that matches directories only, and git does not\"\n    echo \"# treat a symlink as a directory - the pattern would never match.\"\n    for name in ${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}; do echo \"/$name\"; done\n    echo \"$END\"\n  } >> \"$tmp\"\n  if ! cmp -s \"$tmp\" \"$GI\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    cp \"$tmp\" \"$GI\"\n    echo \"updated $GI (${#THIRD_PARTY[@]} third-party links ignored)\"\n  fi\n  rm -f \"$tmp\"\nfi\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R8-02 + R9-02: keep git from ever seeing the current canonical links, so the\n# daily backup's `git add -A` cannot commit an `npx skills add` link.\n#\n# Written to .git/info/exclude, NOT the tracked .gitignore. The set of links is\n# per-machine, while .gitignore is shared through erash11/claude-skills: each\n# machine's sync would rewrite the other's list, the backup would push it, and\n# the Mac's links would stop being ignored - R3 again. info/exclude is never\n# committed. Lines outside the marked block (e.g. /.claude/RESUME.md) are kept.\n# The pre-commit hook from Task 3 is the backstop for a link installed after\n# the last sync.\nEXCL=\"$SRC/.git/info/exclude\"\nBEGIN=\"# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex: third-party symlinks\"\nEND=\"# END generated-by-sync-to-codex\"\nif [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ] && [ -d \"$SRC/.git\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$SRC/.git/info\"\n  tmp=\"$(mktemp)\"\n  if [ -f \"$EXCL\" ]; then\n    awk -v b=\"$BEGIN\" -v e=\"$END\" '\n      $0==b {skip=1} !skip {print} $0==e {skip=0}' \"$EXCL\" > \"$tmp\"\n  fi\n  {\n    echo \"$BEGIN\"\n    echo \"# Rewritten on every sync. Per-machine. Do not edit by hand.\"\n    echo \"# No trailing slash: that matches directories only, and git does not\"\n    echo \"# treat a symlink as a directory - the pattern would never match.\"\n    for name in ${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}; do echo \"/$name\"; done\n    echo \"$END\"\n  } >> \"$tmp\"\n  if ! cmp -s \"$tmp\" \"$EXCL\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    cp \"$tmp\" \"$EXCL\"\n    echo \"updated $EXCL (${#THIRD_PARTY[@]} third-party links excluded)\"\n  fi\n  rm -f \"$tmp\"\nfi\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nGet-ChildItem -LiteralPath $SRC -Directory -Force | ForEach-Object {\n  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }\n  if (Test-IsLink $_.FullName) { $THIRD_PARTY += $_.Name; return }\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md')) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }\n}\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R9-06: enumerate EVERY entry, not -Directory - a dangling reparse point may\n# not report as a directory and would be missed. Classify on the ReparsePoint\n# attribute itself: Test-Path is false for a dangling link.\nGet-ChildItem -LiteralPath $SRC -Force | ForEach-Object {\n  if ($_.Name.StartsWith('.')) { return }\n  if ($_.Attributes -band [IO.FileAttributes]::ReparsePoint) { $THIRD_PARTY += $_.Name; return }\n  if ($_.PSIsContainer -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $_.FullName 'SKILL.md'))) { $MANAGED += $_.Name }\n}\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R8-02: keep .gitignore covering every current canonical link.\n$GI    = Join-Path $SRC '.gitignore'\n$BEGIN = '# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex: third-party symlinks'\n$END   = '# END generated-by-sync-to-codex'\nif (-not $DRY) {\n  $kept = @()\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $GI) {\n    $skip = $false\n    foreach ($line in (Get-Content -LiteralPath $GI)) {\n      if ($line -eq $BEGIN) { $skip = $true; continue }\n      if ($line -eq $END)   { $skip = $false; continue }\n      if (-not $skip) { $kept += $line }\n    }\n  }\n  $block  = @($BEGIN, '# Rewritten on every sync. Do not edit by hand.',\n              '# No trailing slash: a trailing slash never matches a symlink.')\n  $block += ($THIRD_PARTY | ForEach-Object { \"/$_\" })\n  $block += $END\n  Set-Content -LiteralPath $GI -Value ($kept + $block)\n}\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R8-02 + R9-02: per-machine exclude list in .git/info/exclude - never the\n# tracked .gitignore, which both machines share. Written only when the content\n# changed, with LF endings, so a no-op sync never dirties anything.\n$EXCL  = Join-Path $SRC '.git\\info\\exclude'\n$BEGIN = '# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex: third-party symlinks'\n$END   = '# END generated-by-sync-to-codex'\nif ((-not $DRY) -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC '.git') -PathType Container)) {\n  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path (Join-Path $SRC '.git\\info') | Out-Null\n  $kept = @()\n  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $EXCL) {\n    $skip = $false\n    foreach ($line in (Get-Content -LiteralPath $EXCL)) {\n      if ($line -eq $BEGIN) { $skip = $true; continue }\n      if ($line -eq $END)   { $skip = $false; continue }\n      if (-not $skip) { $kept += $line }\n    }\n  }\n  $block  = @($BEGIN, '# Rewritten on every sync. Per-machine. Do not edit by hand.',\n              '# No trailing slash: a trailing slash never matches a symlink.')\n  $block += @($THIRD_PARTY | ForEach-Object { \"/$_\" })\n  $block += $END\n  $newText = (($kept + $block) -join \"`n\") + \"`n\"\n  $oldText = if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $EXCL) { [IO.File]::ReadAllText($EXCL) } else { '' }\n  if ($newText -ne $oldText) {\n    [IO.File]::WriteAllText($EXCL, $newText)\n    Write-Host \"updated $EXCL ($($THIRD_PARTY.Count) third-party links excluded)\"\n  }\n}\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 5b: Install the pre-commit hook that refuses symlink commits (R9-03)**\n\nThe exclude list only covers links that existed at the last sync, and the sync runs only inside `dev-sync` while the backup commits every day. So a fresh `npx skills add` is routinely in the tree before any sync has excluded it — the normal case, not an edge case. This hook is the real guarantee: it refuses any commit that **adds or changes** a mode-120000 entry, while still allowing Task 4's **removal** of the 19 tracked links (a deletion's new mode is `000000`). `daily-backup.ps1` does not pass `--no-verify`, so it holds there too. The failure is visible, not silent: that day's backup commit fails and surfaces at session start through `.errors.log`; running the sync clears it.\n\nHooks live in `.git/hooks`, are per-clone, and are never pushed — Windows needs its own copy when this task is repeated there.\n\n```bash\ntest -e ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit && echo \"EXISTS - stop and merge by hand\" || echo \"no existing hook\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills config --get core.hooksPath || echo \"core.hooksPath unset - .git/hooks is live\"\n```\n\nExpected: `no existing hook` and `core.hooksPath unset`. If a hook already exists, **stop** — do not overwrite it.\n\nCreate `~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit`:\n\n```sh\n#!/bin/sh\n# pre-commit: refuse to commit any NEW or CHANGED symlink (git mode 120000).\n# Deleting a tracked link is allowed: its new mode is 000000.\nbad=$(git diff --cached --raw --no-renames --diff-filter=ACMRT \\\n      | awk -F'\\t' '{ split($1, m, \" \"); if (m[2] == \"120000\") print $2 }')\nif [ -n \"$bad\" ]; then\n  echo \"pre-commit: refusing to commit symlinks (mode 120000):\" >&2\n  echo \"$bad\" | sed 's/^/  /' >&2\n  echo \"These are third-party skill links - dead on Windows, which pulls this repo.\" >&2\n  echo \"Fix: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh   (adds them to .git/info/exclude)\" >&2\n  echo \"then: git reset -q -- <path>\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\nexit 0\n```\n\n```bash\nchmod +x ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit\n```\n\nProve it in a scratch repo before trusting it:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/hooktest && mkdir -p /tmp/hooktest/target\necho x > /tmp/hooktest/target/SKILL.md && echo y > /tmp/hooktest/owned.md\ncd /tmp/hooktest && git init -q . && git config user.email t@t && git config user.name t\nln -s target tracked-link && git add owned.md tracked-link && git commit -q -m baseline\ncp ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit\ngit rm -q --cached tracked-link && git commit -q -m untrack;                     echo \"T1 untrack exit=$? (expect 0)\"\nln -s target newlink && git add newlink && git commit -q -m add;                  echo \"T2 new link exit=$? (expect 1)\"\ngit reset -q -- newlink\necho more >> owned.md && git add owned.md && git commit -q -m edit;                echo \"T3 normal exit=$? (expect 0)\"\nrm owned.md && ln -s target owned.md && git add owned.md && git commit -q -m f2l;   echo \"T4 file-to-link exit=$? (expect 1)\"\n```\n\nExpected: T1 `0`, T2 `1`, T3 `0`, T4 `1`. This exact sequence was run while writing the plan and produced those results. The baseline commit happens **before** the hook is copied in, exactly as the real repo already tracks 19 links today.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- **The install procedure itself (R8-02, residual).** `npx skills add ... -a claude-code` keeps creating links in `~/.claude/skills/`. That is now handled — the sync treats them as third-party and adds them to the ignore block on its next run. One window remains: an install made after the last sync and before a 09:00 backup could still be committed. If `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` ever reads non-zero, add a `pre-commit` hook in `~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/` that rejects staged mode-120000 entries (`daily-backup.ps1` does not pass `--no-verify`, so it would hold).\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- **The install procedure itself (R8-02, R9-03).** `npx skills add ... -a claude-code` keeps creating links in `~/.claude/skills/`, and the procedure is left unchanged. Two layers handle it: the sync adds every current link to the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` on its next run, and — because the sync runs only inside `dev-sync` while the backup commits daily — the **pre-commit hook installed in Task 3 Step 5b** is the actual guarantee. Cost: on a day a new install lands before a sync, the skills repo's backup commit fails visibly (surfaced at session start); running the sync clears it. **Windows** needs the same hook installed in its own clone, since hooks are never pulled.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nls -ld ~                         # must NOT be world-readable. If it is, STOP: changing home permissions is a decision for Eric, not a side effect of this plan (R8-09)\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R9-07: sysadminctl gives piuser the primary group `staff` (20), and a macOS\n# home is normally user:staff with group r-x. \"Not world-readable\" is therefore\n# the wrong test - piuser would read ~ through the GROUP bits. Default chosen\n# here: give piuser its own primary group. (Tightening ~ to drwx------ is the\n# alternative; that is Eric's call - record which was used in the report.)\ndscl . -list /Groups PrimaryGroupID | awk '$2==4242'   # must print nothing (GID unused)\nsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial\nsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial PrimaryGroupID 4242\nsudo dscl . -create /Users/piuser PrimaryGroupID 4242\nid piuser                        # must NOT list staff(20)\nls -ld ~                         # record owner, group and the group bits\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). A few gitignored on-disk links to vendored\n  packages are expected; what must never happen is committing one, because Windows\n  pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). On-disk links to third-party skills are\n  expected; they are listed in the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` (never the tracked\n  `.gitignore`), and a pre-commit hook refuses to commit one. What must never happen is\n  committing a link, because Windows pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n    # What must be zero is TRACKED symlinks. The third-party links legitimately\n    # remain on disk; they are gitignored, so they can never reach Windows.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n    # What must be zero is TRACKED symlinks. The third-party links legitimately\n    # remain on disk; they are excluded per-machine and the pre-commit hook\n    # refuses to commit one, so they can never reach Windows.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n| `third_party_links_in_canonical` | `19` | skills-CLI installs and vendored links — gitignored, expected, **not** an error; moves with every install |\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n| `third_party_links_in_canonical` | `19` | skills-CLI installs and vendored links — excluded per-machine, expected, **not** an error; moves with every install |\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nIt is the first fix in eight rounds that removed code rather than adding a guard.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nIt is the first fix in eight rounds that removed code rather than adding a guard.\n- **Round 9** — Claude (resumed session): **REVISE**, 2 high / 2 medium / 3 low (R9-01 – R9-07). All accepted. Both highs came from the round-8 redesign itself: a real sync ran *before* reconciliation and would have overwritten the two pool copies holding the only copy of their edits, and the generated ignore list lived in the tracked `.gitignore` shared by both machines, so each machine would have erased the other's entries and brought the committed-symlink bug back. Fixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee.\n%%%%END%%%%\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dbdac6fc-ce8d-4b10-9bda-9cc311afb7fa","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d624692a-5010-4379-b55b-54bd9d9ba2c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez6z4YrybGEfdUxvqfpA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cym2JNxywHqbGAfxyuGEQc","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt","old_string":"Never leave hardened-script + legacy-layout: dev-sync fails permanently.","new_string":"Never leave hardened-script + legacy-layout: dev-sync fails permanently.\n\n=== SUPERSEDED 2026-09-12 (review rounds 8-9) ===\nPHASE B, PHASE C and \"AFTER A ROLLBACK\" above describe the DELETED inversion\ndesign (skills-canonicalize.sh). Task 4 no longer inverts anything: all 19\noutward links are third-party and are only UNTRACKED. The sync script no longer\nrefuses canonical symlinks. Do NOT follow PHASE B or PHASE C.\nPHASE A still restores the views, but it predates Task 2's prune: it brings the\n98 pruned skills back into ~/.agents/skills. Prefer ROLLBACK BY TASK below.\n\n=== ROLLBACK BY TASK (current design) ===\n\nTASK 2 (pool prune) - move the 98 back:\n  python3 -c \"import os;A='/Users/kristinarash/.agents/skills-archive/2026-09-12';[os.rename(A+'/'+n,'/Users/kristinarash/.agents/skills/'+n) for n in os.listdir(A)]\"\n\nTASK 3 (sync scripts + pre-commit hook):\n  git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <sync-scripts-sha>\n  git -C ~/.claude/skills push\n  rm ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit\n\nTASK 4 (untrack + reconcile + publish) - no tarball needed:\n  0. If the Task 3 pre-commit hook is installed, remove it first\n     (rm ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit). Re-tracking links is exactly\n     what it exists to refuse.\n  1. git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <untrack-sha>     # re-tracks the 19 links\n     git -C ~/.claude/skills push\n     NOTE: this re-publishes the dead Windows links. Only do it if the\n     untrack itself was wrong.\n  2. Delete the generated block from ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude -\n     the lines from \"# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex\" to\n     \"# END generated-by-sync-to-codex\". Keep every other line\n     (e.g. /.claude/RESUME.md).\n  3. Restore any pool copy the publish overwrote, from\n     ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/<name>\n  4. bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh   # only if Task 3's scripts are kept\n\nTASK 5 (frontmatter) - revert those commits in ~/.claude/skills, newest first.\n  Then reload the daily backup if it is still paused:\n  launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.dailybackup.plist"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6327,"cache_read_input_tokens":465476,"output_tokens":26695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11935},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6327,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":26695,"cache_read_input_tokens":465476,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6327},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cez6z3GiPeWqqWL66FngX","type":"assistant","uuid":"826ba140-b403-47eb-b803-c18aa737ee4b","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:37:25.255Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
