efuse.\n  1. git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <untrack-sha>     # re-tracks the 19 links\n     git -C ~/.claude/skills push\n     NOTE: this re-publishes the dead Windows links. Only do it if the\n     untrack itself was wrong.\n  2. Delete the generated block from ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude -\n     the lines from \"# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex\" to\n     \"# END generated-by-sync-to-codex\". Keep every other line\n     (e.g. /.claude/RESUME.md).\n  3. Restore any pool copy the publish overwrote, from\n     ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/<name>\n  4. bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh   # only if Task 3's scripts are kept\n\nTASK 5 (frontmatter) - revert those commits in ~/.claude/skills, newest first.\n  Then reload the daily backup if it is still paused:\n  launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.dailybackup.plist","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":591,"oldLines":3,"newStart":591,"newLines":41,"lines":["     forward, then: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh"," "," Never leave hardened-script + legacy-layout: dev-sync fails permanently.","+","+=== SUPERSEDED 2026-09-12 (review rounds 8-9) ===","+PHASE B, PHASE C and \"AFTER A ROLLBACK\" above describe the DELETED inversion","+design (skills-canonicalize.sh). Task 4 no longer inverts anything: all 19","+outward links are third-party and are only UNTRACKED. The sync script no longer","+refuses canonical symlinks. Do NOT follow PHASE B or PHASE C.","+PHASE A still restores the views, but it predates Task 2's prune: it brings the","+98 pruned skills back into ~/.agents/skills. Prefer ROLLBACK BY TASK below.","+","+=== ROLLBACK BY TASK (current design) ===","+","+TASK 2 (pool prune) - move the 98 back:","+  python3 -c \"import os;A='/Users/kristinarash/.agents/skills-archive/2026-09-12';[os.rename(A+'/'+n,'/Users/kristinarash/.agents/skills/'+n) for n in os.listdir(A)]\"","+","+TASK 3 (sync scripts + pre-commit hook):","+  git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <sync-scripts-sha>","+  git -C ~/.claude/skills push","+  rm ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit","+","+TASK 4 (untrack + reconcile + publish) - no tarball needed:","+  0. If the Task 3 pre-commit hook is installed, remove it first","+     (rm ~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit). Re-tracking links is exactly","+     what it exists to refuse.","+  1. git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <untrack-sha>     # re-tracks the 19 links","+     git -C ~/.claude/skills push","+     NOTE: this re-publishes the dead Windows links. Only do it if the","+     untrack itself was wrong.","+  2. Delete the generated block from ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude -","+     the lines from \"# BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex\" to","+     \"# END generated-by-sync-to-codex\". Keep every other line","+     (e.g. /.claude/RESUME.md).","+  3. Restore any pool copy the publish overwrote, from","+     ~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/<name>","+  4. bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh   # only if Task 3's scripts are kept","+","+TASK 5 (frontmatter) - revert those commits in ~/.claude/skills, newest first.","+  Then reload the daily backup if it is still paused:","+  launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.dailybackup.plist"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"826ba140-b403-47eb-b803-c18aa737ee4b","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ceff96a6-bbc0-4163-809d-665d973c5fed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez6z4YrybGEfdUxvqfpA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MDDcg4WEXwWW6s5eDQCtsG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r9.md","content":"# Round 9 dispositions — all seven ACCEPTED\n\nBoth highs came from the round-8 redesign. Two premises were re-checked on disk\nbefore fixing:\n\n- **R9-01:** `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` in `~/.agents/skills` are still\n  real directories that **still differ** from canonical. No sync has run on the\n  real layout, so no edits have been lost; the defect is in the plan's order only.\n- **R9-02 / R9-03:** `~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude` exists and already\n  holds one user line (`/.claude/RESUME.md`) that the generated block must\n  preserve. No `pre-commit` hook exists and `core.hooksPath` is unset, so a hook\n  in `.git/hooks` is live and clobbers nothing. `daily-backup.ps1` commits with a\n  plain `git commit` (no `--no-verify`). The only other reference to\n  `sync-to-codex` in scripts/hooks/LaunchAgents is `verify-crossmachine.ps1`,\n  which only `Test-Path`s the file and never runs it — so it cannot trigger the\n  R9-01 overwrite.\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R9-01 | ACCEPTED | Task 4 reordered: **Step 1** untrack → **Step 2 reconcile** (list real-dir pool copies that differ, back each up to `pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, read the diff, copy wanted edits into canonical) → **Step 3 first real sync**. A task-level paragraph states no non-dry sync may run before Step 2 and why. Step 2 also says what it means if it prints nothing: a real sync already ran, and the pool-only edits must come from the VIEWS tarball. The only syncs before Step 3 are Task 3's dry run and scratch-`HOME` tests, which never touch the real pool. |\n| R9-02 | ACCEPTED | Both scripts now write the generated block to **`.git/info/exclude`**, never the tracked `.gitignore`, and only when `$SRC/.git` exists. Lines outside the marked block are preserved. The PowerShell twin compares full text and writes only when it changed, with LF via `[IO.File]::WriteAllText`, so a no-op sync never dirties anything. Task 4 Step 3 asserts that the block is present, that `/.claude/RESUME.md` survived, and that `git diff --quiet -- .gitignore` is clean. `rot.md` invariants, the metrics comment and the metrics table say \"excluded per-machine\" instead of \"gitignored\". |\n| R9-03 | ACCEPTED | New **Task 3 Step 5b** installs a `pre-commit` hook that refuses any commit **adding or changing** a mode-120000 entry, by reading `git diff --cached --raw --diff-filter=ACMRT` and testing the new-mode field. Deletions (new mode `000000`) pass, so Task 4's untrack commit is not blocked. The step refuses to overwrite an existing hook. Out of Scope restated: the install-to-sync gap is the normal case, the hook is the guarantee, the cost is a visible failed backup commit, and Windows needs its own copy. |\n| R9-04 | ACCEPTED | The inventory gets an appended **SUPERSEDED** notice marking PHASE B/C and \"AFTER A ROLLBACK\" as describing the deleted inversion design, warning that PHASE A predates Task 2's prune, plus a new **ROLLBACK BY TASK** section for Tasks 2, 3, 4 and 5. The Task 4 entry has no tarball: remove the hook first, revert the untrack commit (with a warning that this re-publishes the dead Windows links), delete only the generated exclude block, restore overwritten pool copies from `pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, re-run the sync. Task 4 Step 7 points at that entry and explicitly not at PHASE A. |\n| R9-05 | ACCEPTED | `xargs -a` replaced by `git rm --cached --quiet --pathspec-from-file=/tmp/tracked-links.txt`. The step says why: `-a` is GNU-only, and this Mac has git 2.55 (≥ 2.26). |\n| R9-06 | ACCEPTED | Bash enumerates `\"$SRC\"/*` and tests `-L` **before** any directory test, so dangling third-party links are classified and excluded, with a `WARN ... is dangling` line. The PowerShell twin enumerates without `-Directory` and classifies on the `ReparsePoint` attribute directly, since `Test-Path` is false for a dangling link. |\n| R9-07 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 Step 1 no longer uses \"not world-readable\" as the test. It creates a dedicated `pitrial` group (GID 4242, checked unused first), sets it as piuser's primary group, and requires `id piuser` not to list `staff(20)`. A comment names this as the default and names tightening `~` to `drwx------` as the alternative, which is Eric's call and must be recorded in the report. Task 8 is not executed in this session. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6327,"cache_read_input_tokens":465476,"output_tokens":26695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11935},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6327,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":26695,"cache_read_input_tokens":465476,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6327},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":5,"requestId":"req_011Cez6z3GiPeWqqWL66FngX","type":"assistant","uuid":"06a67642-f86b-4d4f-a0f9-84c20e8edcf7","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:37:44.315Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
