{"parentUuid":"3773c516-cff9-4fbb-8ec0-37a0dc8236f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez7RYR7dZXhnhW7WB8XU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Gs8L9PaqY3kJtibaF6GHZ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r9.md","old_string":"## Rejected\n\nNone.","new_string":"## Executed verification (run, not claimed)\n\nThe bash sync script was re-extracted from the revised plan and run with\n`/bin/bash` 3.2.57. The fixture held 2 owned skills, 1 live third-party link,\n1 **dangling** third-party link, a tracked `.gitignore`, and a pre-existing\n`/.claude/RESUME.md` line in `.git/info/exclude`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Run 1 exit / counts | exit 0; `canonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 2` |\n| R9-06 dangling link | classified, `WARN third-party link 'dangling' is dangling`, and listed in the block |\n| R9-02 block location | written to `.git/info/exclude` as `/dangling`, `/theirs` (leading slash, no trailing slash) |\n| R9-02 user line | `/.claude/RESUME.md` **kept** |\n| R9-02 tracked file | `git diff --quiet -- .gitignore` → **unchanged**; `git status` clean |\n| Ignore effect | `theirs` ignored=yes, `dangling` ignored=yes, `mine` ignored=no |\n| Link target | canary still readable |\n| Idempotence | second run printed **0** `updated ... exclude` lines |\n| Guard | owned `mine` turned into a link → `FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill...`, exit 2 |\n| No-repo path, zero links | both syncs exit 0 on bash 3.2, 0 dangling, **no `.git` created** (exclude correctly skipped) |\n\n**R9-03 pre-commit hook**, prototyped in a scratch repo whose link was\ncommitted *before* the hook existed (mirroring the real repo): untrack a\ntracked link → exit **0** (allowed); stage a new link → exit **1** (refused,\nmessage printed); normal file edit → exit **0**; tracked file turned into a\nlink → exit **1**.\n\n**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all `bash`/`sh` script blocks pass\n`bash -n`; the PowerShell twin parses under `pwsh` (179 lines, 0 `Write-Error`\ncalls, 0 `VENDORED`, 5 `Stop-Fatal`, 3 `KEEP_OWNED`). Stale sweep: 0 for\n`GI=\"$SRC/.gitignore\"`, `$GI = Join-Path`, `-Directory -Force`,\n`for d in \"$SRC\"/*/`, `chmod 700`. The single `xargs -a` hit is the prose\nsentence explaining its removal (0 inside any code block); the single\nnon-`-LiteralPath` `Remove-Item` hit is a comment (twin line 150).\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4708,"cache_read_input_tokens":502366,"output_tokens":2248,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":511},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4708,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2248,"cache_read_input_tokens":502366,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4708},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cez7RWuKithqHYsi359jU","type":"assistant","uuid":"29f7f271-6014-46e4-ab4f-d75d668aed4d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:39:21.994Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"29f7f271-6014-46e4-ab4f-d75d668aed4d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d90457fc-55a4-4c91-beb9-bfaecc9c0aa3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Gs8L9PaqY3kJtibaF6GHZ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r9.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"7304af1a-10ce-44a1-a91e-3ae9892e939e","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:39:22.127Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r9.md","oldString":"## Rejected\n\nNone.","newString":"## Executed verification (run, not claimed)\n\nThe bash sync script was re-extracted from the revised plan and run with\n`/bin/bash` 3.2.57. The fixture held 2 owned skills, 1 live third-party link,\n1 **dangling** third-party link, a tracked `.gitignore`, and a pre-existing\n`/.claude/RESUME.md` line in `.git/info/exclude`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Run 1 exit / counts | exit 0; `canonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 2` |\n| R9-06 dangling link | classified, `WARN third-party link 'dangling' is dangling`, and listed in the block |\n| R9-02 block location | written to `.git/info/exclude` as `/dangling`, `/theirs` (leading slash, no trailing slash) |\n| R9-02 user line | `/.claude/RESUME.md` **kept** |\n| R9-02 tracked file | `git diff --quiet -- .gitignore` → **unchanged**; `git status` clean |\n| Ignore effect | `theirs` ignored=yes, `dangling` ignored=yes, `mine` ignored=no |\n| Link target | canary still readable |\n| Idempotence | second run printed **0** `updated ... exclude` lines |\n| Guard | owned `mine` turned into a link → `FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill...`, exit 2 |\n| No-repo path, zero links | both syncs exit 0 on bash 3.2, 0 dangling, **no `.git` created** (exclude correctly skipped) |\n\n**R9-03 pre-commit hook**, prototyped in a scratch repo whose link was\ncommitted *before* the hook existed (mirroring the real repo): untrack a\ntracked link → exit **0** (allowed); stage a new link → exit **1** (refused,\nmessage printed); normal file edit → exit **0**; tracked file turned into a\nlink → exit **1**.\n\n**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all `bash`/`sh` script blocks pass\n`bash -n`; the PowerShell twin parses under `pwsh` (179 lines, 0 `Write-Error`\ncalls, 0 `VENDORED`, 5 `Stop-Fatal`, 3 `KEEP_OWNED`). Stale sweep: 0 for\n`GI=\"$SRC/.gitignore\"`, `$GI = Join-Path`, `-Directory -Force`,\n`for d in \"$SRC\"/*/`, `chmod 700`. The single `xargs -a` hit is the prose\nsentence explaining its removal (0 inside any code block); the single\nnon-`-LiteralPath` `Remove-Item` hit is a comment (twin line 150).\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.","originalFile":"# Round 9 dispositions — all seven ACCEPTED\n\nBoth highs came from the round-8 redesign. Two premises were re-checked on disk\nbefore fixing:\n\n- **R9-01:** `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` in `~/.agents/skills` are still\n  real directories that **still differ** from canonical. No sync has run on the\n  real layout, so no edits have been lost; the defect is in the plan's order only.\n- **R9-02 / R9-03:** `~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude` exists and already\n  holds one user line (`/.claude/RESUME.md`) that the generated block must\n  preserve. No `pre-commit` hook exists and `core.hooksPath` is unset, so a hook\n  in `.git/hooks` is live and clobbers nothing. `daily-backup.ps1` commits with a\n  plain `git commit` (no `--no-verify`). The only other reference to\n  `sync-to-codex` in scripts/hooks/LaunchAgents is `verify-crossmachine.ps1`,\n  which only `Test-Path`s the file and never runs it — so it cannot trigger the\n  R9-01 overwrite.\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R9-01 | ACCEPTED | Task 4 reordered: **Step 1** untrack → **Step 2 reconcile** (list real-dir pool copies that differ, back each up to `pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, read the diff, copy wanted edits into canonical) → **Step 3 first real sync**. A task-level paragraph states no non-dry sync may run before Step 2 and why. Step 2 also says what it means if it prints nothing: a real sync already ran, and the pool-only edits must come from the VIEWS tarball. The only syncs before Step 3 are Task 3's dry run and scratch-`HOME` tests, which never touch the real pool. |\n| R9-02 | ACCEPTED | Both scripts now write the generated block to **`.git/info/exclude`**, never the tracked `.gitignore`, and only when `$SRC/.git` exists. Lines outside the marked block are preserved. The PowerShell twin compares full text and writes only when it changed, with LF via `[IO.File]::WriteAllText`, so a no-op sync never dirties anything. Task 4 Step 3 asserts that the block is present, that `/.claude/RESUME.md` survived, and that `git diff --quiet -- .gitignore` is clean. `rot.md` invariants, the metrics comment and the metrics table say \"excluded per-machine\" instead of \"gitignored\". |\n| R9-03 | ACCEPTED | New **Task 3 Step 5b** installs a `pre-commit` hook that refuses any commit **adding or changing** a mode-120000 entry, by reading `git diff --cached --raw --diff-filter=ACMRT` and testing the new-mode field. Deletions (new mode `000000`) pass, so Task 4's untrack commit is not blocked. The step refuses to overwrite an existing hook. Out of Scope restated: the install-to-sync gap is the normal case, the hook is the guarantee, the cost is a visible failed backup commit, and Windows needs its own copy. |\n| R9-04 | ACCEPTED | The inventory gets an appended **SUPERSEDED** notice marking PHASE B/C and \"AFTER A ROLLBACK\" as describing the deleted inversion design, warning that PHASE A predates Task 2's prune, plus a new **ROLLBACK BY TASK** section for Tasks 2, 3, 4 and 5. The Task 4 entry has no tarball: remove the hook first, revert the untrack commit (with a warning that this re-publishes the dead Windows links), delete only the generated exclude block, restore overwritten pool copies from `pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, re-run the sync. Task 4 Step 7 points at that entry and explicitly not at PHASE A. |\n| R9-05 | ACCEPTED | `xargs -a` replaced by `git rm --cached --quiet --pathspec-from-file=/tmp/tracked-links.txt`. The step says why: `-a` is GNU-only, and this Mac has git 2.55 (≥ 2.26). |\n| R9-06 | ACCEPTED | Bash enumerates `\"$SRC\"/*` and tests `-L` **before** any directory test, so dangling third-party links are classified and excluded, with a `WARN ... is dangling` line. The PowerShell twin enumerates without `-Directory` and classifies on the `ReparsePoint` attribute directly, since `Test-Path` is false for a dangling link. |\n| R9-07 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 Step 1 no longer uses \"not world-readable\" as the test. It creates a dedicated `pitrial` group (GID 4242, checked unused first), sets it as piuser's primary group, and requires `id piuser` not to list `staff(20)`. A comment names this as the default and names tightening `~` to `drwx------` as the alternative, which is Eric's call and must be recorded in the report. Task 8 is not executed in this session. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":6,"newStart":25,"newLines":40,"lines":[" | R9-06 | ACCEPTED | Bash enumerates `\"$SRC\"/*` and tests `-L` **before** any directory test, so dangling third-party links are classified and excluded, with a `WARN ... is dangling` line. The PowerShell twin enumerates without `-Directory` and classifies on the `ReparsePoint` attribute directly, since `Test-Path` is false for a dangling link. |"," | R9-07 | ACCEPTED | Task 8 Step 1 no longer uses \"not world-readable\" as the test. It creates a dedicated `pitrial` group (GID 4242, checked unused first), sets it as piuser's primary group, and requires `id piuser` not to list `staff(20)`. A comment names this as the default and names tightening `~` to `drwx------` as the alternative, which is Eric's call and must be recorded in the report. Task 8 is not executed in this session. |"," ","+## Executed verification (run, not claimed)","+","+The bash sync script was re-extracted from the revised plan and run with","+`/bin/bash` 3.2.57. The fixture held 2 owned skills, 1 live third-party link,","+1 **dangling** third-party link, a tracked `.gitignore`, and a pre-existing","+`/.claude/RESUME.md` line in `.git/info/exclude`.","+","+| Check | Result |","+|---|---|","+| Run 1 exit / counts | exit 0; `canonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 2` |","+| R9-06 dangling link | classified, `WARN third-party link 'dangling' is dangling`, and listed in the block |","+| R9-02 block location | written to `.git/info/exclude` as `/dangling`, `/theirs` (leading slash, no trailing slash) |","+| R9-02 user line | `/.claude/RESUME.md` **kept** |","+| R9-02 tracked file | `git diff --quiet -- .gitignore` → **unchanged**; `git status` clean |","+| Ignore effect | `theirs` ignored=yes, `dangling` ignored=yes, `mine` ignored=no |","+| Link target | canary still readable |","+| Idempotence | second run printed **0** `updated ... exclude` lines |","+| Guard | owned `mine` turned into a link → `FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill...`, exit 2 |","+| No-repo path, zero links | both syncs exit 0 on bash 3.2, 0 dangling, **no `.git` created** (exclude correctly skipped) |","+","+**R9-03 pre-commit hook**, prototyped in a scratch repo whose link was","+committed *before* the hook existed (mirroring the real repo): untrack a","+tracked link → exit **0** (allowed); stage a new link → exit **1** (refused,","+message printed); normal file edit → exit **0**; tracked file turned into a","+link → exit **1**.","+","+**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all `bash`/`sh` script blocks pass","+`bash -n`; the PowerShell twin parses under `pwsh` (179 lines, 0 `Write-Error`","+calls, 0 `VENDORED`, 5 `Stop-Fatal`, 3 `KEEP_OWNED`). Stale sweep: 0 for","+`GI=\"$SRC/.gitignore\"`, `$GI = Join-Path`, `-Directory -Force`,","+`for d in \"$SRC\"/*/`, `chmod 700`. The single `xargs -a` hit is the prose","+sentence explaining its removal (0 inside any code block); the single","+non-`-LiteralPath` `Remove-Item` hit is a comment (twin line 150).","+"," ## Rejected"," "," None."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"29f7f271-6014-46e4-ab4f-d75d668aed4d","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"7304af1a-10ce-44a1-a91e-3ae9892e939e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez7RYR7dZXhnhW7WB8XU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E2vR2SayygeJoLkEGrsmuo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS\ngit add docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt\ngit commit -q -m \"fix: R9-01..R9-07, reconcile before sync, per-machine exclude, pre-commit hook\n\nClaude review round 9:\n- R9-01 a real sync ran before reconciling memory-write/meeting-sync, whose\n  pool copies hold edits found nowhere else. Task 4 now reconciles first.\n- R9-02 the generated ignore list lived in the tracked, shared .gitignore;\n  each machine would erase the other's list. Now .git/info/exclude.\n- R9-03 pre-commit hook refuses adding/changing symlinks, allows removal.\n- R9-04 inventory marks the inversion-era rollback superseded; adds\n  rollback by task.\n- R9-05 xargs -a (GNU-only) -> git rm --pathspec-from-file.\n- R9-06 dangling third-party links now enumerated and excluded.\n- R9-07 piuser gets its own primary group; not-world-readable was the\n  wrong test.\n\nVerified by running on /bin/bash 3.2: exclude block, RESUME.md kept,\n.gitignore unchanged, dangling link excluded, idempotent rerun, guard,\nno-repo path; hook T1-T4; pwsh parse.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit log --oneline -1\ngit pull --rebase -q origin main && git push 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Commit round-9 fixes, rebase, and push"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4708,"cache_read_input_tokens":502366,"output_tokens":2248,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":511},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard