{"parentUuid":"e70ffa07-6b1f-4dca-9f3e-e69f05a858f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cez7Tbe9JQJfesjMpDZJs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GUXxZFPg4J74paz9EWjBkS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/claudex-loop/scripts/runner.py review --host codex --repo /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS --plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md --resume /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/claude-review-r9/claudex-*/result.json --feedback /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r9.md --artifacts /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/claude-review-r10 >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"runner exit=$?\"\npython3 -c \"\nimport json,glob\nf=sorted(glob.glob('/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/claude-review-r10/**/result.json',recursive=True))\nd=json.load(open(f[0])); r=d.get('response') or {}\nprint('status:',d.get('status'),'provider:',d.get('provider'))\nprint('VERDICT:',r.get('verdict'))\nprint('SUMMARY:',r.get('summary'))\nprint('findings:',len(r.get('findings',[])))\nfor x in r.get('findings',[]):\n    print()\n    print('['+x['severity'].upper()+'] '+x['id']+'  '+x['path'][:90])\n    print('  E:',x['evidence'][:600])\n    print('  F:',x['fix'][:300])\nprint(); print('LIMITATIONS:'); [print(' -',l[:220]) for l in r.get('limitations',[])]\n\"","description":"Gate A round 10 with the resumed Claude reviewer","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2479,"cache_read_input_tokens":507074,"output_tokens":842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":163},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2479,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":842,"cache_read_input_tokens":507074,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2479},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cez7Ta77NLkaHDWNvspfT","type":"assistant","uuid":"e84d3fe4-c3af-4c00-af4b-0373954921c7","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:39:40.004Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e84d3fe4-c3af-4c00-af4b-0373954921c7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d90457fc-55a4-4c91-beb9-bfaecc9c0aa3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GUXxZFPg4J74paz9EWjBkS","type":"tool_result","content":"runner exit=0\nstatus: completed provider: claude\nVERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: All seven round-9 fixes are present and look correct. The reconcile step now runs before the first real sync (R9-01), and the generated block moved to the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` with other lines preserved and no churn (R9-02). The pre-commit hook allows deletions and refuses new or changed mode-120000 entries (R9-03). A superseded notice and a ROLLBACK BY TASK section were appended to the inventory and verified on disk (R9-04). `--pathspec-from-file` replaces `xargs -a` (R9-05), dangling links are now classified (R9-06), and Task 8 no longer tests \"world-readable\" (R9-07). One new high-severity defect comes from how the R9-03 hook interacts with daily-backup. When a fresh skills-CLI link is present, the backup's `git add -A` stages it and the hook refuses the commit. daily-backup ignores the commit's exit code and logs \"committed\", so the failure is not visible. The staged link also stays in the index, so running the sync does not clear it. From then on, every daily commit of the canonical repo fails without any message until someone unstages the link by hand. Two low-severity items remain: stale wording and a Task 8 group assumption that probably doesn't hold.\nfindings: 3\n\n[HIGH] R10-01  ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 Sync-Repo (lines 62-67); plan Task 3 Step 5b and Out of\n  E: The plan says that on a day a new install lands before a sync, the backup commit 'fails visibly (surfaced at session start through .errors.log); running the sync clears it.' Neither part holds. (1) Visibility: daily-backup.ps1:65 runs `git commit ... 2>&1 | Out-Null` and never checks `$LASTEXITCODE`. Line 67 logs 'committed N change(s)' regardless, and the only `$Errors.Add` calls for repos are repo-missing, repo-diverged and repo-push. A commit rejected by the hook adds nothing to .errors.log; `$ahead` stays 0, so nothing is pushed and nothing is reported. (2) Clearing: line 64's `git add -A`\n  F: Do both. (a) In daily-backup.ps1, check `$LASTEXITCODE` after the commit, call `$Errors.Add(\"repo-commit:$name\")`, and log the captured output, the same way the push is already handled. (b) Make the sync actually clear the state: after computing THIRD_PARTY, run `git -C \"$SRC\" reset -q -- <each THIR\n\n[LOW] R10-02  docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md (Task 3 Step 4 comments/expecte\n  E: The R9-02 move to `.git/info/exclude` was not carried through all the text. Task 3 Step 4 still says 'CASE 1: ... .gitignore covers it' and 'If `theirs NOT ignored`, the generated `.gitignore` block is wrong'. Step 5 says 'A dry run writes nothing — no `.gitignore` block'. Step 7's commit message, which will stay in erash11/claude-skills history, says 'the .gitignore block covering third-party links is regenerated on every run (R8-02)'. Someone troubleshooting from these notes or that commit would look in the wrong file, and after R9-02 that is the file the sync must never write.\n  F: Change these references to `.git/info/exclude` (per-machine), and mention the pre-commit hook in the Task 3 commit message.\n\n[LOW] R10-03  docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md (Task 8 Step 1)\n  E: The new default gives piuser a separate primary group (`dscl . -create /Users/piuser PrimaryGroupID 4242`) and then requires that `id piuser` does not list staff(20). On macOS, membership in `staff` for local users usually comes from a nested group (staff nests localaccounts, and every local account belongs to that), not from the primary group. If so, `id piuser` still lists staff(20), `sudo -u piuser` still has staff as a supplementary group, and the step stops every time. The stop is safe, but the chosen default can't reach the boundary. I did not verify this on this machine.\n  F: Before relying on the primary-group change, run `dseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff` or `dscl . -read /Groups/staff NestedGroups`. If staff membership is inherited, make the default boundary a home-permission change the user approves in advance (for example `chmod 750 ~` with a non-staff gro\n\nLIMITATIONS:\n - Static review only. I ran no commands, and I did not rerun the host's reported scratch-repo, hook and sync results; I neither confirm nor dispute them.\n - I did not recompute the plan's SHA256.\n - The R10-01 index behaviour (an already-staged path is not dropped when it is later excluded) comes from how git works in general. I did not run it against this repo.\n - I did not verify macOS `staff` group nesting on this machine (R10-03).\n - I could not inspect the Windows clone, its hook state or its scheduled tasks.\n - I did not read the Pi research note or the spec notes.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3bde2880-100f-4619-b32f-1a0867d57041","timestamp":"2026-09-12T19:41:21.874Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"runner exit=0\nstatus: completed provider: claude\nVERDICT: REVISE\nSUMMARY: All seven round-9 fixes are present and look correct. The reconcile step now runs before the first real sync (R9-01), and the generated block moved to the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` with other lines preserved and no churn (R9-02). The pre-commit hook allows deletions and refuses new or changed mode-120000 entries (R9-03). A superseded notice and a ROLLBACK BY TASK section were appended to the inventory and verified on disk (R9-04). `--pathspec-from-file` replaces `xargs -a` (R9-05), dangling links are now classified (R9-06), and Task 8 no longer tests \"world-readable\" (R9-07). One new high-severity defect comes from how the R9-03 hook interacts with daily-backup. When a fresh skills-CLI link is present, the backup's `git add -A` stages it and the hook refuses the commit. daily-backup ignores the commit's exit code and logs \"committed\", so the failure is not visible. The staged link also stays in the index, so running the sync does not clear it. From then on, every daily commit of the canonical repo fails without any message until someone unstages the link by hand. Two low-severity items remain: stale wording and a Task 8 group assumption that probably doesn't hold.\nfindings: 3\n\n[HIGH] R10-01  ~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1 Sync-Repo (lines 62-67); plan Task 3 Step 5b and Out of\n  E: The plan says that on a day a new install lands before a sync, the backup commit 'fails visibly (surfaced at session start through .errors.log); running the sync clears it.' Neither part holds. (1) Visibility: daily-backup.ps1:65 runs `git commit ... 2>&1 | Out-Null` and never checks `$LASTEXITCODE`. Line 67 logs 'committed N change(s)' regardless, and the only `$Errors.Add` calls for repos are repo-missing, repo-diverged and repo-push. A commit rejected by the hook adds nothing to .errors.log; `$ahead` stays 0, so nothing is pushed and nothing is reported. (2) Clearing: line 64's `git add -A`\n  F: Do both. (a) In daily-backup.ps1, check `$LASTEXITCODE` after the commit, call `$Errors.Add(\"repo-commit:$name\")`, and log the captured output, the same way the push is already handled. (b) Make the sync actually clear the state: after computing THIRD_PARTY, run `git -C \"$SRC\" reset -q -- <each THIR\n\n[LOW] R10-02  docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md (Task 3 Step 4 comments/expecte\n  E: The R9-02 move to `.git/info/exclude` was not carried through all the text. Task 3 Step 4 still says 'CASE 1: ... .gitignore covers it' and 'If `theirs NOT ignored`, the generated `.gitignore` block is wrong'. Step 5 says 'A dry run writes nothing — no `.gitignore` block'. Step 7's commit message, which will stay in erash11/claude-skills history, says 'the .gitignore block covering third-party links is regenerated on every run (R8-02)'. Someone troubleshooting from these notes or that commit would look in the wrong file, and after R9-02 that is the file the sync must never write.\n  F: Change these references to `.git/info/exclude` (per-machine), and mention the pre-commit hook in the Task 3 commit message.\n\n[LOW] R10-03  docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md (Task 8 Step 1)\n  E: The new default gives piuser a separate primary group (`dscl . -create /Users/piuser PrimaryGroupID 4242`) and then requires that `id piuser` does not list staff(20). On macOS, membership in `staff` for local users usually comes from a nested group (staff nests localaccounts, and every local account belongs to that), not from the primary group. If so, `id piuser` still lists staff(20), `sudo -u piuser` still has staff as a supplementary group, and the step stops every time. The stop is safe, but the chosen default can't reach the boundary. I did not verify this on this machine.\n  F: Before relying on the primary-group change, run `dseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff` or `dscl . -read /Groups/staff NestedGroups`. If staff membership is inherited, make the default boundary a home-permission change the user approves in advance (for example `chmod 750 ~` with a non-staff gro\n\nLIMITATIONS:\n - Static review only. I ran no commands, and I did not rerun the host's reported scratch-repo, hook and sync results; I neither confirm nor dispute them.\n - I did not recompute the plan's SHA256.\n - The R10-01 index behaviour (an already-staged path is not dropped when it is later excluded) comes from how git works in general. I did not run it against this repo.\n - I did not verify macOS `staff` group nesting on this machine (R10-03).\n - I could not inspect the Windows clone, its hook state or its scheduled tasks.\n - I did not read the Pi research note or the spec notes.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e84d3fe4-c3af-4c00-af4b-0373954921c7","session_i