{"parentUuid":"fe8a4ac4-0b48-46f1-b0a7-890aec618a4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezJXEKsUcnvASTVUNg34","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Paused. Nothing is half-done: the last step was a read-only review.\n\n## Where things stand\n\n**Done and pushed:**\n- **Task 1:** snapshots taken and checked by actually restoring them.\n- **Task 2:** stale skills removed from the folder Pi reads (306 → 208). This can be undone.\n\n**Not started:** Tasks 3–8. None of your skill folders, git repos, or the daily backup have been changed beyond Task 2.\n\n**The plan:** `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`, last pushed as `00730b6`.\n\n## What the last review (round 10) found\n\nThe plan is not approved yet. Most earlier fixes held; there are three new findings:\n\n- **Serious:** the new safety hook would silently break the daily backup. The backup ignores a refused commit and still logs \"committed\". The blocked link also stays staged, so every later backup fails with no message.\n- **Minor:** some text still says `.gitignore` where it should say `.git/info/exclude`.\n- **Minor:** the Pi test user may still inherit the `staff` group, so that boundary step would stop every time.\n\nThe fix for the serious one is small: make the backup report a failed commit, and have the sync unstage any third-party link.\n\n## Big picture\n\nThe review found the plan's biggest error: **all 19 linked skills in your skills repo belong to other people** (installed packages). The plan now leaves them alone instead of copying them into your repo. Your own skills: **42**.\n\nTo continue, say **\"resume\"**. I'll fix those three findings, re-review, then start Task 3.\n\nneeds input: Paused at your request after the round-10 review (plan not yet approved; Tasks 1–2 done). Say \"resume\" to fix the three findings and continue."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512301,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":839,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":242},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":512301,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":839,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":512301},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezJXBPWt9ZaKdKzkcikD","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7aec592-774f-4327-91d1-e6519c5491e3","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:04:48.774Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
