{"parentUuid":"ddac4ede-2ca1-4047-81a2-362e03add03e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezJbJnsk8s7P2jGp1AWd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed the real bug: a refused commit gets discarded but still logged as \"committed.\" The nested-groups issue doesn't apply on this Mac, but I'll add the extra check anyway, plus a new warning about `dev-sync` potentially overwriting drifted skill copies before Task 4—now writing up all fixes and round-10 notes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6083,"cache_read_input_tokens":513197,"output_tokens":25598,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":16955},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6083,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":25598,"cache_read_input_tokens":513197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6083,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6083},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezJbHqa2F6htv76ttcr2","type":"assistant","uuid":"f9269006-efa9-4e5a-b8a3-004d06c6093f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:08:53.135Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f9269006-efa9-4e5a-b8a3-004d06c6093f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezJbJnsk8s7P2jGp1AWd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P7NmYgBauKKje9ArnF1MuN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/r10-fixes.txt","content":"%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R8-02 + R9-02: keep git from ever seeing the current canonical links, so the\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R10-01: an exclude only hides UNTRACKED paths. It does not unstage a link an\n# earlier `git add -A` (e.g. the daily backup) already staged, and it does not\n# untrack a tracked link. So drop every third-party link from the index.\n# `git rm --cached` never touches the link on disk and can never re-track\n# anything - unlike `git reset -- <path>`, which restores from HEAD.\nif [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ] && [ -d \"$SRC/.git\" ]; then\n  for name in ${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}; do\n    if git -C \"$SRC\" ls-files --error-unmatch -- \"$name\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n      git -C \"$SRC\" rm --cached --quiet -- \"$name\"\n      echo \"removed third-party link '$name' from the index (left on disk)\"\n    fi\n  done\nfi\n\n# R8-02 + R9-02: keep git from ever seeing the current canonical links, so the\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R8-02 + R9-02: per-machine exclude list in .git/info/exclude - never the\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R10-01: drop every third-party link from the index (an exclude does not\n# unstage an already-staged path). `git rm --cached` leaves the link on disk\n# and can never re-track anything, unlike a reset to HEAD.\nif ((-not $DRY) -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC '.git') -PathType Container)) {\n  foreach ($name in $THIRD_PARTY) {\n    git -C $SRC ls-files --error-unmatch -- $name 2>$null | Out-Null\n    if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {\n      git -C $SRC rm --cached --quiet -- $name 2>$null | Out-Null\n      Write-Host \"removed third-party link '$name' from the index (left on disk)\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n# R8-02 + R9-02: per-machine exclude list in .git/info/exclude - never the\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n  echo \"Fix: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh   (adds them to .git/info/exclude)\" >&2\n  echo \"then: git reset -q -- <path>\" >&2\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n  echo \"Fix: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh\" >&2\n  echo \"     (it removes these links from the index and adds them to .git/info/exclude)\" >&2\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nThe failure is visible, not silent: that day's backup commit fails and surfaces at session start through `.errors.log`; running the sync clears it.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nThe failure is visible, not silent — **but only once Step 5c is done** (R10-01). Before it, `daily-backup.ps1` discarded the commit's exit code and logged `committed` anyway, and a link already staged by `git add -A` stayed staged, so the refusal repeated silently every day. After 5c the refused commit is recorded as `repo-commit:skills` in `.errors.log` (surfaced at session start), and running the sync removes the link from the index and excludes it.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 5c: Make the daily backup report a refused commit (R10-01)**\n\nThe hook from Step 5b only helps if its refusal is seen. Today `daily-backup.ps1` runs `git commit ... 2>&1 | Out-Null`, never checks the exit code, and logs `committed` regardless — so a refused commit adds nothing to `.errors.log`, nothing is pushed, and it repeats every day. The `git push` a few lines below already captures and checks its result; the commit gets the same treatment.\n\nIn `~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1`, inside `function Sync-Repo`, replace:\n\n```powershell\n        if ($dirty -gt 0) {\n            if (-not $DryRun) {\n                git add -A 2>&1 | Out-Null\n                git commit -m (\"chore: daily backup sync {0} [auto]\" -f (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd')) 2>&1 | Out-Null\n            }\n            Log \"REPO $name : $(if ($DryRun) { '[dry-run] would commit' } else { 'committed' }) $dirty change(s)\"\n        }\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```powershell\n        if ($dirty -gt 0) {\n            if ($DryRun) {\n                Log \"REPO $name : [dry-run] would commit $dirty change(s)\"\n            } else {\n                git add -A 2>&1 | Out-Null\n                git diff --cached --quiet 2>$null\n                if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {\n                    # Dirty but nothing stageable (e.g. modified content inside a\n                    # submodule). Not a failure - there is simply nothing to commit.\n                    Log \"REPO $name : $dirty change(s) but nothing stageable - no commit\"\n                } else {\n                    # R10-01: capture and check the commit, as the push below already\n                    # does. A commit refused by a hook (the skills repo's pre-commit\n                    # rejects symlinks) used to be thrown away by Out-Null and logged\n                    # as \"committed\": a silent failure that repeated every day.\n                    $commitOut = git commit -m (\"chore: daily backup sync {0} [auto]\" -f (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd')) 2>&1\n                    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {\n                        $Errors.Add(\"repo-commit:$name\")\n                        Log \"REPO $name : COMMIT FAILED\"\n                        foreach ($l in $commitOut) { if (\"$l\".Trim()) { Log \"REPO $name : COMMIT ERR | $l\" } }\n                        return\n                    }\n                    Log \"REPO $name : committed $dirty change(s)\"\n                }\n            }\n        }\n```\n\nThe `git diff --cached --quiet` check keeps this change from inventing a new daily error. A repo can be dirty with nothing stageable — modified content inside a submodule — and `git commit` then exits 1 with \"nothing to commit\". Before this change that was silently logged as `committed`; now it is logged plainly as no commit, and only a genuine refusal becomes `repo-commit:<repo>`.\n\n`daily-backup.ps1` is tracked by the `dotclaude` repo (`~/.claude`) and shared with Windows, which runs the same file. There is no second live copy (`.bak-*` and `.win-orig` are backups).\n\nProve it against the **real** `Sync-Repo` function, loaded from the edited file without running the backup. Save as `/tmp/backup-commit-test.ps1`:\n\n```powershell\nparam(\n  [string]$ScriptPath = \"$HOME/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1\",\n  [string]$HookPath   = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"\n)\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n$root = '/tmp/bktest'\n$w    = \"$root/work\"\nif (Test-Path -LiteralPath $root) { Write-Host \"remove $root first\"; exit 2 }\n\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path \"$root/origin.git\", $w | Out-Null\ngit init -q --bare \"$root/origin.git\"\ngit -C $w init -q -b main\ngit -C $w config user.email t@t\ngit -C $w config user.name t\nSet-Content -LiteralPath \"$w/owned.md\" -Value 'x'\ngit -C $w add -A\ngit -C $w commit -q -m base\ngit -C $w remote add origin \"$root/origin.git\"\ngit -C $w push -q origin main 2>$null\nCopy-Item -LiteralPath $HookPath -Destination \"$w/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"\n& chmod +x \"$w/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"\n\n# load Sync-Repo from the real script without running the script\n$ast = [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile($ScriptPath, [ref]$null, [ref]$null)\n$fn  = $ast.FindAll({ param($n) $n -is [System.Management.Automation.Language.FunctionDefinitionAst] -and $n.Name -eq 'Sync-Repo' }, $true) | Select-Object -First 1\n. ([scriptblock]::Create($fn.Extent.Text))\n$U       = '/nonexistent'\n$DryRun  = $false\n$Errors  = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()\n$Results = [System.Collections.Generic.List[object]]::new()\n$script:logLines = @()\nfunction Log($m) { $script:logLines += $m; Write-Host \"LOG: $m\" }\n$fail = 0\n\nWrite-Host \"=== T1: a fresh third-party link lands; the backup must REPORT the refusal ===\"\nNew-Item -ItemType SymbolicLink -Path \"$w/newlink\" -Target \"$w/owned.md\" | Out-Null\nSync-Repo $w 'main'\nif (-not ($Errors -contains 'repo-commit:work'))                  { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: no repo-commit:work in errors ($($Errors -join ','))\"; $fail = 1 }\nif (-not ($script:logLines -match 'COMMIT FAILED'))              { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: no COMMIT FAILED log line\"; $fail = 1 }\nif (-not ($script:logLines -match 'refusing to commit symlinks')) { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: hook reason not logged\"; $fail = 1 }\nif ($script:logLines -match ': committed ')                      { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: still logged 'committed'\"; $fail = 1 }\n\nWrite-Host \"=== T2: a normal change still commits and pushes (no regression) ===\"\ngit -C $w rm -q --cached newlink\n[IO.File]::Delete(\"$w/newlink\")\nSet-Content -LiteralPath \"$w/second.md\" -Value 'y'\n$Errors.Clear(); $script:logLines = @()\nSync-Repo $w 'main'\nif ($Errors.Count -ne 0)                        { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: errors $($Errors -join ',')\"; $fail = 1 }\nif (-not ($script:logLines -match ': committed 1 change')) { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: not committed\"; $fail = 1 }\nif (-not ($script:logLines -match ': pushed'))  { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: not pushed\"; $fail = 1 }\n\nif ($fail) { exit 1 }\nWrite-Host \"ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED\"\nexit 0\n```\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/bktest\npwsh -NoProfile -File /tmp/backup-commit-test.ps1; echo \"exit=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `LOG: REPO work : COMMIT FAILED`, the hook's `refusing to commit symlinks` reason logged, then T2's `committed 1 change(s)` and `pushed`, and finally `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED` with `exit=0`.\n\nCommit it to `dotclaude`. The daily backup is still unloaded from Step 0, so nothing races this edit:\n\n```bash\ngit -C ~/.claude status -sb | head -3\ngit -C ~/.claude add scripts/daily-backup.ps1\ngit -C ~/.claude commit -m \"fix(backup): report a refused commit instead of logging 'committed'\n\nSync-Repo discarded git commit's exit code with Out-Null and logged\n'committed' regardless, so a commit refused by a hook (the skills repo's\npre-commit rejects symlinks) failed silently every day. Now captured and\nchecked like the push; a dirty tree with nothing stageable is logged as\nno commit rather than raised as a new error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit -C ~/.claude push\n```\n\nIf the first line shows the branch behind or diverged, reconcile `dotclaude` before committing.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 1: Read both current scripts and record the baseline**\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n**Also do not run `dev-sync` — or `sync-to-codex.sh` by hand — between Task 3's commit and Task 4 Step 3.** Task 3 pushes the new sync script. Its first real run publishes every owned skill's pool entry as a link, which overwrites the two drifted pool copies before Task 4 Step 2 has reconciled them (R9-01). They stay recoverable from `pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz`, but the safe path is to run Tasks 3 and 4 in one sitting.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Read both current scripts and record the baseline**\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nExpected: `19`, the names, and **no** `NOT A LINK` line. A real directory here would be an owned skill that belongs in the index — stop.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nExpected: `19`, the names, and **no** `NOT A LINK` line. A real directory here would be an owned skill that belongs in the index — stop.\n\nIf it prints `0`, a real sync has already run and removed the links from the index itself (R10-01 behaviour). Confirm with `git status --short | grep -c '^D '` (expect `19`), skip the `git rm` below, and go to Step 2 — which will then most likely report no divergence, meaning the drifted pool copies were overwritten and must be recovered from the VIEWS tarball.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n# CASE 1: the link is skipped, its target survives, .gitignore covers it.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# CASE 1: the link is skipped, its target survives, .git/info/exclude covers it.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nIf the canary is gone, a link reached `MANAGED` — stop. If `theirs NOT ignored`, the generated `.gitignore` block is wrong and the next `npx skills add` would be committed by the daily backup.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nIf the canary is gone, a link reached `MANAGED` — stop. If `theirs NOT ignored`, the generated `.git/info/exclude` block is wrong and the next `npx skills add` would be committed by the daily backup.\n\nTwo more cases (R10-01). An exclude does **not** unstage a path that `git add -A` already staged, and does not untrack a tracked link — so the sync must remove every third-party link from the index itself, without touching it on disk:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/syncstage\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills/owned /tmp/syncstage/.agents/skills/pkg /tmp/syncstage/.codex/skills\nprintf -- '---\\nname: owned\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills/owned/SKILL.md\necho pkg > /tmp/syncstage/.agents/skills/pkg/SKILL.md\ncd /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills && git init -q . && git config user.email t@t && git config user.name t\nln -s ../../.agents/skills/pkg old-link\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"baseline: owned skill + a TRACKED link, as the real repo is today\"\n\n# CASE 3: a fresh install lands and the daily backup's `git add -A` stages it.\nln -s ../../.agents/skills/pkg new-link && git add -A\n\nHOME=/tmp/syncstage /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\necho \"--- index (expect owned/SKILL.md only, no 120000) ---\"\ngit ls-files -s | awk '{print $1, $4}'\necho \"--- on disk (expect both links still there) ---\"\nls -l old-link new-link | cut -c1\ngit check-ignore -q new-link && echo \"new-link excluded\"\ngit check-ignore -q old-link && echo \"old-link excluded\"\necho \"--- status (expect D old-link; new-link invisible) ---\"\ngit status --short\n```\n\nExpected: two `removed third-party link ... from the index (left on disk)` lines, `exit=0`; the index holds **only** `owned/SKILL.md`; both links still on disk (`l`, `l`); both excluded; `git status` shows `D  old-link` and nothing for `new-link`. **CASE 3** is the newly staged link being dropped; **CASE 4** is the tracked link being untracked — exactly Task 4's intent — with nothing re-added.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nA dry run writes nothing — no `.gitignore` block and no manifest.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nA dry run writes nothing — no exclude block, no index change, and no manifest.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nvalidated before any removal (R3-02), and the .gitignore block covering\nthird-party links is regenerated on every run (R8-02).\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nvalidated before any removal (R3-02). Third-party links are hidden through\nthe per-machine .git/info/exclude (R9-02) and removed from the index if\nalready staged or tracked (R10-01); a pre-commit hook in this clone refuses\nto commit a symlink (R9-03).\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nCost: on a day a new install lands before a sync, the skills repo's backup commit fails visibly (surfaced at session start); running the sync clears it.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nCost: on a day a new install lands before a sync, the skills repo's backup commit fails visibly as `repo-commit:skills` (surfaced at session start); running the sync removes the staged link and clears it. Both halves of that sentence were false until Task 3 Step 5c (backup checks its commit) and the sync's index cleanup (R10-01).\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nid piuser                        # must NOT list staff(20)\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nid piuser                        # must NOT list staff(20)\ndseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff   # must say piuser is NOT a member (R10-03: also catches nested membership)\ndscl . -read /Groups/staff NestedGroups 2>&1  # checked 2026-09-12 on this Mac: \"No such key\" - staff nests nothing here\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nFixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nFixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee.\n- **Round 10** — Claude (resumed): **REVISE**, 1 high / 2 low (R10-01 – R10-03). All accepted; R10-03's premise checked and found not to hold on this Mac, with its check added anyway. R10-01: the new hook's refusal was invisible — `daily-backup.ps1` discarded the commit exit code and logged \"committed\", and an already-staged link stayed staged — so the backup would have failed silently every day. Fixes: the backup checks its commit (Task 3 Step 5c); the sync removes third-party links from the index with `git rm --cached`, never a reset to HEAD.\n%%%%END%%%%\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6083,"cache_read_input_tokens":513197,"output_tokens":25598,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":16955},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6083,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":25598,"cache_read_input_tokens":513197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6083,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6083},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezJbHqa2F6htv76ttcr2","type":"assistant","uuid":"d4625b17-39c2-4335-855e-7d131f0609c2","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:09:54.108Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d4625b17-39c2-4335-855e-7d131f0609c2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P7NmYgBauKKje9ArnF1MuN","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/r10-fixes.txt (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"c0318d38-df78-4689-a5a3-033711cedfef","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:09:54.418Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/r10-fixes.txt","content":"%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R8-02 + R9-02: keep git from ever seeing the current canonical links, so the\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R10-01: an exclude only hides UNTRACKED paths. It does not unstage a link an\n# earlier `git add -A` (e.g. the daily backup) already staged, and it does not\n# untrack a tracked link. So drop every third-party link from the index.\n# `git rm --cached` never touches the link on disk and can never re-track\n# anything - unlike `git reset -- <path>`, which restores from HEAD.\nif [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ] && [ -d \"$SRC/.git\" ]; then\n  for name in ${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}; do\n    if git -C \"$SRC\" ls-files --error-unmatch -- \"$name\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n      git -C \"$SRC\" rm --cached --quiet -- \"$name\"\n      echo \"removed third-party link '$name' from the index (left on disk)\"\n    fi\n  done\nfi\n\n# R8-02 + R9-02: keep git from ever seeing the current canonical links, so the\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R8-02 + R9-02: per-machine exclude list in .git/info/exclude - never the\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R10-01: drop every third-party link from the index (an exclude does not\n# unstage an already-staged path). `git rm --cached` leaves the link on disk\n# and can never re-track anything, unlike a reset to HEAD.\nif ((-not $DRY) -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC '.git') -PathType Container)) {\n  foreach ($name in $THIRD_PARTY) {\n    git -C $SRC ls-files --error-unmatch -- $name 2>$null | Out-Null\n    if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {\n      git -C $SRC rm --cached --quiet -- $name 2>$null | Out-Null\n      Write-Host \"removed third-party link '$name' from the index (left on disk)\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n# R8-02 + R9-02: per-machine exclude list in .git/info/exclude - never the\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n  echo \"Fix: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh   (adds them to .git/info/exclude)\" >&2\n  echo \"then: git reset -q -- <path>\" >&2\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n  echo \"Fix: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh\" >&2\n  echo \"     (it removes these links from the index and adds them to .git/info/exclude)\" >&2\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nThe failure is visible, not silent: that day's backup commit fails and surfaces at session start through `.errors.log`; running the sync clears it.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nThe failure is visible, not silent — **but only once Step 5c is done** (R10-01). Before it, `daily-backup.ps1` discarded the commit's exit code and logged `committed` anyway, and a link already staged by `git add -A` stayed staged, so the refusal repeated silently every day. After 5c the refused commit is recorded as `repo-commit:skills` in `.errors.log` (surfaced at session start), and running the sync removes the link from the index and excludes it.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 5c: Make the daily backup report a refused commit (R10-01)**\n\nThe hook from Step 5b only helps if its refusal is seen. Today `daily-backup.ps1` runs `git commit ... 2>&1 | Out-Null`, never checks the exit code, and logs `committed` regardless — so a refused commit adds nothing to `.errors.log`, nothing is pushed, and it repeats every day. The `git push` a few lines below already captures and checks its result; the commit gets the same treatment.\n\nIn `~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1`, inside `function Sync-Repo`, replace:\n\n```powershell\n        if ($dirty -gt 0) {\n            if (-not $DryRun) {\n                git add -A 2>&1 | Out-Null\n                git commit -m (\"chore: daily backup sync {0} [auto]\" -f (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd')) 2>&1 | Out-Null\n            }\n            Log \"REPO $name : $(if ($DryRun) { '[dry-run] would commit' } else { 'committed' }) $dirty change(s)\"\n        }\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```powershell\n        if ($dirty -gt 0) {\n            if ($DryRun) {\n                Log \"REPO $name : [dry-run] would commit $dirty change(s)\"\n            } else {\n                git add -A 2>&1 | Out-Null\n                git diff --cached --quiet 2>$null\n                if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {\n                    # Dirty but nothing stageable (e.g. modified content inside a\n                    # submodule). Not a failure - there is simply nothing to commit.\n                    Log \"REPO $name : $dirty change(s) but nothing stageable - no commit\"\n                } else {\n                    # R10-01: capture and check the commit, as the push below already\n                    # does. A commit refused by a hook (the skills repo's pre-commit\n                    # rejects symlinks) used to be thrown away by Out-Null and logged\n                    # as \"committed\": a silent failure that repeated every day.\n                    $commitOut = git commit -m (\"chore: daily backup sync {0} [auto]\" -f (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd')) 2>&1\n                    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {\n                        $Errors.Add(\"repo-commit:$name\")\n                        Log \"REPO $name : COMMIT FAILED\"\n                        foreach ($l in $commitOut) { if (\"$l\".Trim()) { Log \"REPO $name : COMMIT ERR | $l\" } }\n                        return\n                    }\n                    Log \"REPO $name : committed $dirty change(s)\"\n                }\n            }\n        }\n```\n\nThe `git diff --cached --quiet` check keeps this change from inventing a new daily error. A repo can be dirty with nothing stageable — modified content inside a submodule — and `git commit` then exits 1 with \"nothing to commit\". Before this change that was silently logged as `committed`; now it is logged plainly as no commit, and only a genuine refusal becomes `repo-commit:<repo>`.\n\n`daily-backup.ps1` is tracked by the `dotclaude` repo (`~/.claude`) and shared with Windows, which runs the same file. There is no second live copy (`.bak-*` and `.win-orig` are backups).\n\nProve it against the **real** `Sync-Repo` function, loaded from the edited file without running the backup. Save as `/tmp/backup-commit-test.ps1`:\n\n```powershell\nparam(\n  [string]$ScriptPath = \"$HOME/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1\",\n  [string]$HookPath   = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"\n)\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n$root = '/tmp/bktest'\n$w    = \"$root/work\"\nif (Test-Path -LiteralPath $root) { Write-Host \"remove $root first\"; exit 2 }\n\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path \"$root/origin.git\", $w | Out-Null\ngit init -q --bare \"$root/origin.git\"\ngit -C $w init -q -b main\ngit -C $w config user.email t@t\ngit -C $w config user.name t\nSet-Content -LiteralPath \"$w/owned.md\" -Value 'x'\ngit -C $w add -A\ngit -C $w commit -q -m base\ngit -C $w remote add origin \"$root/origin.git\"\ngit -C $w push -q origin main 2>$null\nCopy-Item -LiteralPath $HookPath -Destination \"$w/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"\n& chmod +x \"$w/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"\n\n# load Sync-Repo from the real script without running the script\n$ast = [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile($ScriptPath, [ref]$null, [ref]$null)\n$fn  = $ast.FindAll({ param($n) $n -is [System.Management.Automation.Language.FunctionDefinitionAst] -and $n.Name -eq 'Sync-Repo' }, $true) | Select-Object -First 1\n. ([scriptblock]::Create($fn.Extent.Text))\n$U       = '/nonexistent'\n$DryRun  = $false\n$Errors  = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()\n$Results = [System.Collections.Generic.List[object]]::new()\n$script:logLines = @()\nfunction Log($m) { $script:logLines += $m; Write-Host \"LOG: $m\" }\n$fail = 0\n\nWrite-Host \"=== T1: a fresh third-party link lands; the backup must REPORT the refusal ===\"\nNew-Item -ItemType SymbolicLink -Path \"$w/newlink\" -Target \"$w/owned.md\" | Out-Null\nSync-Repo $w 'main'\nif (-not ($Errors -contains 'repo-commit:work'))                  { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: no repo-commit:work in errors ($($Errors -join ','))\"; $fail = 1 }\nif (-not ($script:logLines -match 'COMMIT FAILED'))              { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: no COMMIT FAILED log line\"; $fail = 1 }\nif (-not ($script:logLines -match 'refusing to commit symlinks')) { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: hook reason not logged\"; $fail = 1 }\nif ($script:logLines -match ': committed ')                      { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: still logged 'committed'\"; $fail = 1 }\n\nWrite-Host \"=== T2: a normal change still commits and pushes (no regression) ===\"\ngit -C $w rm -q --cached newlink\n[IO.File]::Delete(\"$w/newlink\")\nSet-Content -LiteralPath \"$w/second.md\" -Value 'y'\n$Errors.Clear(); $script:logLines = @()\nSync-Repo $w 'main'\nif ($Errors.Count -ne 0)                        { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: errors $($Errors -join ',')\"; $fail = 1 }\nif (-not ($script:logLines -match ': committed 1 change')) { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: not committed\"; $fail = 1 }\nif (-not ($script:logLines -match ': pushed'))  { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: not pushed\"; $fail = 1 }\n\nif ($fail) { exit 1 }\nWrite-Host \"ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED\"\nexit 0\n```\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/bktest\npwsh -NoProfile -File /tmp/backup-commit-test.ps1; echo \"exit=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `LOG: REPO work : COMMIT FAILED`, the hook's `refusing to commit symlinks` reason logged, then T2's `committed 1 change(s)` and `pushed`, and finally `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED` with `exit=0`.\n\nCommit it to `dotclaude`. The daily backup is still unloaded from Step 0, so nothing races this edit:\n\n```bash\ngit -C ~/.claude status -sb | head -3\ngit -C ~/.claude add scripts/daily-backup.ps1\ngit -C ~/.claude commit -m \"fix(backup): report a refused commit instead of logging 'committed'\n\nSync-Repo discarded git commit's exit code with Out-Null and logged\n'committed' regardless, so a commit refused by a hook (the skills repo's\npre-commit rejects symlinks) failed silently every day. Now captured and\nchecked like the push; a dirty tree with nothing stageable is logged as\nno commit rather than raised as a new error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit -C ~/.claude push\n```\n\nIf the first line shows the branch behind or diverged, reconcile `dotclaude` before committing.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- [ ] **Step 1: Read both current scripts and record the baseline**\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n**Also do not run `dev-sync` — or `sync-to-codex.sh` by hand — between Task 3's commit and Task 4 Step 3.** Task 3 pushes the new sync script. Its first real run publishes every owned skill's pool entry as a link, which overwrites the two drifted pool copies before Task 4 Step 2 has reconciled them (R9-01). They stay recoverable from `pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz`, but the safe path is to run Tasks 3 and 4 in one sitting.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Read both current scripts and record the baseline**\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nExpected: `19`, the names, and **no** `NOT A LINK` line. A real directory here would be an owned skill that belongs in the index — stop.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nExpected: `19`, the names, and **no** `NOT A LINK` line. A real directory here would be an owned skill that belongs in the index — stop.\n\nIf it prints `0`, a real sync has already run and removed the links from the index itself (R10-01 behaviour). Confirm with `git status --short | grep -c '^D '` (expect `19`), skip the `git rm` below, and go to Step 2 — which will then most likely report no divergence, meaning the drifted pool copies were overwritten and must be recovered from the VIEWS tarball.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n# CASE 1: the link is skipped, its target survives, .gitignore covers it.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# CASE 1: the link is skipped, its target survives, .git/info/exclude covers it.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nIf the canary is gone, a link reached `MANAGED` — stop. If `theirs NOT ignored`, the generated `.gitignore` block is wrong and the next `npx skills add` would be committed by the daily backup.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nIf the canary is gone, a link reached `MANAGED` — stop. If `theirs NOT ignored`, the generated `.git/info/exclude` block is wrong and the next `npx skills add` would be committed by the daily backup.\n\nTwo more cases (R10-01). An exclude does **not** unstage a path that `git add -A` already staged, and does not untrack a tracked link — so the sync must remove every third-party link from the index itself, without touching it on disk:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/syncstage\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills/owned /tmp/syncstage/.agents/skills/pkg /tmp/syncstage/.codex/skills\nprintf -- '---\\nname: owned\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills/owned/SKILL.md\necho pkg > /tmp/syncstage/.agents/skills/pkg/SKILL.md\ncd /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills && git init -q . && git config user.email t@t && git config user.name t\nln -s ../../.agents/skills/pkg old-link\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"baseline: owned skill + a TRACKED link, as the real repo is today\"\n\n# CASE 3: a fresh install lands and the daily backup's `git add -A` stages it.\nln -s ../../.agents/skills/pkg new-link && git add -A\n\nHOME=/tmp/syncstage /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\necho \"--- index (expect owned/SKILL.md only, no 120000) ---\"\ngit ls-files -s | awk '{print $1, $4}'\necho \"--- on disk (expect both links still there) ---\"\nls -l old-link new-link | cut -c1\ngit check-ignore -q new-link && echo \"new-link excluded\"\ngit check-ignore -q old-link && echo \"old-link excluded\"\necho \"--- status (expect D old-link; new-link invisible) ---\"\ngit status --short\n```\n\nExpected: two `removed third-party link ... from the index (left on disk)` lines, `exit=0`; the index holds **only** `owned/SKILL.md`; both links still on disk (`l`, `l`); both excluded; `git status` shows `D  old-link` and nothing for `new-link`. **CASE 3** is the newly staged link being dropped; **CASE 4** is the tracked link being untracked — exactly Task 4's intent — with nothing re-added.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nA dry run writes nothing — no `.gitignore` block and no manifest.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nA dry run writes nothing — no exclude block, no index change, and no manifest.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nvalidated before any removal (R3-02), and the .gitignore block covering\nthird-party links is regenerated on every run (R8-02).\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nvalidated before any removal (R3-02). Third-party links are hidden through\nthe per-machine .git/info/exclude (R9-02) and removed from the index if\nalready staged or tracked (R10-01); a pre-commit hook in this clone refuses\nto commit a symlink (R9-03).\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nCost: on a day a new install lands before a sync, the skills repo's backup commit fails visibly (surfaced at session start); running the sync clears it.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nCost: on a day a new install lands before a sync, the skills repo's backup commit fails visibly as `repo-commit:skills` (surfaced at session start); running the sync removes the staged link and clears it. Both halves of that sentence were false until Task 3 Step 5c (backup checks its commit) and the sync's index cleanup (R10-01).\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nid piuser                        # must NOT list staff(20)\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nid piuser                        # must NOT list staff(20)\ndseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff   # must say piuser is NOT a member (R10-03: also catches nested membership)\ndscl . -read /Groups/staff NestedGroups 2>&1  # checked 2026-09-12 on this Mac: \"No such key\" - staff nests nothing here\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nFixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nFixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee.\n- **Round 10** — Claude (resumed): **REVISE**, 1 high / 2 low (R10-01 – R10-03). All accepted; R10-03's premise checked and found not to hold on this Mac, with its check added anyway. R10-01: the new hook's refusal was invisible — `daily-backup.ps1` discarded the commit exit code and logged \"committed\", and an already-staged link stayed staged — so the backup would have failed silently every day. Fixes: the backup checks its commit (Task 3 Step 5c); the sync removes third-party links from the index with `git rm --cached`, never a reset to HEAD.\n%%%%END%%%%\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4625b17-39c2-4335-855e-7d131f0609c2","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c0318d38-df78-4689-a5a3-033711cedfef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezJbJnsk8s7P2jGp1AWd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nak7NDNJCGSiDuRzK3PYur","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r10.md","content":"# Round 10 dispositions — all three ACCEPTED\n\n## Premises re-checked on disk\n\n- **R10-01 confirmed.** `~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1`, `function Sync-Repo`:\n  `git add -A 2>&1 | Out-Null` then `git commit ... 2>&1 | Out-Null`, no\n  `$LASTEXITCODE` check, then `Log \"... committed $dirty change(s)\"` in every\n  case. The only repo `$Errors.Add` calls are `repo-missing`, `repo-diverged`,\n  `repo-push`. A refused commit leaves `$ahead` at 0, so nothing is pushed and\n  an OK result is recorded. Single live copy (`.bak-*`, `.win-orig` are\n  backups); tracked by the `dotclaude` repo and shared with Windows.\n- **R10-03 premise does not hold on this Mac.** `dscl . -read /Groups/staff\n  NestedGroups` → `No such key: NestedGroups`. `kristinarash` is in `staff`\n  through primary GID 20, not nesting. So a separate primary group can remove\n  `staff` membership here. The reviewer's check is still added as the gate,\n  since it costs one line and catches nesting if a future macOS adds it.\n\n## Dispositions\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R10-01 | ACCEPTED — both parts | **(a)** New **Task 3 Step 5c** patches `Sync-Repo` to capture `git commit` output, check `$LASTEXITCODE`, add `repo-commit:<repo>`, log each output line, and `return` — matching how the push is already handled. It also runs `git diff --cached --quiet` first, so a dirty tree with nothing stageable (e.g. submodule content) is logged as \"no commit\" instead of becoming a **new** daily error; today that case is silently logged \"committed\". The step includes a pwsh harness that loads the **real** `Sync-Repo` from the edited file via the AST (without running the backup) and asserts, against a scratch repo with a bare origin and the real hook: T1 a fresh link produces `repo-commit:work`, `COMMIT FAILED`, the hook's reason, and no `committed`; T2 a normal change still commits and pushes. Commit goes to `dotclaude` while the backup is still unloaded. **(b)** Both sync scripts now remove every third-party link from the index with `git rm --cached` before writing the exclude block. Deliberately **not** conditioned on HEAD, and **never** `git reset -- <path>`: `rm --cached` leaves the link on disk and cannot re-track anything, which removes the re-tracking risk the reviewer described instead of guarding around it. Task 3 Step 4 gains CASE 3 (newly staged link dropped) and CASE 4 (tracked link untracked, nothing re-added). The hook's message, Task 3 Step 5b and Out of Scope now describe what actually happens. |\n| R10-02 | ACCEPTED | `.gitignore` wording corrected to `.git/info/exclude` in Task 3 Step 4's CASE 1 comment and failure note, Step 5's dry-run sentence (\"no exclude block, no index change, and no manifest\"), and the Task 3 commit message, which now also names the index cleanup and the pre-commit hook. The remaining `.gitignore` mentions are the deliberate \"never the tracked `.gitignore`\" statements and the `git diff --quiet -- .gitignore` assertion. |\n| R10-03 | ACCEPTED (premise not confirmed; check added) | Task 8 Step 1 adds `dseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff`, which must report non-membership, and records that `staff` has no `NestedGroups` on this Mac as of 2026-09-12. |\n\n## Additional gap found by the host while fixing these\n\nTask 3 commits and **pushes** the new sync script, and Task 4 Step 2 reconciles\nthe drifted pool copies. Anything that runs the sync in between — `dev-sync` on\nthis Mac — would publish links over those copies first, the R9-01 loss by\nanother route. They stay recoverable from the VIEWS tarball, but Task 3 Step 0\nnow says not to run `dev-sync` or the sync between Task 3's commit and Task 4\nStep 3. Task 4 Step 1 also handles finding `0` tracked links (a sync already\nran and untracked them under R10-01) and points at the tarball recovery.\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6083,"cache_read_input_tokens":513197,"output_tokens":25598,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":16955},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6083,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":25598,"cache_read_input_tokens":513197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6083,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6083},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezJbHqa2F6htv76ttcr2","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd0ceb26-1c91-4543-beb8-b7cdb7347093","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:10:11.425Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
