uiet` first, so a dirty tree with nothing stageable (e.g. submodule content) is logged as \"no commit\" instead of becoming a **new** daily error; today that case is silently logged \"committed\". The step includes a pwsh harness that loads the **real** `Sync-Repo` from the edited file via the AST (without running the backup) and asserts, against a scratch repo with a bare origin and the real hook: T1 a fresh link produces `repo-commit:work`, `COMMIT FAILED`, the hook's reason, and no `committed`; T2 a normal change still commits and pushes. Commit goes to `dotclaude` while the backup is still unloaded. **(b)** Both sync scripts now remove every third-party link from the index with `git rm --cached` before writing the exclude block. Deliberately **not** conditioned on HEAD, and **never** `git reset -- <path>`: `rm --cached` leaves the link on disk and cannot re-track anything, which removes the re-tracking risk the reviewer described instead of guarding around it. Task 3 Step 4 gains CASE 3 (newly staged link dropped) and CASE 4 (tracked link untracked, nothing re-added). The hook's message, Task 3 Step 5b and Out of Scope now describe what actually happens. |\n| R10-02 | ACCEPTED | `.gitignore` wording corrected to `.git/info/exclude` in Task 3 Step 4's CASE 1 comment and failure note, Step 5's dry-run sentence (\"no exclude block, no index change, and no manifest\"), and the Task 3 commit message, which now also names the index cleanup and the pre-commit hook. The remaining `.gitignore` mentions are the deliberate \"never the tracked `.gitignore`\" statements and the `git diff --quiet -- .gitignore` assertion. |\n| R10-03 | ACCEPTED (premise not confirmed; check added) | Task 8 Step 1 adds `dseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff`, which must report non-membership, and records that `staff` has no `NestedGroups` on this Mac as of 2026-09-12. |\n\n## Additional gap found by the host while fixing these\n\nTask 3 commits and **pushes** the new sync script, and Task 4 Step 2 reconciles\nthe drifted pool copies. Anything that runs the sync in between — `dev-sync` on\nthis Mac — would publish links over those copies first, the R9-01 loss by\nanother route. They stay recoverable from the VIEWS tarball, but Task 3 Step 0\nnow says not to run `dev-sync` or the sync between Task 3's commit and Task 4\nStep 3. Task 4 Step 1 also handles finding `0` tracked links (a sync already\nran and untracked them under R10-01) and points at the tarball recovery.\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dd0ceb26-1c91-4543-beb8-b7cdb7347093","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
