their edits, and the generated ignore list lived in the tracked `.gitignore` shared by both machines, so each machine would have erased the other's entries and brought the committed-symlink bug back. Fixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee.","+- **Round 10** — Claude (resumed): **REVISE**, 1 high / 2 low (R10-01 – R10-03). All accepted; R10-03's premise checked and found not to hold on this Mac, with its check added anyway. R10-01: the new hook's refusal was invisible — `daily-backup.ps1` discarded the commit exit code and logged \"committed\", and an already-staged link stayed staged — so the backup would have failed silently every day. Fixes: the backup checks its commit (Task 3 Step 5c); the sync removes third-party links from the index with `git rm --cached`, never a reset to HEAD."," "," **Gate A was satisfied at round 6 and is now RE-OPENED (R8-06).** Executing Task 1 found facts the plan did not know (AMEND-01, then round 8's R8-01), so the approval no longer binds this hash. Tasks 1–2 ran under the round-6 approval, and their text is unchanged since. Task 3 onward waits for a fresh APPROVED."," "]},{"oldStart":444,"oldLines":6,"newStart":445,"newLines":8,"lines":[" launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.dailybackup.plist"," ```"," ","+**Also do not run `dev-sync` — or `sync-to-codex.sh` by hand — between Task 3's commit and Task 4 Step 3.** Task 3 pushes the new sync script. Its first real run publishes every owned skill's pool entry as a link, which overwrites the two drifted pool copies before Task 4 Step 2 has reconciled them (R9-01). They stay recoverable from `pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz`, but the safe path is to run Tasks 3 and 4 in one sitting.","+"," - [ ] **Step 1: Read both current scripts and record the baseline**"," "," ```bash"]},{"oldStart":548,"oldLines":6,"newStart":551,"newLines":20,"lines":["   done"," done"," ","+# R10-01: an exclude only hides UNTRACKED paths. It does not unstage a link an","+# earlier `git add -A` (e.g. the daily backup) already staged, and it does not","+# untrack a tracked link. So drop every third-party link from the index.","+# `git rm --cached` never touches the link on disk and can never re-track","+# anything - unlike `git reset -- <path>`, which restores from HEAD.","+if [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ] && [ -d \"$SRC/.git\" ]; then","+  for name in ${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}; do","+    if git -C \"$SRC\" ls-files --error-unmatch -- \"$name\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then","+      git -C \"$SRC\" rm --cached --quiet -- \"$name\"","+      echo \"removed third-party link '$name' from the index (left on disk)\"","+    fi","+  done","+fi","+"," # R8-02 + R9-02: keep git from ever seeing the current canonical links, so the"," # daily backup's `git add -A` cannot commit an `npx skills add` link."," #"]},{"oldStart":765,"oldLines":6,"newStart":782,"newLines":19,"lines":["   }"," }"," ","+# R10-01: drop every third-party link from the index (an exclude does not","+# unstage an already-staged path). `git rm --cached` leaves the link on disk","+# and can never re-track anything, unlike a reset to HEAD.","+if ((-not $DRY) -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC '.git') -PathType Container)) {","+  foreach ($name in $THIRD_PARTY) {","+    git -C $SRC ls-files --error-unmatch -- $name 2>$null | Out-Null","+    if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {","+      git -C $SRC rm --cached --quiet -- $name 2>$null | Out-Null","+      Write-Host \"removed third-party link '$name' from the index (left on disk)\"","+    }","+  }","+}","+"," # R8-02 + R9-02: per-machine exclude list in .git/info/exclude - never the"," # tracked .gitignore, which both machines share. Written only when the content"," # changed, with LF endings, so a no-op sync never dirties anything."]},{"oldStart":920,"oldLines":7,"newStart":950,"newLines":7,"lines":[" echo \"canary - must survive\" > /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/theirs/SKILL.md"," ln -s ../../.agents/skills/theirs /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills/theirs"," ","-# CASE 1: the link is skipped, its target survives, .gitignore covers it.","+# CASE 1: the link is skipped, its target survives, .git/info/exclude covers it."," HOME=/tmp/syncguard /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"case1 exit=$?\""," cat /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills/theirs/SKILL.md"," git -C /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills check-ignore -q theirs && echo \"theirs ignored\" || echo \"theirs NOT ignored\""]},{"oldStart":940,"oldLines":7,"newStart":970,"newLines":34,"lines":[" - **case 1** — `canonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 1`, `case1 exit=0`, the canary **still readable**, `theirs ignored`, `mine tracked`."," - **case 2** — `FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill and is now a symlink ...` and `case2 exit=2`. It must be **this** message. `FATAL no skills found` also exits 2, but it means the fixture lost its last owned skill and the guard was never exercised."," ","-If the canary is gone, a link reached `MANAGED` — stop. If `theirs NOT ignored`, the generated `.gitignore` block is wrong and the next `npx skills add` would be committed by the daily backup.","+If the canary is gone, a link reached `MANAGED` — stop. If `theirs NOT ignored`, the generated `.git/info/exclude` block is wrong and the next `npx skills add` would be committed by the daily backup.","+","+Two more cases (R10-01). An exclude does **not** unstage a path that `git add -A` already staged, and does not untrack a tracked link — so the sync must remove every third-party link from the index itself, without touching it on disk:","+","+```bash","+rm -rf /tmp/syncstage","+mkdir -p /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills/owned /tmp/syncstage/.agents/skills/pkg /tmp/syncstage/.codex/skills","+printf -- '---\\nname: owned\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills/owned/SKILL.md","+echo pkg > /tmp/syncstage/.agents/skills/pkg/SKILL.md","+cd /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills && git init -q . && git config user.email t@t && git config user.name t","+ln -s ../../.agents/skills/pkg old-link","+git add -A && git commit -q -m \"baseline: owned skill + a TRACKED link, as the real repo is today\"","+","+# CASE 3: a fresh install lands and the daily backup's `git add -A` stages it.","+ln -s ../../.agents/skills/pkg new-link && git add -A","+","+HOME=/tmp/syncstage /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"","+echo \"--- index (expect owned/SKILL.md only, no 120000) ---\"","+git ls-files -s | awk '{print $1, $4}'","+echo \"--- on disk (expect both links still there) ---\"","+ls -l old-link new-link | cut -c1","+git check-ignore -q new-link && echo \"new-link excluded\"","+git check-ignore -q old-link && echo \"old-link excluded\"","+echo \"--- status (expect D old-link; new-link invisible) ---\"","+git status --short","+```","+","+Expected: two `removed third-party link ... from the index (left on disk)` lines, `exit=0`; the index holds **only** `owned/SKILL.md`; both links still on disk (`l`, `l`); both excluded; `git status` shows `D  old-link` and nothing for `new-link`. **CASE 3** is the newly staged link being dropped; **CASE 4** is the tracked link being untracked — exactly Task 4's intent — with nothing re-added."," "," - [ ] **Step 4b: Prove the canonical-deletion workflow leaves no debris (R5-01)**"," "]},{"oldStart":985,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1042,"newLines":7,"lines":[" DRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\""," ```"," ","-Expected: `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, `would sync` lines, and `exit=0`. A dry run writes nothing — no `.gitignore` block and no manifest.","+Expected: `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, `would sync` lines, and `exit=0`. A dry run writes nothing — no exclude block, no index change, and no manifest."," "," Earlier drafts expected `exit=2` here and needed a task-ordering workaround (round 3's deadlock). That is gone: third-party links are simply not ours, so there is nothing to refuse."," "]},{"oldStart":993,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1050,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," - [ ] **Step 5b: Install the pre-commit hook that refuses symlink commits (R9-03)**"," ","-The exclude list only covers links that existed at the last sync, and the sync runs only inside `dev-sync` while the backup commits every day. So a fresh `npx skills add` is routinely in the tree before any sync has excluded it — the normal case, not an edge case. This hook is the real guarantee: it refuses any commit that **adds or changes** a mode-120000 entry, while still allowing Task 4's **removal** of the 19 tracked links (a deletion's new mode is `000000`). `daily-backup.ps1` does not pass `--no-verify`, so it holds there too. The failure is visible, not silent: that day's backup commit fails and surfaces at session start through `.errors.log`; running the sync clears it.","+The exclude list only covers links that existed at the last sync, and the sync runs only inside `dev-sync` while the backup commits every day. So a fresh `npx skills add` is routinely in the tree before any sync has excluded it — the normal case, not an edge case. This hook is the real guarantee: it refuses any commit that **adds or changes** a mode-120000 entry, while still allowing Task 4's **removal** of the 19 tracked links (a deletion's new mode is `000000`). `daily-backup.ps1` does not pass `--no-verify`, so it holds there too. The failure is visible, not silent — **but only once Step 5c is done** (R10-01). Before it, `daily-backup.ps1` discarded the commit's exit code and logged `committed` anyway, and a link already staged by `git add -A` stayed staged, so the refusal repeated silently every day. After 5c the refused commit is recorded as `repo-commit:skills` in `.errors.log` (surfaced at session start), and running the sync removes the link from the index and excludes it."," "," Hooks live in `.git/hooks`, are per-clone, and are never pushed — Windows needs its own copy when this task is repeated there."," "]},{"oldStart":1016,"oldLines":8,"newStart":1073,"newLines":8,"lines":["   echo \"pre-commit: refusing to commit symlinks (mode 120000):\" >&2","   echo \"$bad\" | sed 's/^/  /' >&2","   echo \"These are third-party skill links - dead on Windows, which pulls this repo.\" >&2","-  echo \"Fix: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh   (adds them to .git/info/exclude)\" >&2","-  echo \"then: git reset -q -- <path>\" >&2","+  echo \"Fix: bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh\" >&2","+  echo \"     (it removes these links from the index and adds them to .git/info/exclude)\" >&2","   exit 1"," fi"," exit 0"]},{"oldStart":1044,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1101,"newLines":143,"lines":[" "," Expected: T1 `0`, T2 `1`, T3 `0`, T4 `1`. This exact sequence was run while writing the plan and produced those results. The baseline commit happens **before** the hook is copied in, exactly as the real repo already tracks 19 links today."," ","+- [ ] **Step 5c: Make the daily backup report a refused commit (R10-01)**","+","+The hook from Step 5b only helps if its refusal is seen. Today `daily-backup.ps1` runs `git commit ... 2>&1 | Out-Null`, never checks the exit code, and logs `committed` regardless — so a refused commit adds nothing to `.errors.log`, nothing is pushed, and it repeats every day. The `git push` a few lines below already captures and checks its result; the commit gets the same treatment.","+","+In `~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1`, inside `function Sync-Repo`, replace:","+","+```powershell","+        if ($dirty -gt 0) {","+            if (-not $DryRun) {","+                git add -A 2>&1 | Out-Null","+                git commit -m (\"chore: daily backup sync {0} [auto]\" -f (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd')) 2>&1 | Out-Null","+            }","+            Log \"REPO $name : $(if ($DryRun) { '[dry-run] would commit' } else { 'committed' }) $dirty change(s)\"","+        }","+```","+","+with:","+","+```powershell","+        if ($dirty -gt 0) {","+            if ($DryRun) {","+                Log \"REPO $name : [dry-run] would commit $dirty change(s)\"","+            } else {","+                git add -A 2>&1 | Out-Null","+                git diff --cached --quiet 2>$null","+                if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {","+                    # Dirty but nothing stageable (e.g. modified content inside a","+                    # submodule). Not a failure - there is simply nothing to commit.","+                    Log \"REPO $name : $dirty change(s) but nothing stageable - no commit\"","+                } else {","+                    # R10-01: capture and check the commit, as the push below already","+                    # does. A commit refused by a hook (the skills repo's pre-commit","+                    # rejects symlinks) used to be thrown away by Out-Null and logged","+                    # as \"committed\": a silent failure that repeated every day.","+                    $commitOut = git commit -m (\"chore: daily backup sync {0} [auto]\" -f (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd')) 2>&1","+                    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {","+                        $Errors.Add(\"repo-commit:$name\")","+                        Log \"REPO $name : COMMIT FAILED\"","+                        foreach ($l in $commitOut) { if (\"$l\".Trim()) { Log \"REPO $name : COMMIT ERR | $l\" } }","+                        return","+                    }","+                    Log \"REPO $name : committed $dirty change(s)\"","+                }","+            }","+        }","+```","+","+The `git diff --cached --quiet` check keeps this change from inventing a new daily error. A repo can be dirty with nothing stageable — modified content inside a submodule — and `git commit` then exits 1 with \"nothing to commit\". Before this change that was silently logged as `committed`; now it is logged plainly as no commit, and only a genuine refusal becomes `repo-commit:<repo>`.","+","+`daily-backup.ps1` is tracked by the `dotclaude` repo (`~/.claude`) and shared with Windows, which runs the same file. There is no second live copy (`.bak-*` and `.win-orig` are backups).","+","+Prove it against the **real** `Sync-Repo` function, loaded from the edited file without running the backup. Save as `/tmp/backup-commit-test.ps1`:","+","+```powershell","+param(","+  [string]$ScriptPath = \"$HOME/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1\",","+  [string]$HookPath   = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"","+)","+$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'","+$root = '/tmp/bktest'","+$w    = \"$root/work\"","+if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $root) { Write-Host \"remove $root first\"; exit 2 }","+","+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path \"$root/origin.git\", $w | Out-Null","+git init -q --bare \"$root/origin.git\"","+git -C $w init -q -b main","+git -C $w config user.email t@t","+git -C $w config user.name t","+Set-Content -LiteralPath \"$w/owned.md\" -Value 'x'","+git -C $w add -A","+git -C $w commit -q -m base","+git -C $w remote add origin \"$root/origin.git\"","+git -C $w push -q origin main 2>$null","+Copy-Item -LiteralPath $HookPath -Destination \"$w/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"","+& chmod +x \"$w/.git/hooks/pre-commit\"","+","+# load Sync-Repo from the real script without running the script","+$ast = [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile($ScriptPath, [ref]$null, [ref]$null)","+$fn  = $ast.FindAll({ param($n) $n -is [System.Management.Automation.Language.FunctionDefinitionAst] -and $n.Name -eq 'Sync-Repo' }, $true) | Select-Object -First 1","+. ([scriptblock]::Create($fn.Extent.Text))","+$U       = '/nonexistent'","+$DryRun  = $false","+$Errors  = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()","+$Results = [System.Collections.Generic.List[object]]::new()","+$script:logLines = @()","+function Log($m) { $script:logLines += $m; Write-Host \"LOG: $m\" }","+$fail = 0","+","+Write-Host \"=== T1: a fresh third-party link lands; the backup must REPORT the refusal ===\"","+New-Item -ItemType SymbolicLink -Path \"$w/newlink\" -Target \"$w/owned.md\" | Out-Null","+Sync-Repo $w 'main'","+if (-not ($Errors -contains 'repo-commit:work'))                  { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: no repo-commit:work in errors ($($Errors -join ','))\"; $fail = 1 }","+if (-not ($script:logLines -match 'COMMIT FAILED'))              { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: no COMMIT FAILED log line\"; $fail = 1 }","+if (-not ($script:logLines -match 'refusing to commit symlinks')) { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: hook reason not logged\"; $fail = 1 }","+if ($script:logLines -match ': committed ')                      { Write-Host \"FAIL T1: still logged 'committed'\"; $fail = 1 }","+","+Write-Host \"=== T2: a normal change still commits and pushes (no regression) ===\"","+git -C $w rm -q --cached newlink","+[IO.File]::Delete(\"$w/newlink\")","+Set-Content -LiteralPath \"$w/second.md\" -Value 'y'","+$Errors.Clear(); $script:logLines = @()","+Sync-Repo $w 'main'","+if ($Errors.Count -ne 0)                        { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: errors $($Errors -join ',')\"; $fail = 1 }","+if (-not ($script:logLines -match ': committed 1 change')) { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: not committed\"; $fail = 1 }","+if (-not ($script:logLines -match ': pushed'))  { Write-Host \"FAIL T2: not pushed\"; $fail = 1 }","+","+if ($fail) { exit 1 }","+Write-Host \"ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED\"","+exit 0","+```","+","+```bash","+rm -rf /tmp/bktest","+pwsh -NoProfile -File /tmp/backup-commit-test.ps1; echo \"exit=$?\"","+```","+","+Expected: `LOG: REPO work : COMMIT FAILED`, the hook's `refusing to commit symlinks` reason logged, then T2's `committed 1 change(s)` and `pushed`, and finally `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED` with `exit=0`.","+","+Commit it to `dotclaude`. The daily backup is still unloaded from Step 0, so nothing races this edit:","+","+```bash","+git -C ~/.claude status -sb | head -3","+git -C ~/.claude add scripts/daily-backup.ps1","+git -C ~/.claude commit -m \"fix(backup): report a refused commit instead of logging 'committed'","+","+Sync-Repo discarded git commit's exit code with Out-Null and logged","+'committed' regardless, so a commit refused by a hook (the skills repo's","+pre-commit rejects symlinks) failed silently every day. Now captured and","+checked like the push; a dirty tree with nothing stageable is logged as","+no commit rather than raised as a new error.","+","+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"","+git -C ~/.claude push","+```","+","+If the first line shows the branch behind or diverged, reconcile `dotclaude` before committing.","+"," - [ ] **Step 6: Verify `daily-backup` will not publish a symlink (R2-03)**"," "," ```bash"]},{"oldStart":1065,"oldLines":8,"newStart":1259,"newLines":10,"lines":[" pointed into ~/.agents/skills (R1). A symlink in canonical is now never"," published, so that cannot happen. Views are generated from every owned"," skill rather than a 7-name allowlist (R2-01), manifest entries are","-validated before any removal (R3-02), and the .gitignore block covering","-third-party links is regenerated on every run (R8-02).","+validated before any removal (R3-02). Third-party links are hidden through","+the per-machine .git/info/exclude (R9-02) and removed from the index if","+already staged or tracked (R10-01); a pre-commit hook in this clone refuses","+to commit a symlink (R9-03)."," "," Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\""," git push"]},{"oldStart":1112,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1308,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," Expected: `19`, the names, and **no** `NOT A LINK` line. A real directory here would be an owned skill that belongs in the index — stop."," ","+If it prints `0`, a real sync has already run and removed the links from the index itself (R10-01 behaviour). Confirm with `git status --short | grep -c '^D '` (expect `19`), skip the `git rm` below, and go to Step 2 — which will then most likely report no divergence, meaning the drifted pool copies were overwritten and must be recovered from the VIEWS tarball.","+"," ```bash"," cd ~/.claude/skills"," git rm --cached --quiet --pathspec-from-file=/tmp/tracked-links.txt"]},{"oldStart":2382,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2580,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial PrimaryGroupID 4242"," sudo dscl . -create /Users/piuser PrimaryGroupID 4242"," id piuser                        # must NOT list staff(20)","+dseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff   # must say piuser is NOT a member (R10-03: also catches nested membership)","+dscl . -read /Groups/staff NestedGroups 2>&1  # checked 2026-09-12 on this Mac: \"No such key\" - staff nests nothing here"," ls -ld ~                         # record owner, group and the group bits"," sudo -u piuser ls ~/DEV          2>&1 | tail -2"," sudo -u piuser ls ~/SecondBrain  2>&1 | tail -2"]},{"oldStart":2585,"oldLines":7,"newStart":2785,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Rewriting plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) — vendored, overwritten on update."," - **All 19 third-party skills linked into `~/.claude/skills/`** — 14 `skills` CLI installs recorded in `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` (five of them from `mattpocock-skills`), the four `vendor-review/claudex-loop` package skills, and `persistent-localhost`. Same rule as plugins: not ours to rewrite, vendor into the repo, or publish to views. **Windows consequence, stated rather than hidden:** they were already tracked as mode-120000 links that are dead on that box; untracking them means the next `dev-sync` pull deletes the dead links. Install the ones wanted on Windows separately (see `vendored-skill-install`). Nothing regresses; the breakage stops being silent."," - **Cleaning the install ledger (R8-05).** About 30 names archived in Task 2 still have entries in `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json`, so the `skills` CLI may think they are installed or try to update them. That file belongs to the CLI; Eric runs `npx skills remove <name>` for each, or accepts the stale entries. No script in this plan edits the ledger.","-- **The install procedure itself (R8-02, R9-03).** `npx skills add ... -a claude-code` keeps creating links in `~/.claude/skills/`, and the procedure is left unchanged. Two layers handle it: the sync adds every current link to the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` on its next run, and — because the sync runs only inside `dev-sync` while the backup commits daily — the **pre-commit hook installed in Task 3 Step 5b** is the actual guarantee. Cost: on a day a new install lands before a sync, the skills repo's backup commit fails visibly (surfaced at session start); running the sync clears it. **Windows** needs the same hook installed in its own clone, since hooks are never pulled.","+- **The install procedure itself (R8-02, R9-03).** `npx skills add ... -a claude-code` keeps creating links in `~/.claude/skills/`, and the procedure is left unchanged. Two layers handle it: the sync adds every current link to the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` on its next run, and — because the sync runs only inside `dev-sync` while the backup commits daily — the **pre-commit hook installed in Task 3 Step 5b** is the actual guarantee. Cost: on a day a new install lands before a sync, the skills repo's backup commit fails visibly as `repo-commit:skills` (surfaced at session start); running the sync removes the staged link and clears it. Both halves of that sentence were false until Task 3 Step 5c (backup checks its commit) and the sync's index cleanup (R10-01). **Windows** needs the same hook installed in its own clone, since hooks are never pulled."," - Pruning the ~150 pool entries that are third-party installs. Task 2 touches only the 98 that match yesterday's archive. The rest need a human decision via `aios-audit`."," - Migrating all 61 hooks to Pi. Task 8 ports exactly one to measure cost."," - **Adopting Pi.** Task 8 produces a cost number only. Adoption needs a boundary design that is its own project."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0b819e8b-a3b8-476d-8757-741020726df9","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
