{"parentUuid":"ebf33ef9-9ab5-46ad-8b5b-36e44b7f2ea7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezK6dRMUrDkf5ePezWhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed both exit codes: the unpatched control fails with all 4 errors (exit 1), while the guard refuses and leaves everything unchanged (exit 2). The plan is committed and pushed (`dfcc7fb`), and next I'll add these results to the round-11 review notes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3866,"cache_read_input_tokens":552811,"output_tokens":1846,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":431},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1846,"cache_read_input_tokens":552811,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3866},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezK6c2247f5v2K5numje","type":"assistant","uuid":"f8121f75-7f92-4d7a-ad65-8cc6cff6a7d2","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:12:16.463Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f8121f75-7f92-4d7a-ad65-8cc6cff6a7d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezK6dRMUrDkf5ePezWhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LHdxFMTaFodMpEAba9HA1F","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r10.md","old_string":"## Rejected\n\nNone.","new_string":"## Executed verification (run, not claimed)\n\nAll code under test was **extracted from the committed plan text**, not\nretyped: the sync script, the hook, the OLD and NEW `Sync-Repo` blocks, and the\nharness. The plan's OLD backup block matched the real `daily-backup.ps1`\nexactly once; the NEW block was applied to a **copy**\n(`/tmp/daily-backup-patched.ps1`). The real file is untouched\n(`git -C ~/.claude diff --quiet -- scripts/daily-backup.ps1` → clean).\n\n**R10-01 (a) — backup harness.** The harness loads the real `Sync-Repo` from the\nfile via the PowerShell AST, so the function itself is under test and the rest\nof the backup does not run. It uses a scratch repo with a bare origin and the\nplan's hook.\n\n| Run | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Patched copy, T1 (fresh link lands) | `COMMIT FAILED`, six `COMMIT ERR` lines carrying the hook's full refusal, `repo-commit:work` recorded, no `committed` |\n| Patched copy, T2 (normal change) | `committed 1 change(s)`, `pushed`, no errors |\n| Patched copy overall | `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, **exit 0** |\n| **Control:** unpatched real file | **exit 1**, all **4** T1 checks FAIL — it logged `committed 1 change(s)` for the refused commit. This proves the bug is real and that the harness detects it. |\n\n**R10-01 (b) — sync index cleanup**, `/bin/bash` 3.2.57. Fixture: an owned skill\nplus a link **tracked in HEAD** (as the real repo is today), then a fresh link\nstaged by `git add -A`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Index before | `120000 new-link`, `120000 old-link`, `100644 owned/SKILL.md` |\n| Sync output | `removed third-party link 'new-link' ...`, `removed third-party link 'old-link' ...`, exit 0 |\n| Index after | **only** `100644 owned/SKILL.md` |\n| On disk | both still links (`l`, `l`) |\n| Exclude | both excluded |\n| `git status` | `D  old-link` only — nothing re-tracked |\n\n**Guard ordering.** The index cleanup runs after the guard, so a refused run\nmust not touch the index. Fixture: a third-party link re-staged (`120000`),\nthen an owned skill turned into a link. Result: **exit 2**, the\n`FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill` message, **0** `removed` lines, and\nthe staged link still `120000` afterwards — \"No changes made\" is true.\n\n**Regressions re-run on the new script:** `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept, tracked\n`.gitignore` unchanged, dangling link excluded, link-target canary intact,\nsecond run printed 0 `updated` lines, deletion workflow outside a repo exits 0\ntwice with 0 dangling links.\n\n**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all 3 shell scripts pass\n`bash -n`; the PowerShell twin, the patched `daily-backup.ps1` and the harness\nall parse under `pwsh`. Stale sweep returns 0 for\n`then: git reset -q -- <path>`, `.gitignore covers it`, ``no `.gitignore` block``,\n`.gitignore block covering`, and `xargs -a`.\n\nA note on method: two exit codes first printed blank because the shell is zsh,\nwhere `PIPESTATUS` does not exist. They were re-captured without a pipe before\nbeing reported here.\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3866,"cache_read_input_tokens":552811,"output_tokens":1846,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":431},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1846,"cache_read_input_tokens":552811,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3866},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezK6c2247f5v2K5numje","type":"assistant","uuid":"8bff958b-fd0f-4711-b64d-5a913b2dc94e","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:12:30.111Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8bff958b-fd0f-4711-b64d-5a913b2dc94e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LHdxFMTaFodMpEAba9HA1F","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r10.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"1e11f19c-1230-48f4-9990-37289a4086ab","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:12:30.666Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r10.md","oldString":"## Rejected\n\nNone.","newString":"## Executed verification (run, not claimed)\n\nAll code under test was **extracted from the committed plan text**, not\nretyped: the sync script, the hook, the OLD and NEW `Sync-Repo` blocks, and the\nharness. The plan's OLD backup block matched the real `daily-backup.ps1`\nexactly once; the NEW block was applied to a **copy**\n(`/tmp/daily-backup-patched.ps1`). The real file is untouched\n(`git -C ~/.claude diff --quiet -- scripts/daily-backup.ps1` → clean).\n\n**R10-01 (a) — backup harness.** The harness loads the real `Sync-Repo` from the\nfile via the PowerShell AST, so the function itself is under test and the rest\nof the backup does not run. It uses a scratch repo with a bare origin and the\nplan's hook.\n\n| Run | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Patched copy, T1 (fresh link lands) | `COMMIT FAILED`, six `COMMIT ERR` lines carrying the hook's full refusal, `repo-commit:work` recorded, no `committed` |\n| Patched copy, T2 (normal change) | `committed 1 change(s)`, `pushed`, no errors |\n| Patched copy overall | `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, **exit 0** |\n| **Control:** unpatched real file | **exit 1**, all **4** T1 checks FAIL — it logged `committed 1 change(s)` for the refused commit. This proves the bug is real and that the harness detects it. |\n\n**R10-01 (b) — sync index cleanup**, `/bin/bash` 3.2.57. Fixture: an owned skill\nplus a link **tracked in HEAD** (as the real repo is today), then a fresh link\nstaged by `git add -A`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Index before | `120000 new-link`, `120000 old-link`, `100644 owned/SKILL.md` |\n| Sync output | `removed third-party link 'new-link' ...`, `removed third-party link 'old-link' ...`, exit 0 |\n| Index after | **only** `100644 owned/SKILL.md` |\n| On disk | both still links (`l`, `l`) |\n| Exclude | both excluded |\n| `git status` | `D  old-link` only — nothing re-tracked |\n\n**Guard ordering.** The index cleanup runs after the guard, so a refused run\nmust not touch the index. Fixture: a third-party link re-staged (`120000`),\nthen an owned skill turned into a link. Result: **exit 2**, the\n`FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill` message, **0** `removed` lines, and\nthe staged link still `120000` afterwards — \"No changes made\" is true.\n\n**Regressions re-run on the new script:** `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept, tracked\n`.gitignore` unchanged, dangling link excluded, link-target canary intact,\nsecond run printed 0 `updated` lines, deletion workflow outside a repo exits 0\ntwice with 0 dangling links.\n\n**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all 3 shell scripts pass\n`bash -n`; the PowerShell twin, the patched `daily-backup.ps1` and the harness\nall parse under `pwsh`. Stale sweep returns 0 for\n`then: git reset -q -- <path>`, `.gitignore covers it`, ``no `.gitignore` block``,\n`.gitignore block covering`, and `xargs -a`.\n\nA note on method: two exit codes first printed blank because the shell is zsh,\nwhere `PIPESTATUS` does not exist. They were re-captured without a pipe before\nbeing reported here.\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.","originalFile":"# Round 10 dispositions — all three ACCEPTED\n\n## Premises re-checked on disk\n\n- **R10-01 confirmed.** `~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1`, `function Sync-Repo`:\n  `git add -A 2>&1 | Out-Null` then `git commit ... 2>&1 | Out-Null`, no\n  `$LASTEXITCODE` check, then `Log \"... committed $dirty change(s)\"` in every\n  case. The only repo `$Errors.Add` calls are `repo-missing`, `repo-diverged`,\n  `repo-push`. A refused commit leaves `$ahead` at 0, so nothing is pushed and\n  an OK result is recorded. Single live copy (`.bak-*`, `.win-orig` are\n  backups); tracked by the `dotclaude` repo and shared with Windows.\n- **R10-03 premise does not hold on this Mac.** `dscl . -read /Groups/staff\n  NestedGroups` → `No such key: NestedGroups`. `kristinarash` is in `staff`\n  through primary GID 20, not nesting. So a separate primary group can remove\n  `staff` membership here. The reviewer's check is still added as the gate,\n  since it costs one line and catches nesting if a future macOS adds it.\n\n## Dispositions\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R10-01 | ACCEPTED — both parts | **(a)** New **Task 3 Step 5c** patches `Sync-Repo` to capture `git commit` output, check `$LASTEXITCODE`, add `repo-commit:<repo>`, log each output line, and `return` — matching how the push is already handled. It also runs `git diff --cached --quiet` first, so a dirty tree with nothing stageable (e.g. submodule content) is logged as \"no commit\" instead of becoming a **new** daily error; today that case is silently logged \"committed\". The step includes a pwsh harness that loads the **real** `Sync-Repo` from the edited file via the AST (without running the backup) and asserts, against a scratch repo with a bare origin and the real hook: T1 a fresh link produces `repo-commit:work`, `COMMIT FAILED`, the hook's reason, and no `committed`; T2 a normal change still commits and pushes. Commit goes to `dotclaude` while the backup is still unloaded. **(b)** Both sync scripts now remove every third-party link from the index with `git rm --cached` before writing the exclude block. Deliberately **not** conditioned on HEAD, and **never** `git reset -- <path>`: `rm --cached` leaves the link on disk and cannot re-track anything, which removes the re-tracking risk the reviewer described instead of guarding around it. Task 3 Step 4 gains CASE 3 (newly staged link dropped) and CASE 4 (tracked link untracked, nothing re-added). The hook's message, Task 3 Step 5b and Out of Scope now describe what actually happens. |\n| R10-02 | ACCEPTED | `.gitignore` wording corrected to `.git/info/exclude` in Task 3 Step 4's CASE 1 comment and failure note, Step 5's dry-run sentence (\"no exclude block, no index change, and no manifest\"), and the Task 3 commit message, which now also names the index cleanup and the pre-commit hook. The remaining `.gitignore` mentions are the deliberate \"never the tracked `.gitignore`\" statements and the `git diff --quiet -- .gitignore` assertion. |\n| R10-03 | ACCEPTED (premise not confirmed; check added) | Task 8 Step 1 adds `dseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff`, which must report non-membership, and records that `staff` has no `NestedGroups` on this Mac as of 2026-09-12. |\n\n## Additional gap found by the host while fixing these\n\nTask 3 commits and **pushes** the new sync script, and Task 4 Step 2 reconciles\nthe drifted pool copies. Anything that runs the sync in between — `dev-sync` on\nthis Mac — would publish links over those copies first, the R9-01 loss by\nanother route. They stay recoverable from the VIEWS tarball, but Task 3 Step 0\nnow says not to run `dev-sync` or the sync between Task 3's commit and Task 4\nStep 3. Task 4 Step 1 also handles finding `0` tracked links (a sync already\nran and untracked them under R10-01) and points at the tarball recovery.\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":33,"oldLines":6,"newStart":33,"newLines":61,"lines":[" Step 3. Task 4 Step 1 also handles finding `0` tracked links (a sync already"," ran and untracked them under R10-01) and points at the tarball recovery."," ","+## Executed verification (run, not claimed)","+","+All code under test was **extracted from the committed plan text**, not","+retyped: the sync script, the hook, the OLD and NEW `Sync-Repo` blocks, and the","+harness. The plan's OLD backup block matched the real `daily-backup.ps1`","+exactly once; the NEW block was applied to a **copy**","+(`/tmp/daily-backup-patched.ps1`). The real file is untouched","+(`git -C ~/.claude diff --quiet -- scripts/daily-backup.ps1` → clean).","+","+**R10-01 (a) — backup harness.** The harness loads the real `Sync-Repo` from the","+file via the PowerShell AST, so the function itself is under test and the rest","+of the backup does not run. It uses a scratch repo with a bare origin and the","+plan's hook.","+","+| Run | Result |","+|---|---|","+| Patched copy, T1 (fresh link lands) | `COMMIT FAILED`, six `COMMIT ERR` lines carrying the hook's full refusal, `repo-commit:work` recorded, no `committed` |","+| Patched copy, T2 (normal change) | `committed 1 change(s)`, `pushed`, no errors |","+| Patched copy overall | `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, **exit 0** |","+| **Control:** unpatched real file | **exit 1**, all **4** T1 checks FAIL — it logged `committed 1 change(s)` for the refused commit. This proves the bug is real and that the harness detects it. |","+","+**R10-01 (b) — sync index cleanup**, `/bin/bash` 3.2.57. Fixture: an owned skill","+plus a link **tracked in HEAD** (as the real repo is today), then a fresh link","+staged by `git add -A`.","+","+| Check | Result |","+|---|---|","+| Index before | `120000 new-link`, `120000 old-link`, `100644 owned/SKILL.md` |","+| Sync output | `removed third-party link 'new-link' ...`, `removed third-party link 'old-link' ...`, exit 0 |","+| Index after | **only** `100644 owned/SKILL.md` |","+| On disk | both still links (`l`, `l`) |","+| Exclude | both excluded |","+| `git status` | `D  old-link` only — nothing re-tracked |","+","+**Guard ordering.** The index cleanup runs after the guard, so a refused run","+must not touch the index. Fixture: a third-party link re-staged (`120000`),","+then an owned skill turned into a link. Result: **exit 2**, the","+`FATAL 'mine' was an owned, published skill` message, **0** `removed` lines, and","+the staged link still `120000` afterwards — \"No changes made\" is true.","+","+**Regressions re-run on the new script:** `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept, tracked","+`.gitignore` unchanged, dangling link excluded, link-target canary intact,","+second run printed 0 `updated` lines, deletion workflow outside a repo exits 0","+twice with 0 dangling links.","+","+**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all 3 shell scripts pass","+`bash -n`; the PowerShell twin, the patched `daily-backup.ps1` and the harness","+all parse under `pwsh`. Stale sweep returns 0 for","+`then: git reset -q -- <path>`, `.gitignore covers it`, ``no `.gitignore` block``,","+`.gitignore block covering`, and `xargs -a`.","+","+A note on method: two exit codes first printed blank because the shell is zsh,","+where `PIPESTATUS` does not exist. They were re-captured without a pipe before","+being reported here.","+"," ## Rejected"," "," None."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8bff958b-fd0f-4711-b64d-5a913b2dc94e","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
