ntouch /tmp/syncstage/.agents/.sync-v2-ready   # R11-01: this scratch HOME counts as prepared\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nrm -rf /tmp/delsync && mkdir -p /tmp/delsync/{.claude/skills,.agents/skills,.codex/skills}\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nrm -rf /tmp/delsync && mkdir -p /tmp/delsync/{.claude/skills,.agents/skills,.codex/skills}\ntouch /tmp/delsync/.agents/.sync-v2-ready   # R11-01: this scratch HOME counts as prepared\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n**CASE 3** is the newly staged link being dropped; **CASE 4** is the tracked link being untracked — exactly Task 4's intent — with nothing re-added.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n**CASE 3** is the newly staged link being dropped; **CASE 4** is the tracked link being untracked — exactly Task 4's intent — with nothing re-added.\n\n**CASE 5 — the first-run gate (R11-01).** An unprepared machine must refuse a real run and change nothing, while a dry run is always allowed:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/syncready\nmkdir -p /tmp/syncready/.claude/skills/owned /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned /tmp/syncready/.codex/skills\nprintf -- '---\\nname: owned\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncready/.claude/skills/owned/SKILL.md\necho \"pool-only edit - must survive\" > /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned/SKILL.md\nHOME=/tmp/syncready DRY_RUN=1 /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh >/dev/null; echo \"dry, no marker: exit=$? (expect 0)\"\nHOME=/tmp/syncready /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real, no marker: exit=$? (expect 2)\"\ncat /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned/SKILL.md\nls /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex 2>/dev/null || echo \"no manifest written\"\n```\n\nExpected: `dry, no marker: exit=0`; `FATAL this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync` and `real, no marker: exit=2`; the pool-only edit **still readable**; `no manifest written`. This is exactly the Windows situation after its next `dev-sync` pull.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\n- The Windows machine. Both machines are active; this plan changes Mac paths only. `sync-to-codex.ps1` is patched in Task 3, but re-running Tasks 2 and 5 there is separate work after these prove out here.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n- **The Windows machine** (R11-01). Both machines are active; this plan executes on the Mac only. Task 3 pushes the rewritten `sync-to-codex.ps1`, and Windows `dev-sync` runs it right after its next pull. It **refuses any real run** there until `~\\.agents\\.sync-v2-ready` exists, so that pull changes nothing and `dev-sync` reports `FATAL this machine is not prepared`. Until Windows is prepared its views stay exactly as they are, and the seven skills the old twin used to copy stop being refreshed there — a visible, deliberate pause, not a silent overwrite. Preparing Windows is its own session: archive `~\\.agents\\skills` and `~\\.codex\\skills`; run Task 4 Step 2's DIVERGED/diff reconcile against that machine's pool; install the Task 3 Step 5b pre-commit hook in its clone; create the marker; then run the sync. The twin avoids native stderr under `ErrorActionPreference=Stop` so it also runs under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (R11-02), but its behaviour there is verified only when that session happens — this Mac has `pwsh` 7 only.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nFixes: the backup checks its commit (Task 3 Step 5c); the sync removes third-party links from the index with `git rm --cached`, never a reset to HEAD.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nFixes: the backup checks its commit (Task 3 Step 5c); the sync removes third-party links from the index with `git rm --cached`, never a reset to HEAD.\n- **Round 11** — Claude (resumed): **REVISE**, 0 high / 1 medium / 1 low (R11-01, R11-02). Reviewer: all three round-10 fixes hold. R11-01: Windows `dev-sync` would run the rewritten twin straight after its next pull and overwrite all 43 published entries with no snapshot or reconcile. Fix: both scripts refuse any real run until a per-machine `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` marker exists, created only after reconciling — which also turns Task 3's \"don't run dev-sync\" warning into an enforced rule on the Mac. R11-02: the twin's index probe no longer writes stderr, which Windows PowerShell 5.1 would treat as fatal.\n%%%%END%%%%\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f027ace0-4ec0-4eef-8f4c-98c4cd54d049","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9fe385aa-b9aa-437a-a314-f19ff85670dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezKG5JrP6mGcm3brAVTE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D5FX1zqnCt5dqcoE5ewQbc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r11.md","content":"# Round 11 dispositions — both ACCEPTED\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R11-01 | ACCEPTED — option (a), applied to **both** scripts | A first-run gate: a real (non-dry) run refuses with exit 2 and changes nothing unless the per-machine marker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` exists. Dry runs are always allowed. The gate sits **before** ownership enumeration, the guard, the index cleanup, the exclude write and the publish, so a refused run touches nothing. In bash it is a plain file test; in the PowerShell twin it uses `Stop-Fatal`, which is defined above it. **Mac:** the marker is created by the new last paragraph of Task 4 Step 2, only after every DIVERGED pool copy has been decided, so Step 3 is the first real run that can succeed. Task 3 Step 0's prose warning (\"do not run dev-sync between Task 3 and Task 4\") is replaced by a description of the enforced behaviour — the R9-01 route via `dev-sync` is now closed by code rather than by instruction. **Windows:** the next `dev-sync` pull gets a refusal instead of an overwrite. The Out of Scope bullet states the consequence plainly — Windows views freeze, and the seven skills the old twin copied stop refreshing there, until a dedicated Windows session archives both views, runs the Task 4 Step 2 reconcile, installs the hook and creates the marker. **Tests:** every scratch-`HOME` fixture in Task 3 Step 4 and Step 4b now creates the marker, and a new **CASE 5** proves an unprepared machine allows a dry run (exit 0) but refuses a real run (exit 2), leaves a pool-only edit intact, and writes no manifest. |\n| R11-02 | ACCEPTED | The twin's index probe is now `$tracked = git -C $SRC ls-files -- $name` and tests for non-empty output. There is no `--error-unmatch` and no `2>$null`. The `git rm --cached` inside the branch runs only for a tracked path, so it writes no stderr, and its `2>$null` is removed too. `#Requires -Version 7` was deliberately **not** added: the twin being replaced ran under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (`powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File`), so requiring 7 would turn every Windows `dev-sync` into a hard failure. Making the script 5.1-safe is the smaller change. The Out of Scope bullet records that 5.1 behaviour is verified only on Windows, since this Mac has `pwsh` 7 only. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2483,"cache_read_input_tokens":558677,"output_tokens":12852,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6883},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2483,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":12852,"cache_read_input_tokens":558677,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2483,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2483},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezKG3ibWYAzYfXhvAKiT","type":"assistant","uuid":"69f971b0-b8f0-4496-876a-96d17e7e11ef","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:16:22.867Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
