\nplan parse: all OK (3 shell scripts)\nbash script has gate: True | twin has gate: True\ntwin --error-unmatch left: 1 | twin 2>$null left: 1\nstale 'Also do not run `dev-sync`': 0\nfixtures ready\n\n######## CASE 5: first-run gate (no marker) ########\ndry, no marker: exit=0 (expect 0)\nreal, no marker: exit=2 (expect 2)\nFATAL this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync (/tmp/t11/ready/.agents/.sync-v2-ready missing).\npool-only edit - must survive\nno manifest written\npool copy untouched (real dir)\n\n######## CASE 1 + regressions (marker present) ########\nrun1 exit=0 (expect 0)\nWARN third-party link 'dangling' is dangling\ncanonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 2\nRESUME kept\n.gitignore unchanged\ntheirs    ignored=yes\ndangling  ignored=yes\nmine      ignored=no\ncanary - must survive\nrun2 exit=0  updated-lines=0  (expect 0 0)\nguard exit=2 (expect 2)\n1\n\n######## CASE 3 + 4: index cleanup ########\nexit=0 (expect 0)\n2\nindex after:\n  100644 owned/SKILL.md\nstatus:\nD  old-link\n\n######## refused run leaves the index alone ########\nrun1 exit=0 (expect 0)\nrefused exit=2 (expect 2)\nremoved-lines=0  pkglink=120000  (expect 0 120000)\n\n######## deletion workflow, no .git, bash 3.2 ########\nfirst=0\nsecond=0\ndangling=0 (expect 0)\n\n######## pwsh twin parse ########\npwsh exit=0 (expect 0)\nWrite-Error CALLS remaining:    0   (expect 0)\nVENDORED remaining:             0   (expect 0)\nStop-Fatal calls:               6\nKEEP_OWNED references:          3\npwsh parse OK","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":22,"oldLines":6,"newStart":22,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **Round 8** — **Claude** as reviewer (the Codex usage limit was reached; Eric approved the switch): **REVISE**, 2 high / 4 medium / 5 low (R8-01 – R8-11). All accepted. R8-01 was the most consequential finding of the whole review: **all 19 outward links are third-party**, so Task 4's inversion script was deleted and ownership became structural instead of a name list. It is the first fix in eight rounds that removed code rather than adding a guard."," - **Round 9** — Claude (resumed session): **REVISE**, 2 high / 2 medium / 3 low (R9-01 – R9-07). All accepted. Both highs came from the round-8 redesign itself: a real sync ran *before* reconciliation and would have overwritten the two pool copies holding the only copy of their edits, and the generated ignore list lived in the tracked `.gitignore` shared by both machines, so each machine would have erased the other's entries and brought the committed-symlink bug back. Fixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee."," - **Round 10** — Claude (resumed): **REVISE**, 1 high / 2 low (R10-01 – R10-03). All accepted; R10-03's premise checked and found not to hold on this Mac, with its check added anyway. R10-01: the new hook's refusal was invisible — `daily-backup.ps1` discarded the commit exit code and logged \"committed\", and an already-staged link stayed staged — so the backup would have failed silently every day. Fixes: the backup checks its commit (Task 3 Step 5c); the sync removes third-party links from the index with `git rm --cached`, never a reset to HEAD.","+- **Round 11** — Claude (resumed): **REVISE**, 0 high / 1 medium / 1 low (R11-01, R11-02). Reviewer: all three round-10 fixes hold. R11-01: Windows `dev-sync` would run the rewritten twin straight after its next pull and overwrite all 43 published entries with no snapshot or reconcile. Fix: both scripts refuse any real run until a per-machine `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` marker exists, created only after reconciling — which also turns Task 3's \"don't run dev-sync\" warning into an enforced rule on the Mac. R11-02: the twin's index probe no longer writes stderr, which Windows PowerShell 5.1 would treat as fatal."," "," **Gate A was satisfied at round 6 and is now RE-OPENED (R8-06).** Executing Task 1 found facts the plan did not know (AMEND-01, then round 8's R8-01), so the approval no longer binds this hash. Tasks 1–2 ran under the round-6 approval, and their text is unchanged since. Task 3 onward waits for a fresh APPROVED."," "]},{"oldStart":445,"oldLines":7,"newStart":446,"newLines":7,"lines":[" launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.dailybackup.plist"," ```"," ","-**Also do not run `dev-sync` — or `sync-to-codex.sh` by hand — between Task 3's commit and Task 4 Step 3.** Task 3 pushes the new sync script. Its first real run publishes every owned skill's pool entry as a link, which overwrites the two drifted pool copies before Task 4 Step 2 has reconciled them (R9-01). They stay recoverable from `pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz`, but the safe path is to run Tasks 3 and 4 in one sitting.","+**Running `dev-sync` between Task 3 and Task 4 is safe, but its sync step will report an error.** Task 3 pushes a sync script whose first real run would overwrite every owned skill's pool entry — including the two drifted copies — before Task 4 Step 2 reconciles them (R9-01). So the script refuses any real run until the per-machine marker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` exists, and that marker is created only at the end of Task 4 Step 2 (R11-01). Until then the sync fails with `FATAL this machine is not prepared` and changes nothing. The same holds on Windows: its first pull of the new script is refused until its own pool is archived and reconciled."," "," - [ ] **Step 1: Read both current scripts and record the baseline**"," "]},{"oldStart":485,"oldLines":6,"newStart":486,"newLines":22,"lines":[" DRY=\"${DRY_RUN:-0}\""," MANIFEST_NAME=\".generated-by-sync-to-codex\""," ","+# R11-01: FIRST-RUN GATE. A real run replaces every owned skill's pool and codex","+# entry with a link (a copy on Windows). A machine must be prepared first - its","+# views archived and its drifted pool copies reconciled (plan Task 4 Step 2 on","+# the Mac; the same steps on Windows) - and marks that with this per-machine","+# file. dev-sync runs this script right after a pull, so without the gate the","+# first run on an unprepared machine overwrites those copies unannounced.","+# Dry runs never write, so they are always allowed.","+READY=\"$HOME/.agents/.sync-v2-ready\"","+if [ \"$DRY\" = \"0\" ] && [ ! -f \"$READY\" ]; then","+  echo \"FATAL this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync ($READY missing).\" >&2","+  echo \"      Archive ~/.agents/skills and ~/.codex/skills and reconcile drifted\" >&2","+  echo \"      pool copies first (plan Task 4 Step 2), then: touch $READY\" >&2","+  echo \"      No changes made. DRY_RUN=1 is always allowed.\" >&2","+  exit 2","+fi","+"," # R8-01: OWNERSHIP IS STRUCTURAL, NOT A LIST."," #"," #   a real directory in ~/.claude/skills  = Eric wrote it   -> ours to publish"]},{"oldStart":746,"oldLines":6,"newStart":763,"newLines":14,"lines":["   exit $code"," }"," ","+# R11-01: first-run gate - see the bash twin. dev-sync runs this right after a","+# pull, so without it the first Windows run would overwrite every owned skill's","+# pool and codex copy with no snapshot and no reconcile.","+$READY = Join-Path $HOME '.agents\\.sync-v2-ready'","+if ((-not $DRY) -and -not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $READY)) {","+  Stop-Fatal \"this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync ($READY missing). Archive ~\\.agents\\skills and ~\\.codex\\skills, reconcile drifted pool copies (plan Task 4 Step 2), then create $READY. No changes made. DRY_RUN=1 is always allowed.\" 2","+}","+"," # R8-01: ownership is structural. A reparse point in canonical was installed"," # by the skills CLI or vendored - never ours - and can never enter MANAGED,"," # which makes deleting through a link impossible by construction."]},{"oldStart":787,"oldLines":9,"newStart":812,"newLines":14,"lines":[" # and can never re-track anything, unlike a reset to HEAD."," if ((-not $DRY) -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $SRC '.git') -PathType Container)) {","   foreach ($name in $THIRD_PARTY) {","-    git -C $SRC ls-files --error-unmatch -- $name 2>$null | Out-Null","-    if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {","-      git -C $SRC rm --cached --quiet -- $name 2>$null | Out-Null","+    # R11-02: no --error-unmatch and no 2>$null. For an untracked path that form","+    # writes to stderr, and in Windows PowerShell 5.1 redirected native stderr","+    # becomes an error record that ends the script under EAP=Stop - before the","+    # exclude block or the views are written. Plain ls-files prints the path","+    # when it is tracked and nothing otherwise, and writes no stderr.","+    $tracked = git -C $SRC ls-files -- $name","+    if ($tracked) {","+      git -C $SRC rm --cached --quiet -- $name | Out-Null","       Write-Host \"removed third-party link '$name' from the index (left on disk)\"","     }","   }"]},{"oldStart":937,"oldLines":6,"newStart":967,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ```bash"," rm -rf /tmp/syncguard"," mkdir -p /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills /tmp/syncguard/.agents/skills /tmp/syncguard/.codex/skills","+touch /tmp/syncguard/.agents/.sync-v2-ready   # R11-01: this scratch HOME counts as prepared"," git -C /tmp/syncguard/.claude/skills init -q"," "," # TWO owned skills and one third-party install. Two, not one: with a single"]},{"oldStart":977,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1008,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ```bash"," rm -rf /tmp/syncstage"," mkdir -p /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills/owned /tmp/syncstage/.agents/skills/pkg /tmp/syncstage/.codex/skills","+touch /tmp/syncstage/.agents/.sync-v2-ready   # R11-01: this scratch HOME counts as prepared"," printf -- '---\\nname: owned\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills/owned/SKILL.md"," echo pkg > /tmp/syncstage/.agents/skills/pkg/SKILL.md"," cd /tmp/syncstage/.claude/skills && git init -q . && git config user.email t@t && git config user.name t"]},{"oldStart":999,"oldLines":12,"newStart":1031,"newLines":28,"lines":[" "," Expected: two `removed third-party link ... from the index (left on disk)` lines, `exit=0`; the index holds **only** `owned/SKILL.md`; both links still on disk (`l`, `l`); both excluded; `git status` shows `D  old-link` and nothing for `new-link`. **CASE 3** is the newly staged link being dropped; **CASE 4** is the tracked link being untracked — exactly Task 4's intent — with nothing re-added."," ","+**CASE 5 — the first-run gate (R11-01).** An unprepared machine must refuse a real run and change nothing, while a dry run is always allowed:","+","+```bash","+rm -rf /tmp/syncready","+mkdir -p /tmp/syncready/.claude/skills/owned /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned /tmp/syncready/.codex/skills","+printf -- '---\\nname: owned\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\n' > /tmp/syncready/.claude/skills/owned/SKILL.md","+echo \"pool-only edit - must survive\" > /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned/SKILL.md","+HOME=/tmp/syncready DRY_RUN=1 /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh >/dev/null; echo \"dry, no marker: exit=$? (expect 0)\"","+HOME=/tmp/syncready /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"real, no marker: exit=$? (expect 2)\"","+cat /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned/SKILL.md","+ls /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex 2>/dev/null || echo \"no manifest written\"","+```","+","+Expected: `dry, no marker: exit=0`; `FATAL this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync` and `real, no marker: exit=2`; the pool-only edit **still readable**; `no manifest written`. This is exactly the Windows situation after its next `dev-sync` pull.","+"," - [ ] **Step 4b: Prove the canonical-deletion workflow leaves no debris (R5-01)**"," "," This is the normal path after someone deletes a skill and `dev-sync` pulls it. Round 5 caught that the generated link goes dangling, `-e` reads false, and the entry gets silently dropped from the manifest — leaving permanent untracked debris the audit could not see."," "," ```bash"," rm -rf /tmp/delsync && mkdir -p /tmp/delsync/{.claude/skills,.agents/skills,.codex/skills}","+touch /tmp/delsync/.agents/.sync-v2-ready   # R11-01: this scratch HOME counts as prepared"," for s in keeper goner; do","   mkdir -p /tmp/delsync/.claude/skills/$s","   printf -- '---\\nname: %s\\ndescription: Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\\n---\\nbody\\n' \"$s\" \\"]},{"oldStart":1351,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1399,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," If the pool copy holds edits worth keeping, copy them **into canonical** (`cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<s>/. ~/.claude/skills/<s>/`) — they are then committed with this task. If canonical wins, do nothing. **Do not skip reading the diffs**: Step 3 discards whatever is left only in the pool. The backup is the recovery path if a call turns out wrong."," ","+Only when every DIVERGED name has been decided, mark this machine prepared. The sync refuses every real run until this file exists (R11-01), so this is the single switch that allows Step 3:","+","+```bash","+touch ~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready && ls -l ~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready","+```","+"," - [ ] **Step 3: First real sync — publish the views and write the per-machine exclude block**"," "," ```bash"]},{"oldStart":2790,"oldLines":5,"newStart":2844,"newLines":5,"lines":[" - Migrating all 61 hooks to Pi. Task 8 ports exactly one to measure cost."," - **Adopting Pi.** Task 8 produces a cost number only. Adoption needs a boundary design that is its own project."," - Deleting any skill outright. Everything moves to an archive folder or is recoverable from git.","-- The Windows machine. Both machines are active; this plan changes Mac paths only. `sync-to-codex.ps1` is patched in Task 3, but re-running Tasks 2 and 5 there is separate work after these prove out here.","+- **The Windows machine** (R11-01). Both machines are active; this plan executes on the Mac only. Task 3 pushes the rewritten `sync-to-codex.ps1`, and Windows `dev-sync` runs it right after its next pull. It **refuses any real run** there until `~\\.agents\\.sync-v2-ready` exists, so that pull changes nothing and `dev-sync` reports `FATAL this machine is not prepared`. Until Windows is prepared its views stay exactly as they are, and the seven skills the old twin used to copy stop being refreshed there — a visible, deliberate pause, not a silent overwrite. Preparing Windows is its own session: archive `~\\.agents\\skills` and `~\\.codex\\skills`; run Task 4 Step 2's DIVERGED/diff reconcile against that machine's pool; install the Task 3 Step 5b pre-commit hook in its clone; create the marker; then run the sync. The twin avoids native stderr under `ErrorActionPreference=Stop` so it also runs under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (R11-02), but its behaviour there is verified only when that session happens — this Mac has `pwsh` 7 only."," - Mining the 414 JSONL sessions to reverse-engineer harness behaviour (video gap #9). Real, but its own project."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md"]}},"classifierMetaLines":"{\"meta\":{\"gitStatus\":{\"clean\":true}}}\n","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9f6fbf5a-375c-4d65-a88b-04bf94dd2dfe","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
