{"parentUuid":"35b96118-b52b-4865-a104-c420211a43eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezKX2c3oAC3vwvRLDibw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E6oMQfd7dQ7wtmj5kDbg2F","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS\ngit add docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md\ngit commit -q -m \"fix: R11-01..R11-02, first-run gate on both sync scripts\n\nClaude review round 11 (0 high):\n- R11-01 Windows dev-sync would run the rewritten twin right after its next\n  pull and overwrite all 43 published entries with no snapshot or reconcile.\n  Both scripts now refuse any real run until the per-machine marker\n  ~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready exists; dry runs are always allowed. On the Mac\n  the marker is created only at the end of Task 4 Step 2, so Task 3's\n  'do not run dev-sync' warning is now enforced by code. Windows views\n  pause visibly until a dedicated prep session.\n- R11-02 the twin's index probe no longer writes native stderr, which\n  Windows PowerShell 5.1 treats as fatal under ErrorActionPreference=Stop.\n\nVerified by running on /bin/bash 3.2: CASE 5 gate (dry 0, real 2, pool-only\nedit survives, no manifest), CASE 1-4, guard, refused-run index unchanged,\ndeletion workflow; pwsh parse of the twin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit log --oneline -1\ngit pull --rebase -q origin main && git push 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Commit and push the round-11 plan fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":967,"cache_read_input_tokens":580755,"output_tokens":1921,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":205},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":967,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0}