{"parentUuid":"006af7e7-8319-4cac-91f1-426bed90566a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezKX2c3oAC3vwvRLDibw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0162vUQBzUQPi5xmeeEVKxrC","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r11.md","old_string":"## Rejected\n\nNone.","new_string":"## Executed verification (run, not claimed)\n\nThe sync script and the PowerShell twin were extracted from the plan after the\nfixes were applied (11 replacements, each matching exactly once). The bash\nscript ran under `/bin/bash` 3.2.57. Exit codes were captured directly, with\noutput redirected to files, so no pipe masked them.\n\n**R11-01 — CASE 5, the first-run gate** (no marker; canonical `owned` skill; a\nreal-directory pool copy holding a pool-only edit):\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `DRY_RUN=1`, no marker | **exit 0** |\n| Real run, no marker | **exit 2**, `FATAL this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync (.../.agents/.sync-v2-ready missing).` |\n| Pool-only edit | still readable: `pool-only edit - must survive` |\n| Manifest | **not written** |\n| Pool copy | still a **real directory**, not replaced by a link |\n\n**Regressions, marker present:**\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| CASE 1 | exit 0, `canonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 2`, dangling link warned and excluded, `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept, tracked `.gitignore` unchanged, `theirs`/`dangling` ignored, `mine` not ignored, canary intact |\n| Idempotence | second run exit 0, **0** `updated` lines |\n| Guard | owned `mine` turned into a link → **exit 2**, owned-became-link FATAL present |\n| CASE 3 + 4 | exit 0, 2 `removed third-party link` lines, index holds only `owned/SKILL.md`, `git status` shows `D  old-link` only |\n| Refused run leaves the index alone | re-staged link `120000` → refused run **exit 2**, **0** `removed` lines, link still `120000` |\n| Deletion workflow, no `.git` | both runs exit 0, 0 dangling links |\n\n**R11-02 / PowerShell twin:** parses under `pwsh` 7 (exit 0). 0 `Write-Error \"` calls, 0 `VENDORED`, 6 `Stop-Fatal` calls (one is the new gate), 3 `KEEP_OWNED`. The only\n`--error-unmatch` and the only `2>$null` in the twin sit on a single **comment** line (twin line 75, the R11-02 explanation), not in code. Windows PowerShell 5.1 behaviour cannot be exercised on this Mac and is recorded as such in Out of Scope.\n\n**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all 3 shell scripts pass `bash -n`; both scripts contain the `sync-v2-ready` gate; the replaced \"Also do not run `dev-sync`\" warning appears 0 times.\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":967,"cache_read_input_tokens":580755,"output_tokens":1921,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":205},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":967,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1921,"cache_read_input_tokens":580755,"cache_creation_input_tokens":967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":967},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezKX1VZmdWepsb7kJ2tQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d3a6852-a703-43d9-9cca-2c089ef83840","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:18:00.022Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"2d3a6852-a703-43d9-9cca-2c089ef83840","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0162vUQBzUQPi5xmeeEVKxrC","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r11.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"4a5d0780-0f29-4277-a0ab-546c1e74ffc4","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:18:00.248Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r11.md","oldString":"## Rejected\n\nNone.","newString":"## Executed verification (run, not claimed)\n\nThe sync script and the PowerShell twin were extracted from the plan after the\nfixes were applied (11 replacements, each matching exactly once). The bash\nscript ran under `/bin/bash` 3.2.57. Exit codes were captured directly, with\noutput redirected to files, so no pipe masked them.\n\n**R11-01 — CASE 5, the first-run gate** (no marker; canonical `owned` skill; a\nreal-directory pool copy holding a pool-only edit):\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `DRY_RUN=1`, no marker | **exit 0** |\n| Real run, no marker | **exit 2**, `FATAL this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync (.../.agents/.sync-v2-ready missing).` |\n| Pool-only edit | still readable: `pool-only edit - must survive` |\n| Manifest | **not written** |\n| Pool copy | still a **real directory**, not replaced by a link |\n\n**Regressions, marker present:**\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| CASE 1 | exit 0, `canonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 2`, dangling link warned and excluded, `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept, tracked `.gitignore` unchanged, `theirs`/`dangling` ignored, `mine` not ignored, canary intact |\n| Idempotence | second run exit 0, **0** `updated` lines |\n| Guard | owned `mine` turned into a link → **exit 2**, owned-became-link FATAL present |\n| CASE 3 + 4 | exit 0, 2 `removed third-party link` lines, index holds only `owned/SKILL.md`, `git status` shows `D  old-link` only |\n| Refused run leaves the index alone | re-staged link `120000` → refused run **exit 2**, **0** `removed` lines, link still `120000` |\n| Deletion workflow, no `.git` | both runs exit 0, 0 dangling links |\n\n**R11-02 / PowerShell twin:** parses under `pwsh` 7 (exit 0). 0 `Write-Error \"` calls, 0 `VENDORED`, 6 `Stop-Fatal` calls (one is the new gate), 3 `KEEP_OWNED`. The only\n`--error-unmatch` and the only `2>$null` in the twin sit on a single **comment** line (twin line 75, the R11-02 explanation), not in code. Windows PowerShell 5.1 behaviour cannot be exercised on this Mac and is recorded as such in Out of Scope.\n\n**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all 3 shell scripts pass `bash -n`; both scripts contain the `sync-v2-ready` gate; the replaced \"Also do not run `dev-sync`\" warning appears 0 times.\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.","originalFile":"# Round 11 dispositions — both ACCEPTED\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R11-01 | ACCEPTED — option (a), applied to **both** scripts | A first-run gate: a real (non-dry) run refuses with exit 2 and changes nothing unless the per-machine marker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` exists. Dry runs are always allowed. The gate sits **before** ownership enumeration, the guard, the index cleanup, the exclude write and the publish, so a refused run touches nothing. In bash it is a plain file test; in the PowerShell twin it uses `Stop-Fatal`, which is defined above it. **Mac:** the marker is created by the new last paragraph of Task 4 Step 2, only after every DIVERGED pool copy has been decided, so Step 3 is the first real run that can succeed. Task 3 Step 0's prose warning (\"do not run dev-sync between Task 3 and Task 4\") is replaced by a description of the enforced behaviour — the R9-01 route via `dev-sync` is now closed by code rather than by instruction. **Windows:** the next `dev-sync` pull gets a refusal instead of an overwrite. The Out of Scope bullet states the consequence plainly — Windows views freeze, and the seven skills the old twin copied stop refreshing there, until a dedicated Windows session archives both views, runs the Task 4 Step 2 reconcile, installs the hook and creates the marker. **Tests:** every scratch-`HOME` fixture in Task 3 Step 4 and Step 4b now creates the marker, and a new **CASE 5** proves an unprepared machine allows a dry run (exit 0) but refuses a real run (exit 2), leaves a pool-only edit intact, and writes no manifest. |\n| R11-02 | ACCEPTED | The twin's index probe is now `$tracked = git -C $SRC ls-files -- $name` and tests for non-empty output. There is no `--error-unmatch` and no `2>$null`. The `git rm --cached` inside the branch runs only for a tracked path, so it writes no stderr, and its `2>$null` is removed too. `#Requires -Version 7` was deliberately **not** added: the twin being replaced ran under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (`powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File`), so requiring 7 would turn every Windows `dev-sync` into a hard failure. Making the script 5.1-safe is the smaller change. The Out of Scope bullet records that 5.1 behaviour is verified only on Windows, since this Mac has `pwsh` 7 only. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":6,"newStart":5,"newLines":40,"lines":[" | R11-01 | ACCEPTED — option (a), applied to **both** scripts | A first-run gate: a real (non-dry) run refuses with exit 2 and changes nothing unless the per-machine marker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` exists. Dry runs are always allowed. The gate sits **before** ownership enumeration, the guard, the index cleanup, the exclude write and the publish, so a refused run touches nothing. In bash it is a plain file test; in the PowerShell twin it uses `Stop-Fatal`, which is defined above it. **Mac:** the marker is created by the new last paragraph of Task 4 Step 2, only after every DIVERGED pool copy has been decided, so Step 3 is the first real run that can succeed. Task 3 Step 0's prose warning (\"do not run dev-sync between Task 3 and Task 4\") is replaced by a description of the enforced behaviour — the R9-01 route via `dev-sync` is now closed by code rather than by instruction. **Windows:** the next `dev-sync` pull gets a refusal instead of an overwrite. The Out of Scope bullet states the consequence plainly — Windows views freeze, and the seven skills the old twin copied stop refreshing there, until a dedicated Windows session archives both views, runs the Task 4 Step 2 reconcile, installs the hook and creates the marker. **Tests:** every scratch-`HOME` fixture in Task 3 Step 4 and Step 4b now creates the marker, and a new **CASE 5** proves an unprepared machine allows a dry run (exit 0) but refuses a real run (exit 2), leaves a pool-only edit intact, and writes no manifest. |"," | R11-02 | ACCEPTED | The twin's index probe is now `$tracked = git -C $SRC ls-files -- $name` and tests for non-empty output. There is no `--error-unmatch` and no `2>$null`. The `git rm --cached` inside the branch runs only for a tracked path, so it writes no stderr, and its `2>$null` is removed too. `#Requires -Version 7` was deliberately **not** added: the twin being replaced ran under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (`powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File`), so requiring 7 would turn every Windows `dev-sync` into a hard failure. Making the script 5.1-safe is the smaller change. The Out of Scope bullet records that 5.1 behaviour is verified only on Windows, since this Mac has `pwsh` 7 only. |"," ","+## Executed verification (run, not claimed)","+","+The sync script and the PowerShell twin were extracted from the plan after the","+fixes were applied (11 replacements, each matching exactly once). The bash","+script ran under `/bin/bash` 3.2.57. Exit codes were captured directly, with","+output redirected to files, so no pipe masked them.","+","+**R11-01 — CASE 5, the first-run gate** (no marker; canonical `owned` skill; a","+real-directory pool copy holding a pool-only edit):","+","+| Check | Result |","+|---|---|","+| `DRY_RUN=1`, no marker | **exit 0** |","+| Real run, no marker | **exit 2**, `FATAL this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync (.../.agents/.sync-v2-ready missing).` |","+| Pool-only edit | still readable: `pool-only edit - must survive` |","+| Manifest | **not written** |","+| Pool copy | still a **real directory**, not replaced by a link |","+","+**Regressions, marker present:**","+","+| Case | Result |","+|---|---|","+| CASE 1 | exit 0, `canonical manifest: 2 entries; third-party links: 2`, dangling link warned and excluded, `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept, tracked `.gitignore` unchanged, `theirs`/`dangling` ignored, `mine` not ignored, canary intact |","+| Idempotence | second run exit 0, **0** `updated` lines |","+| Guard | owned `mine` turned into a link → **exit 2**, owned-became-link FATAL present |","+| CASE 3 + 4 | exit 0, 2 `removed third-party link` lines, index holds only `owned/SKILL.md`, `git status` shows `D  old-link` only |","+| Refused run leaves the index alone | re-staged link `120000` → refused run **exit 2**, **0** `removed` lines, link still `120000` |","+| Deletion workflow, no `.git` | both runs exit 0, 0 dangling links |","+","+**R11-02 / PowerShell twin:** parses under `pwsh` 7 (exit 0). 0 `Write-Error \"` calls, 0 `VENDORED`, 6 `Stop-Fatal` calls (one is the new gate), 3 `KEEP_OWNED`. The only","+`--error-unmatch` and the only `2>$null` in the twin sit on a single **comment** line (twin line 75, the R11-02 explanation), not in code. Windows PowerShell 5.1 behaviour cannot be exercised on this Mac and is recorded as such in Out of Scope.","+","+**Plan-wide:** all embedded python compiles; all 3 shell scripts pass `bash -n`; both scripts contain the `sync-v2-ready` gate; the replaced \"Also do not run `dev-sync`\" warning appears 0 times.","+"," ## Rejected"," "," None."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUI