{"parentUuid":"7ef6ac54-b9b9-481c-b245-f3b2deb736bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezKdMZVB5kaca5VfU4KA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V77f33zciioW4EnbfGp5ek","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/r12-fixes.txt","content":"%%%%OLD%%%%\n# R11-01: FIRST-RUN GATE. A real run replaces every owned skill's pool and codex\n%%%%NEW%%%%\n# R12-01: accept only 0 or 1. Every destructive branch below tests DRY with\n# either = \"0\" or = \"1\", so any other value (DRY_RUN=true, yes, 2) would skip the\n# first-run gate AND still run the publish loop's rm -rf. Refuse it up front.\ncase \"$DRY\" in\n  0|1) ;;\n  *) echo \"FATAL DRY_RUN must be 0 or 1, got '$DRY'. No changes made.\" >&2\n     exit 2 ;;\nesac\n\n# R11-01: FIRST-RUN GATE. A real run replaces every owned skill's pool and codex\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nThis is exactly the Windows situation after its next `dev-sync` pull.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nThis is exactly the Windows situation after its next `dev-sync` pull.\n\n**CASE 5b — a mistyped dry-run flag (R12-01).** Every destructive branch tests `DRY` against `0` or `1`, so any other value must be refused outright rather than fall between the two:\n\n```bash\nHOME=/tmp/syncready DRY_RUN=true /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"DRY_RUN=true: exit=$? (expect 2)\"\ncat /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned/SKILL.md\ntest -L /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned && echo \"pool copy REPLACED - wrong\" || echo \"pool copy untouched\"\n```\n\nExpected: `FATAL DRY_RUN must be 0 or 1, got 'true'`, `exit=2`, the pool-only edit still readable, and `pool copy untouched`. Without the check, this exact command skipped the gate and replaced the pool copy with a link. The PowerShell twin is not affected: it computes `$DRY = $env:DRY_RUN -eq '1'`, so any other value is a real run and meets the gate.\n%%%%END%%%%\n%%%%OLD%%%%\nR11-02: the twin's index probe no longer writes stderr, which Windows PowerShell 5.1 would treat as fatal.\n%%%%NEW%%%%\nR11-02: the twin's index probe no longer writes stderr, which Windows PowerShell 5.1 would treat as fatal.\n- **Round 12** — Claude (resumed): **APPROVED**, 1 low (R12-01): in the bash script a `DRY_RUN` value other than `0`/`1` skipped the first-run gate yet still ran the destructive publish loop. Fixed anyway, because on an unprepared machine it is a data-loss route; the fix changes the plan hash, so round 13 re-confirms before execution.\n%%%%END%%%%\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2112,"cache_read_input_tokens":583950,"output_tokens":4598,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2253},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2112,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4598,"cache_read_input_tokens":583950,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2112},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezKdKwVVbMWnUj2oS9mV","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd1a67c0-31c5-49d4-a5dd-a513b894e19b","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:19:41.924Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
