{"parentUuid":"3f3b373f-4ace-42b2-ab88-acf98951d56f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DsxV8FPqUsyb5jTp4U42Sr","type":"tool_result","content":"applied 3 replacements\nplan parse: all OK (3 shell scripts)\nvalidation precedes gate: True\nfixtures ready\n######## unprepared machine (no marker) ########\nDRY_RUN=true  exit=2  pool=realdir manifest=no  msg=1\nDRY_RUN=yes   exit=2  pool=realdir manifest=no  msg=1\nDRY_RUN=2     exit=2  pool=realdir manifest=no  msg=1\nDRY_RUN=1     exit=0  pool=realdir manifest=no   (expect 0, realdir, no)\nunset (real)  exit=2  pool=realdir manifest=no  gate-msg=1   (expect 2, realdir, no, 1)\npool-only edit - must survive\n\n######## prepared machine (marker present) ########\nDRY_RUN=1     exit=0  pool=realdir manifest=no   (expect 0, realdir, no)\nDRY_RUN=0     exit=0  pool=LINK manifest=yes   (expect 0, LINK, yes)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e46fa2f1-ffec-4077-8fe4-12e8af873955","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:20:35.890Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"applied 3 replacements\nplan parse: all OK (3 shell scripts)\nvalidation precedes gate: True\nfixtures ready\n######## unprepared machine (no marker) ########\nDRY_RUN=true  exit=2  pool=realdir manifest=no  msg=1\nDRY_RUN=yes   exit=2  pool=realdir manifest=no  msg=1\nDRY_RUN=2     exit=2  pool=realdir manifest=no  msg=1\nDRY_RUN=1     exit=0  pool=realdir manifest=no   (expect 0, realdir, no)\nunset (real)  exit=2  pool=realdir manifest=no  gate-msg=1   (expect 2, realdir, no, 1)\npool-only edit - must survive\n\n######## prepared machine (marker present) ########\nDRY_RUN=1     exit=0  pool=realdir manifest=no   (expect 0, realdir, no)\nDRY_RUN=0     exit=0  pool=LINK manifest=yes   (expect 0, LINK, yes)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":23,"oldLines":6,"newStart":23,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **Round 9** — Claude (resumed session): **REVISE**, 2 high / 2 medium / 3 low (R9-01 – R9-07). All accepted. Both highs came from the round-8 redesign itself: a real sync ran *before* reconciliation and would have overwritten the two pool copies holding the only copy of their edits, and the generated ignore list lived in the tracked `.gitignore` shared by both machines, so each machine would have erased the other's entries and brought the committed-symlink bug back. Fixes: reconcile first; per-machine `.git/info/exclude`; a pre-commit hook as the real guarantee."," - **Round 10** — Claude (resumed): **REVISE**, 1 high / 2 low (R10-01 – R10-03). All accepted; R10-03's premise checked and found not to hold on this Mac, with its check added anyway. R10-01: the new hook's refusal was invisible — `daily-backup.ps1` discarded the commit exit code and logged \"committed\", and an already-staged link stayed staged — so the backup would have failed silently every day. Fixes: the backup checks its commit (Task 3 Step 5c); the sync removes third-party links from the index with `git rm --cached`, never a reset to HEAD."," - **Round 11** — Claude (resumed): **REVISE**, 0 high / 1 medium / 1 low (R11-01, R11-02). Reviewer: all three round-10 fixes hold. R11-01: Windows `dev-sync` would run the rewritten twin straight after its next pull and overwrite all 43 published entries with no snapshot or reconcile. Fix: both scripts refuse any real run until a per-machine `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` marker exists, created only after reconciling — which also turns Task 3's \"don't run dev-sync\" warning into an enforced rule on the Mac. R11-02: the twin's index probe no longer writes stderr, which Windows PowerShell 5.1 would treat as fatal.","+- **Round 12** — Claude (resumed): **APPROVED**, 1 low (R12-01): in the bash script a `DRY_RUN` value other than `0`/`1` skipped the first-run gate yet still ran the destructive publish loop. Fixed anyway, because on an unprepared machine it is a data-loss route; the fix changes the plan hash, so round 13 re-confirms before execution."," "," **Gate A was satisfied at round 6 and is now RE-OPENED (R8-06).** Executing Task 1 found facts the plan did not know (AMEND-01, then round 8's R8-01), so the approval no longer binds this hash. Tasks 1–2 ran under the round-6 approval, and their text is unchanged since. Task 3 onward waits for a fresh APPROVED."," "]},{"oldStart":486,"oldLines":6,"newStart":487,"newLines":15,"lines":[" DRY=\"${DRY_RUN:-0}\""," MANIFEST_NAME=\".generated-by-sync-to-codex\""," ","+# R12-01: accept only 0 or 1. Every destructive branch below tests DRY with","+# either = \"0\" or = \"1\", so any other value (DRY_RUN=true, yes, 2) would skip the","+# first-run gate AND still run the publish loop's rm -rf. Refuse it up front.","+case \"$DRY\" in","+  0|1) ;;","+  *) echo \"FATAL DRY_RUN must be 0 or 1, got '$DRY'. No changes made.\" >&2","+     exit 2 ;;","+esac","+"," # R11-01: FIRST-RUN GATE. A real run replaces every owned skill's pool and codex"," # entry with a link (a copy on Windows). A machine must be prepared first - its"," # views archived and its drifted pool copies reconciled (plan Task 4 Step 2 on"]},{"oldStart":1046,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1056,"newLines":16,"lines":[" "," Expected: `dry, no marker: exit=0`; `FATAL this machine is not prepared for the v2 sync` and `real, no marker: exit=2`; the pool-only edit **still readable**; `no manifest written`. This is exactly the Windows situation after its next `dev-sync` pull."," ","+**CASE 5b — a mistyped dry-run flag (R12-01).** Every destructive branch tests `DRY` against `0` or `1`, so any other value must be refused outright rather than fall between the two:","+","+```bash","+HOME=/tmp/syncready DRY_RUN=true /bin/bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"DRY_RUN=true: exit=$? (expect 2)\"","+cat /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned/SKILL.md","+test -L /tmp/syncready/.agents/skills/owned && echo \"pool copy REPLACED - wrong\" || echo \"pool copy untouched\"","+```","+","+Expected: `FATAL DRY_RUN must be 0 or 1, got 'true'`, `exit=2`, the pool-only edit still readable, and `pool copy untouched`. Without the check, this exact command skipped the gate and replaced the pool copy with a link. The PowerShell twin is not affected: it computes `$DRY = $env:DRY_RUN -eq '1'`, so any other value is a real run and meets the gate.","+"," - [ ] **Step 4b: Prove the canonical-deletion workflow leaves no debris (R5-01)**"," "," This is the normal path after someone deletes a skill and `dev-sync` pulls it. Round 5 caught that the generated link goes dangling, `-e` reads false, and the entry gets silently dropped from the manifest — leaving permanent untracked debris the audit could not see."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md"]}},"classifierMetaLines":"{\"meta\":{\"gitStatus\":{\"clean\":true}}}\n","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3f3b373f-4ace-42b2-ab88-acf98951d56f","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
