{"parentUuid":"065434ec-7e73-4d7d-8628-97ccf17a08dd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Z8K4gz6LyMfmYVPaeGesK","type":"tool_result","content":"c85284b fix: R12-01, refuse any DRY_RUN value other than 0 or 1\n   5779c56..c85284b  main -> main","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d1afdc47-c146-44e6-ba06-45ff19a39834","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:20:58.328Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"c85284b fix: R12-01, refuse any DRY_RUN value other than 0 or 1\n   5779c56..c85284b  main -> main","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"gitOperation":{"push":{"branch":"main"}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"065434ec-7e73-4d7d-8628-97ccf17a08dd","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d1afdc47-c146-44e6-ba06-45ff19a39834","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezKkeLiwPM2QG8xCdihx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SqNVEbhcUsTJTcXrefjogC","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r12.md","old_string":"## Scope of this round","new_string":"## Executed verification (run, not claimed)\n\nThe fixed script was extracted from the plan after applying the change (3\nreplacements, each matching exactly once) and run under `/bin/bash` 3.2.57.\nExit codes were captured directly, not through a pipe. All embedded python\ncompiles, all 3 shell scripts pass `bash -n`, and the `case \"$DRY\"` validation\nsits **before** the first-run gate in the script text.\n\nBefore the change, the script tested `DRY` in seven places: lines 32, 111, 133,\n203 and 246 test `= \"0\"`, lines 233 and 261 test `= \"1\"`. That confirms the\nbetween-state the reviewer described.\n\n**Fixed script, unprepared machine** (no marker; pool copy is a real directory\nholding a pool-only edit):\n\n| `DRY_RUN` | exit | pool copy | manifest | message |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `true` | **2** | real dir | no | `FATAL DRY_RUN must be 0 or 1, got 'true'` |\n| `yes` | **2** | real dir | no | same, `got 'yes'` |\n| `2` | **2** | real dir | no | same, `got '2'` |\n| `1` | 0 | real dir | no | dry run |\n| unset (real run) | **2** | real dir | no | `FATAL this machine is not prepared` |\n\nThe pool-only edit still read `pool-only edit - must survive` afterwards.\n\n**Fixed script, prepared machine** (marker present): `DRY_RUN=1` → exit 0, no\nwrites; `DRY_RUN=0` → exit 0, pool copy replaced by a link and manifest written.\nThe normal path is intact.\n\n**Control — the pre-fix script**, extracted with `git show 5779c56:` from the\nlast committed plan (asserted to lack the `case` block), on a fresh unprepared\nfixture with `DRY_RUN=true`: **exit 0**, **no** gate message, pool copy\n**replaced by a link**, the pool-only edit gone (the path now resolves to the\ncanonical file), and no manifest written. The finding reproduced exactly and\nsilently, so the fix and CASE 5b both test something real.\n\n## Scope of this round"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4950,"cache_read_input_tokens":591439,"output_tokens":1873,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":508},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4950,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1873,"cache_read_input_tokens":591439,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4950},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezKkd1MYCshJ6aCwzXmi","type":"assistant","uuid":"639c6a73-e6a4-461d-9d90-b8e0e4d3355e","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:21:04.802Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"639c6a73-e6a4-461d-9d90-b8e0e4d3355e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SqNVEbhcUsTJTcXrefjogC","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r12.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"96aa3221-4417-43f5-af2d-9153026da54b","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:21:04.990Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/aios-dispositions-r12.md","oldString":"## Scope of this round","newString":"## Executed verification (run, not claimed)\n\nThe fixed script was extracted from the plan after applying the change (3\nreplacements, each matching exactly once) and run under `/bin/bash` 3.2.57.\nExit codes were captured directly, not through a pipe. All embedded python\ncompiles, all 3 shell scripts pass `bash -n`, and the `case \"$DRY\"` validation\nsits **before** the first-run gate in the script text.\n\nBefore the change, the script tested `DRY` in seven places: lines 32, 111, 133,\n203 and 246 test `= \"0\"`, lines 233 and 261 test `= \"1\"`. That confirms the\nbetween-state the reviewer described.\n\n**Fixed script, unprepared machine** (no marker; pool copy is a real directory\nholding a pool-only edit):\n\n| `DRY_RUN` | exit | pool copy | manifest | message |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `true` | **2** | real dir | no | `FATAL DRY_RUN must be 0 or 1, got 'true'` |\n| `yes` | **2** | real dir | no | same, `got 'yes'` |\n| `2` | **2** | real dir | no | same, `got '2'` |\n| `1` | 0 | real dir | no | dry run |\n| unset (real run) | **2** | real dir | no | `FATAL this machine is not prepared` |\n\nThe pool-only edit still read `pool-only edit - must survive` afterwards.\n\n**Fixed script, prepared machine** (marker present): `DRY_RUN=1` → exit 0, no\nwrites; `DRY_RUN=0` → exit 0, pool copy replaced by a link and manifest written.\nThe normal path is intact.\n\n**Control — the pre-fix script**, extracted with `git show 5779c56:` from the\nlast committed plan (asserted to lack the `case` block), on a fresh unprepared\nfixture with `DRY_RUN=true`: **exit 0**, **no** gate message, pool copy\n**replaced by a link**, the pool-only edit gone (the path now resolves to the\ncanonical file), and no manifest written. The finding reproduced exactly and\nsilently, so the fix and CASE 5b both test something real.\n\n## Scope of this round","originalFile":"# Round 12 disposition — ACCEPTED (after an APPROVED verdict)\n\nRound 12 returned **APPROVED** with one low finding. It is fixed anyway, because\non an unprepared machine it is a route to exactly the data loss the R11-01 gate\nexists to prevent. Per the plan's own rule, an approval binds only the hash it\nwas issued against, so this round-13 request asks for re-confirmation of a\nsingle, narrow change.\n\n| ID | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| R12-01 | ACCEPTED | `sync-to-codex.sh` validates `DRY` once, **before** the first-run gate: `case \"$DRY\" in 0\\|1) ;; *) FATAL ... exit 2 ;; esac`. Every later branch keeps testing `= \"0\"` or `= \"1\"`. After validation those are the only two possible values, so no value can fall between them. A mistyped flag now refuses with `FATAL DRY_RUN must be 0 or 1, got '<value>'. No changes made.` New **CASE 5b** in Task 3 Step 4 runs `DRY_RUN=true` on the unprepared `/tmp/syncready` fixture and expects exit 2, the pool-only edit intact, and the pool copy still a real directory. **The PowerShell twin is not changed:** it computes `$DRY = $env:DRY_RUN -eq '1'`, a single boolean, so any other value is a real run and is stopped by the gate; there is no between-state. |\n\n## Rejected\n\nNone.\n\n## Scope of this round\n\nOnly the R12-01 lines changed: the `case` block, CASE 5b, and one review-history\nbullet. No other script logic changed.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":6,"newStart":14,"newLines":42,"lines":[" "," None."," ","+## Executed verification (run, not claimed)","+","+The fixed script was extracted from the plan after applying the change (3","+replacements, each matching exactly once) and run under `/bin/bash` 3.2.57.","+Exit codes were captured directly, not through a pipe. All embedded python","+compiles, all 3 shell scripts pass `bash -n`, and the `case \"$DRY\"` validation","+sits **before** the first-run gate in the script text.","+","+Before the change, the script tested `DRY` in seven places: lines 32, 111, 133,","+203 and 246 test `= \"0\"`, lines 233 and 261 test `= \"1\"`. That confirms the","+between-state the reviewer described.","+","+**Fixed script, unprepared machine** (no marker; pool copy is a real directory","+holding a pool-only edit):","+","+| `DRY_RUN` | exit | pool copy | manifest | message |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| `true` | **2** | real dir | no | `FATAL DRY_RUN must be 0 or 1, got 'true'` |","+| `yes` | **2** | real dir | no | same, `got 'yes'` |","+| `2` | **2** | real dir | no | same, `got '2'` |","+| `1` | 0 | real dir | no | dry run |","+| unset (real run) | **2** | real dir | no | `FATAL this machine is not prepared` |","+","+The pool-only edit still read `pool-only edit - must survive` afterwards.","+","+**Fixed script, prepared machine** (marker present): `DRY_RUN=1` → exit 0, no","+writes; `DRY_RUN=0` → exit 0, pool copy replaced by a link and manifest written.","+The normal path is intact.","+","+**Control — the pre-fix script**, extracted with `git show 5779c56:` from the","+last committed plan (asserted to lack the `case` block), on a fresh unprepared","+fixture with `DRY_RUN=true`: **exit 0**, **no** gate message, pool copy","+**replaced by a link**, the pool-only edit gone (the path now resolves to the","+canonical file), and no manifest written. The finding reproduced exactly and","+silently, so the fix and CASE 5b both test something real.","+"," ## Scope of this round"," "," Only the R12-01 lines changed: the `case` block, CASE 5b, and one review-history"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"639c6a73-e6a4-461d-9d90-b8e0e4d3355e","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
