{"parentUuid":"32e86e2e-ff3c-43be-b8e5-91d4d42c90d8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3SjwAqvkANE78ZKPgAfXT","type":"tool_result","content":"=== owned skills whose pool copy is a REAL dir that DIFFERS (Task 4 Step 2 scan) ===\nDIVERGED capture-insight\nDIVERGED claude-stack-doctor\nDIVERGED CreateSkill\nDIVERGED five-slides-generator\nDIVERGED forecast-capture\nDIVERGED graphify\nDIVERGED Harvest\nDIVERGED improve-system\nDIVERGED ingest-book\nDIVERGED ingest-resource\nDIVERGED interview-me\nDIVERGED library-review\nDIVERGED meeting-prep\nDIVERGED meeting-sync\nDIVERGED memory-write\nDIVERGED name-meetings\nDIVERGED pp-fireflies\nDIVERGED project-triage\nDIVERGED Science\nDIVERGED session-miner\nDIVERGED sports-science-research-grounding\nDIVERGED weekly-review\n\n################ memory-write   ( - canonical   + pool ) ################\n--- files that differ ---\nFiles memory-write/SKILL.md and POOL:memory-write/SKILL.md differ\n--- newest mtime each side ---\ncanonical: 2026-09-02 13:57 memory-write/SKILL.md\npool:      2026-08-07 15:08 POOL:memory-write/SKILL.md\n--- unified diff (first 70 lines) ---\ndiff -ru memory-write/SKILL.md POOL:memory-write/SKILL.md\n--- memory-write/SKILL.md\t2026-09-02 13:57:21\n+++ POOL:memory-write/SKILL.md\t2026-08-07 15:08:16\n@@ -1,13 +1,11 @@\n ---\n name: memory-write\n description: >\n-  Writes, updates, removes, and recalls facts in the two-tier memory system at\n-  ~/.claude/global-memory/ and ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/. Use for write\n-  requests such as \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"update memory\", \"save this\",\n-  and \"forget about\", and for recall requests such as \"did we already…?\",\n-  \"what did we decide about X?\", and \"do you remember…?\". For writes, selects\n-  the correct tier and enforces deduplication and character caps. For recall,\n-  checks the injected snapshot first, then follows the memsearch retrieval ladder.\n+  Saves durable facts to the two-tier memory system at ~/.claude/global-memory/ and\n+  ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/. Triggers on \"remember this\", \"note that\",\n+  \"update memory\", \"save this\", \"forget about\". Picks the correct tier (structured\n+  per-project vs global scratchpad), then handles add / replace / remove with dedup\n+  and character-cap enforcement.\n ---\n \n # Memory Write\n@@ -40,63 +38,19 @@\n 3. **Dedup check** — substring scan; if the fact already exists, skip or update in place.\n 4. **Cap check** for Tier B — `wc -c < ~/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md` (or USER.md). If over cap, consolidate (merge similar entries, prune stale) before adding.\n 5. **Write** the change.\n-   - Tier A: create a new file with proper frontmatter (name, description, metadata.type) and add a one-line pointer to that slug's `MEMORY.md` index. `name:` follows the rule below.\n+   - Tier A: create a new file with proper frontmatter (name, description, metadata.type) and add a one-line pointer to that slug's `MEMORY.md` index.\n    - Tier B: append under the correct `##` section.\n 6. **Confirm** in one line: `Saved — will be active from next session.`\n \n-## The `name:` field — bare kebab slug\n-\n-**`name:` = the filename stem minus its leading type token, kebab-cased.** The type\n-already lives in `metadata.type` and the filename already carries the prefix; repeating\n-it in `name:` is the third copy.\n-\n-| File | `name:` |\n-|---|---|\n-| `project_automation-cadence.md` | `automation-cadence` |\n-| `user_sports-teams.md` | `sports-teams` |\n-| `reference_baylor-house-style.md` | `baylor-house-style` |\n-| `feedback_project_idea_capture.md` | `project-idea-capture` |\n-\n-Note the last row: strip only the **leading** token. `feedback_project_idea_capture.md`\n-is a feedback memory *about* project-idea capture — its name keeps the word `project`.\n-\n-`[[links]]` target this bare name, never the filename and never a prefixed variant.\n-\n-This rule exists because it was previously unwritten: an audit on 2026-09-02 found the\n-corpus split 59 bare / 58 prefixed, which broke 37 links. Both forms look right in\n-isolation, so without a stated rule the split regrows on every write.\n-\n ## Actions\n \n - **add** — append (default)\n - **replace** — substring match + swap. Preferred over add when updating an existing fact.\n - **remove** — confirm with the user before deleting.\n \n-## Retrieval — the tiered ladder\n-\n-When the user asks about past context, decisions, or \"did we already…?\", climb in order and stop as soon as the question is answered. Do not run memsearch when the answer is already in the injected snapshot.\n-\n-1. **Tier 0** — scan what is already in context (USER.md, MEMORY.md, today's compiled log). Zero cost.\n-2. **L1** — `memsearch search \"query\" --top-k 5`. Hybrid vector + keyword across all indexed paths: Tier A files (including the retired Windows slugs), daily logs, transcripts.\n-3. **L2** — `memsearch expand <chunk_hash>`. Full markdown section around a hit.\n-4. **L3** — `memsearch transcript <session_id>`. Raw dialogue. Last resort.\n-5. **Fallback** — say \"I don't have a record of that.\"\n-\n-## Daily compiled logs — read-only\n\n################ meeting-sync   ( - canonical   + pool ) ################\n--- files that differ ---\nFiles meeting-sync/SKILL.md and POOL:meeting-sync/SKILL.md differ\n--- newest mtime each side ---\ncanonical: 2026-08-15 13:33 meeting-sync/SKILL.md\npool:      2026-08-07 21:34 POOL:meeting-sync/SKILL.md\n--- unified diff (first 70 lines) ---\ndiff -ru meeting-sync/SKILL.md POOL:meeting-sync/SKILL.md\n--- meeting-sync/SKILL.md\t2026-08-15 13:33:32\n+++ POOL:meeting-sync/SKILL.md\t2026-08-07 21:34:28\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n ---\n name: meeting-sync\n-description: Sync new Fireflies transcripts into the SecondBrain vault; audit vault filenames for drift against Fireflies titles. Idempotent. Use when the user says \"sync meetings\", \"pull latest meetings\", \"/meeting-sync\", \"update meeting notes\", \"any new meetings?\", or when invoked by weekly-review. Also for filename drift — \"are any meeting files misnamed?\", \"did a meeting get renamed after export?\", \"why is this meeting titled differently in Fireflies than in the vault?\", \"audit the meeting filenames\".\n+description: Pulls new Fireflies meeting transcripts into the SecondBrain vault as structured markdown summaries, and audits vault filenames for drift against current Fireflies titles. Idempotent — re-running won't duplicate. Use when the user says \"sync meetings\", \"pull latest meetings\", \"/meeting-sync\", \"update meeting notes\", \"any new meetings?\", or when invoked by the weekly-review skill. Also use for filename drift questions — \"are any meeting files misnamed?\", \"did a meeting get renamed after export?\", \"why is this meeting titled differently in Fireflies than in the vault?\", \"audit the meeting filenames\".\n argument-hint: \"[days-back]\"\n ---\n \n@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@\n ## Paths — shared config\n \n Vault and state-file paths live in `~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json` (single source of truth):\n-- `vault_inbox_meetings` — export target (`/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings`)\n+- `vault_inbox_meetings` — export target (`/Users/kristinarash/Desktop/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings`)\n - `meeting_sync_state_file` — idempotency ledger (`.sync-state.json` in that folder)\n - `meeting_lookback_days` — default window (14)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c7871c41-59a7-4d3f-84e9-703a57d52362","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:25:47.160Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== owned skills whose pool copy is a REAL dir that DIFFERS (Task 4 Step 2 scan) ===\nDIVERGED capture-insight\nDIVERGED claude-stack-doctor\nDIVERGED CreateSkill\nDIVERGED five-slides-generator\nDIVERGED forecast-capture\nDIVERGED graphify\nDIVERGED Harvest\nDIVERGED improve-system\nDIVERGED ingest-book\nDIVERGED ingest-resource\nDIVERGED interv