ten. |\n| 5b | Hook installed after confirming none existed and `core.hooksPath` unset; executable; sha matches plan. Installed hook T1 untrack exit 0, T2 new link exit 1 (reason printed), T3 normal exit 0, T4 file→link exit 1 |\n| 5c | `daily-backup.ps1` patched (plan's OLD block matched the real file exactly once); parses under `pwsh`. Harness on the **real patched file + installed hook**: `COMMIT FAILED` with hook reason recorded, then normal change `committed` + `pushed`, `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, exit 0. Committed to dotclaude **by name only** as `d3e0955` and pushed (11 live session logs left unstaged) |\n| 6 | `git status` in the skills repo showed exactly `M sync-to-codex.ps1` and `M sync-to-codex.sh` |\n| 7 | Committed `8193bb9` and pushed. **The new pre-commit hook allowed it** — first live confirmation that it does not block normal commits |\n\n## Task 4 — premise correction found before execution\n\nTask 4 Step 2 expected \"at least\" `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` to be\nDIVERGED. The scan found **22** owned skills whose pool copy is a real\ndirectory that differs from canonical. The two named in the plan were read in\nfull, and in both the pool copy is an **older version**, not unique work:\n\n- `memory-write` — pool `SKILL.md` dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-09-02. The pool copy lacks the `name:`-slug rule and the retrieval-ladder section that canonical has.\n- `meeting-sync` — pool dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-08-15. The pool copy carries the pre-migration path `/Users/kristinarash/Desktop/SecondBrain/...`.\n\nThe scan also had a gap the plan did not cover: it considered only\ndirectories with a `SKILL.md`. The publish also replaces the pool's `_shared`\nsupport directory and any real directories in `~/.codex/skills` for managed\nnames. Both are now included in the triage and the backup.\n\nThe plan's step logic already handles any number of DIVERGED names, so this is\nrecorded here rather than edited into the approved plan, which keeps its hash\nvalid.","originalFile":"# Gate A — plan approval record — 2026-09-12\n\n**Plan:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`\n**Approved SHA-256:** `71b5242ea6dadac667878bc6d4617facbfaa1958a75975762e2d2da40928c432`\n**Committed as:** `c85284b` (erash11/KeystoneOS)\n**Verdict:** APPROVED, 0 findings — round 13, Claude reviewer (resumed session)\n\nThe approval binds this hash only. This record lives in its own file so that\nmarking Gate A satisfied does not edit the approved plan and silently\ninvalidate its approval. The plan's own line 22 still says \"RE-OPENED\"; this\nfile supersedes that line for the hash above.\n\n## Review history\n\n| Round | Reviewer | Verdict | Findings |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1–6 | Codex | REVISE ×5, then APPROVED | 10 → 9 → 7 → 4 → 1 → 0 |\n| 7 | Codex | REVISE | 5 (vendored-chain amendment found during Task 1) |\n| — | — | — | Codex usage limit reached; Eric approved switching to Claude |\n| 8 | Claude | REVISE | 11 (R8-01: all 19 links are third-party; inversion deleted) |\n| 9 | Claude | REVISE | 7 (reconcile before sync; per-machine exclude; pre-commit hook) |\n| 10 | Claude | REVISE | 3 (backup silently swallowed a refused commit) |\n| 11 | Claude | REVISE | 2, 0 high (Windows first-run gate) |\n| 12 | Claude | APPROVED | 1 low (DRY_RUN typo bypassed the gate) — fixed anyway |\n| 13 | Claude | **APPROVED** | **0** |\n\nReviewer's stated limitations, carried as execution risk: static review only;\nWindows PowerShell 5.1 behaviour unverified; **APPROVED covers the plan text\nonly — Gates B, C and D must still verify the implementation.**\n\n## Pre-flight state at approval (read-only, verified)\n\n| Check | State |\n|---|---|\n| Plan on disk | matches the approved hash; KeystoneOS in sync with origin |\n| `com.keystone.dailybackup` | loaded; **last run exited 1** (the known `repo-diverged` / `manifest-unmanaged` errors) — Task 3 Step 0 unloads it |\n| `~/.claude/skills` | clean, in sync with origin, **19** tracked mode-120000 links, **no** pre-commit hook |\n| `~/.claude` (dotclaude) | in sync with origin; working tree dirty with live session `.jsonl` logs only. Task 3 Step 5c commits `scripts/daily-backup.ps1` **by name**, so those logs are not swept in |\n| Current `sync-to-codex.sh` | 15 lines, 7-name `SHARED`, `rm -rf` + `cp -R` — matches the plan's baseline |\n| Current `sync-to-codex.ps1` | 13 lines, `Remove-Item -Recurse` + `Copy-Item` — matches the plan's baseline |\n| `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` | absent — correct; created only at the end of Task 4 Step 2 |\n\n## Execution so far\n\n- Task 1 — done (`d2e4a3b`)\n- Task 2 — done (`f54c8d9`)\n- Task 3 — starting under this approval\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":44,"oldLines":4,"newStart":44,"newLines":35,"lines":[" "," - Task 1 — done (`d2e4a3b`)"," - Task 2 — done (`f54c8d9`)","-- Task 3 — starting under this approval","+- **Task 3 — done.** Every step verified on the real, installed files:","+","+| Step | Evidence |","+|---|---|","+| 0 | `com.keystone.dailybackup` unloaded (`launchctl list` no longer shows it) |","+| 2–3 | Both scripts installed byte-for-byte from the approved plan (sha256 of each installed file == the staged extract); original mode `0644` kept; `bash -n` OK |","+| 3b | Installed twin parses under `pwsh`: 205 lines, 0 `Write-Error` calls, 6 `Stop-Fatal`, first-run gate and `.git/info/exclude` present |","+| 4 / 4b | Against the **installed** script on `/bin/bash` 3.2: CASE 1 exit 0 (link skipped, canary intact, `theirs` ignored, `mine` tracked); CASE 2 exit 2 (owned-became-link FATAL); CASE 3+4 exit 0 (2 links removed from the index, only `owned/SKILL.md` left, `D old-link`); CASE 5 dry exit 0 / real exit 2 with gate message; CASE 5b `DRY_RUN=true` exit 2, pool copy untouched; deletion workflow exits 0 twice, 0 dangling, archived under `agents` + `codex`, manifest cleaned |","+| 5 | **Real layout**, `DRY_RUN=1`: exit 0, `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, 86 `would sync` lines (43 × 2 views). Fingerprints of index, `info/exclude`, pool listing and codex listing **identical before and after**; `memory-write`/`meeting-sync` still real dirs; no manifest, no marker. Nothing written. |","+| 5b | Hook installed after confirming none existed and `core.hooksPath` unset; executable; sha matches plan. Installed hook T1 untrack exit 0, T2 new link exit 1 (reason printed), T3 normal exit 0, T4 file→link exit 1 |","+| 5c | `daily-backup.ps1` patched (plan's OLD block matched the real file exactly once); parses under `pwsh`. Harness on the **real patched file + installed hook**: `COMMIT FAILED` with hook reason recorded, then normal change `committed` + `pushed`, `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, exit 0. Committed to dotclaude **by name only** as `d3e0955` and pushed (11 live session logs left unstaged) |","+| 6 | `git status` in the skills repo showed exactly `M sync-to-codex.ps1` and `M sync-to-codex.sh` |","+| 7 | Committed `8193bb9` and pushed. **The new pre-commit hook allowed it** — first live confirmation that it does not block normal commits |","+","+## Task 4 — premise correction found before execution","+","+Task 4 Step 2 expected \"at least\" `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` to be","+DIVERGED. The scan found **22** owned skills whose pool copy is a real","+directory that differs from canonical. The two named in the plan were read in","+full, and in both the pool copy is an **older version**, not unique work:","+","+- `memory-write` — pool `SKILL.md` dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-09-02. The pool copy lacks the `name:`-slug rule and the retrieval-ladder section that canonical has.","+- `meeting-sync` — pool dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-08-15. The pool copy carries the pre-migration path `/Users/kristinarash/Desktop/SecondBrain/...`.","+","+The scan also had a gap the plan did not cover: it considered only","+directories with a `SKILL.md`. The publish also replaces the pool's `_shared`","+support directory and any real direct