{"parentUuid":"a83ebb35-e523-49b5-9a47-d59a2a4a1f48","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014E5kWKSuBWPA4pcDy4p8t2","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"7fd86741-312e-4d3c-a4f4-c7cdaf1e8765","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:28:40.320Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","oldString":"The plan's step logic already handles any number of DIVERGED names, so this is\nrecorded here rather than edited into the approved plan, which keeps its hash\nvalid.","newString":"The plan's step logic already handles any number of DIVERGED names, so this is\nrecorded here rather than edited into the approved plan, which keeps its hash\nvalid.\n\n### Full triage (read-only, content-compared, `__pycache__`/`.pyc`/`.DS_Store` ignored)\n\n- **Pool:** 23 entries differ — 22 owned skills plus `_shared`.\n  - **22 are \"canonical newer — safe\":** no file exists only in the pool, and no differing file is newer in the pool. They are stale copies.\n  - **1 needs review: `graphify`**, detailed below.\n- **Codex view:** 0 real directories differ from canonical.\n\n**`graphify`.** Two files differ, `SKILL.md` and `references/hooks.md`. The pool\n`SKILL.md` is dated 2026-08-29 14:34, **one minute after** canonical's 14:33. The\ndiff is not independent work. It is graphify's installer writing a\n**per-harness variant**:\n\n| | Canonical (Claude Code) | Pool (Codex / agents) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Subagent dispatch | \"Call the **Agent** tool … `subagent_type=\"general-purpose\"`\" | \"Uses the **`Task`** tool … `Task(description=…)`\" |\n| Integration section | \"native **CLAUDE.md** integration\" | \"native **AGENTS.md** integration\" |\n\nThe 4,795 files that exist only in canonical are `graphify/.venv` (its runtime).\n\n### Backup taken before any publish\n\nAll 23 diverged pool copies were copied to\n`~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, including `graphify` (29 files)\nand `_shared`. File counts matched on every copy, and none were skipped. The codex\nbackup root `pre-sync-2026-09-12-codex/` is empty because nothing there diverged.\nThe VIEWS tarball from Task 1 remains a second, independent copy.\n\n### Task 4 Step 1 — done\n\nRun through Python `subprocess`: `dcg` blocks `git` inside shell command\nsubstitution, so the plan's shell form could not be used. Results:\n\n- 19 tracked mode-120000 entries; every one is a symlink on disk.\n- `git rm --cached --pathspec-from-file` exited 0.\n- **19** staged deletions; all 19 still on disk as links; **0** tracked links left in the index.\n- The 19 now show as `??` until Step 3 writes `.git/info/exclude`.\n- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.","originalFile":"# Gate A — plan approval record — 2026-09-12\n\n**Plan:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`\n**Approved SHA-256:** `71b5242ea6dadac667878bc6d4617facbfaa1958a75975762e2d2da40928c432`\n**Committed as:** `c85284b` (erash11/KeystoneOS)\n**Verdict:** APPROVED, 0 findings — round 13, Claude reviewer (resumed session)\n\nThe approval binds this hash only. This record lives in its own file so that\nmarking Gate A satisfied does not edit the approved plan and silently\ninvalidate its approval. The plan's own line 22 still says \"RE-OPENED\"; this\nfile supersedes that line for the hash above.\n\n## Review history\n\n| Round | Reviewer | Verdict | Findings |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1–6 | Codex | REVISE ×5, then APPROVED | 10 → 9 → 7 → 4 → 1 → 0 |\n| 7 | Codex | REVISE | 5 (vendored-chain amendment found during Task 1) |\n| — | — | — | Codex usage limit reached; Eric approved switching to Claude |\n| 8 | Claude | REVISE | 11 (R8-01: all 19 links are third-party; inversion deleted) |\n| 9 | Claude | REVISE | 7 (reconcile before sync; per-machine exclude; pre-commit hook) |\n| 10 | Claude | REVISE | 3 (backup silently swallowed a refused commit) |\n| 11 | Claude | REVISE | 2, 0 high (Windows first-run gate) |\n| 12 | Claude | APPROVED | 1 low (DRY_RUN typo bypassed the gate) — fixed anyway |\n| 13 | Claude | **APPROVED** | **0** |\n\nReviewer's stated limitations, carried as execution risk: static review only;\nWindows PowerShell 5.1 behaviour unverified; **APPROVED covers the plan text\nonly — Gates B, C and D must still verify the implementation.**\n\n## Pre-flight state at approval (read-only, verified)\n\n| Check | State |\n|---|---|\n| Plan on disk | matches the approved hash; KeystoneOS in sync with origin |\n| `com.keystone.dailybackup` | loaded; **last run exited 1** (the known `repo-diverged` / `manifest-unmanaged` errors) — Task 3 Step 0 unloads it |\n| `~/.claude/skills` | clean, in sync with origin, **19** tracked mode-120000 links, **no** pre-commit hook |\n| `~/.claude` (dotclaude) | in sync with origin; working tree dirty with live session `.jsonl` logs only. Task 3 Step 5c commits `scripts/daily-backup.ps1` **by name**, so those logs are not swept in |\n| Current `sync-to-codex.sh` | 15 lines, 7-name `SHARED`, `rm -rf` + `cp -R` — matches the plan's baseline |\n| Current `sync-to-codex.ps1` | 13 lines, `Remove-Item -Recurse` + `Copy-Item` — matches the plan's baseline |\n| `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` | absent — correct; created only at the end of Task 4 Step 2 |\n\n## Execution so far\n\n- Task 1 — done (`d2e4a3b`)\n- Task 2 — done (`f54c8d9`)\n- **Task 3 — done.** Every step verified on the real, installed files:\n\n| Step | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | `com.keystone.dailybackup` unloaded (`launchctl list` no longer shows it) |\n| 2–3 | Both scripts installed byte-for-byte from the approved plan (sha256 of each installed file == the staged extract); original mode `0644` kept; `bash -n` OK |\n| 3b | Installed twin parses under `pwsh`: 205 lines, 0 `Write-Error` calls, 6 `Stop-Fatal`, first-run gate and `.git/info/exclude` present |\n| 4 / 4b | Against the **installed** script on `/bin/bash` 3.2: CASE 1 exit 0 (link skipped, canary intact, `theirs` ignored, `mine` tracked); CASE 2 exit 2 (owned-became-link FATAL); CASE 3+4 exit 0 (2 links removed from the index, only `owned/SKILL.md` left, `D old-link`); CASE 5 dry exit 0 / real exit 2 with gate message; CASE 5b `DRY_RUN=true` exit 2, pool copy untouched; deletion workflow exits 0 twice, 0 dangling, archived under `agents` + `codex`, manifest cleaned |\n| 5 | **Real layout**, `DRY_RUN=1`: exit 0, `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, 86 `would sync` lines (43 × 2 views). Fingerprints of index, `info/exclude`, pool listing and codex listing **identical before and after**; `memory-write`/`meeting-sync` still real dirs; no manifest, no marker. Nothing written. |\n| 5b | Hook installed after confirming none existed and `core.hooksPath` unset; executable; sha matches plan. Installed hook T1 untrack exit 0, T2 new link exit 1 (reason printed), T3 normal exit 0, T4 file→link exit 1 |\n| 5c | `daily-backup.ps1` patched (plan's OLD block matched the real file exactly once); parses under `pwsh`. Harness on the **real patched file + installed hook**: `COMMIT FAILED` with hook reason recorded, then normal change `committed` + `pushed`, `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, exit 0. Committed to dotclaude **by name only** as `d3e0955` and pushed (11 live session logs left unstaged) |\n| 6 | `git status` in the skills repo showed exactly `M sync-to-codex.ps1` and `M sync-to-codex.sh` |\n| 7 | Committed `8193bb9` and pushed. **The new pre-commit hook allowed it** — first live confirmation that it does not block normal commits |\n\n## Task 4 — premise correction found before execution\n\nTask 4 Step 2 expected \"at least\" `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` to be\nDIVERGED. The scan found **22** owned skills whose pool copy is a real\ndirectory that differs from canonical. The two named in the plan were read in\nfull, and in both the pool copy is an **older version**, not unique work:\n\n- `memory-write` — pool `SKILL.md` dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-09-02. The pool copy lacks the `name:`-slug rule and the retrieval-ladder section that canonical has.\n- `meeting-sync` — pool dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-08-15. The pool copy carries the pre-migration path `/Users/kristinarash/Desktop/SecondBrain/...`.\n\nThe scan also had a gap the plan did not cover: it considered only\ndirectories with a `SKILL.md`. The publish also replaces the pool's `_shared`\nsupport directory and any real directories in `~/.codex/skills` for managed\nnames. Both are now included in the triage and the backup.\n\nThe plan's step logic already handles any number of DIVERGED names, so this is\nrecorded here rather than edited into the approved plan, which keeps its hash\nvalid.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":76,"oldLines":3,"newStart":76,"newLines":41,"lines":[" The plan's step logic already handles any number of DIVERGED names, so this is"," recorded here rather than edited into the approved plan, which keeps its hash"," valid.","+","+### Full triage (read-only, content-compared, `__pycache__`/`.pyc`/`.DS_Store` ignored)","+","+- **Pool:** 23 entries differ — 22 owned skills plus `_shared`.","+  - **22 are \"canonical newer — safe\":** no file exists only in the pool, and no differing file is newer in the pool. They are stale copies.","+  - **1 needs review: `graphify`**, detailed below.","+- **Codex view:** 0 real directories differ from canonical.","+","+**`graphify`.** Two files differ, `SKILL.md` and `references/hooks.md`. The pool","+`SKILL.md` is dated 2026-08-29 14:34, **one minute after** canonical's 14:33. The","+diff is not independent work. It is graphify's installer writing a","+**per-harness variant**:","+","+| | Canonical (Claude Code) | Pool (Codex / agents) |","+|---|---|---|","+| Subagent dispatch | \"Call the **Agent** tool … `subagent_type=\"general-purpose\"`\" | \"Uses the **`Task`** tool … `Task(description=…)`\" |","+| Integration section | \"native **CLAUDE.md** integration\" | \"native **AGENTS.md** integration\" |","+","+The 4,795 files that exist only in canonical are `graphify/.venv` (its runtime).","+","+### Backup taken before any publish","+","+All 23 diverged pool copies were copied to","+`~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, including `graphify` (29 files)","+and `_shared`. File counts matched on every copy, and none were skipped. The codex","+backup root `pre-sync-2026-09-12-codex/` is empty because nothing there diverged.","+The VIEWS tarball from Task 1 remains a second, independent copy.","+","+### Task 4 Step 1 — done","+","+Run through Python `subprocess`: `dcg` blocks `git` inside shell command","+substitution, so the plan's shell form could not be used. Results:","+","+- 19 tracked mode-120000 entries; every one is a symlink on disk.","+- `git rm --cached --pathspec-from-file` exited 0.","+- **19** staged deletions; all 19 still on disk as links; **0** tracked links left in the index.","+- The 19 now show as `??` until Step 3 writes `.git/info/exclude`.","+- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a83ebb35-e523-49b5-9a47-d59a2a4a1f48","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
