{"parentUuid":"4b9dd88d-c6c0-4049-9496-0ebb1ea60327","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jm7GPyR1FMG5wDmXWB6SFD","type":"tool_result","content":"=== graphify skill files (excluding .venv) that name the pool or codex skill paths ===\n(none)\n\n=== installer code inside .venv that writes skill files per platform ===\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/llm.py\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/cli.py\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/__main__.py\n\n=== matching lines (first 20) ===\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:92:        # The generic Agent-Skills target: project ./.agents/skills, global the\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:93:        # spec's user-global ~/.agents/skills (read by `npx skills` and compliant\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:94:        # frameworks), NOT amp's ~/.config/agents/skills.\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:438:        # Amp searches .agents/skills (project) and ~/.config/agents/skills (user),\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:446:        # The generic cross-framework Agent-Skills target. Global: ~/.agents/skills\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:448:        # frameworks); project: ./.agents/skills. The CLI accepts `skills` as an\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:1524:    \"\"\"User-scope Amp install: skill into ~/.config/agents/skills + AGENTS.md.\"\"\"\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:1535:    \"\"\"`graphify agents install`: skill into ~/.agents/skills + AGENTS.md.\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:1538:    lands the skill at the spec's user-global ~/.agents/skills (set in\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:1582:        # Project-scoped: skill in .agents/skills/ PLUS the .agents/rules +\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:1590:        # root. `agents` -> ./.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md.\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:1800:    # Amp also drops a user-scope skill at ~/.config/agents/skills, which the\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/graphify/install.py:1803:    # The generic agents platform's user-scope skill lives at ~/.agents/skills,\n\n=== graphify runtime memory ===\n---\nname: graphify-runtime-setup\ndescription: \"graphify's Python package lives in a venv inside the skill dir, not globally; SKILL.md's own pip install step fails under PEP 668\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 53bc7e39-8ea3-4b0c-9787-4ed6d66f5acc\n  modified: 2026-08-29T19:34:51.928Z\n---\n\n**Set up 2026-08-29.** The `graphify` skill's Step 1 says `pip install graphifyy` — that\n**fails on this Mac** (Python 3.14 is PEP 668-managed). The package is instead installed\nin a dedicated venv:\n\n```\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/bin/python\n```\n\nRun every `scripts/*.py` step with that interpreter, not bare `python3`. `graphify install`\ndoes not touch the venv, so an upgrade leaves it intact.\n\n**Two skill copies exist and both carry a version stamp** (`.graphify_version`):\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/graphify/` — Claude Code\n- `~/.agents/skills/graphify/` — the generic `agents` convention, read by Codex-style harnesses\n\n`graphify install` updates **one platform at a time**. Running only `--platform claude`\nleaves `~/.agents` stale, and the version warning keeps firing from there even though the\nClaude copy is current. Update both: `--platform claude` **and** `--platform agents`.\n(Two more stamps exist under `~/.codex-migration-backups/` — those are backups, leave them.)\n\n**The old manifest was Windows-era.** A `--update` in `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings` reported\nall 264 files as new because the June manifest held `graphify-out\\GRAPH_REPORT.md`\n(backslash). After a path migration, `--update` is not incremental — plan a full rebuild.\n\n**Two traps when rebuilding a folder that already has a graph:**\n1. Move the old `graphify-out` **outside** the corpus before re-detecting. Left as a sibling\n   backup inside the folder it inflated the corpus from 265 to 327 files (its cache JSON got\n   scanned as code).\n2. The semantic cache keys on file paths, so a path change makes it a 0% hit — budget for\n   full re-extraction, not a cheap top-up.\n\n**Extraction agents can die mid-write.** A session rate limit killed 3 of 12 agents and left\none chunk's JSON truncated. Do not re-run blindly — a truncated chunk is usually salvageable\nby `raw_decode`-ing each complete object out of the `nodes`/`edges` arrays and dropping the\npartial tail. That recovered all 22 files of the dead chunk with nothing lost.\n\nRelated: [[dev-layout-and-discovery]]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"929bc9f9-38e9-4fa6-9769-88c4662404bb","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:31:00.426Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== graphify skill files (excluding .venv) that name the pool or codex skill paths ===\n(none)\n\n=== installer code inside .venv that writes skill files per platform ===\n