{"parentUuid":"2aeaa345-63fc-4a13-899c-1e71e562cb19","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Pick up from the handoff `/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-12-harness-skill-audit.md` and set next steps.\n   - Make all skills harness-agnostic (Claude Code, Codex, Pi), as in the video.\n   - Build an audit skill that reviews the whole system and helps evolve it.\n   - Have Codex review the plan and any generated code.\n   - Follow the video's advice for the Pi harness setup.\n   - User then said \"run it now\" (execute the plan).\n   - When the Codex quota ran out, the user said \"use claude, that fine\" (Claude as reviewer).\n   - The user said \"pause\", then \"resume\".\n   - Output style: ELI5 / ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English, short sentences. When a decision is needed: at most 2 options plus a recommendation.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Canonical skills location is `~/.claude/skills/`, which is its own git repo (erash11/claude-skills).\n     - Views: `~/.agents/skills` (Pi, Cowork) and `~/.codex/skills` (Codex) are generated by `sync-to-codex.sh` and its `.ps1` twin.\n     - Views are symlinks on Mac and copies on Windows.\n   - Ownership is structural: a real directory in canonical is owned; a symlink is third-party.\n     - 42 owned skills, 43 published entries (42 plus `_shared`), 19 third-party links.\n     - The 19 links are: 14 skills-CLI installs in `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` (5 of them mattpocock-skills), 4 from `vendor-review/claudex-loop`, and persistent-localhost.\n   - `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` manifest records ownership in each view.\n   - Per-machine `.git/info/exclude` holds a generated block listing the links. The tracked `.gitignore` is never used for this.\n   - Pre-commit hook refuses added or changed mode-120000 entries and allows deletions.\n   - First-run gate: marker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` is required for real runs. `DRY_RUN` must be 0 or 1.\n   - The sync removes third-party links from the index with `git rm --cached`, never with a reset to HEAD.\n   - `daily-backup.ps1` Sync-Repo now checks the commit exit code and records `repo-commit:<repo>`.\n   - Portable frontmatter contract:\n     - `name` must equal the directory name (TitleCase allowed).\n     - `description` needs a positive \"Use when\" clause AND a negative \"Do not use\" clause (word-boundary matched).\n     - Allowed keys include effort, user-invocable, repository and homepage.\n   - `rot.md` decay tiers; `aios-audit` is a project-level compound skill that delegates to os-audit, brain-audit, improve-system, claude-stack-doctor and doctor-plus.\n   - Review runner:\n     - `python3 ~/.claude/skills/claudex-loop/scripts/runner.py review --host codex` makes Claude the reviewer; `--host claude` makes Codex the reviewer.\n     - Supports `--resume <result.json> --feedback <file>` and `--artifacts`.\n   - Verification is done by running code extracted from the plan text, using `/bin/bash` 3.2.57.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Plan:** `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`\n     - About 2,800 lines, 8 tasks.\n     - APPROVED at round 13, sha256 `71b5242ea6dadac667878bc6d4617facbfaa1958a75975762e2d2da40928c432`, commit c85284b.\n     - **Do not edit it** (that would invalidate the approval).\n     - Task list:\n       - T1 snapshot\n       - T2 prune the pool\n       - T3 harden the sync scripts + hook + backup fix\n       - T4 untrack links, reconcile, publish\n       - T5 portable frontmatter plus checker\n       - T6 rot.md plus aios-audit plus aios-metrics.py\n       - T7 monthly launchd metrics (no commits)\n       - T8 Pi trial as a separate user `piuser` (own group `pitrial`, GID 4242), cost measurement only\n     - Gates B–D are still pending.\n   - **Approval record:** `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`\n     - Records the Gate A approval, pre-flight state, Task 3 evidence table, the Task 4 premise correction, the full triage, graphify details, backup info and the Task 4 Step 1 result.\n     - The latest edits are not yet committed.\n   - **Inventory:** `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt`\n     - Includes the AMEND-01 note and a SUPERSEDED notice for the inversion-era rollback.\n     - Also contains \"ROLLBACK BY TASK\" (Tasks 2–5).\n   - **Other audit files:** `2026-09-12-pool-prune.txt`.\n   - **Installed:** `~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh` (273 lines) and `sync-to-codex.ps1` (205 lines), from the approved plan. Committed as 8193bb9 and pushed. Key bash sections, in order:\n     1. Header vars, with `DRY=\"${DRY_RUN:-0}\"`.\n     2. DRY validation: `case \"$DRY\" in 0|1) ;; *) FATAL ... exit 2 ;; esac`.\n     3. READY gate.\n     4. `MANAGED`/`THIRD_PARTY` enumeration over `\"$SRC\"/*`, testing `-L` first and warning on dangling links.\n     5. Owned-became-link guard, reading the old manifests.\n     6. Index cleanup (`git rm --cached` for links in the index).\n     7. Exclude block written to `.git/info/exclude` between BEGIN/END markers, preserving other lines.\n     8. Validated retirement: a `valid_entry()` check (no separators, dots or glob characters), containment check, per-view archive to `retired-<date>/{agents,codex}` via `cp -RP`, and `KEEP_OWNED`.\n     9. Publish loop.\n     10. Manifest write.\n   - **Installed:** `~/.claude/skills/.git/hooks/pre-commit`, executable:\n     ```sh\n     #!/bin/sh\n     bad=$(git diff --cached --raw --no-renames --diff-filter=ACMRT \\\n           | awk -F'\\t' '{ split($1, m, \" \"); if (m[2] == \"120000\") print $2 }')\n     if [ -n \"$bad\" ]; then ... exit 1; fi\n     exit 0\n     ```\n   - **Patched:** `~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1`, committed as d3e0955 in dotclaude.\n     - Sync-Repo commit block: `git diff --cached --quiet` first (nothing stageable is logged as no commit).\n     - Then `$commitOut = git commit ... 2>&1`; on nonzero exit it does `$Errors.Add(\"repo-commit:$name\")`, logs COMMIT FAILED/ERR, and returns.\n   - **Memory:** `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md`\n     - Corrected: the skills directory IS a git repo.\n     - Adds traps and the architecture; the MEMORY.md index line was updated.\n   - **Job tmp:** `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/`\n     - Review artifacts: codex-review-r1..r7, claude-review-r8..r13.\n     - Dispositions files: r1–r12.\n     - `apply-fixes.py` (applies OLD/NEW replacement pairs, each exactly once).\n     - `parse-check.ps1`.\n     - Staged extracts in `/tmp/stage/`.\n   - **Backups:**\n     - `~/.claude/skills-archive/pre-canonical-VIEWS-2026-09-12.tgz` (includes .agents/vendor-review and .skill-lock.json)\n     - `pre-canonical-CANONICAL-2026-09-12.tgz` (reference only)\n     - `~/.agents/skills-archive/2026-09-12/` (98 pruned)\n     - `~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/` (23 diverged pool copies, including graphify and _shared)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - dcg blocked several command shapes. Workarounds:\n\n     | Blocked | Workaround |\n     |---|---|\n     | Redirects to dynamic or `$VAR` paths | Write tool or literal paths |\n     | `mv` with variable paths | Python `os.rename` |\n     | `shutil.rmtree` in a heredoc | Literal `rm -rf /tmp/...` |\n     | `pwsh -Command` with `$` | `pwsh -File` script |\n     | `$(git ...)` inside a shell substitution | Python `subprocess` |\n     | Complex heredocs with many substitutions | Data file plus apply-fixes.py |\n\n   - zsh has no PIPESTATUS: capture exit codes by redirecting output to files, not via pipes.\n   - Task 1 archive restored 57 of 61 because of the vendor-review two-hop chain: rebuilt the VIEWS tarball.\n   - Codex usage limit reached (reset 4:46 PM): the user approved switching to Claude as reviewer.\n   - Case 2 test exited 2 for the wrong reason (only one owned skill): fixture changed to two owned skills.\n   - bash 3.2 empty array under `set -u`: fixed with `${THIRD_PARTY[@]+\"${THIRD_PARTY[@]}\"}`.\n   - `.gitignore` trailing-slash patterns do not match symlinks: moved to `.git/info/exclude`.\n   - `xargs -a` is GNU-only: replaced with `git rm --cached --pathspec-from-file`.\n   - Many reviewer findings (R1–R12) were all accepted and fixed.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: the architecture, and a safety chain verified by real runs:\n     - first-run gate\n     - DRY validation\n     - owned-became-link guard\n     - index cleanup\n     - exclude\n     - hook\n     - backup error reporting\n   - Found while preparing Task 4:\n     - 23 diverged pool copies, not 2. Codex view: 0.\n     - 22 are stale, so canonical wins.\n     - graphify: the pool copy is the installer's Codex/agents variant (Task tool / AGENTS.md vs canonical's Agent tool / CLAUDE.md), 1 minute newer; canonical graphify holds a 4795-file .venv.\n     - The pool `_shared` directory and the codex view were added to the triage.\n   - Current state:\n     - Daily backup is UNLOADED; it must be reloaded at Task 5 Step 7, or by hand if the migration is abandoned.\n     - 19 links are staged as deletions and show as `??`. No `git add -A` may run before Step 3.\n     - Marker is absent.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-12-harness-skill-audit.md pick up with what our next steps should be. I want all my skills to be harness agnositic like the video talked about.  I want to develop an audit skill that will review my entire system and help me evolve and grow it. I want codex to review the plan an any code that is generated. I want to follow alot of what the video says when setting up my Pi harness as well.\"\n   - \"run it now\"\n   - \"use claude, that fine\"\n   - \"pause\"\n   - \"resume\"\n   - Security/handling constraints carried from context (keep in effect):\n     - Never point Pi at `~/DEV`.\n     - Never go near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data; never paste its contents into chat, an artifact or an external service).\n     - Pi ships no sandbox or approval prompts, so the trial runs only under a real OS boundary.\n     - Hooks exist in two copies; patch both.\n     - No global `pip install`.\n     - `timeout` is not installed.\n     - dcg blocks `find -delete`.\n     - Global MEMORY.md is at 2,489/2,500 chars.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Task 4, remaining:\n     - Decide graphify.\n     - Create marker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` (end of Step 2).\n     - Step 3: first real sync. Expect `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, the exclude block written, `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept, `.gitignore` unchanged, all 19 `check-ignore` yes.\n     - Step 4: stage and inspect; no 120000 entries.\n     - Step 5: roster check. Expect 42, 19 and 61; `_shared` OK; meeting-sync resolves `_shared`.\n     - Step 6: manifest 43, nothing missing, link targets correct; record the pool skill count.\n     - Step 7: /reload-skills check, commit (\"chore: stop tracking third-party skill symlinks\"), push.\n   - Commit the approval-record edits to KeystoneOS.\n   - Tasks 5–8.\n   - Gate B (after T5), Gate C (after T7), Gate D (verification before completion).\n   - Reload the daily backup at the end of Task 5.\n   - Final report with a `result:` line.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Executing Task 4 of the approved plan. Step 1 is done (19 links untracked via Python subprocess). The full divergence triage and backup of 23 pool copies are done. The graphify diff was read.\n\n   The last actions:\n   - Updated `docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md` with the triage, graphify details, backup facts and the Step 1 result (not yet committed).\n   - Was about to call the advisor on the graphify decision before creating the marker and running the first real publish.\n\n   My stated framing to the user:\n   > \"If canonical wins, as the plan says, Codex and Pi get Claude-flavored dispatch instructions for graphify. The Codex variant is backed up and can be regenerated by re-running graphify's installer.\"\n\n   And:\n   > \"The next step creates the 'prepared' marker and runs the first **real** publish on your live system. Before that, I'm getting a second opinion on this call.\"\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   1. Call advisor on the graphify decision. Leaning toward canonical wins: the pool variant is regenerable by the installer and backed up in pre-sync-2026-09-12. Flag a follow-up that graphify needs a harness-neutral SKILL.md (Task 5), or treatment as vendored.\n   2. Record the decision in the approval file.\n   3. `touch ~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready`.\n   4. Run Task 4 Step 3 (the real sync via Python subprocess to avoid dcg), then Steps 4–7 per the plan.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"9844f1f3-a4af-4e7b-bcbe-3df96c838cbf","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:32:26.207Z","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
