{"parentUuid":"074f95c0-fdcb-4116-9afc-66fbe593bcb2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezLgALFo4nwgHoRCCT9L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AJeDqdMA9d68Traxzbfhsq","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","old_string":"- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.\n","new_string":"- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.\n\n### Task 4 Step 2 — decisions\n\n**All 22 stale copies: canonical wins.** Nothing is copied into canonical.\n\n**The plan's premise did not hold.** R2-01 and R9-01 assumed the pool held\nedits that exist nowhere else. The reconcile tested that and found none: every\npool copy is older, and one still carries the pre-migration\n`Desktop/SecondBrain` path. The reconcile did its job by proving that nothing\nneeds to move.\n\n**`graphify`: canonical wins; the Codex variant stays archived** in\n`pre-sync-2026-09-12/graphify`. No name-list exception was added, because a\nlist would bring back the R7-01 regression. Two known costs:\n\n1. **Codex and Pi get the Claude-flavoured body.** They will read \"call the\n   Agent tool\" and \"CLAUDE.md\". Task 5 fixes frontmatter only, not skill\n   bodies, so this stays open (out of scope for this plan).\n2. **Write-through, verified in graphify's installer source.**\n   `graphify install --platform agents` calls `_copy_skill_file(\"agents\")`.\n   That function writes `~/.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` with a temp file\n   plus `os.replace`, and replaces `references/` with `rmtree` plus\n   `os.replace`. After Step 3 that path is a link to canonical, so the command\n   writes the Codex variant **into canonical**. The next daily backup would\n   then commit it. **Do not run `--platform agents` any more**; running\n   `--platform claude` alone is now enough. This is the first `aios-audit`\n   finding and a `rot.md` line for Task 6.\n\nMarker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` created after these decisions.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2095,"cache_read_input_tokens":91736,"output_tokens":2472,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":353},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2095,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2472,"cache_read_input_tokens":91736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2095},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezLg9QgoN9joSnYJUsq9","type":"assistant","uuid":"63fe0b07-931f-4963-be31-7b4635f9476c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:33:04.692Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"63fe0b07-931f-4963-be31-7b4635f9476c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AJeDqdMA9d68Traxzbfhsq","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b7fb6501-147f-429a-a9c6-d1c564de98c7","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:33:05.297Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","oldString":"- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.\n","newString":"- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.\n\n### Task 4 Step 2 — decisions\n\n**All 22 stale copies: canonical wins.** Nothing is copied into canonical.\n\n**The plan's premise did not hold.** R2-01 and R9-01 assumed the pool held\nedits that exist nowhere else. The reconcile tested that and found none: every\npool copy is older, and one still carries the pre-migration\n`Desktop/SecondBrain` path. The reconcile did its job by proving that nothing\nneeds to move.\n\n**`graphify`: canonical wins; the Codex variant stays archived** in\n`pre-sync-2026-09-12/graphify`. No name-list exception was added, because a\nlist would bring back the R7-01 regression. Two known costs:\n\n1. **Codex and Pi get the Claude-flavoured body.** They will read \"call the\n   Agent tool\" and \"CLAUDE.md\". Task 5 fixes frontmatter only, not skill\n   bodies, so this stays open (out of scope for this plan).\n2. **Write-through, verified in graphify's installer source.**\n   `graphify install --platform agents` calls `_copy_skill_file(\"agents\")`.\n   That function writes `~/.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` with a temp file\n   plus `os.replace`, and replaces `references/` with `rmtree` plus\n   `os.replace`. After Step 3 that path is a link to canonical, so the command\n   writes the Codex variant **into canonical**. The next daily backup would\n   then commit it. **Do not run `--platform agents` any more**; running\n   `--platform claude` alone is now enough. This is the first `aios-audit`\n   finding and a `rot.md` line for Task 6.\n\nMarker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` created after these decisions.\n","originalFile":"# Gate A — plan approval record — 2026-09-12\n\n**Plan:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`\n**Approved SHA-256:** `71b5242ea6dadac667878bc6d4617facbfaa1958a75975762e2d2da40928c432`\n**Committed as:** `c85284b` (erash11/KeystoneOS)\n**Verdict:** APPROVED, 0 findings — round 13, Claude reviewer (resumed session)\n\nThe approval binds this hash only. This record lives in its own file so that\nmarking Gate A satisfied does not edit the approved plan and silently\ninvalidate its approval. The plan's own line 22 still says \"RE-OPENED\"; this\nfile supersedes that line for the hash above.\n\n## Review history\n\n| Round | Reviewer | Verdict | Findings |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1–6 | Codex | REVISE ×5, then APPROVED | 10 → 9 → 7 → 4 → 1 → 0 |\n| 7 | Codex | REVISE | 5 (vendored-chain amendment found during Task 1) |\n| — | — | — | Codex usage limit reached; Eric approved switching to Claude |\n| 8 | Claude | REVISE | 11 (R8-01: all 19 links are third-party; inversion deleted) |\n| 9 | Claude | REVISE | 7 (reconcile before sync; per-machine exclude; pre-commit hook) |\n| 10 | Claude | REVISE | 3 (backup silently swallowed a refused commit) |\n| 11 | Claude | REVISE | 2, 0 high (Windows first-run gate) |\n| 12 | Claude | APPROVED | 1 low (DRY_RUN typo bypassed the gate) — fixed anyway |\n| 13 | Claude | **APPROVED** | **0** |\n\nReviewer's stated limitations, carried as execution risk: static review only;\nWindows PowerShell 5.1 behaviour unverified; **APPROVED covers the plan text\nonly — Gates B, C and D must still verify the implementation.**\n\n## Pre-flight state at approval (read-only, verified)\n\n| Check | State |\n|---|---|\n| Plan on disk | matches the approved hash; KeystoneOS in sync with origin |\n| `com.keystone.dailybackup` | loaded; **last run exited 1** (the known `repo-diverged` / `manifest-unmanaged` errors) — Task 3 Step 0 unloads it |\n| `~/.claude/skills` | clean, in sync with origin, **19** tracked mode-120000 links, **no** pre-commit hook |\n| `~/.claude` (dotclaude) | in sync with origin; working tree dirty with live session `.jsonl` logs only. Task 3 Step 5c commits `scripts/daily-backup.ps1` **by name**, so those logs are not swept in |\n| Current `sync-to-codex.sh` | 15 lines, 7-name `SHARED`, `rm -rf` + `cp -R` — matches the plan's baseline |\n| Current `sync-to-codex.ps1` | 13 lines, `Remove-Item -Recurse` + `Copy-Item` — matches the plan's baseline |\n| `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` | absent — correct; created only at the end of Task 4 Step 2 |\n\n## Execution so far\n\n- Task 1 — done (`d2e4a3b`)\n- Task 2 — done (`f54c8d9`)\n- **Task 3 — done.** Every step verified on the real, installed files:\n\n| Step | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | `com.keystone.dailybackup` unloaded (`launchctl list` no longer shows it) |\n| 2–3 | Both scripts installed byte-for-byte from the approved plan (sha256 of each installed file == the staged extract); original mode `0644` kept; `bash -n` OK |\n| 3b | Installed twin parses under `pwsh`: 205 lines, 0 `Write-Error` calls, 6 `Stop-Fatal`, first-run gate and `.git/info/exclude` present |\n| 4 / 4b | Against the **installed** script on `/bin/bash` 3.2: CASE 1 exit 0 (link skipped, canary intact, `theirs` ignored, `mine` tracked); CASE 2 exit 2 (owned-became-link FATAL); CASE 3+4 exit 0 (2 links removed from the index, only `owned/SKILL.md` left, `D old-link`); CASE 5 dry exit 0 / real exit 2 with gate message; CASE 5b `DRY_RUN=true` exit 2, pool copy untouched; deletion workflow exits 0 twice, 0 dangling, archived under `agents` + `codex`, manifest cleaned |\n| 5 | **Real layout**, `DRY_RUN=1`: exit 0, `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, 86 `would sync` lines (43 × 2 views). Fingerprints of index, `info/exclude`, pool listing and codex listing **identical before and after**; `memory-write`/`meeting-sync` still real dirs; no manifest, no marker. Nothing written. |\n| 5b | Hook installed after confirming none existed and `core.hooksPath` unset; executable; sha matches plan. Installed hook T1 untrack exit 0, T2 new link exit 1 (reason printed), T3 normal exit 0, T4 file→link exit 1 |\n| 5c | `daily-backup.ps1` patched (plan's OLD block matched the real file exactly once); parses under `pwsh`. Harness on the **real patched file + installed hook**: `COMMIT FAILED` with hook reason recorded, then normal change `committed` + `pushed`, `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, exit 0. Committed to dotclaude **by name only** as `d3e0955` and pushed (11 live session logs left unstaged) |\n| 6 | `git status` in the skills repo showed exactly `M sync-to-codex.ps1` and `M sync-to-codex.sh` |\n| 7 | Committed `8193bb9` and pushed. **The new pre-commit hook allowed it** — first live confirmation that it does not block normal commits |\n\n## Task 4 — premise correction found before execution\n\nTask 4 Step 2 expected \"at least\" `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` to be\nDIVERGED. The scan found **22** owned skills whose pool copy is a real\ndirectory that differs from canonical. The two named in the plan were read in\nfull, and in both the pool copy is an **older version**, not unique work:\n\n- `memory-write` — pool `SKILL.md` dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-09-02. The pool copy lacks the `name:`-slug rule and the retrieval-ladder section that canonical has.\n- `meeting-sync` — pool dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-08-15. The pool copy carries the pre-migration path `/Users/kristinarash/Desktop/SecondBrain/...`.\n\nThe scan also had a gap the plan did not cover: it considered only\ndirectories with a `SKILL.md`. The publish also replaces the pool's `_shared`\nsupport directory and any real directories in `~/.codex/skills` for managed\nnames. Both are now included in the triage and the backup.\n\nThe plan's step logic already handles any number of DIVERGED names, so this is\nrecorded here rather than edited into the approved plan, which keeps its hash\nvalid.\n\n### Full triage (read-only, content-compared, `__pycache__`/`.pyc`/`.DS_Store` ignored)\n\n- **Pool:** 23 entries differ — 22 owned skills plus `_shared`.\n  - **22 are \"canonical newer — safe\":** no file exists only in the pool, and no differing file is newer in the pool. They are stale copies.\n  - **1 needs review: `graphify`**, detailed below.\n- **Codex view:** 0 real directories differ from canonical.\n\n**`graphify`.** Two files differ, `SKILL.md` and `references/hooks.md`. The pool\n`SKILL.md` is dated 2026-08-29 14:34, **one minute after** canonical's 14:33. The\ndiff is not independent work. It is graphify's installer writing a\n**per-harness variant**:\n\n| | Canonical (Claude Code) | Pool (Codex / agents) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Subagent dispatch | \"Call the **Agent** tool … `subagent_type=\"general-purpose\"`\" | \"Uses the **`Task`** tool … `Task(description=…)`\" |\n| Integration section | \"native **CLAUDE.md** integration\" | \"native **AGENTS.md** integration\" |\n\nThe 4,795 files that exist only in canonical are `graphify/.venv` (its runtime).\n\n### Backup taken before any publish\n\nAll 23 diverged pool copies were copied to\n`~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, including `graphify` (29 files)\nand `_shared`. File counts matched on every copy, and none were skipped. The codex\nbackup root `pre-sync-2026-09-12-codex/` is empty because nothing there diverged.\nThe VIEWS tarball from Task 1 remains a second, independent copy.\n\n### Task 4 Step 1 — done\n\nRun through Python `subprocess`: `dcg` blocks `git` inside shell command\nsubstitution, so the plan's shell form could not be used. Results:\n\n- 19 tracked mode-120000 entries; every one is a symlink on disk.\n- `git rm --cached --pathspec-from-file` exited 0.\n- **19** staged deletions; all 19 still on disk as links; **0** tracked links left in the index.\n- The 19 now show as `??` until Step 3 writes `.git/info/exclude`.\n- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":114,"oldLines":3,"newStart":114,"newLines":32,"lines":[" - **19** staged deletions; all 19 still on disk as links; **0** tracked links left in the index."," - The 19 now show as `??` until Step 3 writes `.git/info/exclude`."," - No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.","+","+### Task 4 Step 2 — decisions","+","+**All 22 stale copies: canonical wins.** Nothing is copied into canonical.","+","+**The plan's premise did not hold.** R2-01 and R9-01 assumed the pool held","+edits that exist nowhere else. The reconcile tested that and found none: every","+pool copy is older, and one still carries the pre-migration","+`Desktop/SecondBrain` path. The reconcile did its job by proving that nothing","+needs to move.","+","+**`graphify`: canonical wins; the Codex variant stays archived** in","+`pre-sync-2026-09-12/graphify`. No name-list exception was added, because a","+list would bring back the R7-01 regression. Two known costs:","+","+1. **Codex and Pi get the Claude-flavoured body.** They will read \"call the","+   Agent tool\" and \"CLAUDE.md\". Task 5 fixes frontmatter only, not skill","+   bodies, so this stays open (out of scope for this plan).","+2. **Write-through, verified in graphify's installer source.**","+   `graphify install --platform agents` calls `_copy_skill_file(\"agents\")`.","+   That function writes `~/.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` with a temp file","+   plus `os.replace`, and replaces `references/` with `rmtree` plus","+   `os.replace`. After Step 3 that path is a link to canonical, so the command","+   writes the Codex variant **into canonical**. The next daily backup would","+   then commit it. **Do not run `--platform agents` any more**; running","+   `--platform claude` alone is now enough. This is the first `aios-audit`","+   finding and a `rot.md` line for Task 6.","+","+Marker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` created after these decisions."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"63fe0b07-931f-4963-be31-7b4635f9476c","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"b7fb6501-147f-429a-a9c6-d1c564de98c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezLgALFo4nwgHoRCCT9L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FyVcj7CMxFTZgBQ1ETnn4W","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_graphify-runtime-setup.md","old_string":"**Two skill copies exist and both carry a version stamp** (`.graphify_version`):\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/graphify/` — Claude Code\n- `~/.agents/skills/graphify/` — the generic `agents` convention, read by Codex-style harnesses\n\n`graphify install` updates **one platform at a time**. Running only `--platform claude`\nleaves `~/.agents` stale, and the version warning keeps firing from there even though the\nClaude copy is current. Update both: `--platform claude` **and** `--platform agents`.","new_string":"**Since 2026-09-12 there is ONE skill copy.** `~/.agents/skills/graphify` and\n`~/.codex/skills/graphify` are symlinks to `~/.claude/skills/graphify/` (made by\n`sync-to-codex.sh`). Upgrade with `--platform claude` ONLY.\n\n**Never run `graphify install --platform agents` now.** Its installer writes\n`~/.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` and `references/` by path, so it follows the link and\noverwrites the canonical Claude copy with the Codex variant (\"Task tool\", \"AGENTS.md\").\nThe daily backup would then commit that. Before 9/12 the advice was \"update both\"; that\nadvice is now wrong. The old Codex variant is archived at\n`~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/graphify`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2095,"cache_read_input_tokens":91736,"output_tokens":2472,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":353},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2095,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2472,"cache_read_input_tokens":91736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2095},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezLg9QgoN9joSnYJUsq9","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a16d8a8-7d96-4d5f-91bb-ebd319ee7d01","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:33:10.386Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"5a16d8a8-7d96-4d5f-91bb-ebd319ee7d01","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FyVcj7CMxFTZgBQ1ETnn4W","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_graphify-runtime-setup.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"7bb0d3cd-cc8a-45d0-8eee-c7a0f570b10b","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:33:11.023Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_graphify-runtime-setup.md","oldString":"**Two skill copies exist and both carry a version stamp** (`.graphify_version`):\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/graphify/` — Claude Code\n- `~/.agents/skills/graphify/` — the generic `agents` convention, read by Codex-style harnesses\n\n`graphify install` updates **one platform at a time**. Running only `--platform claude`\nleaves `~/.agents` stale, and the version warning keeps firing from there even though the\nClaude copy is current. Update both: `--platform claude` **and** `--platform agents`.","newString":"**Since 2026-09-12 there is ONE skill copy.** `~/.agents/skills/graphify` and\n`~/.codex/skills/graphify` are symlinks to `~/.claude/skills/graphify/` (made by\n`sync-to-codex.sh`). Upgrade with `--platform claude` ONLY.\n\n**Never run `graphify install --platform agents` now.** Its installer writes\n`~/.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` and `references/` by path, so it follows the link and\noverwrites the canonical Claude copy with the Codex variant (\"Task tool\", \"AGENTS.md\").\nThe daily backup would then commit that. Before 9/12 the advice was \"update both\"; that\nadvice is now wrong. The old Codex variant is archived at\n`~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/graphify`.","originalFile":"---\nname: graphify-runtime-setup\ndescription: \"graphify's Python package lives in a venv inside the skill dir, not globally; SKILL.md's own pip install step fails under PEP 668\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 53bc7e39-8ea3-4b0c-9787-4ed6d66f5acc\n  modified: 2026-08-29T19:34:51.928Z\n---\n\n**Set up 2026-08-29.** The `graphify` skill's Step 1 says `pip install graphifyy` — that\n**fails on this Mac** (Python 3.14 is PEP 668-managed). The package is instead installed\nin a dedicated venv:\n\n```\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/graphify/.venv/bin/python\n```\n\nRun every `scripts/*.py` step with that interpreter, not bare `python3`. `graphify install`\ndoes not touch the venv, so an upgrade leaves it intact.\n\n**Two skill copies exist and both carry a version stamp** (`.graphify_version`):\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/graphify/` — Claude Code\n- `~/.agents/skills/graphify/` — the generic `agents` convention, read by Codex-style harnesses\n\n`graphify install` updates **one platform at a time**. Running only `--platform claude`\nleaves `~/.agents` stale, and the version warning keeps firing from there even though the\nClaude copy is current. Update both: `--platform claude` **and** `--platform agents`.\n(Two more stamps exist under `~/.codex-migration-backups/` — those are backups, leave them.)\n\n**The old manifest was Windows-era.** A `--update` in `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings` reported\nall 264 files as new because the June manifest held `graphify-out\\GRAPH_REPORT.md`\n(backslash). After a path migration, `--update` is not incremental — plan a full rebuild.\n\n**Two traps when rebuilding a folder that already has a graph:**\n1. Move the old `graphify-out` **outside** the corpus before re-detecting. Left as a sibling\n   backup inside the folder it inflated the corpus from 265 to 327 files (its cache JSON got\n   scanned as code).\n2. The semantic cache keys on file paths, so a path change makes it a 0% hit — budget for\n   full re-extraction, not a cheap top-up.\n\n**Extraction agents can die mid-write.** A session rate limit killed 3 of 12 agents and left\none chunk's JSON truncated. Do not re-run blindly — a truncated chunk is usually salvageable\nby `raw_decode`-ing each complete object out of the `nodes`/`edges` arrays and dropping the\npartial tail. That recovered all 22 files of the dead chunk with nothing lost.\n\nRelated: [[dev-layout-and-discovery]]\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: 53bc7e39-8ea3-4b0c-9787-4ed6d66f5acc","-  modified: 2026-08-29T19:34:51.928Z","+  modified: 2026-09-12T22:33:10.641Z"," ---"," "," **Set up 2026-08-29.** The `graphify` skill's Step 1 says `pip install graphifyy` — that"]},{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":14,"newStart":19,"newLines":16,"lines":[" Run every `scripts/*.py` step with that interpreter, not bare `python3`. `graphify install`"," does not touch the venv, so an upgrade leaves it intact."," ","-**Two skill copies exist and both carry a version stamp** (`.graphify_version`):","+**Since 2026-09-12 there is ONE skill copy.** `~/.agents/skills/graphify` and","+`~/.codex/skills/graphify` are symlinks to `~/.claude/skills/graphify/` (made by","+`sync-to-codex.sh`). Upgrade with `--platform claude` ONLY."," ","-- `~/.claude/skills/graphify/` — Claude Code","-- `~/.agents/skills/graphify/` — the generic `agents` convention, read by Codex-style harnesses","-","-`graphify install` updates **one platform at a time**. Running only `--platform claude`","-leaves `~/.agents` stale, and the version warning keeps firing from there even though the","-Claude copy is current. Update both: `--platform claude` **and** `--platform agents`.","+**Never run `graphify install --platform agents` now.** Its installer writes","+`~/.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` and `references/` by path, so it follows the link and","+overwrites the canonical Claude copy with the Codex variant (\"Task tool\", \"AGENTS.md\").","+The daily backup would then commit that. Before 9/12 the advice was \"update both\"; that","+advice is now wrong. The old Codex variant is archived at","+`~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/graphify`."," (Two more stamps exist under `~/.codex-migration-backups/` — those are backups, leave them.)"," "," **The old manifest was Windows-era.** A `--update` in `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings` reported"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5a16d8a8-7d96-4d5f-91bb-ebd319ee7d01","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
