{"parentUuid":"b18b0b32-33d8-41f2-ab00-46677206a098","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Camt3ZttfF7YU2ofQFMzd","type":"tool_result","content":"1428\t- [ ] **Step 3: First real sync — publish the views and write the per-machine exclude block**\n1429\t\n1430\t```bash\n1431\tbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n1432\tsed -n '/BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex/,/END generated-by-sync-to-codex/p' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude\n1433\techo \"--- lines outside the block preserved? ---\"\n1434\tgrep -v -e 'generated-by-sync-to-codex' -e '^/' -e '^# ' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude || true\n1435\tgrep -qx '/.claude/RESUME.md' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude && echo \"pre-existing /.claude/RESUME.md kept\" || echo \"RESUME.md line LOST\"\n1436\techo \"--- tracked .gitignore untouched by the sync? ---\"\n1437\tgit -C ~/.claude/skills diff --quiet -- .gitignore && echo \".gitignore unchanged\" || echo \".gitignore MODIFIED\"\n1438\t```\n1439\t\n1440\tExpected: `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, `exit=0`; a block listing all 19 names with a **leading slash and no trailing slash**; `pre-existing /.claude/RESUME.md kept`; `.gitignore unchanged`.\n1441\t\n1442\t> **Why `.git/info/exclude` and not `.gitignore` (R9-02).** The set of links is per-machine, but `.gitignore` is tracked and shared through `erash11/claude-skills`. Windows' sync would rewrite the block with *its* links — none — the backup would push that, and on the next pull the Mac's 19 links would stop being ignored and get committed again. `info/exclude` is never committed, so each machine keeps its own list.\n1443\t>\n1444\t> **Why no trailing slash.** A trailing slash matches directories only, and git does not treat a symlink as a directory, so `/anti-sleep/` would match nothing.\n1445\t\n1446\tProve every link is actually ignored:\n1447\t\n1448\t```bash\n1449\tcd ~/.claude/skills\n1450\twhile IFS= read -r s; do\n1451\t  printf '%-28s ignored=%s ondisk=%s\\n' \"$s\" \\\n1452\t    \"$(git check-ignore -q \"$s\" && echo yes || echo NO)\" \\\n1453\t    \"$(ls -ld \"$s\" | cut -c1)\"\n1454\tdone < /tmp/tracked-links.txt\n1455\t```\n1456\t\n1457\tExpected: `ignored=yes` and `ondisk=l` for all 19. A single `NO` means the pattern is wrong — fix before staging.\n1458\t\n1459\t- [ ] **Step 4: Stage, then inspect the index (R2-03)**\n1460\t\n1461\t`git ls-files` reads the *index*, so it is checked **after** staging:\n1462\t\n1463\t```bash\n1464\tcd ~/.claude/skills\n1465\tgit add -A\n1466\techo \"--- staged symlinks (mode 120000) - MUST be empty ---\"\n1467\tgit ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"'\n1468\techo \"--- staged summary ---\"\n1469\tgit diff --cached --stat | tail -3\n1470\t```\n1471\t\n1472\tExpected: the `120000` list prints **nothing**; the summary shows 19 deletions plus any content moved into canonical in Step 2 — and **no** `.gitignore` change. If any `120000` entry survives, `git reset` and stop. (The Task 3 pre-commit hook would refuse the commit anyway; this check is so you find out now, not at commit time.)\n1473\t\n1474\t- [ ] **Step 5: Verify the owned roster is intact and `_shared` still resolves**\n1475\t\n1476\t```bash\n1477\techo \"owned real dirs with SKILL.md (expect 42):\"\n1478\tfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type d ! -path ~/.claude/skills -exec test -f {}/SKILL.md \\; -print | wc -l\n1479\techo \"third-party links (expect 19):\"\n1480\tfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\n1481\techo \"total resolvable SKILL.md (expect 61):\"\n1482\tfind -L ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\n1483\techo \"--- dangling links (must be empty) ---\"\n1484\tfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print\n1485\ttest -f ~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared OK\"\n1486\tpython3 -c \"\n1487\timport pathlib\n1488\tp = pathlib.Path.home()/'.claude/skills/meeting-sync/scripts/sync.py'\n1489\tcfg = p.resolve().parents[2]/'_shared/config.json'\n1490\tprint('meeting-sync resolves _shared:', cfg.exists())\n1491\t\"\n1492\t```\n1493\t\n1494\tExpected: `42`, `19`, `61`, no dangling output, `_shared OK`, and `True`. The `True` is the R2 check: 10+ skills reach `_shared` through `parents[2]`.\n1495\t\n1496\t- [ ] **Step 6: Prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**\n1497\t\n1498\t```bash\n1499\tDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh >/dev/null; echo \"idempotent dry exit=$?\"\n1500\tMAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\n1501\techo \"--- manifest size (expect 43) ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"\n1502\techo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"\n1503\twhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\n1504\techo \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"\n1505\twhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\n1506\techo \"--- managed links not resolving to canonical (must be empty) ---\"\n1507\twhile IFS= read -r s; do\n1508\t  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n1509\t  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"\n1510\tdone < \"$MAN\"\n1511\tpython3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py 2>/dev/null | grep '^pool_skills=' || echo \"(metrics script not written until Task 6 - count by hand:)\"\n1512\tfind -L ~/.agents/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\n1513\t```\n1514\t\n1515\tExpected: `idempotent dry exit=0`; manifest **43** lines; all three lists **empty**. **Record the pool skill count printed last** — Task 8 compares against it.\n1516\t\n1517\tSuccess is measured against the **manifest**, never against `ls ~/.claude/skills`: the repo also holds `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1` and `CLAUDE.md`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view.\n1518\t\n1519\t- [ ] **Step 7: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n1520\t\n1521\tRun `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61 — untracking changes git, not what the harness reads from disk). If it dropped, roll back using **\"TASK 4\" under \"ROLLBACK BY TASK\"** in `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt` — not PHASE A, which predates Task 2 and would restore the 98 pruned skills (R9-04).\n1522\t\n1523\t```bash\n1524\tcd ~/.claude/skills\n1525\tgit add -A\n1526\tgit status --short | head\n1527\tgit commit -m \"chore: stop tracking third-party skill symlinks\n1528\t\n1529\tAll 19 outward links in this repo are third-party: 14 skills-CLI installs\n1530\trecorded in ~/.agents/.skill-lock.json (five of them mattpocock-skills),\n1531\t4 from the vendor-review/claudex-loop package, plus persistent-localhost.\n1532\tThey were tracked as mode-120000 and pushed, i.e. dead links on Windows.\n1533\t\n1534\tThey stay on disk and keep working here. Git ignores them through the\n1535\tper-machine .git/info/exclude, which sync-to-codex.sh regenerates; the\n1536\tpre-commit hook refuses any future symlink commit.\n1537\t\n1538\tCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n1539\tgit push\n1540\t```\n1541\t\n1542\tExpected: the commit succeeds — the hook allows deletions — and the push succeeds.\n1543\t\n1544\t---\n1545\t"}]},"uuid":"d3a59a0b-3e85-4192-b04d-c92853a95b28","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:33:29.041Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","content":"- [ ] **Step 3: First real sync — publish the views and write the per-machine exclude block**\n\n```bash\nbash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\nsed -n '/BEGIN generated-by-sync-to-codex/,/END generated-by-sync-to-codex/p' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude\necho \"--- lines outside the block preserved? ---\"\ngrep -v -e 'generated-by-sync-to-codex' -e '^/' -e '^# ' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude || true\ngrep -qx '/.claude/RESUME.md' ~/.claude/skills/.git/info/exclude && echo \"pre-existing /.claude/RESUME.md kept\" || echo \"RESUME.md line LOST\"\necho \"--- tracked .gitignore untouched by the sync? ---\"\ngit -C ~/.claude/skills diff --quiet -- .gitignore && echo \".gitignore unchanged\" || echo \".gitignore MODIFIED\"\n```\n\nExpected: `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, `exit=0`; a block listing all 19 names with a **leading slash and no trailing slash**; `pre-existing /.claude/RESUME.md kept`; `.gitignore unchanged`.\n\n> **Why `.git/info/exclude` and not `.gitignore` (R9-02).** The set of links is per-machine, but `.gitignore` is tracked and shared through `erash11/claude-skills`. Windows' sync would rewrite the block with *its* links — none — the backup would push that, and on the next pull the Mac's 19 links would stop being ignored and get committed again. `info/exclude` is never committed, so each machine keeps its own list.\n>\n> **Why no trailing slash.** A trailing slash matches directories only, and git does not treat a symlink as a directory, so `/anti-sleep/` would match nothing.\n\nProve every link is actually ignored:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do\n  printf '%-28s ignored=%s ondisk=%s\\n' \"$s\" \\\n    \"$(git check-ignore -q \"$s\" && echo yes || echo NO)\" \\\n    \"$(ls -ld \"$s\" | cut -c1)\"\ndone < /tmp/tracked-links.txt\n```\n\nExpected: `ignored=yes` and `ondisk=l` for all 19. A single `NO` means the pattern is wrong — fix before staging.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Stage, then inspect the index (R2-03)**\n\n`git ls-files` reads the *index*, so it is checked **after** staging:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\necho \"--- staged symlinks (mode 120000) - MUST be empty ---\"\ngit ls-files -s | awk '$1==\"120000\"'\necho \"--- staged summary ---\"\ngit diff --cached --stat | tail -3\n```\n\nExpected: the `120000` list prints **nothing**; the summary shows 19 deletions plus any content moved into canonical in Step 2 — and **no** `.gitignore` change. If any `120000` entry survives, `git reset` and stop. (The Task 3 pre-commit hook would refuse the commit anyway; this check is so you find out now, not at commit time.)\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Verify the owned roster is intact and `_shared` still resolves**\n\n```bash\necho \"owned real dirs with SKILL.md (expect 42):\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type d ! -path ~/.claude/skills -exec test -f {}/SKILL.md \\; -print | wc -l\necho \"third-party links (expect 19):\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l\necho \"total resolvable SKILL.md (expect 61):\"\nfind -L ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\necho \"--- dangling links (must be empty) ---\"\nfind ~/.claude/skills -maxdepth 1 -type l ! -exec test -e {} \\; -print\ntest -f ~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.json && echo \"_shared OK\"\npython3 -c \"\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path.home()/'.claude/skills/meeting-sync/scripts/sync.py'\ncfg = p.resolve().parents[2]/'_shared/config.json'\nprint('meeting-sync resolves _shared:', cfg.exists())\n\"\n```\n\nExpected: `42`, `19`, `61`, no dangling output, `_shared OK`, and `True`. The `True` is the R2 check: 10+ skills reach `_shared` through `parents[2]`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prove every managed entry landed (R3-06)**\n\n```bash\nDRY_RUN=1 bash ~/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh >/dev/null; echo \"idempotent dry exit=$?\"\nMAN=~/.agents/skills/.generated-by-sync-to-codex\necho \"--- manifest size (expect 43) ---\"; wc -l < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the pool (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed entries MISSING from the codex view (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do [ -e ~/.codex/skills/\"$s\" ] || echo \"MISSING $s\"; done < \"$MAN\"\necho \"--- managed links not resolving to canonical (must be empty) ---\"\nwhile IFS= read -r s; do\n  t=\"$(readlink ~/.agents/skills/\"$s\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n  [ \"$t\" = \"$HOME/.claude/skills/$s\" ] || echo \"WRONG-TARGET $s -> ${t:-not-a-link}\"\ndone < \"$MAN\"\npython3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py 2>/dev/null | grep '^pool_skills=' || echo \"(metrics script not written until Task 6 - count by hand:)\"\nfind -L ~/.agents/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md | wc -l\n```\n\nExpected: `idempotent dry exit=0`; manifest **43** lines; all three lists **empty**. **Record the pool skill count printed last** — Task 8 compares against it.\n\nSuccess is measured against the **manifest**, never against `ls ~/.claude/skills`: the repo also holds `docs/`, `sync-to-codex.sh`, `sync-to-codex.ps1` and `CLAUDE.md`, which are not skills and must never appear in a view.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Confirm Claude Code still loads the roster, then commit**\n\nRun `/reload-skills` in a Claude Code session, then `/skills`. Expected: the same personal-skill count as before (61 — untracking changes git, not what the harness reads from disk). If it dropped, roll back using **\"TASK 4\" under \"ROLLBACK BY TASK\"** in `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pre-canonical-inventory.txt` — not PHASE A, which predates Task 2 and would restore the 98 pruned skills (R9-04).\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.claude/skills\ngit add -A\ngit status --short | head\ngit commit -m \"chore: stop tracking third-party skill symlinks\n\nAll 19 outward links in this repo are third-party: 14 skills-CLI installs\nrecorded in ~/.agents/.skill-lock.json (five of them mattpocock-skills),\n4 from the vendor-review/claudex-loop package, plus persistent-localhost.\nThey were tracked as mode-120000 and pushed, i.e. dead links on Windows.\n\nThey stay on disk and keep working here. Git ignores them through the\nper-machine .git/info/exclude, which sync-to-codex.sh regenerates; the\npre-commit hook refuses any future symlink commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\ngit push\n```\n\nExpected: the commit succeeds — the hook allows deletions — and the push succeeds.\n\n---\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1428,"totalLines":2869}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b18b0b32-33d8-41f2-ab00-46677206a098","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
