{"parentUuid":"84b6a62a-e28c-407e-8eb3-ba5fa51671df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezLuy7CnbNhL9Jdg1csk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MPhuBEqRTTJ2eP2yS7t6gH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t5-failing-frontmatter.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1388,"cache_read_input_tokens":130500,"output_tokens":89,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1388,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":89,"cache_read_input_tokens":130500,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1388},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CezLuxFriqXLpfRWZ94Pi","type":"assistant","uuid":"54bf1208-c8ab-45be-ad5b-09ab9ac95243","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:35:58.933Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"54bf1208-c8ab-45be-ad5b-09ab9ac95243","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPhuBEqRTTJ2eP2yS7t6gH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t=== Harvest :: name 'harvest' != directory 'Harvest' | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n2\t---\n3\tname: harvest\n4\tdescription: Distill a finished project into evergreen Knowledge/ articles in the SecondBrain vault and log the shipped artifact in the output ledger. Use when the user says \"/harvest <project>\", \"harvest this project\", \"distill what we learned from X\", declares a project finished/shipped/done, or when a session ends with a clearly shipped deliverable worth recording.\n5\targument-hint: \"[project]\"\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t=== capture-insight :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n9\t---\n10\tname: capture-insight\n11\tdescription: Capture a story, win, or lesson the user just shared as a permanent atomic note in the SecondBrain vault. Use when the user tells a story or lesson and says \"capture this\", \"save this win/lesson\", \"that's worth a note\", or \"/capture-insight\". For end-of-day structured capture use interview-me; for whole-project distillation use harvest; for plain facts use memory-write.\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t=== claude-stack-doctor :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n15\t---\n16\tname: claude-stack-doctor\n17\tdescription: Health-check Eric's automation/memory stack in one pass, and verify the Mac-to-Windows handoff actually works — launchd agents (com.keystone.morning, agysync, dailybackup, rituals, reconcile, adjudicate), Python venvs, memsearch, memory-compiler flush pipeline, backup freshness, and context budget — and diagnose what's silently broken. Use when the user says \"/claude-stack-doctor\", \"stack doctor\", \"is my stack healthy\", \"did my scheduled jobs run\", \"check the memory pipeline\", \"why didn't the backup run\", or when closeout/morning sessions should verify automation health.\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t=== closeout :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n21\t---\n22\tname: closeout\n23\tdescription: End-of-session sign-off ritual. Sweeps loose ends, commits and pushes what needs it, verifies memory capture, writes a cross-harness handoff, and reports \"clear to sign off\" or what's still open. Use when the user says \"/closeout\", \"any loose ends?\", \"am I good to sign off?\", \"close out for the night\", \"closing out\", \"goodnight\", \"wrap up for the day\", or asks for a system health check before leaving.\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t=== dev-sync :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n27\t---\n28\tname: dev-sync\n29\tdescription: \"Bring this machine into line with GitHub and load back the context that came with it: locate DEV automatically, pull config and skills, inventory every project, commit and push local work, pull the other machine's work, clone what is missing, report conflicts, then read the repo's STATUS and latest handoff and report where the last session left off. Use when Eric switches machines, sits down to start work, says 'sync DEV', asks whether everything is pushed, or asks where he left off.\"\n30\t---\n31\t\n32\t=== doctor-plus :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n33\t---\n34\tname: doctor-plus\n35\tdescription: Runs Claude Code's built-in /doctor health check, then audits the workspace against the 6 then-and-now context-engineering shifts Anthropic shipped with the Claude 5 models (rules to judgement, examples to interfaces, upfront to progressive disclosure, repeats to tool descriptions, CLAUDE.md memory to auto-memory, simple specs to rich references). Reports findings first, fixes only on approval. Triggers on \"/doctor-plus\", \"doctor plus\", \"doctor-plus\", \"extended doctor\", \"then and now audit\", \"context checkup\".\n36\t---\n37\t\n38\t=== fireflies-intake :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n39\t---\n40\tname: fireflies-intake\n41\tdescription: One-command Fireflies pipeline — sync new meeting transcripts into the SecondBrain vault, rename generically-titled meetings, then report exactly what was ingested. Use when the user says \"/fireflies-intake\", \"ingest my recent fireflies meetings\", \"sync meetings that aren't in the second brain yet\", \"pull in the new meetings\", \"meeting ingestion\", or asks whether all recent meetings have been ingested.\n42\targument-hint: \"[since-date]\"\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t=== five-slides-generator :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n46\t---\n47\tname: five-slides-generator\n48\tdescription: \"Generate a '5 Slides in 5 Minutes' PowerPoint deck for Baylor Athletics Applied Performance — research, narrative, pptxgenjs, .pptx build, QA. Use whenever the user mentions '5 slides,' '5 slides in 5 minutes,' or gives a topic they want a Performance School deck on. Also trigger for a cross-functional staff presentation, a quick sport science deck, or any short educational deck in the established series format (CMJ, GPS, VBT are prior examples).\"\n49\targument-hint: \"[topic]\"\n50\t---\n51\t\n52\t=== forecast-capture :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n53\t---\n54\tname: forecast-capture\n55\tdescription: Capture and freeze the CFB Victory Model's pre-game forecasts before kickoff, then report what moved since last week. Run every Wednesday during the season. Use when the user says \"/forecast-capture\", \"capture the forecast\", \"freeze this week's predictions\", \"run the CFB capture\", \"did we capture this week\", or asks whether the weekly model snapshot has been taken.\n56\t---\n57\t\n58\t=== game-film-timestamps :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n59\t---\n60\tname: game-film-timestamps\n61\tdescription: >\n62\t  Fix wrong startTime/endTime values in football game film JSON exported from Hudl, DVSport, or\n63\t  similar. Fetches correct wall-clock timestamps from the ESPN API and writes corrected copies.\n64\t  Use whenever the user mentions fixing or correcting play-by-play timestamps in game film JSON,\n65\t  or has files with \"OFF\", \"DEF\", or \"KICKS\" in the filename and mentions timestamps or time issues.\n66\targument-hint: \"[game-files folder]\"\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t=== graphify :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n70\t---\n71\tname: graphify\n72\tdescription: \"Use for any question about a codebase, its architecture, file relationships, or project content — especially when graphify-out/ exists, where the question should be treated as a graphify query first. Turns any input (code, docs, papers, images, videos) into a persistent knowledge graph with god nodes, community detection, and query/path/explain tools.\"\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t=== html-to-pdf :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n76\t---\n77\tname: html-to-pdf\n78\tdescription: Render any local HTML report, deck, or dashboard to a print-ready PDF via headless Chrome — replaces the manual Ctrl+P → Save as PDF ritual. Use when the user says \"export this to PDF\", \"print version\", \"PDF for the coaches\", \"make this printable\", or a coach-facing HTML deliverable needs a shareable/printable copy.\n79\targument-hint: \"[html-path] [out-pdf]\"\n80\t---\n81\t\n82\t=== improve-system :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n83\t---\n84\tname: improve-system\n85\tdescription: Audit the SecondBrain vault for rot — stale seed notes, conflicting claims, and duplicate notes — and propose merge/archive/update actions. Use when the user says \"/improve-system\", \"audit my notes\", \"audit the vault\", \"find stale/duplicate notes\", or \"clean up my second brain\". For mining sessions for missed learnings use session-miner; for capturing a win/lesson use capture-insight; for improving a skill use write-a-skill.\n86\t---\n87\t\n88\t=== ingest-book :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n89\t---\n90\tname: ingest-book\n91\tdescription: Ingest a book (PDF/EPUB full-text, Kindle highlights, or framework-only from a physical book) into the SecondBrain library as atomized, citable advisor entries. Use when the user wants to \"ingest a book\", \"add a book to my library/advisors\", \"/ingest-book\", or points at a book file for the advisor system. For articles/transcripts/general resources use ingest-resource instead.\n92\targument-hint: \"[book file or title] [domain]\"\n93\t---\n94\t\n95\t=== ingest-resource :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n96\t---\n97\tname: ingest-resource\n98\tdescription: Ingest any article, YouTube link, transcript, PDF, or note into the SecondBrain vault — routes it to Knowledge/ (stable info) or Projects/ (active work), adds a summary block, and cross-links related notes with [[wikilinks]]. Use when the user shares a URL, file, or pasted content and says \"ingest\", \"save this\", \"add to my vault/second brain\", \"/ingest-resource\", or drops a resource with intent to keep it.\n99\targument-hint: \"[URL or file path]\"\n100\t---\n101\t\n102\t=== library-review :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n103\t---\n104\tname: library-review\n105\tdescription: Review a book-library domain for gaps, contested entries, and missing coverage, and propose new entries. Manual loop — proposes, you approve. Use when the user says \"review my library\", \"/library-review <domain>\", \"what's missing from my <domain> advisor\", or after a batch of ingestion.\n106\targument-hint: \"[domain]\"\n107\t---\n108\t\n109\t=== meeting-prep :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n110\t---\n111\tname: meeting-prep\n112\tdescription: Pre-meeting readiness brief for a project — what changed, what's open, every deliverable path. Use when the user says \"/meeting-prep <project>\", \"I have a meeting with <person> — are we in a good spot on <project>?\", \"verify we're up to speed before the meeting\", \"get me ready for this afternoon's meeting\", or names an upcoming coach/staff meeting.\n113\targument-hint: \"[project]\"\n114\t---\n115\t\n116\t=== meeting-sync :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n117\t---\n118\tname: meeting-sync\n119\tdescription: Sync new Fireflies transcripts into the SecondBrain vault; audit vault filenames for drift against Fireflies titles. Idempotent. Use when the user says \"sync meetings\", \"pull latest meetings\", \"/meeting-sync\", \"update meeting notes\", \"any new meetings?\", or when invoked by weekly-review. Also for filename drift — \"are any meeting files misnamed?\", \"did a meeting get renamed after export?\", \"why is this meeting titled differently in Fireflies than in the vault?\", \"audit the meeting filenames\".\n120\targument-hint: \"[days-back]\"\n121\t---\n122\t\n123\t=== memory-write :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n124\t---\n125\tname: memory-write\n126\tdescription: >\n127\t  Writes, updates, removes, and recalls facts in the two-tier memory system at\n128\t  ~/.claude/global-memory/ and ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/. Use for write\n129\t  requests such as \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"update memory\", \"save this\",\n130\t  and \"forget about\", and for recall requests such as \"did we already…?\",\n131\t  \"what did we decide about X?\", and \"do you remember…?\". For writes, selects\n132\t  the correct tier and enforces deduplication and character caps. For recall,\n133\t  checks the injected snapshot first, then follows the memsearch retrieval ladder.\n134\t---\n135\t\n136\t=== name-meetings :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n137\t---\n138\tname: name-meetings\n139\tdescription: Detects Fireflies meetings with generic titles (empty, \"Zoom Meeting\", \"Recording\", date-only, etc.), proposes structured names based on AI summary + participants, and applies approved renames via the Fireflies API. Use when user says \"/name-meetings\", \"name my meetings\", \"rename untitled meetings\", \"fix meeting titles\", \"my meetings have no names\", or when invoked by meeting-sync.\n140\targument-hint: \"[days-back]\"\n141\t---\n142\t\n143\t=== new-project :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n144\t---\n145\tname: new-project\n146\tdescription: Scaffold a new project in DEV the standard way: git repo, AGENTS.md with the session routine, CLAUDE.md pointer, docs/STATUS.md, .gitignore, private GitHub repo under erash11. Use when Eric starts a new project or says 'set this up as a repo'.\n147\t---\n148\t\n149\t=== pbir-report-builder :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n150\t---\n151\tname: pbir-report-builder\n152\tdescription: \"Generates Power BI report pages, visuals, and IBCS-compliant variance charts by writing PBIR JSON into PBIP project folders. Use whenever the user wants to create a Power BI page, add visuals, generate KPI cards, build charts, tables or dashboard layouts, or mentions 'PBIR', 'IBCS', 'variance chart', 'variance table', 'actual vs plan'.\"\n153\t---\n154\t\n155\t=== pp-catapult-openfield-connect :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n156\t---\n157\tname: pp-catapult-openfield-connect\n158\tdescription: \"Every Catapult GPS metric — ACWR, velocity benchmarks, load reports — from one command, with a local SQLite mirror for offline analysis. Trigger phrases: `check ACWR for the squad`, `what is the player load from today's session`, `compare the last two matches`, `who is at injury risk`, `generate a weekly load report`, `sync Catapult data`, `use catapult-openfield-connect`, `run catapult CLI`.\"\n159\tauthor: \"erash11\"\n160\tlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\n161\targument-hint: \"<command> [args] | install cli|mcp\"\n162\tallowed-tools: \"Read Bash\"\n163\tmetadata:\n164\t  openclaw:\n165\t    requires:\n166\t      bins:\n167\t        - catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli\n168\t    install:\n169\t      - kind: go\n170\t        bins: [catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli]\n171\t        module: github.com/mvanhorn/printing-press-library/library/health/catapult-openfield-connect/cmd/catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli\n172\t---\n173\t\n174\t=== pp-espn :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n175\t---\n176\tname: pp-espn\n177\tdescription: \"ESPN sports CLI — live scores, standings, team stats, schedules, polls, rankings, and game summaries (box score, leaders, scoring plays, odds, win probability) across NFL / NBA / MLB / NHL / NCAA / MLS / EPL / WNBA. Use for 'what's the score of the Lakers game', 'Patriots schedule this week', 'NFL standings', 'box score', head-to-head comparisons, 'who's on top of the AP poll'. No API key required.\"\n178\tauthor: \"Matt Van Horn\"\n179\tlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\n180\targument-hint: \"<command> [args] | install cli|mcp\"\n181\tallowed-tools: \"Read Bash\"\n182\tmetadata:\n183\t  openclaw:\n184\t    requires:\n185\t      bins:\n186\t        - espn-pp-cli\n187\t    install:\n188\t      - kind: go\n189\t        bins: [espn-pp-cli]\n190\t        module: github.com/mvanhorn/printing-press-library/library/media-and-entertainment/espn/cmd/espn-pp-cli\n191\t---\n192\t\n193\t=== pp-fireflies :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n194\t---\n195\tname: pp-fireflies\n196\tdescription: \"Query Fireflies via fireflies-pp-cli — offline transcript search, cross-meeting intelligence, speaker analytics, local SQLite. For writing vault summaries use meeting-sync instead. Trigger phrases: `find stale action items from meetings`, `search my meeting transcripts for`, `who talked most in recent meetings`, `sync fireflies meetings`, `use fireflies-pp-cli`, `run fireflies`, `what did we discuss with`.\"\n197\tauthor: \"Nikica Jokic\"\n198\tlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\n199\targument-hint: \"<command> [args] | install cli|mcp\"\n200\tallowed-tools: \"Read Bash\"\n201\tmetadata:\n202\t  openclaw:\n203\t    requires:\n204\t      bins:\n205\t        - fireflies-pp-cli\n206\t    install:\n207\t      - kind: go\n208\t        bins: [fireflies-pp-cli]\n209\t        module: github.com/mvanhorn/printing-press-library/library/productivity/fireflies/cmd/fireflies-pp-cli\n210\t---\n211\t\n212\t=== pp-zotero-research-library :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n213\t---\n214\tname: pp-zotero-research-library\n215\tdescription: \"Your entire Zotero research library, searchable offline — version-based incremental sync into SQLite with full-text search no other Zotero tool has. Trigger phrases: `search my Zotero library`, `what does my library say about`, `find papers about`, `sync my Zotero library`, `what did I add to Zotero this week`, `get the citation for`, `use zotero-research-library`, `run zotero cli`.\"\n216\tauthor: \"Eric Rash\"\n217\tlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\n218\targument-hint: \"<command> [args] | install cli|mcp\"\n219\tallowed-tools: \"Read Bash\"\n220\tmetadata:\n221\t  openclaw:\n222\t    requires:\n223\t      bins:\n224\t        - zotero-research-library-pp-cli\n225\t    install:\n226\t      - kind: go\n227\t        bins: [zotero-research-library-pp-cli]\n228\t        module: github.com/mvanhorn/printing-press-library/library/productivity/zotero-research-library/cmd/zotero-research-library-pp-cli\n229\t---\n230\t\n231\t=== project-triage :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n232\t---\n233\tname: project-triage\n234\tdescription: Generate the DEV/ project triage HTML dashboard for today or a backfill date, surfacing drift between curated and current state. Use when the user says \"project triage\", \"/project-triage\", \"run my project review\", \"dev dashboard\", \"what's open in DEV\", \"morning review\", or asks to see the open-projects HTML.\n235\targument-hint: \"[YYYY-MM-DD]\"\n236\t---\n237\t\n238\t=== project :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n239\t---\n240\tname: project\n241\tdescription: Manage the portfolio project registry (ideas, updates, ranking, promotion, dev stages) and render/publish the dashboard. Triggers on \"/project\", \"new idea:\", \"log progress on\", \"project update\", \"add to my project inbox\", \"show my projects\", \"re-rank my projects\", \"set the stage on\", \"mark <project> as spec'd/planned/shipped\".\n242\t---\n243\t\n244\t=== session-miner :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n245\t---\n246\tname: session-miner\n247\tdescription: Mine recent Claude Code sessions for learnings that never got captured — repeated corrections, decisions with rationale, gotchas, and workflows worth turning into skills — and route each to memory, the vault, or a skill edit. Use when the user says \"/session-miner\", \"what did we miss\", \"review recent sessions\", \"mine my history\", or \"anything from this week worth keeping?\".\n248\t---\n249\t\n250\t=== sports-science-research-grounding :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n251\t---\n252\tname: sports-science-research-grounding\n253\tdescription: Use automatically for substantive questions about sport science, return to play or sport, rehabilitation, strength and conditioning, workload, recovery, testing, athlete health, injury, performance, research-backed answers, and Zotero full-library batch processing. Searches the user's Zotero library first, clearly labels external peer-reviewed fallback sources, and applies tier-aware model routing during bounded batch work.\n254\t---\n255\t\n256\t=== startup :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n257\t---\n258\tname: startup\n259\tdescription: \"Start of day, or sitting down at either machine: sync this machine against GitHub, then report where the last session left off and wait. Use when Eric says '/startup', 'good morning', 'starting up', 'where did I leave off', 'what was I working on', 'picking this back up', or opens a session without naming a task.\"\n260\t---\n261\t\n262\t=== status-report :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n263\t---\n264\tname: status-report\n265\tdescription: Build the every-two-weeks Applied Performance status report for Kenny Boyd and Chris Ruf — paste-ready email, one-page PDF, internal record. Use when the user says \"/status-report\", \"build my status report\", \"time for the Chris report\", \"biweekly update\", \"status update for Chris and Kenny\", \"what do I send Chris this week\", or when a scheduled report date arrives.\n266\t---\n267\t\n268\t=== weekly-review :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n269\t---\n270\tname: weekly-review\n271\tdescription: Friday close-of-week synthesis ritual. Pulls the last 7 days of meetings, interview notes, and permanent notes from the SecondBrain vault and produces a single weekly review note covering themes, project status, decisions, stale action items, essay angles, and next-week priorities. Use when user says \"/weekly-review\", \"weekly review\", \"Friday review\", \"let's do this week's review\", \"weekly synthesis\", or \"what should I work on next week?\".\n272\t---\n273\t"}]},"uuid":"ae07cfcc-050a-4b87-9c08-30f04a42def6","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:35:59.103Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t5-failing-frontmatter.txt","content":"=== Harvest :: name 'harvest' != directory 'Harvest' | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: harvest\ndescription: Distill a finished project into evergreen Knowledge/ articles in the SecondBrain vault and log the shipped artifact in the output ledger. Use when the user says \"/harvest <project>\", \"harvest this project\", \"distill what we learned from X\", declares a project finished/shipped/done, or when a session ends with a clearly shipped deliverable worth recording.\nargument-hint: \"[project]\"\n---\n\n=== capture-insight :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: capture-insight\ndescription: Capture a story, win, or lesson the user just shared as a permanent atomic note in the SecondBrain vault. Use when the user tells a story or lesson and says \"capture this\", \"save this win/lesson\", \"that's worth a note\", or \"/capture-insight\". For end-of-day structured capture use interview-me; for whole-project distillation use harvest; for plain facts use memory-write.\n---\n\n=== claude-stack-doctor :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: claude-stack-doctor\ndescription: Health-check Eric's automation/memory stack in one pass, and verify the Mac-to-Windows handoff actually works — launchd agents (com.keystone.morning, agysync, dailybackup, rituals, reconcile, adjudicate), Python venvs, memsearch, memory-compiler flush pipeline, backup freshness, and context budget — and diagnose what's silently broken. Use when the user says \"/claude-stack-doctor\", \"stack doctor\", \"is my stack healthy\", \"did my scheduled jobs run\", \"check the memory pipeline\", \"why didn't the backup run\", or when closeout/morning sessions should verify automation health.\n---\n\n=== closeout :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: closeout\ndescription: End-of-session sign-off ritual. Sweeps loose ends, commits and pushes what needs it, verifies memory capture, writes a cross-harness handoff, and reports \"clear to sign off\" or what's still open. Use when the user says \"/closeout\", \"any loose ends?\", \"am I good to sign off?\", \"close out for the night\", \"closing out\", \"goodnight\", \"wrap up for the day\", or asks for a system health check before leaving.\n---\n\n=== dev-sync :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: dev-sync\ndescription: \"Bring this machine into line with GitHub and load back the context that came with it: locate DEV automatically, pull config and skills, inventory every project, commit and push local work, pull the other machine's work, clone what is missing, report conflicts, then read the repo's STATUS and latest handoff and report where the last session left off. Use when Eric switches machines, sits down to start work, says 'sync DEV', asks whether everything is pushed, or asks where he left off.\"\n---\n\n=== doctor-plus :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: doctor-plus\ndescription: Runs Claude Code's built-in /doctor health check, then audits the workspace against the 6 then-and-now context-engineering shifts Anthropic shipped with the Claude 5 models (rules to judgement, examples to interfaces, upfront to progressive disclosure, repeats to tool descriptions, CLAUDE.md memory to auto-memory, simple specs to rich references). Reports findings first, fixes only on approval. Triggers on \"/doctor-plus\", \"doctor plus\", \"doctor-plus\", \"extended doctor\", \"then and now audit\", \"context checkup\".\n---\n\n=== fireflies-intake :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: fireflies-intake\ndescription: One-command Fireflies pipeline — sync new meeting transcripts into the SecondBrain vault, rename generically-titled meetings, then report exactly what was ingested. Use when the user says \"/fireflies-intake\", \"ingest my recent fireflies meetings\", \"sync meetings that aren't in the second brain yet\", \"pull in the new meetings\", \"meeting ingestion\", or asks whether all recent meetings have been ingested.\nargument-hint: \"[since-date]\"\n---\n\n=== five-slides-generator :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: five-slides-generator\ndescription: \"Generate a '5 Slides in 5 Minutes' PowerPoint deck for Baylor Athletics Applied Performance — research, narrative, pptxgenjs, .pptx build, QA. Use whenever the user mentions '5 slides,' '5 slides in 5 minutes,' or gives a topic they want a Performance School deck on. Also trigger for a cross-functional staff presentation, a quick sport science deck, or any short educational deck in the established series format (CMJ, GPS, VBT are prior examples).\"\nargument-hint: \"[topic]\"\n---\n\n=== forecast-capture :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: forecast-capture\ndescription: Capture and freeze the CFB Victory Model's pre-game forecasts before kickoff, then report what moved since last week. Run every Wednesday during the season. Use when the user says \"/forecast-capture\", \"capture the forecast\", \"freeze this week's predictions\", \"run the CFB capture\", \"did we capture this week\", or asks whether the weekly model snapshot has been taken.\n---\n\n=== game-film-timestamps :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: game-film-timestamps\ndescription: >\n  Fix wrong startTime/endTime values in football game film JSON exported from Hudl, DVSport, or\n  similar. Fetches correct wall-clock timestamps from the ESPN API and writes corrected copies.\n  Use whenever the user mentions fixing or correcting play-by-play timestamps in game film JSON,\n  or has files with \"OFF\", \"DEF\", or \"KICKS\" in the filename and mentions timestamps or time issues.\nargument-hint: \"[game-files folder]\"\n---\n\n=== graphify :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: graphify\ndescription: \"Use for any question about a codebase, its architecture, file relationships, or project content — especially when graphify-out/ exists, where the question should be treated as a graphify query first. Turns any input (code, docs, papers, images, videos) into a persistent knowledge graph with god nodes, community detection, and query/path/explain tools.\"\n---\n\n=== html-to-pdf :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: html-to-pdf\ndescription: Render any local HTML report, deck, or dashboard to a print-ready PDF via headless Chrome — replaces the manual Ctrl+P → Save as PDF ritual. Use when the user says \"export this to PDF\", \"print version\", \"PDF for the coaches\", \"make this printable\", or a coach-facing HTML deliverable needs a shareable/printable copy.\nargument-hint: \"[html-path] [out-pdf]\"\n---\n\n=== improve-system :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: improve-system\ndescription: Audit the SecondBrain vault for rot — stale seed notes, conflicting claims, and duplicate notes — and propose merge/archive/update actions. Use when the user says \"/improve-system\", \"audit my notes\", \"audit the vault\", \"find stale/duplicate notes\", or \"clean up my second brain\". For mining sessions for missed learnings use session-miner; for capturing a win/lesson use capture-insight; for improving a skill use write-a-skill.\n---\n\n=== ingest-book :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: ingest-book\ndescription: Ingest a book (PDF/EPUB full-text, Kindle highlights, or framework-only from a physical book) into the SecondBrain library as atomized, citable advisor entries. Use when the user wants to \"ingest a book\", \"add a book to my library/advisors\", \"/ingest-book\", or points at a book file for the advisor system. For articles/transcripts/general resources use ingest-resource instead.\nargument-hint: \"[book file or title] [domain]\"\n---\n\n=== ingest-resource :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: ingest-resource\ndescription: Ingest any article, YouTube link, transcript, PDF, or note into the SecondBrain vault — routes it to Knowledge/ (stable info) or Projects/ (active work), adds a summary block, and cross-links related notes with [[wikilinks]]. Use when the user shares a URL, file, or pasted content and says \"ingest\", \"save this\", \"add to my vault/second brain\", \"/ingest-resource\", or drops a resource with intent to keep it.\nargument-hint: \"[URL or file path]\"\n---\n\n=== library-review :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: library-review\ndescription: Review a book-library domain for gaps, contested entries, and missing coverage, and propose new entries. Manual loop — proposes, you approve. Use when the user says \"review my library\", \"/library-review <domain>\", \"what's missing from my <domain> advisor\", or after a batch of ingestion.\nargument-hint: \"[domain]\"\n---\n\n=== meeting-prep :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: meeting-prep\ndescription: Pre-meeting readiness brief for a project — what changed, what's open, every deliverable path. Use when the user says \"/meeting-prep <project>\", \"I have a meeting with <person> — are we in a good spot on <project>?\", \"verify we're up to speed before the meeting\", \"get me ready for this afternoon's meeting\", or names an upcoming coach/staff meeting.\nargument-hint: \"[project]\"\n---\n\n=== meeting-sync :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: meeting-sync\ndescription: Sync new Fireflies transcripts into the SecondBrain vault; audit vault filenames for drift against Fireflies titles. Idempotent. Use when the user says \"sync meetings\", \"pull latest meetings\", \"/meeting-sync\", \"update meeting notes\", \"any new meetings?\", or when invoked by weekly-review. Also for filename drift — \"are any meeting files misnamed?\", \"did a meeting get renamed after export?\", \"why is this meeting titled differently in Fireflies than in the vault?\", \"audit the meeting filenames\".\nargument-hint: \"[days-back]\"\n---\n\n=== memory-write :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: memory-write\ndescription: >\n  Writes, updates, removes, and recalls facts in the two-tier memory system at\n  ~/.claude/global-memory/ and ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/. Use for write\n  requests such as \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"update memory\", \"save this\",\n  and \"forget about\", and for recall requests such as \"did we already…?\",\n  \"what did we decide about X?\", and \"do you remember…?\". For writes, selects\n  the correct tier and enforces deduplication and character caps. For recall,\n  checks the injected snapshot first, then follows the memsearch retrieval ladder.\n---\n\n=== name-meetings :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: name-meetings\ndescription: Detects Fireflies meetings with generic titles (empty, \"Zoom Meeting\", \"Recording\", date-only, etc.), proposes structured names based on AI summary + participants, and applies approved renames via the Fireflies API. Use when user says \"/name-meetings\", \"name my meetings\", \"rename untitled meetings\", \"fix meeting titles\", \"my meetings have no names\", or when invoked by meeting-sync.\nargument-hint: \"[days-back]\"\n---\n\n=== new-project :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: new-project\ndescription: Scaffold a new project in DEV the standard way: git repo, AGENTS.md with the session routine, CLAUDE.md pointer, docs/STATUS.md, .gitignore, private GitHub repo under erash11. Use when Eric starts a new project or says 'set this up as a repo'.\n---\n\n=== pbir-report-builder :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: pbir-report-builder\ndescription: \"Generates Power BI report pages, visuals, and IBCS-compliant variance charts by writing PBIR JSON into PBIP project folders. Use whenever the user wants to create a Power BI page, add visuals, generate KPI cards, build charts, tables or dashboard layouts, or mentions 'PBIR', 'IBCS', 'variance chart', 'variance table', 'actual vs plan'.\"\n---\n\n=== pp-catapult-openfield-connect :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: pp-catapult-openfield-connect\ndescription: \"Every Catapult GPS metric — ACWR, velocity benchmarks, load reports — from one command, with a local SQLite mirror for offline analysis. Trigger phrases: `check ACWR for the squad`, `what is the player load from today's session`, `compare the last two matches`, `who is at injury risk`, `generate a weekly load report`, `sync Catapult data`, `use catapult-openfield-connect`, `run catapult CLI`.\"\nauthor: \"erash11\"\nlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\nargument-hint: \"<command> [args] | install cli|mcp\"\nallowed-tools: \"Read Bash\"\nmetadata:\n  openclaw:\n    requires:\n      bins:\n        - catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli\n    install:\n      - kind: go\n        bins: [catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli]\n        module: github.com/mvanhorn/printing-press-library/library/health/catapult-openfield-connect/cmd/catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli\n---\n\n=== pp-espn :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: pp-espn\ndescription: \"ESPN sports CLI — live scores, standings, team stats, schedules, polls, rankings, and game summaries (box score, leaders, scoring plays, odds, win probability) across NFL / NBA / MLB / NHL / NCAA / MLS / EPL / WNBA. Use for 'what's the score of the Lakers game', 'Patriots schedule this week', 'NFL standings', 'box score', head-to-head comparisons, 'who's on top of the AP poll'. No API key required.\"\nauthor: \"Matt Van Horn\"\nlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\nargument-hint: \"<command> [args] | install cli|mcp\"\nallowed-tools: \"Read Bash\"\nmetadata:\n  openclaw:\n    requires:\n      bins:\n        - espn-pp-cli\n    install:\n      - kind: go\n        bins: [espn-pp-cli]\n        module: github.com/mvanhorn/printing-press-library/library/media-and-entertainment/espn/cmd/espn-pp-cli\n---\n\n=== pp-fireflies :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: pp-fireflies\ndescription: \"Query Fireflies via fireflies-pp-cli — offline transcript search, cross-meeting intelligence, speaker analytics, local SQLite. For writing vault summaries use meeting-sync instead. Trigger phrases: `find stale action items from meetings`, `search my meeting transcripts for`, `who talked most in recent meetings`, `sync fireflies meetings`, `use fireflies-pp-cli`, `run fireflies`, `what did we discuss with`.\"\nauthor: \"Nikica Jokic\"\nlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\nargument-hint: \"<command> [args] | install cli|mcp\"\nallowed-tools: \"Read Bash\"\nmetadata:\n  openclaw:\n    requires:\n      bins:\n        - fireflies-pp-cli\n    install:\n      - kind: go\n        bins: [fireflies-pp-cli]\n        module: github.com/mvanhorn/printing-press-library/library/productivity/fireflies/cmd/fireflies-pp-cli\n---\n\n=== pp-zotero-research-library :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: pp-zotero-research-library\ndescription: \"Your entire Zotero research library, searchable offline — version-based incremental sync into SQLite with full-text search no other Zotero tool has. Trigger phrases: `search my Zotero library`, `what does my library say about`, `find papers about`, `sync my Zotero library`, `what did I add to Zotero this week`, `get the citation for`, `use zotero-research-library`, `run zotero cli`.\"\nauthor: \"Eric Rash\"\nlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\nargument-hint: \"<command> [args] | install cli|mcp\"\nallowed-tools: \"Read Bash\"\nmetadata:\n  openclaw:\n    requires:\n      bins:\n        - zotero-research-library-pp-cli\n    install:\n      - kind: go\n        bins: [zotero-research-library-pp-cli]\n        module: github.com/mvanhorn/printing-press-library/library/productivity/zotero-research-library/cmd/zotero-research-library-pp-cli\n---\n\n=== project-triage :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: project-triage\ndescription: Generate the DEV/ project triage HTML dashboard for today or a backfill date, surfacing drift between curated and current state. Use when the user says \"project triage\", \"/project-triage\", \"run my project review\", \"dev dashboard\", \"what's open in DEV\", \"morning review\", or asks to see the open-projects HTML.\nargument-hint: \"[YYYY-MM-DD]\"\n---\n\n=== project :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: project\ndescription: Manage the portfolio project registry (ideas, updates, ranking, promotion, dev stages) and render/publish the dashboard. Triggers on \"/project\", \"new idea:\", \"log progress on\", \"project update\", \"add to my project inbox\", \"show my projects\", \"re-rank my projects\", \"set the stage on\", \"mark <project> as spec'd/planned/shipped\".\n---\n\n=== session-miner :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: session-miner\ndescription: Mine recent Claude Code sessions for learnings that never got captured — repeated corrections, decisions with rationale, gotchas, and workflows worth turning into skills — and route each to memory, the vault, or a skill edit. Use when the user says \"/session-miner\", \"what did we miss\", \"review recent sessions\", \"mine my history\", or \"anything from this week worth keeping?\".\n---\n\n=== sports-science-research-grounding :: no standalone positive clause ('Use when ...') - Claude will not trigger (a 'use when' governed by 'do not use when' does not count) | no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: sports-science-research-grounding\ndescription: Use automatically for substantive questions about sport science, return to play or sport, rehabilitation, strength and conditioning, workload, recovery, testing, athlete health, injury, performance, research-backed answers, and Zotero full-library batch processing. Searches the user's Zotero library first, clearly labels external peer-reviewed fallback sources, and applies tier-aware model routing during bounded batch work.\n---\n\n=== startup :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: startup\ndescription: \"Start of day, or sitting down at either machine: sync this machine against GitHub, then report where the last session left off and wait. Use when Eric says '/startup', 'good morning', 'starting up', 'where did I leave off', 'what was I working on', 'picking this back up', or opens a session without naming a task.\"\n---\n\n=== status-report :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: status-report\ndescription: Build the every-two-weeks Applied Performance status report for Kenny Boyd and Chris Ruf — paste-ready email, one-page PDF, internal record. Use when the user says \"/status-report\", \"build my status report\", \"time for the Chris report\", \"biweekly update\", \"status update for Chris and Kenny\", \"what do I send Chris this week\", or when a scheduled report date arrives.\n---\n\n=== weekly-review :: no negative clause ('Do not use ...') - Codex over-fires\n---\nname: weekly-review\ndescription: Friday close-of-week synthesis ritual. Pulls the last 7 days of meetings, interview notes, and permanent notes from the SecondBrain vault and produces a single weekly review note covering themes, project status, decisions, stale action items, essay angles, and next-week priorities. Use when user says \"/weekly-review\", \"weekly review\", \"Friday review\", \"let's do this week's review\", \"weekly synthesis\", or \"what should I work on next week?\".\n---\n","numLines":273,"startLine":1,"totalLines":273}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"54bf1208-c8ab-45be-ad5b-09ab9ac95243","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
