{"parentUuid":"7dc5841c-eb28-45c2-ba7d-002d405f3a7f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0135VXtHtd6sHxxU6uZz7wfk","type":"tool_result","content":"name: library-advisor\ndescription: Consult a grounded domain advisor built from your curated book library. Answers ONLY from ingested library entries, cites every claim, and explicitly separates grounded knowledge from general knowledge. Use when the user says \"ask my <domain> advisor\", \"/library-advisor <domain> <question>\", \"what would my library say about…\", \"consult my library advisor\", or consults a standing advisor. Domains live in SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/advisors/. NOT FOR the built-in /advisor reviewer command, which is a different tool.\nargument-hint: \"[domain] [question]\"\n=== library-review ===\nname: library-review\ndescription: >-\n  Review a book-library domain for gaps, contested entries, and missing coverage, and\n  propose new entries. Manual loop — proposes, you approve. Use when the user says\n  \"review my library\", \"/library-review <domain>\", \"what's missing from my <domain>\n  advisor\", or after a batch of ingestion. Do not use to ask the library a question (use\n  library-advisor) or to add a new book (use ingest-book).\nargument-hint: \"[domain]\"\n=== git: library-advisor changed? ===\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"28284073-71de-4b9f-a30e-b430e615485d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:41:25.967Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"name: library-advisor\ndescription: Consult a grounded domain advisor built from your curated book library. Answers ONLY from ingested library entries, cites every claim, and explicitly separates grounded knowledge from general knowledge. Use when the user says \"ask my <domain> advisor\", \"/library-advisor <domain> <question>\", \"what would my library say about…\", \"consult my library advisor\", or consults a standing advisor. Domains live in SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/advisors/. NOT FOR the built-in /advisor reviewer command, which is a different tool.\nargument-hint: \"[domain] [question]\"\n=== library-review ===\nname: library-review\ndescription: >-\n  Review a book-library domain for gaps, contested entries, and missing coverage, and\n  propose new entries. Manual loop — proposes, you approve. Use when the user says\n  \"review my library\", \"/library-review <domain>\", \"what's missing from my <domain>\n  advisor\", or after a batch of ingestion. Do not use to ask the library a question (use\n  library-advisor) or to add a new book (use ingest-book).\nargument-hint: \"[domain]\"\n=== git: library-advisor changed? ===","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7dc5841c-eb28-45c2-ba7d-002d405f3a7f","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
