{"parentUuid":"fb76afb7-67c5-4d53-b555-2b5d84292c36","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014La4XSih5LY6XxV3cXA9S4","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"20fa0e17-fef9-4381-a214-1f66c8bad78f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:45:27.668Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","oldString":"Committed `5f80203` (erash11/claude-skills) and pushed; HEAD == upstream; tree clean. The pre-commit hook allowed the deletions. |","newString":"Committed `5f80203` (erash11/claude-skills) and pushed; HEAD == upstream; tree clean. The pre-commit hook allowed the deletions. |\n\n## Task 5 — evidence\n\n| Step | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Checker extracted byte-for-byte from plan lines 1583–1732 (150 lines); compiles; `chmod +x`. |\n| 2 | Baseline `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`, exit 1. Empty inventory: `FATAL no SKILL.md found`, exit 2. Bad fixtures: all four FAIL for the stated reason (negonly: no standalone positive; dupekey: duplicate key; badquote: unbalanced quote; fragments: both clauses missing), exit 1. `dcg` blocks `rm -rf` inside a heredoc, so fixtures were built in fresh folders under the job tmp dir instead. |\n| 3 | 33 descriptions rewritten from a hand-written file, in plan priority order, five per batch, checker after each batch (every batch: 0 still failing). Only the description block changed (plus `Harvest` `name:` → `Harvest`). Word-diff vs HEAD: only connector words removed (`Triggers on`, `Trigger phrases`, `whenever`, `instead.`, `automatically`). A real YAML loader (`uv run --with pyyaml`) parses all 42; **`new-project` was invalid YAML before** (unquoted `: `). Bodies byte-identical to HEAD: a first pass normalised CRLF in `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn`; reverted to the original bytes. `library-advisor` got one extra `Do not use` sentence. |\n| 4 | `checked 42 skills, 0 failing, 42 portable`, exit 0. |\n| 5 | Headless runs, not interactive sessions (background job). `claude -p` with Bash/Write/Edit denied and a 3-turn cap; `codex exec -s read-only`. `memory-write`, `pp-zotero-research-library`, `meeting-prep`: loaded in **both** harnesses. `library-review`: loaded in Codex; **not listed in Claude Code at all**. |\n\n**Finding from Step 5, verified:** `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides`\nsets 12 canonical skills `\"off\"`: 7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`,\n`capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5\nthird-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code\nomits them from its skill list. Codex does not read that file, so it loads\nthem. This predates Task 5 (three of the seven were never edited). Two\nconsequences:\n\n- Harness parity is broken by config, not by frontmatter. This is an `aios-audit` finding.\n- Task 4 Step 7's \"`/skills` shows 61\" can never hold: Claude Code exposes 49 of the 61 (35 of 42 owned). The count was already this before the migration.\n\nA side-effect check after the `memory-write` runs found no memory file written\nin either harness.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":156,"oldLines":3,"newStart":156,"newLines":27,"lines":[" | 5 | 42 owned, 19 links, 61 resolvable `SKILL.md`, 0 dangling, `_shared OK`, meeting-sync resolves `_shared`: True |"," | 6 | Idempotent dry run exit 0; manifest 43 in both views; nothing missing; no wrong targets. **Pool skill count = 210** (Task 8 baseline) |"," | 7 | `/reload-skills` needs an interactive session, so this background job could not run it. Disk-level substitute: 61 resolvable `SKILL.md` (Step 5). **Eric to confirm `/skills` shows 61 in a live session.** Committed `5f80203` (erash11/claude-skills) and pushed; HEAD == upstream; tree clean. The pre-commit hook allowed the deletions. |","+","+## Task 5 — evidence","+","+| Step | Evidence |","+|---|---|","+| 1 | Checker extracted byte-for-byte from plan lines 1583–1732 (150 lines); compiles; `chmod +x`. |","+| 2 | Baseline `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`, exit 1. Empty inventory: `FATAL no SKILL.md found`, exit 2. Bad fixtures: all four FAIL for the stated reason (negonly: no standalone positive; dupekey: duplicate key; badquote: unbalanced quote; fragments: both clauses missing), exit 1. `dcg` blocks `rm -rf` inside a heredoc, so fixtures were built in fresh folders under the job tmp dir instead. |","+| 3 | 33 descriptions rewritten from a hand-written file, in plan priority order, five per batch, checker after each batch (every batch: 0 still failing). Only the description block changed (plus `Harvest` `name:` → `Harvest`). Word-diff vs HEAD: only connector words removed (`Triggers on`, `Trigger phrases`, `whenever`, `instead.`, `automatically`). A real YAML loader (`uv run --with pyyaml`) parses all 42; **`new-project` was invalid YAML before** (unquoted `: `). Bodies byte-identical to HEAD: a first pass normalised CRLF in `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn`; reverted to the original bytes. `library-advisor` got one extra `Do not use` sentence. |","+| 4 | `checked 42 skills, 0 failing, 42 portable`, exit 0. |","+| 5 | Headless runs, not interactive sessions (background job). `claude -p` with Bash/Write/Edit denied and a 3-turn cap; `codex exec -s read-only`. `memory-write`, `pp-zotero-research-library`, `meeting-prep`: loaded in **both** harnesses. `library-review`: loaded in Codex; **not listed in Claude Code at all**. |","+","+**Finding from Step 5, verified:** `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides`","+sets 12 canonical skills `\"off\"`: 7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`,","+`capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5","+third-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code","+omits them from its skill list. Codex does not read that file, so it loads","+them. This predates Task 5 (three of the seven were never edited). Two","+consequences:","+","+- Harness parity is broken by config, not by frontmatter. This is an `aios-audit` finding.","+- Task 4 Step 7's \"`/skills` shows 61\" can never hold: Claude Code exposes 49 of the 61 (35 of 42 owned). The count was already this before the migration.","+","+A side-effect check after the `memory-write` runs found no memory file written","+in either harness."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fb76afb7-67c5-4d53-b555-2b5d84292c36","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
