{"parentUuid":"ca84b0b1-f30d-4af9-8e4d-310822fb9341","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["<context_guidance>\n  <tip>\n    Reading to Edit the file? Read is correct — Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against.\n    Reading to analyze, summarize, or extract from the file? Use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code) — the bytes stay in the sandbox and only what your code prints enters your conversation.\n  </tip>\n</context_guidance>"],"hookName":"PreToolUse:Read","toolUseID":"toolu_01FimavkRwedsUFsAMnwP1Eh","hookEvent":"PreToolUse"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b185bf99-5963-4258-a9fc-9b5594575a08","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:45:37.863Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPreToolUse:Read hook additional context: <context_guidance>\n  <tip>\n    Reading to Edit the file? Read is correct — Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against.\n    Reading to analyze, summarize, or extract from the file? Use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code) — the bytes stay in the sandbox and only what your code prints enters your conversation.\n  </tip>\n</context_guidance>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"785b76fe-1565-4502-807e-86c24702d7e0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FimavkRwedsUFsAMnwP1Eh","type":"tool_result","content":"1881\t### Task 6: `rot.md` and the `aios-audit` compound skill\n1882\t\n1883\t**Files:**\n1884\t- Create: `~/.claude/rot.md`\n1885\t- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md`\n1886\t- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py`\n1887\t- Modify: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md` (cross-reference line only)\n1888\t\n1889\t**Interfaces:**\n1890\t- Consumes: `skill-portability-check.py` (Task 5) and the canonical repo (Task 4).\n1891\t- Produces: `aios-metrics.py`, printing a machine-readable metrics block Task 7's launchd job captures.\n1892\t\n1893\t**Placement is deliberate.** This skill is **project-level**, in `KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/`, not global — the promotion rule from the video (31:32). It gets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/` only after proving useful across 2+ projects.\n1894\t\n1895\t**It must not become a sixth audit skill.** Five exist and each owns a layer:\n1896\t\n1897\t| Existing skill | Owns |\n1898\t|---|---|\n1899\t| `os-audit` (project) | project data: routing, index truth, freshness, duplication |\n1900\t| `brain-audit` | SecondBrain as a system — the four C's |\n1901\t| `improve-system` | note-level rot: stale seeds, duplicates, conflicts |\n1902\t| `claude-stack-doctor` | automation plumbing: launchd, venvs, memsearch, backup freshness |\n1903\t| `doctor-plus` | context-engineering posture of the workspace |\n1904\t\n1905\t`aios-audit` owns the one layer none of them touch — **the harness itself**: skill roster, agents, hooks, rules, cross-harness parity. It **delegates** the other five rather than re-implementing them.\n1906\t\n1907\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write `~/.claude/rot.md`**\n1908\t\n1909\tNote the `Last audited` column (R10): every layer starts `unknown` except Skills, which was genuinely audited. A date is written only after that layer's check actually runs.\n1910\t\n1911\t```markdown\n1912\t# rot.md — how fast each AIOS layer goes stale\n1913\t\n1914\tAudit each layer on its own clock, not all at once. `aios-audit` reads this\n1915\tfile: any layer past due, or marked `unknown`, is a finding.\n1916\t\n1917\t**A date here is a receipt, not an intention.** Write one only after that\n1918\tlayer's check in the last column has actually run and produced output.\n1919\t\n1920\t| Layer | Where it lives | Rots | Audit every | Last audited | Owner | Concrete check |\n1921\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1922\t| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | unknown | memory-write | Read USER.md; flag any role, family, or career fact contradicted by the last 90 days of sessions. |\n1923\t| Substrate | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `~/DEV/*.md` routers | slow | 3 months | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 1 (routing integrity). |\n1924\t| Skills | `~/.claude/skills/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-12 | aios-audit | `skill-portability-check.py` + never-used list + the crutch test below. |\n1925\t| Agents | `~/.claude/agents/` | fast | 1 month | unknown | aios-audit | Count `*.md`. Currently **0 exist** — report \"no agents defined\" and skip until one does. |\n1926\t| Rules | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` behaviour rules, output styles | fastest | 1 week | unknown | aios-audit | Diff CLAUDE.md against the last 7 days of sessions: any rule contradicted by what actually happened, and any correction the user repeated twice that is not yet a rule. |\n1927\t| Hooks | `~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/` | slow | 6 months | unknown | claude-stack-doctor | Delegate. Also diff the two copies — they must match (`hook-two-copies-trap`). |\n1928\t| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | **aios-audit itself** | Audited directly — see the delegation contract below. `improve-system` does NOT cover these stores. Check: every `MEMORY.md` index line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index; `global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under its 2,500-char cap; flag time-dimensioned facts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures). |\n1929\t| Memory (vault notes) | `~/SecondBrain/` notes | medium | 1 month | unknown | improve-system | Delegate — but read-only, per the contract below. |\n1930\t| Data feeds | Fireflies, GPS, CFBD, Zotero | varies | 1 week | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 3 (freshness). |\n1931\t| Vault | `~/SecondBrain/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | brain-audit | Delegate to `brain-audit` (four C's score). |\n1932\t| Context posture | workspace-wide | medium | 3 months | unknown | doctor-plus | Delegate to `doctor-plus`. |\n1933\t\n1934\t## The question that governs a skill's fate\n1935\t\n1936\tNot \"how often did I run it?\" but **\"would the current model do this fine\n1937\twithout the skill?\"** If yes, the skill is a crutch that now limits the model.\n1938\tDelete it. Keep only skills carrying tacit knowledge the model cannot know:\n1939\tforce-plate thresholds, GPS conventions, Baylor reporting norms, Eric's own\n1940\troutines.\n1941\t\n1942\tSeasonal skills (`forecast-capture`, `ingest-book`) are exempt from low-use\n1943\tpressure. Judge them in season.\n1944\t\n1945\t## Delegation contract (R2-09)\n1946\t\n1947\tA delegate is invoked **read-only**, for a **named scope**, and its receipt is\n1948\twritten **only** for the scope it actually covered.\n1949\t\n1950\t1. **Read-only.** Before invoking a delegate, instruct it explicitly: report\n1951\t   findings, apply nothing, write no ledger, create no files. Several delegates\n1952\t   (`improve-system` among them) begin by applying previously approved proposals\n1953\t   — that must be suppressed. `aios-audit` writes only its own report and the\n1954\t   `Last audited` column.\n1955\t2. **Scope must be verified, not assumed.** A delegate's actual coverage is what\n1956\t   its body scans, not what this table wishes it scanned. `improve-system` scans\n1957\t   `~/SecondBrain/` — Notes, Knowledge, Projects. It does **not** touch\n1958\t   `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` or `global-memory/`. Those are audited by\n1959\t   `aios-audit` directly.\n1960\t3. **A receipt covers only what was checked.** If a delegate returns findings for\n1961\t   a narrower scope than its row claims, write the date **and** a scope note, or\n1962\t   leave the row `unknown`. Never stamp a date because a delegate exited cleanly.\n1963\t\n1964\t## Layout invariants the audit must assert\n1965\t\n1966\t- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n1967\t  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). On-disk links to third-party skills are\n1968\t  expected; they are listed in the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` (never the tracked\n1969\t  `.gitignore`), and a pre-commit hook refuses to commit one. What must never happen is\n1970\t  committing a link, because Windows pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n1971\t- `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are **generated views**. Each carries\n1972\t  a `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` manifest. Every entry **in the manifest** must be\n1973\t  a symlink on Mac (a copy on Windows); wrong representation is drift.\n1974\t- Entries **not** in the manifest are third-party installs (`npx skills add`).\n1975\t  They are counted and reported, **never** flagged as errors and never pruned.\n1976\t- Support directories (`_shared/`) have no SKILL.md and must never be pruned.\n1977\t\n1978\t## Direction of travel\n1979\t\n1980\t**Fewer skills, stricter rules.** Skills get deleted; rules get sharpened.\n1981\t```\n1982\t\n1983\tVerify: `head -30 ~/.claude/rot.md`\n1984\t\n1985\t- [ ] **Step 2: Write the metrics script**\n1986\t\n1987\tCreate `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py`. Counting is deduped by real path (R6) and session globbing is explicitly recursive:\n1988\t\n1989\t```python\n1990\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n1991\t\"\"\"Machine-readable AIOS metrics. stdlib only. Prints key=value lines only.\"\"\"\n1992\timport os, re, glob, subprocess, collections, datetime, sys, hashlib\n1993\t\n1994\tH = os.path.expanduser(\"~\")\n1995\tCANON = f\"{H}/.claude/skills\"\n1996\tPOOL = f\"{H}/.agents/skills\"\n1997\tCODEX = f\"{H}/.codex/skills\"\n1998\tBUILTIN = {'exit','clear','compact','rename','color','login','logout','plugin',\n1999\t'doctor','help','model','config','resume','cost','status','init','agents','mcp',\n2000\t'hooks','memory','review','vim','terminal-setup','install-github-app','add-dir',\n2001\t'bug','release-notes','pr-comments','ide','permissions','statusline',\n2002\t'output-style','todos','export','privacy-settings','upgrade','fast','artifacts',\n2003\t'tasks','loop','context','usage','rewind','sandbox','feedback','worktrees',\n2004\t'skills','reload-skills','reload-plugins','bashes','keybindings','theme'}\n2005\t\n2006\t# R8-01: ownership is structural. A real directory holding a SKILL.md is ours;\n2007\t# a symlink was installed by the skills CLI or vendored. The same rule is used\n2008\t# by skill-portability-check.py and both sync scripts - no name list to keep\n2009\t# in step across four files.\n2010\t\n2011\tdef owned(root):\n2012\t    \"\"\"Names under root that are OURS: a real directory holding a SKILL.md.\"\"\"\n2013\t    out = set()\n2014\t    for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, \"*\")):\n2015\t        b = os.path.basename(d)\n2016\t        if b.startswith('.') or os.path.islink(d):\n2017\t            continue\n2018\t        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\")):\n2019\t            out.add(b)\n2020\t    return out\n2021\t\n2022\tdef skills_in(root):\n2023\t    \"\"\"Count distinct skills under root, deduped by real path (R6).\n2024\t    glob traverses symlinked dirs, so a link and its target counted twice.\"\"\"\n2025\t    seen = set()\n2026\t    for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, \"*\")):\n2027\t        s = os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\")\n2028\t        if os.path.isfile(s):\n2029\t            seen.add(os.path.realpath(s))\n2030\t    return len(seen)\n2031\t\n2032\tdef names_in(root):\n2033\t    return {os.path.basename(d) for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, \"*\"))\n2034\t            if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\"))}\n2035\t\n2036\tdef usage():\n2037\t    c = collections.Counter()\n2038\t    for f in glob.glob(f\"{H}/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl\", recursive=True):\n2039\t        try:\n2040\t            for line in open(f, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\"):\n2041\t                if 'Skill' not in line and 'command-name' not in line:\n2042\t                    continue\n2043\t                for m in re.finditer(\n2044\t                        r'\"name\"\\s*:\\s*\"Skill\"\\s*,\\s*\"input\"\\s*:\\s*\\{[^}]*?\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"([^\"]+)\"', line):\n2045\t                    c[m.group(1)] += 1\n2046\t                for m in re.finditer(r'<command-name>/([a-zA-Z0-9:_-]+)</command-name>', line):\n2047\t                    c[m.group(1)] += 1\n2048\t        except Exception:\n2049\t            pass\n2050\t    return {k: v for k, v in c.items()\n2051\t            if k.split(':')[-1] not in BUILTIN and k not in BUILTIN}\n2052\t\n2053\tdef roster_tokens():\n2054\t    \"\"\"Frontmatter chars / 4 - what the OWNED roster costs per session.\n2055\t    Symlinked third-party skills are excluded; their cost is not ours to tune.\"\"\"\n2056\t    total = 0\n2057\t    for p in glob.glob(f\"{CANON}/*/SKILL.md\"):\n2058\t        if os.path.islink(os.path.dirname(p)):\n2059\t            continue\n2060\t        try:\n2061\t            t = open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\").read()\n2062\t            end = t.find(\"\\n---\", 3)\n2063\t            if t.startswith(\"---\") and end != -1:\n2064\t                total += len(t[4:end])\n2065\t        except Exception:\n2066\t            pass\n2067\t    return total // 4\n2068\t\n2069\tMANIFEST = \".generated-by-sync-to-codex\"\n2070\t\n2071\tdef view_manifest(root):\n2072\t    \"\"\"Entries sync-to-codex.sh owns in this view. Anything else is a\n2073\t    third-party install (R2-02) and is reported, never flagged as an error.\"\"\"\n2074\t    p = os.path.join(root, MANIFEST)\n2075\t    if not os.path.isfile(p):\n2076\t        return None\n2077\t    return {l.strip() for l in open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\") if l.strip()}\n2078\t\n2079\tSUPPORT = {\"_shared\"}\n2080\t\n2081\tdef tracked_symlinks():\n2082\t    \"\"\"Mode-120000 entries in the canonical repo's index. These are the ones\n2083\t    that reach Windows and break there; raw on-disk links do not, once\n2084\t    gitignored. Must be 0.\"\"\"\n2085\t    try:\n2086\t        out = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", CANON, \"ls-files\", \"-s\"],\n2087\t                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)\n2088\t        if out.returncode != 0:\n2089\t            return \"git_error\"\n2090\t        return sum(1 for l in out.stdout.splitlines() if l.startswith(\"120000\"))\n2091\t    except Exception:\n2092\t        return \"git_error\"\n2093\t\n2094\tdef canonical_expected():\n2095\t    \"\"\"What the views SHOULD carry: every canonical skill plus support dirs.\n2096\t    R3-07: the view's own manifest is not evidence. An empty or stale manifest\n2097\t    would otherwise report zero drift while every skill was missing.\"\"\"\n2098\t    want = set()\n2099\t    for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(CANON, \"*\")):\n2100\t        b = os.path.basename(d)\n2101\t        if b.startswith('.'):\n2102\t            continue\n2103\t        if os.path.islink(d):        # R8-01: third-party link, not ours to publish\n2104\t            continue\n2105\t        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\")) or b in SUPPORT:\n2106\t            want.add(b)\n2107\t    return want\n2108\t\n2109\tdef view_drift(root):\n2110\t    \"\"\"Drift = any way a view fails to be a faithful generated copy of\n2111\t    canonical. Checks membership against CANONICAL (not the manifest),\n2112\t    representation for this platform, link targets, and copy freshness.\"\"\"\n2113\t    man = view_manifest(root)\n2114\t    if man is None:\n2115\t        return \"no_manifest\"\n2116\t    want = canonical_expected()\n2117\t    expect_link = (sys.platform == \"darwin\")\n2118\t    n = 0\n2119\t\n2120\t    # 1. Manifest must agree with canonical, in both directions.\n2121\t    n += len(want - man)          # canonical skill the manifest forgot\n2122\t    n += len(man - want)          # manifest claims something canonical dropped\n2123\t\n2124\t    for name in want:\n2125\t        d = os.path.join(root, name)\n2126\t        src = os.path.join(CANON, name)\n2127\t        if not os.path.exists(d):\n2128\t            n += 1                                    # missing entirely\n2129\t        elif expect_link:\n2130\t            if not os.path.islink(d):\n2131\t                n += 1                                # edited the view\n2132\t            elif os.path.realpath(d) != os.path.realpath(src):\n2133\t                n += 1                                # link points somewhere else\n2134\t        else:\n2135\t            if os.path.islink(d):\n2136\t                n += 1                                # Windows expects a copy\n2137\t            elif not _same_tree(d, src):\n2138\t                n += 1                                # stale copy\n2139\t    return n\n2140\t\n2141\tdef _same_tree(a, b):\n2142\t    \"\"\"Staleness check for copy-mode views. R4-04: sizes are not enough - a\n2143\t    same-length edit to a trigger phrase, a command or a config value leaves\n2144\t    size signatures identical while behaviour differs. Hash the contents, and\n2145\t    treat an unreadable file as a verification FAILURE, never as a match.\"\"\"\n2146\t    def snap(root_):\n2147\t        out = {}\n2148\t        for dp, _, fs in os.walk(root_):\n2149\t            for f in fs:\n2150\t                p = os.path.join(dp, f)\n2151\t                rel = os.path.relpath(p, root_)\n2152\t                try:\n2153\t                    h = hashlib.sha256()\n2154\t                    with open(p, \"rb\") as fh:\n2155\t                        for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(65536), b\"\"):\n2156\t                            h.update(chunk)\n2157\t                    out[rel] = h.hexdigest()\n2158\t                except OSError as e:\n2159\t                    # Unreadable => cannot verify => must count as drift.\n2160\t                    out[rel] = f\"UNREADABLE:{e.errno}\"\n2161\t        return out\n2162\t    sa, sb = snap(a), snap(b)\n2163\t    if any(v.startswith(\"UNREADABLE:\") for v in sa.values()) or \\\n2164\t       any(v.startswith(\"UNREADABLE:\") for v in sb.values()):\n2165\t        return False\n2166\t    return sa == sb\n2167\t\n2168\tdef third_party_in_view(root):\n2169\t    \"\"\"Entries present in the view but not managed by sync-to-codex.\n2170\t    Informational: these are npx-installed skills other harnesses may need.\"\"\"\n2171\t    man = view_manifest(root)\n2172\t    if man is None:\n2173\t        return \"no_manifest\"\n2174\t    n = 0\n2175\t    for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, \"*\")):\n2176\t        b = os.path.basename(d)\n2177\t        if b.startswith('.') or b in man:\n2178\t            continue\n2179\t        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\")):\n2180\t            n += 1\n2181\t    return n\n2182\t\n2183\tdef dangling_in_view(root):\n2184\t    \"\"\"R5-01: abandoned links left after a canonical skill was deleted.\n2185\t    These are invisible to every other check - view_drift only looks at\n2186\t    names canonical still has, and third_party_in_view needs a readable\n2187\t    SKILL.md, which a dangling link does not provide. Uses os.listdir and\n2188\t    os.path.lexists so a broken link is still seen.\"\"\"\n2189\t    if not os.path.isdir(root):\n2190\t        return 0\n2191\t    n = 0\n2192\t    for b in os.listdir(root):\n2193\t        if b.startswith('.'):\n2194\t            continue\n2195\t        p = os.path.join(root, b)\n2196\t        if os.path.islink(p) and not os.path.exists(p):\n2197\t            n += 1\n2198\t    return n\n2199\t\n2200\tu = usage()\n2201\tcanon_names = owned(CANON)          # R8-01: owned roster = real directories\n2202\tout = [\n2203\t    (\"date\", datetime.date.today().isoformat()),\n2204\t    (\"canonical_skills\", len(canon_names)),\n2205\t    (\"third_party_links_in_canonical\",\n2206\t     len([d for d in glob.glob(f\"{CANON}/*\") if os.path.islink(d)])),\n2207\t    (\"pool_entries\", len(glob.glob(f\"{POOL}/*\"))),\n2208\t    (\"pool_skills\", skills_in(POOL)),\n2209\t    (\"codex_skills\", skills_in(CODEX)),\n2210\t    (\"project_skills\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/DEV/*/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md\"))),\n2211\t    # What must be zero is TRACKED symlinks. The third-party links legitimately\n2212\t    # remain on disk; they are excluded per-machine and the pre-commit hook\n2213\t    # refuses to commit one, so they can never reach Windows.\n2214\t    (\"tracked_symlinks_in_canonical\", tracked_symlinks()),\n2215\t    (\"pool_view_drift\", view_drift(POOL)),\n2216\t    (\"codex_view_drift\", view_drift(CODEX)),\n2217\t    (\"pool_third_party\", third_party_in_view(POOL)),\n2218\t    (\"codex_third_party\", third_party_in_view(CODEX)),\n2219\t    (\"pool_dangling\", dangling_in_view(POOL)),\n2220\t    (\"codex_dangling\", dangling_in_view(CODEX)),\n2221\t    (\"agents\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/.claude/agents/*.md\"))),\n2222\t    (\"hooks_claude\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/.claude/hooks/*\"))),\n2223\t    (\"hooks_codex\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/.codex/hooks/*\"))),\n2224\t    (\"sessions\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl\", recursive=True))),\n2225\t    (\"skills_ever_used\", len(u)),\n2226\t    (\"skills_used_3plus\", len([k for k, v in u.items() if v >= 3])),\n2227\t    (\"skills_used_once\", len([k for k, v in u.items() if v == 1])),\n2228\t    (\"never_used\", len(canon_names - set(u))),\n2229\t    (\"roster_tokens_est\", roster_tokens()),\n2230\t]\n2231\trc = subprocess.run([sys.executable, f\"{H}/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skill-portability-check.py\"],\n2232\t                    capture_output=True, text=True)\n2233\tm = re.search(r\"(\\d+) failing\", rc.stdout)\n2234\tout.append((\"portability_failures\", m.group(1) if m else f\"error_rc{rc.returncode}\"))\n2235\t\n2236\tfor k, v in out:\n2237\t    print(f\"{k}={v}\")\n2238\t```\n2239\t\n2240\t- [ ] **Step 3: Run it and check every value**\n2241\t\n2242\t```bash\n2243\tchmod +x ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\n2244\tpython3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\n2245\t```\n2246\t\n2247\tExpected: `key=value` lines only, no stack trace, and specifically:\n2248\t\n2249\t| Key | Expected | Meaning |\n2250\t|---|---|---|\n2251\t| `canonical_skills` | `42` | the roster we own — real directories only |\n2252\t| `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` | `0` | Task 4 invariant — no link may be **committed** |\n2253\t| `third_party_links_in_canonical` | `19` | skills-CLI installs and vendored links — excluded per-machine, expected, **not** an error; moves with every install |\n2254\t| `pool_view_drift` | `0` | every managed entry is represented correctly for this platform |\n2255\t| `codex_view_drift` | `0` | same, for the Codex view |\n2256\t| `pool_third_party` | `~150` | **informational, not an error** — `npx skills add` installs the audit reports but never touches (R2-02) |\n2257\t| `pool_dangling` / `codex_dangling` | `0` | abandoned links from a deleted canonical skill — invisible to every other check (R5-01) |\n2258\t| `project_skills` | `2` | `os-audit` + `aios-audit` |\n2259\t| `portability_failures` | `0` | Task 5 passed |\n2260\t\n2261\tA non-zero `*_drift` means someone edited a generated view instead of the canonical source — fix before continuing. A large `*_third_party` is expected and correct; it is a number to watch, not a failure. `no_manifest` in either drift field means `sync-to-codex.sh` has not run since Task 3.\n2262\t\n2263\t- [ ] **Step 4: Write the `aios-audit` skill**\n2264\t\n2265\tInvoke `CreateSkill` first — it owns skill authoring here. Create `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md` with frontmatter that satisfies Task 5's contract:\n2266\t\n2267\t```yaml\n2268\t---\n2269\tname: aios-audit\n2270\tdescription: >-\n2271\t  Audit the whole AI operating system across decay tiers - skills, agents,\n2272\t  hooks, rules, memory, and cross-harness parity between Claude Code, Codex,\n2273\t  and Pi - then propose exactly two next builds. Use when the user says\n2274\t  \"/aios-audit\", \"audit my system\", \"audit my AI OS\", \"audit the bloat\",\n2275\t  \"is my setup rotting\", \"what should I cut\", \"are my skills portable\",\n2276\t  \"monthly skill audit\", or when rot.md shows a layer past its audit date.\n2277\t  Do not use for project data drift, routing, or index freshness - use\n2278\t  os-audit. Do not use for launchd, venv, or backup health - use\n2279\t  claude-stack-doctor. Do not use for SecondBrain note rot - use\n2280\t  improve-system or brain-audit.\n2281\tmetadata:\n2282\t  short-description: Decay-tier audit of the AI OS; delegates to the five layer-specific audit skills.\n2283\targument-hint: \"[optional: a layer name from rot.md]\"\n2284\tallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Agent\n2285\t---\n2286\t```\n2287\t\n2288\tThe body must specify, in order:\n2289\t\n2290\t1. **Read-only.** The only writes are the report and `rot.md`'s `Last audited` column. **Never delete a skill during the audit** — propose, then wait for approval.\n2291\t2. **Step 0 — read `~/.claude/rot.md`.** Compute days since each layer's `Last audited`. A layer that is past due **or `unknown`** gets audited this run; layers inside their window are reported green and skipped. That is what makes a monthly run cheap.\n2292\t3. **Step 1 — run `python3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py`** and capture every value.\n2293\t4. **Step 2 — assert the layout invariants** from `rot.md`. `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical`, `pool_view_drift`, `codex_view_drift`, `pool_dangling` and `codex_dangling` must all be `0`. `third_party_links_in_canonical` (19 today) is **information, not a finding** — it changes every time a skill is installed. Drift means someone edited a generated view instead of the canonical repo; a dangling count means a deleted canonical skill left an abandoned link behind — both are RED. Report `pool_third_party` and `codex_third_party` as **information**, never as errors — those are deliberately preserved installs.\n2294\t5. **Step 3 — delegate under the contract, do not duplicate.** For each due layer, invoke the owning skill named in the `rot.md` table **read-only**, following the delegation contract in `rot.md`: suppress any apply/ledger step, state the scope you need, and fold the findings under that layer's heading. Audit the harness layer and the agent-memory stores directly — no delegate covers those.\n2295\t6. **Step 4 — the harness layer, audited directly:**\n2296\t   - **Bloat:** every canonical skill never invoked across all sessions. List them.\n2297\t   - **Crutch test:** for each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md` question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge), or SEASONAL, one line of reasoning each.\n2298\t   - **Overlap:** skills whose descriptions cover the same trigger space. Recommend merging.\n2299\t   - **Parity:** run `skill-portability-check.py`. Every failure is a finding.\n2300\t   - **Promotion:** global skills used in fewer than 2 projects — demotion candidates. Project skills used in 2+ — promotion candidates.\n2301\t   - **Rules:** diff `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` against the last 7 days of sessions. Report rules contradicted by what actually happened, and corrections the user repeated twice that are not yet rules.\n2302\t   - **Agents:** count `~/.claude/agents/*.md`. If `0`, report \"no agents defined\" and skip — do not invent a finding.\n2303\t7. **Step 5 — write the report** to `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-YYYY-MM-DD.md` and update `Last audited` in `rot.md` **only for layers whose check actually ran and produced output**. Do **not** write to `aios-trend.md`: `aios-audit-cron.sh` is its single writer (R8-08) — two writers produced rows with no header. Commit the cron's waiting trend row as part of the audit.\n2304\t8. **Step 6 — end with exactly two proposed next builds,** ranked, each with the one command that starts it. Not ten. Two.\n2305\t\n2306\t- [ ] **Step 5: Cross-reference `os-audit` so the two do not fight**\n2307\t\n2308\tAdd near the top of `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md`:\n2309\t\n2310\t```markdown\n2311\t> Scope note: this skill audits **project data** — routing, indexes, freshness,\n2312\t> duplication. The harness layer (skills, agents, hooks, rules, cross-harness\n2313\t> parity) belongs to `aios-audit`, which calls this skill for the data layer.\n2314\t```\n2315\t\n2316\t- [ ] **Step 6: Smoke-test end to end**\n2317\t\n2318\tIn a Claude Code session with cwd `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`, run `/reload-skills`, then type \"audit my AI OS\". Expected: `aios-audit` fires, reads `rot.md`, runs the metrics script, produces a report, and ends with exactly two proposals.\n2319\t\n2320\t```bash\n2321\tls -l ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-*.md\n2322\tgrep -c 'unknown' ~/.claude/rot.md\n2323\t```\n2324\t\n2325\tExpected: a report file exists. The `unknown` count should have **dropped** by exactly the number of layers whose checks ran — not to zero.\n2326\t\n2327\t- [ ] **Step 7: Commit**\n2328\t\n2329\t```bash\n2330\tcd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS\n2331\tcp ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md\n2332\tgit add .claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md .claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md \\\n2333\t        scripts/aios-metrics.py docs/rot.md docs/audits/\n2334\tgit commit -m \"feat: aios-audit compound skill + rot.md decay tiers\n2335\t\n2336\tCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n2337\t```\n2338\t\n2339\t---\n2340\t"}]},"uuid":"29abc9cc-61cf-44d9-b57e-fb5cb00dac10","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:45:37.929Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md","content":"### Task 6: `rot.md` and the `aios-audit` compound skill\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `~/.claude/rot.md`\n- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md`\n- Create: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py`\n- Modify: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md` (cross-reference line only)\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: `skill-portability-check.py` (Task 5) and the canonical repo (Task 4).\n- Produces: `aios-metrics.py`, printing a machine-readable metrics block Task 7's launchd job captures.\n\n**Placement is deliberate.** This skill is **project-level**, in `KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/`, not global — the promotion rule from the video (31:32). It gets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/` only after proving useful across 2+ projects.\n\n**It must not become a sixth audit skill.** Five exist and each owns a layer:\n\n| Existing skill | Owns |\n|---|---|\n| `os-audit` (project) | project data: routing, index truth, freshness, duplication |\n| `brain-audit` | SecondBrain as a system — the four C's |\n| `improve-system` | note-level rot: stale seeds, duplicates, conflicts |\n| `claude-stack-doctor` | automation plumbing: launchd, venvs, memsearch, backup freshness |\n| `doctor-plus` | context-engineering posture of the workspace |\n\n`aios-audit` owns the one layer none of them touch — **the harness itself**: skill roster, agents, hooks, rules, cross-harness parity. It **delegates** the other five rather than re-implementing them.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write `~/.claude/rot.md`**\n\nNote the `Last audited` column (R10): every layer starts `unknown` except Skills, which was genuinely audited. A date is written only after that layer's check actually runs.\n\n```markdown\n# rot.md — how fast each AIOS layer goes stale\n\nAudit each layer on its own clock, not all at once. `aios-audit` reads this\nfile: any layer past due, or marked `unknown`, is a finding.\n\n**A date here is a receipt, not an intention.** Write one only after that\nlayer's check in the last column has actually run and produced output.\n\n| Layer | Where it lives | Rots | Audit every | Last audited | Owner | Concrete check |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | unknown | memory-write | Read USER.md; flag any role, family, or career fact contradicted by the last 90 days of sessions. |\n| Substrate | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `~/DEV/*.md` routers | slow | 3 months | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 1 (routing integrity). |\n| Skills | `~/.claude/skills/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-12 | aios-audit | `skill-portability-check.py` + never-used list + the crutch test below. |\n| Agents | `~/.claude/agents/` | fast | 1 month | unknown | aios-audit | Count `*.md`. Currently **0 exist** — report \"no agents defined\" and skip until one does. |\n| Rules | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` behaviour rules, output styles | fastest | 1 week | unknown | aios-audit | Diff CLAUDE.md against the last 7 days of sessions: any rule contradicted by what actually happened, and any correction the user repeated twice that is not yet a rule. |\n| Hooks | `~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/` | slow | 6 months | unknown | claude-stack-doctor | Delegate. Also diff the two copies — they must match (`hook-two-copies-trap`). |\n| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | **aios-audit itself** | Audited directly — see the delegation contract below. `improve-system` does NOT cover these stores. Check: every `MEMORY.md` index line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index; `global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under its 2,500-char cap; flag time-dimensioned facts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures). |\n| Memory (vault notes) | `~/SecondBrain/` notes | medium | 1 month | unknown | improve-system | Delegate — but read-only, per the contract below. |\n| Data feeds | Fireflies, GPS, CFBD, Zotero | varies | 1 week | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 3 (freshness). |\n| Vault | `~/SecondBrain/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | brain-audit | Delegate to `brain-audit` (four C's score). |\n| Context posture | workspace-wide | medium | 3 months | unknown | doctor-plus | Delegate to `doctor-plus`. |\n\n## The question that governs a skill's fate\n\nNot \"how often did I run it?\" but **\"would the current model do this fine\nwithout the skill?\"** If yes, the skill is a crutch that now limits the model.\nDelete it. Keep only skills carrying tacit knowledge the model cannot know:\nforce-plate thresholds, GPS conventions, Baylor reporting norms, Eric's own\nroutines.\n\nSeasonal skills (`forecast-capture`, `ingest-book`) are exempt from low-use\npressure. Judge them in season.\n\n## Delegation contract (R2-09)\n\nA delegate is invoked **read-only**, for a **named scope**, and its receipt is\nwritten **only** for the scope it actually covered.\n\n1. **Read-only.** Before invoking a delegate, instruct it explicitly: report\n   findings, apply nothing, write no ledger, create no files. Several delegates\n   (`improve-system` among them) begin by applying previously approved proposals\n   — that must be suppressed. `aios-audit` writes only its own report and the\n   `Last audited` column.\n2. **Scope must be verified, not assumed.** A delegate's actual coverage is what\n   its body scans, not what this table wishes it scanned. `improve-system` scans\n   `~/SecondBrain/` — Notes, Knowledge, Projects. It does **not** touch\n   `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` or `global-memory/`. Those are audited by\n   `aios-audit` directly.\n3. **A receipt covers only what was checked.** If a delegate returns findings for\n   a narrower scope than its row claims, write the date **and** a scope note, or\n   leave the row `unknown`. Never stamp a date because a delegate exited cleanly.\n\n## Layout invariants the audit must assert\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). On-disk links to third-party skills are\n  expected; they are listed in the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` (never the tracked\n  `.gitignore`), and a pre-commit hook refuses to commit one. What must never happen is\n  committing a link, because Windows pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n- `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are **generated views**. Each carries\n  a `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` manifest. Every entry **in the manifest** must be\n  a symlink on Mac (a copy on Windows); wrong representation is drift.\n- Entries **not** in the manifest are third-party installs (`npx skills add`).\n  They are counted and reported, **never** flagged as errors and never pruned.\n- Support directories (`_shared/`) have no SKILL.md and must never be pruned.\n\n## Direction of travel\n\n**Fewer skills, stricter rules.** Skills get deleted; rules get sharpened.\n```\n\nVerify: `head -30 ~/.claude/rot.md`\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write the metrics script**\n\nCreate `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py`. Counting is deduped by real path (R6) and session globbing is explicitly recursive:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Machine-readable AIOS metrics. stdlib only. Prints key=value lines only.\"\"\"\nimport os, re, glob, subprocess, collections, datetime, sys, hashlib\n\nH = os.path.expanduser(\"~\")\nCANON = f\"{H}/.claude/skills\"\nPOOL = f\"{H}/.agents/skills\"\nCODEX = f\"{H}/.codex/skills\"\nBUILTIN = {'exit','clear','compact','rename','color','login','logout','plugin',\n'doctor','help','model','config','resume','cost','status','init','agents','mcp',\n'hooks','memory','review','vim','terminal-setup','install-github-app','add-dir',\n'bug','release-notes','pr-comments','ide','permissions','statusline',\n'output-style','todos','export','privacy-settings','upgrade','fast','artifacts',\n'tasks','loop','context','usage','rewind','sandbox','feedback','worktrees',\n'skills','reload-skills','reload-plugins','bashes','keybindings','theme'}\n\n# R8-01: ownership is structural. A real directory holding a SKILL.md is ours;\n# a symlink was installed by the skills CLI or vendored. The same rule is used\n# by skill-portability-check.py and both sync scripts - no name list to keep\n# in step across four files.\n\ndef owned(root):\n    \"\"\"Names under root that are OURS: a real directory holding a SKILL.md.\"\"\"\n    out = set()\n    for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, \"*\")):\n        b = os.path.basename(d)\n        if b.startswith('.') or os.path.islink(d):\n            continue\n        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\")):\n            out.add(b)\n    return out\n\ndef skills_in(root):\n    \"\"\"Count distinct skills under root, deduped by real path (R6).\n    glob traverses symlinked dirs, so a link and its target counted twice.\"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, \"*\")):\n        s = os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\")\n        if os.path.isfile(s):\n            seen.add(os.path.realpath(s))\n    return len(seen)\n\ndef names_in(root):\n    return {os.path.basename(d) for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, \"*\"))\n            if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\"))}\n\ndef usage():\n    c = collections.Counter()\n    for f in glob.glob(f\"{H}/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl\", recursive=True):\n        try:\n            for line in open(f, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\"):\n                if 'Skill' not in line and 'command-name' not in line:\n                    continue\n                for m in re.finditer(\n                        r'\"name\"\\s*:\\s*\"Skill\"\\s*,\\s*\"input\"\\s*:\\s*\\{[^}]*?\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"([^\"]+)\"', line):\n                    c[m.group(1)] += 1\n                for m in re.finditer(r'<command-name>/([a-zA-Z0-9:_-]+)</command-name>', line):\n                    c[m.group(1)] += 1\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    return {k: v for k, v in c.items()\n            if k.split(':')[-1] not in BUILTIN and k not in BUILTIN}\n\ndef roster_tokens():\n    \"\"\"Frontmatter chars / 4 - what the OWNED roster costs per session.\n    Symlinked third-party skills are excluded; their cost is not ours to tune.\"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    for p in glob.glob(f\"{CANON}/*/SKILL.md\"):\n        if os.path.islink(os.path.dirname(p)):\n            continue\n        try:\n            t = open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\").read()\n            end = t.find(\"\\n---\", 3)\n            if t.startswith(\"---\") and end != -1:\n                total += len(t[4:end])\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    return total // 4\n\nMANIFEST = \".generated-by-sync-to-codex\"\n\ndef view_manifest(root):\n    \"\"\"Entries sync-to-codex.sh owns in this view. Anything else is a\n    third-party install (R2-02) and is reported, never flagged as an error.\"\"\"\n    p = os.path.join(root, MANIFEST)\n    if not os.path.isfile(p):\n        return None\n    return {l.strip() for l in open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\") if l.strip()}\n\nSUPPORT = {\"_shared\"}\n\ndef tracked_symlinks():\n    \"\"\"Mode-120000 entries in the canonical repo's index. These are the ones\n    that reach Windows and break there; raw on-disk links do not, once\n    gitignored. Must be 0.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        out = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", CANON, \"ls-files\", \"-s\"],\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)\n        if out.returncode != 0:\n            return \"git_error\"\n        return sum(1 for l in out.stdout.splitlines() if l.startswith(\"120000\"))\n    except Exception:\n        return \"git_error\"\n\ndef canonical_expected():\n    \"\"\"What the views SHOULD carry: every canonical skill plus support dirs.\n    R3-07: the view's own manifest is not evidence. An empty or stale manifest\n    would otherwise report zero drift while every skill was missing.\"\"\"\n    want = set()\n    for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(CANON, \"*\")):\n        b = os.path.basename(d)\n        if b.startswith('.'):\n            continue\n        if os.path.islink(d):        # R8-01: third-party link, not ours to publish\n            continue\n        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\")) or b in SUPPORT:\n            want.add(b)\n    return want\n\ndef view_drift(root):\n    \"\"\"Drift = any way a view fails to be a faithful generated copy of\n    canonical. Checks membership against CANONICAL (not the manifest),\n    representation for this platform, link targets, and copy freshness.\"\"\"\n    man = view_manifest(root)\n    if man is None:\n        return \"no_manifest\"\n    want = canonical_expected()\n    expect_link = (sys.platform == \"darwin\")\n    n = 0\n\n    # 1. Manifest must agree with canonical, in both directions.\n    n += len(want - man)          # canonical skill the manifest forgot\n    n += len(man - want)          # manifest claims something canonical dropped\n\n    for name in want:\n        d = os.path.join(root, name)\n        src = os.path.join(CANON, name)\n        if not os.path.exists(d):\n            n += 1                                    # missing entirely\n        elif expect_link:\n            if not os.path.islink(d):\n                n += 1                                # edited the view\n            elif os.path.realpath(d) != os.path.realpath(src):\n                n += 1                                # link points somewhere else\n        else:\n            if os.path.islink(d):\n                n += 1                                # Windows expects a copy\n            elif not _same_tree(d, src):\n                n += 1                                # stale copy\n    return n\n\ndef _same_tree(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Staleness check for copy-mode views. R4-04: sizes are not enough - a\n    same-length edit to a trigger phrase, a command or a config value leaves\n    size signatures identical while behaviour differs. Hash the contents, and\n    treat an unreadable file as a verification FAILURE, never as a match.\"\"\"\n    def snap(root_):\n        out = {}\n        for dp, _, fs in os.walk(root_):\n            for f in fs:\n                p = os.path.join(dp, f)\n                rel = os.path.relpath(p, root_)\n                try:\n                    h = hashlib.sha256()\n                    with open(p, \"rb\") as fh:\n                        for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(65536), b\"\"):\n                            h.update(chunk)\n                    out[rel] = h.hexdigest()\n                except OSError as e:\n                    # Unreadable => cannot verify => must count as drift.\n                    out[rel] = f\"UNREADABLE:{e.errno}\"\n        return out\n    sa, sb = snap(a), snap(b)\n    if any(v.startswith(\"UNREADABLE:\") for v in sa.values()) or \\\n       any(v.startswith(\"UNREADABLE:\") for v in sb.values()):\n        return False\n    return sa == sb\n\ndef third_party_in_view(root):\n    \"\"\"Entries present in the view but not managed by sync-to-codex.\n    Informational: these are npx-installed skills other harnesses may need.\"\"\"\n    man = view_manifest(root)\n    if man is None:\n        return \"no_manifest\"\n    n = 0\n    for d in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, \"*\")):\n        b = os.path.basename(d)\n        if b.startswith('.') or b in man:\n            continue\n        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, \"SKILL.md\")):\n            n += 1\n    return n\n\ndef dangling_in_view(root):\n    \"\"\"R5-01: abandoned links left after a canonical skill was deleted.\n    These are invisible to every other check - view_drift only looks at\n    names canonical still has, and third_party_in_view needs a readable\n    SKILL.md, which a dangling link does not provide. Uses os.listdir and\n    os.path.lexists so a broken link is still seen.\"\"\"\n    if not os.path.isdir(root):\n        return 0\n    n = 0\n    for b in os.listdir(root):\n        if b.startswith('.'):\n            continue\n        p = os.path.join(root, b)\n        if os.path.islink(p) and not os.path.exists(p):\n            n += 1\n    return n\n\nu = usage()\ncanon_names = owned(CANON)          # R8-01: owned roster = real directories\nout = [\n    (\"date\", datetime.date.today().isoformat()),\n    (\"canonical_skills\", len(canon_names)),\n    (\"third_party_links_in_canonical\",\n     len([d for d in glob.glob(f\"{CANON}/*\") if os.path.islink(d)])),\n    (\"pool_entries\", len(glob.glob(f\"{POOL}/*\"))),\n    (\"pool_skills\", skills_in(POOL)),\n    (\"codex_skills\", skills_in(CODEX)),\n    (\"project_skills\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/DEV/*/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md\"))),\n    # What must be zero is TRACKED symlinks. The third-party links legitimately\n    # remain on disk; they are excluded per-machine and the pre-commit hook\n    # refuses to commit one, so they can never reach Windows.\n    (\"tracked_symlinks_in_canonical\", tracked_symlinks()),\n    (\"pool_view_drift\", view_drift(POOL)),\n    (\"codex_view_drift\", view_drift(CODEX)),\n    (\"pool_third_party\", third_party_in_view(POOL)),\n    (\"codex_third_party\", third_party_in_view(CODEX)),\n    (\"pool_dangling\", dangling_in_view(POOL)),\n    (\"codex_dangling\", dangling_in_view(CODEX)),\n    (\"agents\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/.claude/agents/*.md\"))),\n    (\"hooks_claude\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/.claude/hooks/*\"))),\n    (\"hooks_codex\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/.codex/hooks/*\"))),\n    (\"sessions\", len(glob.glob(f\"{H}/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl\", recursive=True))),\n    (\"skills_ever_used\", len(u)),\n    (\"skills_used_3plus\", len([k for k, v in u.items() if v >= 3])),\n    (\"skills_used_once\", len([k for k, v in u.items() if v == 1])),\n    (\"never_used\", len(canon_names - set(u))),\n    (\"roster_tokens_est\", roster_tokens()),\n]\nrc = subprocess.run([sys.executable, f\"{H}/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skill-portability-check.py\"],\n                    capture_output=True, text=True)\nm = re.search(r\"(\\d+) failing\", rc.stdout)\nout.append((\"portability_failures\", m.group(1) if m else f\"error_rc{rc.returncode}\"))\n\nfor k, v in out:\n    print(f\"{k}={v}\")\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run it and check every value**\n\n```bash\nchmod +x ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\npython3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\n```\n\nExpected: `key=value` lines only, no stack trace, and specifically:\n\n| Key | Expected | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `canonical_skills` | `42` | the roster we own — real directories only |\n| `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` | `0` | Task 4 invariant — no link may be **committed** |\n| `third_party_links_in_canonical` | `19` | skills-CLI installs and vendored links — excluded per-machine, expected, **not** an error; moves with every install |\n| `pool_view_drift` | `0` | every managed entry is represented correctly for this platform |\n| `codex_view_drift` | `0` | same, for the Codex view |\n| `pool_third_party` | `~150` | **informational, not an error** — `npx skills add` installs the audit reports but never touches (R2-02) |\n| `pool_dangling` / `codex_dangling` | `0` | abandoned links from a deleted canonical skill — invisible to every other check (R5-01) |\n| `project_skills` | `2` | `os-audit` + `aios-audit` |\n| `portability_failures` | `0` | Task 5 passed |\n\nA non-zero `*_drift` means someone edited a generated view instead of the canonical source — fix before continuing. A large `*_third_party` is expected and correct; it is a number to watch, not a failure. `no_manifest` in either drift field means `sync-to-codex.sh` has not run since Task 3.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Write the `aios-audit` skill**\n\nInvoke `CreateSkill` first — it owns skill authoring here. Create `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md` with frontmatter that satisfies Task 5's contract:\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: aios-audit\ndescription: >-\n  Audit the whole AI operating system across decay tiers - skills, agents,\n  hooks, rules, memory, and cross-harness parity between Claude Code, Codex,\n  and Pi - then propose exactly two next builds. Use when the user says\n  \"/aios-audit\", \"audit my system\", \"audit my AI OS\", \"audit the bloat\",\n  \"is my setup rotting\", \"what should I cut\", \"are my skills portable\",\n  \"monthly skill audit\", or when rot.md shows a layer past its audit date.\n  Do not use for project data drift, routing, or index freshness - use\n  os-audit. Do not use for launchd, venv, or backup health - use\n  claude-stack-doctor. Do not use for SecondBrain note rot - use\n  improve-system or brain-audit.\nmetadata:\n  short-description: Decay-tier audit of the AI OS; delegates to the five layer-specific audit skills.\nargument-hint: \"[optional: a layer name from rot.md]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Agent\n---\n```\n\nThe body must specify, in order:\n\n1. **Read-only.** The only writes are the report and `rot.md`'s `Last audited` column. **Never delete a skill during the audit** — propose, then wait for approval.\n2. **Step 0 — read `~/.claude/rot.md`.** Compute days since each layer's `Last audited`. A layer that is past due **or `unknown`** gets audited this run; layers inside their window are reported green and skipped. That is what makes a monthly run cheap.\n3. **Step 1 — run `python3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py`** and capture every value.\n4. **Step 2 — assert the layout invariants** from `rot.md`. `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical`, `pool_view_drift`, `codex_view_drift`, `pool_dangling` and `codex_dangling` must all be `0`. `third_party_links_in_canonical` (19 today) is **information, not a finding** — it changes every time a skill is installed. Drift means someone edited a generated view instead of the canonical repo; a dangling count means a deleted canonical skill left an abandoned link behind — both are RED. Report `pool_third_party` and `codex_third_party` as **information**, never as errors — those are deliberately preserved installs.\n5. **Step 3 — delegate under the contract, do not duplicate.** For each due layer, invoke the owning skill named in the `rot.md` table **read-only**, following the delegation contract in `rot.md`: suppress any apply/ledger step, state the scope you need, and fold the findings under that layer's heading. Audit the harness layer and the agent-memory stores directly — no delegate covers those.\n6. **Step 4 — the harness layer, audited directly:**\n   - **Bloat:** every canonical skill never invoked across all sessions. List them.\n   - **Crutch test:** for each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md` question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge), or SEASONAL, one line of reasoning each.\n   - **Overlap:** skills whose descriptions cover the same trigger space. Recommend merging.\n   - **Parity:** run `skill-portability-check.py`. Every failure is a finding.\n   - **Promotion:** global skills used in fewer than 2 projects — demotion candidates. Project skills used in 2+ — promotion candidates.\n   - **Rules:** diff `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` against the last 7 days of sessions. Report rules contradicted by what actually happened, and corrections the user repeated twice that are not yet rules.\n   - **Agents:** count `~/.claude/agents/*.md`. If `0`, report \"no agents defined\" and skip — do not invent a finding.\n7. **Step 5 — write the report** to `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-YYYY-MM-DD.md` and update `Last audited` in `rot.md` **only for layers whose check actually ran and produced output**. Do **not** write to `aios-trend.md`: `aios-audit-cron.sh` is its single writer (R8-08) — two writers produced rows with no header. Commit the cron's waiting trend row as part of the audit.\n8. **Step 6 — end with exactly two proposed next builds,** ranked, each with the one command that starts it. Not ten. Two.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Cross-reference `os-audit` so the two do not fight**\n\nAdd near the top of `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md`:\n\n```markdown\n> Scope note: this skill audits **project data** — routing, indexes, freshness,\n> duplication. The harness layer (skills, agents, hooks, rules, cross-harness\n> parity) belongs to `aios-audit`, which calls this skill for the data layer.\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Smoke-test end to end**\n\nIn a Claude Code session with cwd `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`, run `/reload-skills`, then type \"audit my AI OS\". Expected: `aios-audit` fires, reads `rot.md`, runs the metrics script, produces a report, and ends with exactly two proposals.\n\n```bash\nls -l ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-*.md\ngrep -c 'unknown' ~/.claude/rot.md\n```\n\nExpected: a report file exists. The `unknown` count should have **dropped** by exactly the number of layers whose checks ran — not to zero.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS\ncp ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md\ngit add .claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md .claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md \\\n        scripts/aios-metrics.py docs/rot.md docs/audits/\ngit commit -m \"feat: aios-audit compound skill + rot.md decay tiers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---\n","numLines":460,"startLine":1881,"totalLines":2869}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"785b76fe-1565-4502-807e-86c24702d7e0","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
