{"parentUuid":"3245cb15-c107-4355-b1bb-ae1a7608b0b8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EtfEjSpZ8V2QPtbYoJij3V","type":"tool_result","content":"205\t## The Required Structure\n206\t\n207\tEvery SKILL.md has two parts:\n208\t\n209\t### 1. YAML Frontmatter (Single-Line Description)\n210\t\n211\t```yaml\n212\t---\n213\tname: SkillName\n214\tdescription: [What it does]. USE WHEN [intent triggers using OR]. [Additional capabilities].\n215\timplements: Science              # Optional: declares Science Protocol compliance\n216\tscience_cycle_time: meso         # Optional: micro | meso | macro\n217\t---\n218\t```\n219\t\n220\t**Rules:**\n221\t- `name` uses **TitleCase**\n222\t- `description` is a **single line** (not multi-line with `|`)\n223\t- `USE WHEN` keyword is **MANDATORY** (Claude Code parses this for skill activation)\n224\t- Use intent-based triggers with `OR` for multiple conditions\n225\t- **Max 500 characters recommended, 650 hard ceiling.** Claude Code has a total character budget for all skill descriptions combined. In practice, descriptions over ~650 chars cause skills to be silently dropped from the session listing — the skill becomes invisible and unroutable. Keep descriptions tight: brief prose summary + USE WHEN trigger keywords. Move detailed explanations to the SKILL.md body, not the YAML description.\n226\t- **NO separate `triggers:` or `workflows:` arrays in YAML**\n227\t\n228\t### Science Protocol Compliance (Optional)\n229\t\n230\tSkills that involve systematic investigation, iteration, or evidence-based improvement can declare Science Protocol compliance:\n231\t\n232\t```yaml\n233\timplements: Science\n234\tscience_cycle_time: meso\n235\t```\n236\t\n237\t**What This Means:**\n238\t- The skill embodies the scientific method: Goal → Observe → Hypothesize → Experiment → Measure → Analyze → Iterate\n239\t- This is documentation of the mapping, not runtime coupling\n240\t- Skills implement Science like classes implement interfaces—they follow the pattern independently\n241\t\n242\t**Cycle Time Options:**\n243\t| Level | Cycle Time | Formality | Example Skills |\n244\t|-------|------------|-----------|----------------|\n245\t| `micro` | Seconds-Minutes | Implicit (internalized) | Most skills |\n246\t| `meso` | Hours-Days | Explicit when stuck | Evals, Research, Development |\n247\t| `macro` | Weeks-Months | Formal documentation | Major architecture work |\n248\t\n249\t**Skills That Implement Science:**\n250\t- **Development** - TDD is Science (test = goal, code = experiment, pass/fail = analysis)\n251\t- **Evals** - Prompt optimization through systematic experimentation\n252\t- **Research** - Investigation through hypotheses and evidence gathering\n253\t- **Council** - Debate as parallel hypothesis testing\n254\t\n255\t**See:** `~/.claude/skills/Science/Protocol.md` for the full protocol interface\n256\t\n257\t### 2. Markdown Body (Workflow Routing + Examples + Documentation)\n258\t\n259\t```markdown\n260\t# SkillName\n261\t\n262\t[Brief description of what the skill does]\n263\t\n264\t## Voice Notification\n265\t\n266\t**When executing a workflow, do BOTH:**\n267\t\n268\t1. **Send voice notification**:\n269\t   ```bash\n270\t   curl -s -X POST http://localhost:31337/notify \\\n271\t     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n272\t     -d '{\"message\": \"Running the WORKFLOWNAME workflow in the SKILLNAME skill to ACTION\"}' \\\n273\t     > /dev/null 2>&1 &\n274\t   ```\n275\t\n276\t2. **Output text notification**:\n277\t   ```\n278\t   Running the **WorkflowName** workflow in the **SkillName** skill to ACTION...\n279\t   ```\n280\t\n281\t**Full documentation:** `~/.claude/LIFEOS/DOCUMENTATION/Notifications/NotificationSystem.md`\n282\t\n283\t## Workflow Routing\n284\t\n285\tThe notification announces workflow execution. The routing table tells Claude which workflow to execute:\n286\t\n287\t| Workflow | Trigger | File |\n288\t|----------|---------|------|\n289\t| **WorkflowOne** | \"trigger phrase\" | `Workflows/WorkflowOne.md` |\n290\t| **WorkflowTwo** | \"another trigger\" | `Workflows/WorkflowTwo.md` |\n291\t\n292\t## Examples\n293\t\n294\t**Example 1: [Common use case]**\n295\t```\n296\tUser: \"[Typical user request]\"\n297\t→ Invokes WorkflowOne workflow\n298\t→ [What skill does]\n299\t→ [What user gets back]\n300\t```\n301\t\n302\t**Example 2: [Another use case]**\n303\t```\n304\tUser: \"[Another typical request]\"\n305\t→ [Process]\n306\t→ [Output]\n307\t```\n308\t\n309\t## [Additional Sections]\n310\t\n311\t[Documentation, quick reference, critical paths, etc.]\n312\t```\n313\t\n314\t**Workflow routing format:** Table with Workflow, Trigger, File columns\n315\t- Workflow names in **TitleCase** matching file names\n316\t- Simple trigger description\n317\t- File path in backticks\n318\t\n319\t**When to show the workflow message:**\n320\t- ONLY output the message when actually loading and executing a workflow file\n321\t- If the skill handles the request directly without calling a workflow, do NOT show the message\n322\t- The message indicates \"I'm reading and following instructions from a workflow file\"\n323\t\n324\t---"}]},"uuid":"8a7c6114-0612-4a42-911f-ef1bba3c19ca","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:49:49.818Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/LIFEOS/DOCUMENTATION/Skills/SkillSystem.md","content":"## The Required Structure\n\nEvery SKILL.md has two parts:\n\n### 1. YAML Frontmatter (Single-Line Description)\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: SkillName\ndescription: [What it does]. USE WHEN [intent triggers using OR]. [Additional capabilities].\nimplements: Science              # Optional: declares Science Protocol compliance\nscience_cycle_time: meso         # Optional: micro | meso | macro\n---\n```\n\n**Rules:**\n- `name` uses **TitleCase**\n- `description` is a **single line** (not multi-line with `|`)\n- `USE WHEN` keyword is **MANDATORY** (Claude Code parses this for skill activation)\n- Use intent-based triggers with `OR` for multiple conditions\n- **Max 500 characters recommended, 650 hard ceiling.** Claude Code has a total character budget for all skill descriptions combined. In practice, descriptions over ~650 chars cause skills to be silently dropped from the session listing — the skill becomes invisible and unroutable. Keep descriptions tight: brief prose summary + USE WHEN trigger keywords. Move detailed explanations to the SKILL.md body, not the YAML description.\n- **NO separate `triggers:` or `workflows:` arrays in YAML**\n\n### Science Protocol Compliance (Optional)\n\nSkills that involve systematic investigation, iteration, or evidence-based improvement can declare Science Protocol compliance:\n\n```yaml\nimplements: Science\nscience_cycle_time: meso\n```\n\n**What This Means:**\n- The skill embodies the scientific method: Goal → Observe → Hypothesize → Experiment → Measure → Analyze → Iterate\n- This is documentation of the mapping, not runtime coupling\n- Skills implement Science like classes implement interfaces—they follow the pattern independently\n\n**Cycle Time Options:**\n| Level | Cycle Time | Formality | Example Skills |\n|-------|------------|-----------|----------------|\n| `micro` | Seconds-Minutes | Implicit (internalized) | Most skills |\n| `meso` | Hours-Days | Explicit when stuck | Evals, Research, Development |\n| `macro` | Weeks-Months | Formal documentation | Major architecture work |\n\n**Skills That Implement Science:**\n- **Development** - TDD is Science (test = goal, code = experiment, pass/fail = analysis)\n- **Evals** - Prompt optimization through systematic experimentation\n- **Research** - Investigation through hypotheses and evidence gathering\n- **Council** - Debate as parallel hypothesis testing\n\n**See:** `~/.claude/skills/Science/Protocol.md` for the full protocol interface\n\n### 2. Markdown Body (Workflow Routing + Examples + Documentation)\n\n```markdown\n# SkillName\n\n[Brief description of what the skill does]\n\n## Voice Notification\n\n**When executing a workflow, do BOTH:**\n\n1. **Send voice notification**:\n   ```bash\n   curl -s -X POST http://localhost:31337/notify \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"message\": \"Running the WORKFLOWNAME workflow in the SKILLNAME skill to ACTION\"}' \\\n     > /dev/null 2>&1 &\n   ```\n\n2. **Output text notification**:\n   ```\n   Running the **WorkflowName** workflow in the **SkillName** skill to ACTION...\n   ```\n\n**Full documentation:** `~/.claude/LIFEOS/DOCUMENTATION/Notifications/NotificationSystem.md`\n\n## Workflow Routing\n\nThe notification announces workflow execution. The routing table tells Claude which workflow to execute:\n\n| Workflow | Trigger | File |\n|----------|---------|------|\n| **WorkflowOne** | \"trigger phrase\" | `Workflows/WorkflowOne.md` |\n| **WorkflowTwo** | \"another trigger\" | `Workflows/WorkflowTwo.md` |\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: [Common use case]**\n```\nUser: \"[Typical user request]\"\n→ Invokes WorkflowOne workflow\n→ [What skill does]\n→ [What user gets back]\n```\n\n**Example 2: [Another use case]**\n```\nUser: \"[Another typical request]\"\n→ [Process]\n→ [Output]\n```\n\n## [Additional Sections]\n\n[Documentation, quick reference, critical paths, etc.]\n```\n\n**Workflow routing format:** Table with Workflow, Trigger, File columns\n- Workflow names in **TitleCase** matching file names\n- Simple trigger description\n- File path in backticks\n\n**When to show the workflow message:**\n- ONLY output the message when actually loading and executing a workflow file\n- If the skill handles the request directly without calling a workflow, do NOT show the message\n- The message indicates \"I'm reading and following instructions from a workflow file\"\n\n---","numLines":120,"startLine":205,"totalLines":1098}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3245cb15-c107-4355-b1bb-ae1a7608b0b8","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
