{"parentUuid":"18719d83-31f1-4a74-bf66-b395b8b37aab","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RwwK8qod78aUNrurqqZMfF","type":"tool_result","content":"15:## Today's context\n20:## The lens: four failure modes, two context types\n38:## Step 0 — Prior report and recent evidence\n43:## Execution\n49:### Check 1 — Routing integrity (\"does everything it points to exist?\")\n57:### Check 2 — Index truth (\"do the indexes match the disk?\")\n63:### Check 3 — Freshness (\"are the data feeds current?\")\n77:### Check 4 — Bloat, duplication, and organization (\"does anything live twice, or in the wrong place, or for no reason?\")\n92:### Check 5 — Hygiene and silent failures (\"what's broken or exposed without anyone noticing?\")\n101:### Check 6 — Context placement (\"is everything on the right side of the expertise/situational line?\")\n108:## Output — the report\n126:## Failure-mode exposure\n135:## Since last audit\n138:## What would make your agent wrong-answer you today\n141:## Findings by check\n146:## Questions for you\n149:## Fix list (batched, await approval)\n160:## Notes\n     166 /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md\n=== improve-system apply step (to suppress) ===\n16:## Step 0 — read the pending ledger first\n20:Do this **before** scanning. Apply anything marked `approved` (then mark it `applied`),\n36:Output a short report grouped by issue type with a proposed action per item (merge / archive / update status / no action). **Apply nothing until the user picks.** Archive = move to `Archive/`, never delete.\n=== brain-audit writes ===\n3:description: Score the second brain as a system — the four C's (context, connections, capabilities, cadence) — write a dated report to ~/SecondBrain/audits/, append the score to a trend table, and end by proposing exactly two next builds. Use when the user says \"/brain-audit\", \"audit my second brain\", \"score my brain\", \"is my second brain working\", \"how healthy is my system\", \"level up my brain\", \"what should I build next for my brain\", or when a monthly ritual is due. NOT FOR automation plumbing — launchd jobs, venvs, backup freshness (use claude-stack-doctor). NOT FOR note-level rot — stale seeds, duplicates, conflicting claims (use improve-system).\n10:The point is the **trend**, not any single run. A score that only exists once is\n51:## Step 4 — write the report\n58:Then append one row to `~/SecondBrain/audits/_trend.md` (create with a header if\n94:- **Scoring drift breaks the trend.** If a rubric anchor in Step 2 is changed, note the\n95:  change in `_trend.md` on that row, or the column stops meaning one thing.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"88ea9441-a59e-4af3-aa59-26ea57a66962","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:49:54.226Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"15:## Today's context\n20:## The lens: four failure modes, two context types\n38:## Step 0 — Prior report and recent evidence\n43:## Execution\n49:### Check 1 — Routing integrity (\"does everything it points to exist?\")\n57:### Check 2 — Index truth (\"do the indexes match the disk?\")\n63:### Check 3 — Freshness (\"are the data feeds current?\")\n77:### Check 4 — Bloat, duplication, and organization (\"does anything live twice, or in the wrong place, or for no reason?\")\n92:### Check 5 — Hygiene and silent failures (\"what's broken or exposed without anyone noticing?\")\n101:### Check 6 — Context placement (\"is everything on the right side of the expertise/situational line?\")\n108:## Output — the report\n126:## Failure-mode exposure\n135:## Since last audit\n138:## What would make your agent wrong-answer you today\n141:## Findings by check\n146:## Questions for you\n149:## Fix list (batched, await approval)\n160:## Notes\n     166 /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md\n=== improve-system apply step (to suppress) ===\n16:## Step 0 — read the pending ledger first\n20:Do this **before** scanning. Apply anything marked `approved` (then mark it `applied`),\n36:Output a short report grouped by issue type with a proposed action per item (merge / archive / update status / no action). **Apply nothing until the user picks.** Archive = move to `Archive/`, never delete.\n=== brain-audit writes ===\n3:description: Score the second brain as a system — the four C's (context, connections, capabilities, cadence) — write a dated report to ~/SecondBrain/audits/, append the score to a trend table, and end by proposing exactly two next builds. Use when the user says \"/brain-audit\", \"audit my second brain\", \"score my brain\", \"is my second brain working\", \"how healthy is my system\", \"level up my brain\", \"what should I build next for my brain\", or when a monthly ritual is due. NOT FOR automation plumbing — launchd jobs, venvs, backup freshness (use claude-stack-doctor). NOT FOR note-level rot — stale seeds, duplicates, conflicting claims (use improve-system).\n10:The point is the **trend**, not any single run. A score that only exists once is\n51:## Step 4 — write the report\n58:Then append one row to `~/SecondBrain/audits/_trend.md` (create with a header if\n94:- **Scoring drift breaks the trend.** If a rubric anchor in Step 2 is changed, note the\n95:  change in `_trend.md` on that row, or the column stops meaning one thing.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"18719d83-31f1-4a74-bf66-b395b8b37aab","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
