{"parentUuid":"a2774941-a0e2-4435-a8f7-28265cf65df1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lj34uMLUwpDFtpXrZVcU6M","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t6-aios-audit-SKILL.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"42be09e4-319a-4aec-93c7-a7453b143c1d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:51:09.770Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t6-aios-audit-SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: aios-audit\ndescription: >-\n  Audit the whole AI operating system across decay tiers - skills, agents,\n  hooks, rules, memory, and cross-harness parity between Claude Code, Codex,\n  and Pi - then propose exactly two next builds. Use when the user says\n  \"/aios-audit\", \"audit my system\", \"audit my AI OS\", \"audit the bloat\",\n  \"is my setup rotting\", \"what should I cut\", \"are my skills portable\",\n  \"monthly skill audit\", or when rot.md shows a layer past its audit date.\n  Do not use for project data drift, routing, or index freshness - use\n  os-audit. Do not use for launchd, venv, or backup health - use\n  claude-stack-doctor. Do not use for SecondBrain note rot - use\n  improve-system or brain-audit.\nmetadata:\n  short-description: Decay-tier audit of the AI OS; delegates to the five layer-specific audit skills.\nargument-hint: \"[optional: a layer name from rot.md]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Agent\n---\n\n# AIOS Audit — is the harness itself still true?\n\nFive audit skills already exist, and each owns one layer. This skill owns the\nlayer none of them touch: **the harness** — skill roster, agents, hooks, rules,\nagent memory, and parity between Claude Code, Codex, and Pi. For every other\nlayer it **delegates**; it never re-implements another audit.\n\n| Delegate | Owns |\n|---|---|\n| `os-audit` (project) | project data: routing, index truth, freshness, duplication |\n| `brain-audit` | SecondBrain as a system — the four C's |\n| `improve-system` | note-level rot: stale seeds, duplicates, conflicts |\n| `claude-stack-doctor` | automation plumbing: launchd, venvs, memsearch, backup freshness |\n| `doctor-plus` | context-engineering posture of the workspace |\n\nIf `$ARGUMENTS` names one layer from `rot.md`, audit only that layer.\n\n## 1. Read-only\n\nThe only writes are the report file and the `Last audited` column of\n`~/.claude/rot.md`. **Never delete, archive, disable, or edit a skill during the\naudit.** Propose, then wait for approval. A deletion proposal that turns out wrong\nis cheap; a deletion is not.\n\n## 2. Step 0 — read `~/.claude/rot.md`\n\nFor each layer, compute days since `Last audited`. A layer that is **past due or\n`unknown`** is audited this run. A layer inside its window is reported green and\nskipped — that is what keeps a monthly run cheap. Read the delegation contract and\nthe layout invariants in `rot.md` before going further; they bind every step below.\n\n## 3. Step 1 — run the metrics\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\n```\n\nCapture every `key=value` line. Any stack trace, or a value like `git_error`,\n`no_manifest` or `error_rc…`, is itself a RED finding — do not guess the number.\n\n## 4. Step 2 — assert the layout invariants\n\n| Key | Must be | If not |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` | `0` | RED — a link was committed; Windows gets a dead file |\n| `pool_view_drift`, `codex_view_drift` | `0` | RED — someone edited a generated view instead of `~/.claude/skills/` |\n| `pool_dangling`, `codex_dangling` | `0` | RED — a deleted canonical skill left an abandoned link |\n| `portability_failures` | `0` | RED — see the parity check in Step 4 |\n\nInformation, never findings: `third_party_links_in_canonical` (changes with every\ninstall), `pool_third_party`, `codex_third_party` (deliberately preserved installs).\n\n## 5. Step 3 — delegate under the contract\n\nFor each due layer, invoke the owner named in `rot.md`, **read-only**:\n\n- Say it plainly in the invocation: *report findings only; apply nothing, write no\n  ledger, create no files.*\n- `improve-system` applies previously approved proposals in its own Step 0 —\n  suppress that explicitly. `brain-audit` appends to its own trend table — suppress\n  that too, or leave the Vault layer `unknown`.\n- Name the scope you need. Fold the delegate's findings under that layer's heading.\n- A receipt covers only what was checked. If the delegate covered less than its\n  row claims, write the date **with a scope note**, or leave the row `unknown`.\n  Never stamp a date because a delegate exited cleanly.\n\nThe Memory (agent) layer has no delegate — audit it directly: every `MEMORY.md`\nindex line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index;\n`~/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under 2,500 chars; flag time-dimensioned\nfacts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures).\n\n## 6. Step 4 — the harness layer, audited directly\n\n- **Bloat.** List every canonical skill never invoked across all sessions\n  (`never_used` from the metrics; name them).\n- **Crutch test.** For each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md`\n  question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend\n  DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge the model cannot know), or SEASONAL. One line of\n  reasoning each.\n- **Overlap.** Skills whose descriptions claim the same trigger space. Recommend\n  a merge, or a sharper `Do not use … (use X)` clause on both.\n- **Parity.** Run `python3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skill-portability-check.py`;\n  every failure is a finding. Then check config-level parity, which the linter\n  cannot see: list canonical skills set `\"off\"` in `~/.claude/settings.json`\n  `skillOverrides`. Those are hidden in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi.\n  Each one needs a decision: switch it back on, or retire it from canonical.\n- **Promotion.** Global skills used in fewer than 2 projects — demotion\n  candidates. Project skills used in 2+ projects — promotion candidates.\n- **Rules.** Diff `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` against the last 7 days of sessions.\n  Report rules contradicted by what actually happened, and corrections the user\n  repeated twice that are not yet rules.\n- **Hooks.** Compare `hooks_claude` with `hooks_codex`, then diff the two\n  directories by name. The copies must match (patch both, always).\n- **Agents.** If `agents=0`, report \"no agents defined\" and skip. Do not invent a finding.\n\n## 7. Step 5 — write the report\n\nWrite `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-YYYY-MM-DD.md` with one section per\nlayer (green-skipped layers get one line). Update `Last audited` in\n`~/.claude/rot.md` **only for layers whose check actually ran and produced\noutput**, then `cp ~/.claude/rot.md ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/rot.md`.\n\nDo **not** write to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` — `scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh` is\nits single writer. If the cron left an uncommitted trend row, commit it together\nwith this report.\n\n## 8. Step 6 — end with exactly two proposed next builds\n\nRanked. Each with the one command or sentence that starts it. Not ten. Two.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Monthly nudge**\n```\nUser: \"audit my AI OS\"\n→ reads rot.md: Skills and Rules past due, Hooks inside its window\n→ metrics: all invariants 0; never_used=19\n→ delegates nothing for Skills/Rules (owned here); skips Hooks green\n→ report with crutch-test verdicts, 2 parity decisions, 2 next builds\n```\n\n**One layer**\n```\nUser: \"/aios-audit Memory (agent)\"\n→ audits only the agent-memory stores directly\n→ stamps that one row in rot.md; every other row untouched\n```\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- **Linter green is not parity.** `skill-portability-check.py` reads frontmatter\n  only. A skill set `\"off\"` in `skillOverrides` passes it and still never fires in\n  Claude Code, while Codex (which ignores that file) loads it. Found 2026-09-12:\n  12 canonical skills off in Claude, live in Codex.\n- **Views are links into canonical.** Anything that writes into\n  `~/.agents/skills/<owned>/` by path writes canonical. `graphify install\n  --platform agents` does exactly that and overwrites the Claude variant — upgrade\n  graphify with `--platform claude` only.\n- **Concurrent sessions commit your work.** `closeout` in another session sweeps\n  every uncommitted change in the repos it visits. Commit the report as soon as it\n  is written, not at the end of a long session.\n- **Description length has a budget.** Claude Code caps the combined skill\n  description size; very long descriptions risk a skill silently dropping out of\n  the listing. When recommending a sharper `Do not use` clause, keep the whole\n  description near 650 characters.\n- **`dcg` blocks some shell shapes** (`rm -rf` inside heredocs, `$VAR` redirects,\n  `git` inside command substitution). Use Python `subprocess` or literal paths;\n  do not try to bypass the guard.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2774941-a0e2-4435-a8f7-28265cf65df1","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
