{"parentUuid":"ea90bfdb-4afe-49e9-adda-97eeba4b299d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezN5GrfpzwJRb27jzGPY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Gate B for KeystoneOS results in REVISE: the checker's raw-text parsing lets invalid frontmatter slip through (as with the earlier `new-project` bug), and 7 skills disabled in Claude but still published elsewhere inflate the \"42 portable\" claim. I've also finished the skills-repo inspection and read it first to check for overlap before picking fixes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6258,"cache_read_input_tokens":294664,"output_tokens":1266,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":955},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6258,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":294664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6258},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezN5FxbKJdvoDyJR6iXp","attributionSkill":"CreateSkill","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d882cb3-73db-489b-9947-48c3cc4a0a4c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:51:25.354Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"6d882cb3-73db-489b-9947-48c3cc4a0a4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezN5GrfpzwJRb27jzGPY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0141uYyvJ74aGtZHMgWMygNZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-skills && python3 - claudex-*/result.json <<'PY'\nimport json,sys\nr=json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); v=r[\"response\"]\nprint(\"status:\",r[\"status\"],\"| VERDICT:\",v[\"verdict\"]); print(\"summary:\",v[\"summary\"])\nfor f in v[\"findings\"]: print(f\"\\n[{f['id']}] {f['severity']} {f['path']}\\n  evidence: {f['evidence']}\\n  fix: {f['fix']}\")\nprint(\"\\ncoverage:\",v[\"coverage\"]); print(\"limitations:\",v[\"limitations\"])\nPY","description":"Read the Gate B skills-repo inspection result"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6258,"cache_read_input_tokens":294664,"output_tokens":1266,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":955},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6258,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":294664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6258},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezN5FxbKJdvoDyJR6iXp","attributionSkill":"CreateSkill","type":"assistant","uuid":"3dbf505a-e867-4d02-bb8f-16b8c28dff08","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:51:26.464Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"3dbf505a-e867-4d02-bb8f-16b8c28dff08","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141uYyvJ74aGtZHMgWMygNZ","type":"tool_result","content":"status: completed | VERDICT: REVISE\nsummary: Three concrete defects remain: a destructive root-alias case, a Git casing mismatch, and false-positive portability validation.\n\n[R13-01] high /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh:247\n  evidence: Neither twin validates the resolved view roots before publishing. On a prepared machine where ~/.agents/skills points to ~/.claude/skills, the source entries pass the real-directory check, but removing $dst/$s deletes the canonical skill itself. Link mode then replaces it with a self-referencing link. The retirement containment check only compares the destination against itself and does not prevent this.\n  fix: Before any mutation, resolve canonical and both destination roots, including ancestor links/junctions. Reject aliases and overlapping trees. Apply the same preflight to both twins and reject a destination manifest that redirects writes outside its view.\n\n[R13-02] medium /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/harvest/SKILL.md:2\n  evidence: The declaration changed to 'Harvest', but git ls-files still records harvest/SKILL.md and harvest/Workflows/Harvest.md. A fresh checkout therefore creates lowercase 'harvest', while the checker compares the directory and declared name case-sensitively. The Mac's existing uppercase directory masks this mismatch; the portability report explicitly cites that local spelling as the reason for changing the name.\n  fix: Make the Git-recorded directory spelling and declared name agree. Prefer preserving the existing lowercase name and references, or explicitly record a case-only directory rename through an intermediate name. Validate the Git tree spelling as well as the current filesystem.\n\n[R13-03] medium /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skill-portability-check.py:27\n  evidence: The regex scalar reader does not validate YAML despite serving as the portability gate. For example, 'description: Use when testing: examples. Do not use otherwise.' passes its clause, length, and quote checks, although the embedded colon-space makes this an invalid plain YAML scalar. Thus the recurring audit can report zero failures for a skill that a YAML-based loader cannot load.\n  fix: Parse YAML with a declared dependency, or enforce a genuinely restricted serialization format that rejects unsupported YAML syntax. Validate scalar types and the complete frontmatter syntax before checking trigger clauses.\n\ncoverage: ['Verified the on-disk plan SHA256 matches the supplied hash; reviewed the supplied plan and tracked diff.', 'Read both installed sync scripts and the portability checker.', 'Inspected the 19 deleted Git symlink entries and their surviving on-disk links.', 'Traced dev-sync, startup/closeout behavior, daily-backup Sync-Repo, the installed pre-commit hook, and related error-log writers.', 'Inspected Git-recorded Harvest paths and the portability report.']\nlimitations: ['Static review only: no edits, tests, delegation, or harness execution.', 'Bulk reads of skill bodies and research notes were truncated; complete body-level coverage is not claimed.', 'Windows filesystem behavior, fresh-checkout loading, and Pi isolation were not exercised.', 'Tasks 6–8 were assessed from the plan, not verified as completed implementations.']\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e9331125-02fe-47e5-8625-ef207d9dc385","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:51:29.830Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"status: completed | VERDICT: REVISE\nsummary: Three concrete defects remain: a destructive root-alias case, a Git casing mismatch, and false-positive portability validation.\n\n[R13-01] high /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh:247\n  evidence: Neither twin validates the resolved view roots before publishing. On a prepared machine where ~/.agents/skills points to ~/.claude/skills, the source entries pass the real-directory check, but removing $dst/$s deletes the canonical skill itself. Link mode then replaces it with a self-referencing link. The retirement containment check only compares the destination against itself and does not prevent this.\n  fix: Before any mutation, resolve canonical and both destination roots, including ancestor links/junctions. Reject aliases and overlapping trees. Apply the same preflight to both twins and reject a destination manifest that redirects writes outside its view.\n\n[R13-02] medium /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/harvest/SKILL.md:2\n  evidence: The declaration changed to 'Harvest', but git ls-files still records harvest/SKILL.md and harvest/Workflows/Harvest.md. A fresh checkout therefore creates lowercase 'harvest', while the checker compares the directory and declared name case-sensitively. The Mac's existing uppercase directory masks this mismatch; the portability report explicitly cites that local spelling as the reason for changing the name.\n  fix: Make the Git-recorded directory spelling and declared name agree. Prefer preserving the existing lowercase name and references, or explicitly record a case-only directory rename through an intermediate name. Validate the Git tree spelling as well as the current filesystem.\n\n[R13-03] medium /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skill-portability-check.py:27\n  evidence: The regex scalar reader does not validate YAML despite serving as the portability gate. For example, 'description: Use when testing: examples. Do not use otherwise.' passes its clause, length, and quote checks, although the embedded colon-space makes this an invalid plain YAML scalar. Thus the recurring audit can report zero failures for a skill that a YAML-based loader cannot load.\n  fix: Parse YAML with a declared dependency, or enforce a genuinely restricted serialization format that rejects unsupported YAML syntax. Validate scalar types and the complete frontmatter syntax before checking trigger clauses.\n\ncoverage: ['Verified the on-disk plan SHA256 matches the supplied hash; reviewed the supplied plan and tracked diff.', 'Read both installed sync scripts and the portability checker.', 'Inspected the 19 deleted Git symlink entries and their surviving on-disk links.', 'Traced dev-sync, startup/closeout behavior, daily-backup Sync-Repo, the installed pre-commit hook, and related error-log writers.', 'Inspected Git-recorded Harvest paths and the portability report.']\nlimitations: ['Static review only: no edits, tests, delegation, or harness execution.', 'Bulk reads of skill bodies and research notes were truncated; complete body-level coverage is not claimed.', 'Windows filesystem behavior, fresh-checkout loading, and Pi isolation were not exercised.', 'Tasks 6–8 were assessed from the plan, not verified as completed implementations.']","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3dbf505a-e867-4d02-bb8f-16b8c28dff08","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
