{"parentUuid":"a1352048-9663-4409-ad5b-18ed24eb7e41","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019bfkho2C1nQC4Ypr5YgTG5","type":"tool_result","content":"=== claude-stack-doctor ===\nname: claude-stack-doctor\ndescription: >-\n  Health-check Eric's automation/memory stack in one pass, and verify the Mac-to-Windows\n  handoff actually works — launchd agents (com.keystone.morning, agysync, dailybackup,\n  rituals, reconcile, adjudicate), Python venvs, memsearch, memory-compiler flush\n  pipeline, backup freshness, and context budget — and diagnose what's silently broken.\n  Use when the user says \"/claude-stack-doctor\", \"stack doctor\", \"is my stack healthy\",\n  \"did my scheduled jobs run\", \"check the memory pipeline\", \"why didn't the backup run\",\n  or when closeout/morning sessions should verify automation health. Do not use to run\n  the backup itself (use backup) or to audit context-engineering practice (use\n  doctor-plus).\n=== memory-write ===\nname: memory-write\ndescription: >-\n  Writes, updates, removes, and recalls facts in the two-tier memory system at\n  ~/.claude/global-memory/ and ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/. Use for write requests\n  such as \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"update memory\", \"save this\", and \"forget\n  about\", and for recall requests such as \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about\n  X?\", and \"do you remember…?\". For writes, selects the correct tier and enforces\n  deduplication and character caps. For recall, checks the injected snapshot first, then\n  follows the memsearch retrieval ladder. Do not use for a story or lesson worth a vault\n  note (use capture-insight) or for an article or resource to keep (use\n  ingest-resource).\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ced869f8-4909-4ba0-be75-28380812fb36","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:52:48.124Z","toolUseResult":{"std