{"parentUuid":"cd480d96-2b44-4d94-9c41-81da33dc8645","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- claude-stack-doctor: Health-check Eric's automation/memory stack in one pass and verify the Mac-to-Windows handoff works: launchd agents, Python venvs, memsearch, the memory-compiler flush pipeline, backup freshness, and context budget. Use when the user says \"/claude-stack-doctor\", \"stack doctor\", \"is my stack healthy\", \"did my scheduled jobs run\", \"check the memory pipeline\", \"why didn't the backup run\", or when closeout/morning sessions should verify automation health. Do not use to run the backup itself (use backup) or to audit context-engineering practice (use doctor-plus).\n- library-advisor: Consult a grounded domain advisor built from the curated book library; answers only from ingested entries and cites every claim. Use when the user says \"ask my <domain> advisor\", \"/library-advisor <domain> <question>\", \"what would my library say about…\", \"consult my library advisor\", or consults a standing advisor. Domains live in SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/advisors/. NOT FOR the built-in /advisor reviewer command. Do not use to review a domain for gaps or missing coverage, as in \"review my library\" (use library-review).\n- memory-write: Writes, updates, removes, and recalls facts in the two-tier memory system (~/.claude/global-memory/ and ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/). Use for write requests such as \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"update memory\", \"save this\", and \"forget about\", and for recall requests such as \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about X?\", and \"do you remember…?\". Picks the tier, dedups, and enforces caps; recall checks the injected snapshot, then memsearch. Do not use for a story or lesson worth a vault note (use capture-insight) or an article to keep (use ingest-resource).","skillCount":3,"isInitial":false,"names":["claude-stack-doctor","library-advisor","memory-write"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3f0cd248-5c9d-4e67-a497-55ea812306ee","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:57:20.605Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- claude-stack-doctor: Health-check Eric's automation/memory stack in one pass and verify the Mac-to-Windows handoff works: launchd agents, Python venvs, memsearch, the memory-compiler flush pipeline, backup freshness, and context budget. Use when the user says \"/claude-stack-doctor\", \"stack doctor\", \"is my stack healthy\", \"did my scheduled jobs run\", \"check the memory pipeline\", \"why didn't the backup run\", or when closeout/morning sessions should verify automation health. Do not use to run the backup itself (use backup) or to audit context-engineering practice (use doctor-plus).\n- library-advisor: Consult a grounded domain advisor built from the curated book library; answers only from ingested entries and cites every claim. Use when the user says \"ask my <domain> advisor\", \"/library-advisor <domain> <question>\", \"what would my library say about…\", \"consult my library advisor\", or consults a standing advisor. Domains live in SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/advisors/. NOT FOR the built-in /advisor reviewer command. Do not use to review a domain for gaps or missing coverage, as in \"review my library\" (use library-review).\n- memory-write: Writes, updates, removes, and recalls facts in the two-tier memory system (~/.claude/global-memory/ and ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/). Use for write requests such as \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"update memory\", \"save this\", and \"forget about\", and for recall requests such as \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about X?\", and \"do you remember…?\". Picks the tier, dedups, and enforces caps; recall checks the injected snapshot, then memsearch. Do not use for a story or lesson worth a vault note (use capture-insight) or an article to keep (use ingest-resource).\n</system-reminder>"}],"sessio