{"parentUuid":"a4e947d9-b8da-4358-86e0-c3469f450b2b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VtStA6iKucLimJsPVEh3c8","type":"tool_result","content":"commit exit=0\ne47e3af fix: Gate B - checker rejects unloadable YAML and reports config parity\ne47e3af830617033b063597d95847172e1b51c93\ne47e3af830617033b063597d95847172e1b51c93","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8657f963-197b-49eb-8f36-2afb901632f3","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:58:04.631Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"commit exit=0\ne47e3af fix: Gate B - checker rejects unloadable YAML and reports config parity\ne47e3af830617033b063597d95847172e1b51c93\ne47e3af830617033b063597d95847172e1b51c93","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierMetaLines":"{\"meta\":{\"repoVisibility\":{\"remote\":\"erash11/DEV\",\"branch\":\"main\",\"visibility\":\"private\"}}}\n","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a4e947d9-b8da-4358-86e0-c3469f450b2b","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"5e90d4e0-4a1b-46aa-8a6a-5a1b3af0d22c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PfNMGgtMZGxsoJ9zkWcErB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Skill portability normalization - 2026-09-12\n2\t\n3\tContract: name (== directory name, TitleCase allowed) + description with\n4\tBOTH a positive 'Use when' clause and a negative 'Do not use' clause.\n5\targument-hint and allowed-tools are Claude-only; metadata is Codex-only.\n6\t\n7\t```\n8\t\n9\tchecked 42 skills, 0 failing, 42 portable\n10\t```\n11\t\n12\t## What changed\n13\t\n14\t- Baseline: `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`. After: 0 failing.\n15\t- 33 descriptions rewritten: a `Do not use ... (use <sibling>)` clause added to all 33; 9 also had\n16\t  `Triggers on` / `Trigger phrases:` / `Use whenever` / `Use automatically for` turned into a `Use when` clause.\n17\t  Every existing trigger phrase was kept. Word-diff against HEAD: only connector words were removed.\n18\t- `Harvest`: `name: harvest` -> `name: Harvest` (contract: name == directory; `CreateSkill` already loads with a TitleCase name).\n19\t- `new-project`: its description was **invalid YAML** before (an unquoted `: `). Now a `>-` block; all 42 parse with a real YAML loader.\n20\t- `library-advisor` (already passing) got one extra `Do not use` sentence pointing gap reviews to `library-review` (see the extra row below for why).\n21\t- Bodies: byte-identical to HEAD in every file. `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn` carry CRLF line endings; a first pass normalised them and was reverted to the original bytes.\n22\t\n23\t## Live trigger test (Step 5)\n24\t\n25\tHeadless runs, not interactive sessions: `claude -p` (stream-json, 3-turn cap, Bash/Write/Edit denied) and\n26\t`codex exec -s read-only`. FIRED = the harness loaded that skill's SKILL.md. Exit 1 on Claude rows is the turn cap, not a failure.\n27\t\n28\t| skill | prompt | Claude Code | Codex |\n29\t|---|---|---|---|\n30\t| memory-write | note that the skill portability trigger test ran on 2026-09-12 | FIRED | FIRED |\n31\t| pp-zotero-research-library | search my Zotero library for papers about acute chronic workload ratio | FIRED | FIRED |\n32\t| meeting-prep | verify we're up to speed before the meeting about KeystoneOS | FIRED | FIRED (run stopped after the skill loaded) |\n33\t\n34\t### Extra row — `library-review`, and a harness-parity gap it exposed\n35\t\n36\tPrompt: `review my library - what's missing from my sport-science advisor?`. Codex: **FIRED**. Claude Code: first run loaded `library-advisor` instead;\n37\ta re-run loaded no skill (NOT-FIRED).\n38\t\n39\tCause, verified: `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` sets `library-review` to `\"off\"`, so it is absent from\n40\tClaude Code's startup skill list (121 entries). This predates Task 5 — it also hides `ArXiv`, `ISA` and `Science`,\n41\twhich Task 5 never edited. Codex does not read `skillOverrides`, so it loaded the skill. It is therefore\n42\treplaced by `meeting-prep` in the table above.\n43\t\n44\t**Parity gap for `aios-audit`:** 12 skills in the canonical repo are off in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi —\n45\t7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`, `capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5\n46\tthird-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code sees 35 of the 42 owned skills.\n47\tThe publish step still ships all 42 to the views. Decide per skill: switch it back on, or retire it from canonical.\n48\t\n49\tThe `library-advisor` sentence added during the first run stays: it is accurate, and it matters in Codex and Pi,\n50\twhere both skills are live.\n51\t\n52\tSide-effect check: no memory file was written by either memory-write run (Claude's subagent had no write tools;\n53\tCodex's sandbox refused the write).\n54\t"}]},"uuid":"9abdbfd0-041c-4cf4-8255-cc75ac88ddf4","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:58:04.763Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-portability.md","content":"# Skill portability normalization - 2026-09-12\n\nContract: name (== directory name, TitleCase allowed) + description with\nBOTH a positive 'Use when' clause and a negative 'Do not use' clause.\nargument-hint and allowed-tools are Claude-only; metadata is Codex-only.\n\n```\n\nchecked 42 skills, 0 failing, 42 portable\n```\n\n## What changed\n\n- Baseline: `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`. After: 0 failing.\n- 33 descriptions rewritten: a `Do not use ... (use <sibling>)` clause added to all 33; 9 also had\n  `Triggers on` / `Trigger phrases:` / `Use whenever` / `Use automatically for` turned into a `Use when` clause.\n  Every existing trigger phrase was kept. Word-diff against HEAD: only connector words were removed.\n- `Harvest`: `name: harvest` -> `name: Harvest` (contract: name == directory; `CreateSkill` already loads with a TitleCase name).\n- `new-project`: its description was **invalid YAML** before (an unquoted `: `). Now a `>-` block; all 42 parse with a real YAML loader.\n- `library-advisor` (already passing) got one extra `Do not use` sentence pointing gap reviews to `library-review` (see the extra row below for why).\n- Bodies: byte-identical to HEAD in every file. `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn` carry CRLF line endings; a first pass normalised them and was reverted to the original bytes.\n\n## Live trigger test (Step 5)\n\nHeadless runs, not interactive sessions: `claude -p` (stream-json, 3-turn cap, Bash/Write/Edit denied) and\n`codex exec -s read-only`. FIRED = the harness loaded that skill's SKILL.md. Exit 1 on Claude rows is the turn cap, not a failure.\n\n| skill | prompt | Claude Code | Codex |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| memory-write | note that the skill portability trigger test ran on 2026-09-12 | FIRED | FIRED |\n| pp-zotero-research-library | search my Zotero library for papers about acute chronic workload ratio | FIRED | FIRED |\n| meeting-prep | verify we're up to speed before the meeting about KeystoneOS | FIRED | FIRED (run stopped after the skill loaded) |\n\n### Extra row — `library-review`, and a harness-parity gap it exposed\n\nPrompt: `review my library - what's missing from my sport-science advisor?`. Codex: **FIRED**. Claude Code: first run loaded `library-advisor` instead;\na re-run loaded no skill (NOT-FIRED).\n\nCause, verified: `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` sets `library-review` to `\"off\"`, so it is absent from\nClaude Code's startup skill list (121 entries). This predates Task 5 — it also hides `ArXiv`, `ISA` and `Science`,\nwhich Task 5 never edited. Codex does not read `skillOverrides`, so it loaded the skill. It is therefore\nreplaced by `meeting-prep` in the table above.\n\n**Parity gap for `aios-audit`:** 12 skills in the canonical repo are off in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi —\n7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`, `capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5\nthird-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code sees 35 of the 42 owned skills.\nThe publish step still ships all 42 to the views. Decide per skill: switch it back on, or retire it from canonical.\n\nThe `library-advisor` sentence added during the first run stays: it is accurate, and it matters in Codex and Pi,\nwhere both skills are live.\n\nSide-effect check: no memory file was written by either memory-write run (Claude's subagent had no write tools;\nCodex's sandbox refused the write).\n","numLines":54,"startLine":1,"totalLines":54}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5e90d4e0-4a1b-46aa-8a6a-5a1b3af0d22c","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"9abdbfd0-041c-4cf4-8255-cc75ac88ddf4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezNYZuMM3ssR5QGWN2L1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JDGWUUi6XmAKeXLT1DJryQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-dispositions-r1.md","content":"# Gate B round 1 dispositions\n\nTwo fresh Codex inspections: skills repo (base `3ab4467`) and KeystoneOS (base `8c4c028`).\nBoth REVISE. Four distinct findings (R13-03 and B-01 are the same defect).\n\n| ID | Sev | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R13-01 | high | ACCEPTED | Both sync twins resolve canonical and both view roots through every link in the root and its ancestors (bash: `cd -P`/`pwd -P`, resolving upward for a root not yet created; PowerShell: walks each segment and follows `Target`, 40-hop loop cap, 5.1-safe), then refuse with exit 2 and no changes when any two roots are the same tree or nested (case-folded). Dry runs are refused too. A dangling root link is refused. Manifest lines still cannot redirect writes: `valid_entry` admits only plain basenames, and publish targets come from canonical names. |\n| R13-02 | medium | ACCEPTED | Git records `harvest/`; the Mac's `Harvest` spelling hid it. `name:` reverted to `harvest`, local folder renamed through an intermediate name, views republished (`Harvest` links archived and retired, `harvest` links created). The checker now compares each directory with git's recorded spelling. |\n| R13-03 / B-01 | medium | ACCEPTED | The checker flags any plain YAML scalar containing `: ` or ` #` (continuation lines included). Quoted and block scalars are exempt. Regression fixtures: colon-space, inline comment, multi-line colon (all FAIL); block, quoted, plain with `#` inside a word (all PASS). Cross-checked with PyYAML over 48 files: 0 disagreements. A declared PyYAML dependency was rejected: the plan requires stdlib only (PEP 668). |\n| B-02 | medium | ACCEPTED IN PART | Configuration-aware parity is now enforced: an owned skill set `\"off\"` in Claude Code `skillOverrides` but published to the views is a checker failure. The real roster now reports **7 failing** (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`, `capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`), and nothing else. **Not done: choosing the enabled roster.** Re-enabling in Claude or retiring from canonical changes what Eric sees in every harness, and those overrides were set deliberately in the 2026-09-12 skill audit. That is recorded as a decision for Eric; `library-review` stays an open acceptance case until he decides. |\n\n## Additional change (not a finding)\n\nThe LifeOS skill-system doc warns that descriptions over ~650 chars risk being dropped from\nClaude Code's skill listing. Three Task 5 rewrites crossed it; all three are now under 600\n(`claude-stack-doctor` 564, `memory-write` 573, `library-advisor` 529). Every trigger phrase kept.\n\n## Executed verification\n\n- Sync, bash 3.2, scratch HOMEs, marker present: normal exit 0 (link published); pool root →\n  canonical exit 2; same with `DRY_RUN=1` exit 2; ancestor `~/.codex` → `~/.claude` exit 2;\n  codex view → pool view exit 2; pool view nested in canonical exit 2; `~/.codex` missing exit 0;\n  dangling pool root exit 2; pool → canonical via other letter case exit 2. Canonical intact in all 9.\n- PowerShell twin: 0 parse errors; resolver/overlap functions extracted from the AST and run on\n  real symlinks under pwsh 7: direct, ancestor and relative-target aliases detected; not-yet-created\n  root not flagged; case-different path flagged; link loop returns null; `/x/skills` vs\n  `/x/skills-archive` not flagged. Windows PowerShell 5.1 itself not exercised (no Windows here).\n- Real layout: dry run exit 0; real run exit 0; both views hold `harvest` → canonical `harvest`;\n  manifests 43 entries; metrics drift 0/0, dangling 0/0, tracked links 0.\n- Checker: real roster 7 failing, all override-only; old fixtures unchanged (bad exit 1, empty exit 2).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11168,"cache_read_input_tokens":342171,"output_tokens":4838,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1769},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11168,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4838,"cache_read_input_tokens":342171,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11168},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":5,"requestId":"req_011CezNYYke3cwAdxvH5G9Ue","attributionSkill":"CreateSkill","type":"assistant","uuid":"9f9fc94b-6068-44b9-9303-ab42727984ba","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:58:20.038Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
