{"parentUuid":"d3519e5b-5399-4d40-9bd8-a9a94d7a1a8f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezNcxq6dzLiLCEjKdi3z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both fixes are pushed and clean (drift/dangling/tracked links all 0). Next I'll update the portability report (checker output, Harvest bullet, Gate B section), log Gate B round 1 in the execution log, and check if the runner supports `--feedback` for a fresh reviewer inspection—then commit these together before re-inspecting.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7291,"cache_read_input_tokens":353339,"output_tokens":4018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":647},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7291,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4018,"cache_read_input_tokens":353339,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7291},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezNcwXiHv9KkNSpeeG6b","attributionSkill":"CreateSkill","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f0c30ee-16be-49b8-8973-31df936849e8","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:58:31.600Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"5f0c30ee-16be-49b8-8973-31df936849e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezNcxq6dzLiLCEjKdi3z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QWRw3jCnJvfJmBgvz1PU1h","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-portability.md","content":"# Skill portability normalization - 2026-09-12\n\nContract: name (== directory name, TitleCase allowed) + description with\nBOTH a positive 'Use when' clause and a negative 'Do not use' clause.\nargument-hint and allowed-tools are Claude-only; metadata is Codex-only.\nAfter Gate B the checker also rejects unloadable plain YAML, compares each\ndirectory with git's recorded spelling, and fails any owned skill that is\noff in Claude Code's `skillOverrides` but published to Codex and Pi.\n\nChecker output after Gate B round 1 (`e47e3af`):\n\n```\nFAIL ArXiv\n       - off in Claude Code (settings skillOverrides) but published to the Codex and Pi views - re-enable it or retire it from canonical\nFAIL ISA\n       - (same)\nFAIL Science\n       - (same)\nFAIL capture-insight\n       - (same)\nFAIL library-review\n       - (same)\nFAIL pp-espn\n       - (same)\nFAIL session-miner\n       - (same)\n\nchecked 42 skills, 7 failing, 35 portable\n```\n\n**Frontmatter: 0 failures. Parity: 7 failures, pending Eric's roster decision** (see the last section).\n\n## What changed\n\n- Baseline: `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`. Frontmatter failures after Task 5: 0.\n- 33 descriptions rewritten: a `Do not use ... (use <sibling>)` clause added to all 33; 9 also had\n  `Triggers on` / `Trigger phrases:` / `Use whenever` / `Use automatically for` turned into a `Use when` clause.\n  Every existing trigger phrase was kept. Word-diff against HEAD: only connector words were removed.\n- `harvest`: briefly renamed `Harvest` to match the Mac's folder spelling, then **reverted** (Gate B R13-02):\n  git records `harvest/`, so a fresh checkout is lowercase. The local folder case was corrected and the views republished.\n- `new-project`: its description was **invalid YAML** before (an unquoted `: `). Now a `>-` block; all 42 parse with a real YAML loader.\n- `library-advisor` (already passing) got one extra `Do not use` sentence pointing gap reviews to `library-review` (see the extra row below for why).\n- `claude-stack-doctor`, `memory-write`, `library-advisor` trimmed to 564 / 573 / 529 chars after Gate B, to stay under the\n  ~650-char listing budget. Triggers kept.\n- Bodies: byte-identical to HEAD in every file. `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn` carry CRLF line endings; a first pass normalised them and was reverted to the original bytes.\n\n## Live trigger test (Step 5)\n\nHeadless runs, not interactive sessions: `claude -p` (stream-json, 3-turn cap, Bash/Write/Edit denied) and\n`codex exec -s read-only`. FIRED = the harness loaded that skill's SKILL.md. Exit 1 on Claude rows is the turn cap, not a failure.\n\n| skill | prompt | Claude Code | Codex |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| memory-write | note that the skill portability trigger test ran on 2026-09-12 | FIRED | FIRED |\n| pp-zotero-research-library | search my Zotero library for papers about acute chronic workload ratio | FIRED | FIRED |\n| meeting-prep | verify we're up to speed before the meeting about KeystoneOS | FIRED | FIRED (run stopped after the skill loaded) |\n| **library-review** (open acceptance case) | review my library - what's missing from my sport-science advisor? | **NOT FIRED** — off in `skillOverrides` | FIRED |\n\n`memory-write` and `library-advisor` were trimmed after these runs; their trigger phrases are unchanged.\n\n### `library-review`, and the harness-parity gap it exposed\n\nClaude Code's first run loaded `library-advisor` instead; a re-run loaded no skill.\n\nCause, verified: `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` sets `library-review` to `\"off\"`, so it is absent from\nClaude Code's startup skill list (121 entries). This predates Task 5 — it also hides `ArXiv`, `ISA` and `Science`,\nwhich Task 5 never edited. Codex does not read `skillOverrides`, so it loaded the skill.\n\n12 skills in the canonical repo are off in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi —\n7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`, `capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5\nthird-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code sees 35 of the 42 owned skills.\nThe publish step still ships all 42 to the views. **The checker now fails the 7 owned ones** (Gate B B-02).\nResolving them is a roster decision: switch each back on in Claude Code, or retire it from canonical so no\nharness loads it. `library-review` stays in the table above until that is decided.\n\nThe `library-advisor` sentence added during the first run stays: it is accurate, and it matters in Codex and Pi,\nwhere both skills are live.\n\nSide-effect check: no memory file was written by either memory-write run (Claude's subagent had no write tools;\nCodex's sandbox refused the write).\n\n## Gate B (Codex code inspection)\n\nRound 1: skills repo REVISE (1 high, 2 medium), KeystoneOS REVISE (2 medium). All four distinct findings were\naccepted and fixed in `8c6bb7a` (claude-skills) and `e47e3af` (KeystoneOS), except choosing the enabled roster\nfor B-02, which is left to Eric. Dispositions and executed verification:\n`~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-dispositions-r1.md`, summarised in `2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7291,"cache_read_input_tokens":353339,"output_tokens":4018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":647},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7291,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4018,"cache_read_input_tokens":353339,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7291},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezNcwXiHv9KkNSpeeG6b","attributionSkill":"CreateSkill","type":"assistant","uuid":"c8b50efc-dedd-48d7-8bf6-3cd5f644be3a","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:58:50.016Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"c8b50efc-dedd-48d7-8bf6-3cd5f644be3a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QWRw3jCnJvfJmBgvz1PU1h","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-portability.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"2237524f-c218-4b9b-82e6-e5da111925e1","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:58:50.202Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-portability.md","content":"# Skill portability normalization - 2026-09-12\n\nContract: name (== directory name, TitleCase allowed) + description with\nBOTH a positive 'Use when' clause and a negative 'Do not use' clause.\nargument-hint and allowed-tools are Claude-only; metadata is Codex-only.\nAfter Gate B the checker also rejects unloadable plain YAML, compares each\ndirectory with git's recorded spelling, and fails any owned skill that is\noff in Claude Code's `skillOverrides` but published to Codex and Pi.\n\nChecker output after Gate B round 1 (`e47e3af`):\n\n```\nFAIL ArXiv\n       - off in Claude Code (settings skillOverrides) but published to the Codex and Pi views - re-enable it or retire it from canonical\nFAIL ISA\n       - (same)\nFAIL Science\n       - (same)\nFAIL capture-insight\n       - (same)\nFAIL library-review\n       - (same)\nFAIL pp-espn\n       - (same)\nFAIL session-miner\n       - (same)\n\nchecked 42 skills, 7 failing, 35 portable\n```\n\n**Frontmatter: 0 failures. Parity: 7 failures, pending Eric's roster decision** (see the last section).\n\n## What changed\n\n- Baseline: `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`. Frontmatter failures after Task 5: 0.\n- 33 descriptions rewritten: a `Do not use ... (use <sibling>)` clause added to all 33; 9 also had\n  `Triggers on` / `Trigger phrases:` / `Use whenever` / `Use automatically for` turned into a `Use when` clause.\n  Every existing trigger phrase was kept. Word-diff against HEAD: only connector words were removed.\n- `harvest`: briefly renamed `Harvest` to match the Mac's folder spelling, then **reverted** (Gate B R13-02):\n  git records `harvest/`, so a fresh checkout is lowercase. The local folder case was corrected and the views republished.\n- `new-project`: its description was **invalid YAML** before (an unquoted `: `). Now a `>-` block; all 42 parse with a real YAML loader.\n- `library-advisor` (already passing) got one extra `Do not use` sentence pointing gap reviews to `library-review` (see the extra row below for why).\n- `claude-stack-doctor`, `memory-write`, `library-advisor` trimmed to 564 / 573 / 529 chars after Gate B, to stay under the\n  ~650-char listing budget. Triggers kept.\n- Bodies: byte-identical to HEAD in every file. `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn` carry CRLF line endings; a first pass normalised them and was reverted to the original bytes.\n\n## Live trigger test (Step 5)\n\nHeadless runs, not interactive sessions: `claude -p` (stream-json, 3-turn cap, Bash/Write/Edit denied) and\n`codex exec -s read-only`. FIRED = the harness loaded that skill's SKILL.md. Exit 1 on Claude rows is the turn cap, not a failure.\n\n| skill | prompt | Claude Code | Codex |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| memory-write | note that the skill portability trigger test ran on 2026-09-12 | FIRED | FIRED |\n| pp-zotero-research-library | search my Zotero library for papers about acute chronic workload ratio | FIRED | FIRED |\n| meeting-prep | verify we're up to speed before the meeting about KeystoneOS | FIRED | FIRED (run stopped after the skill loaded) |\n| **library-review** (open acceptance case) | review my library - what's missing from my sport-science advisor? | **NOT FIRED** — off in `skillOverrides` | FIRED |\n\n`memory-write` and `library-advisor` were trimmed after these runs; their trigger phrases are unchanged.\n\n### `library-review`, and the harness-parity gap it exposed\n\nClaude Code's first run loaded `library-advisor` instead; a re-run loaded no skill.\n\nCause, verified: `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` sets `library-review` to `\"off\"`, so it is absent from\nClaude Code's startup skill list (121 entries). This predates Task 5 — it also hides `ArXiv`, `ISA` and `Science`,\nwhich Task 5 never edited. Codex does not read `skillOverrides`, so it loaded the skill.\n\n12 skills in the canonical repo are off in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi —\n7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`, `capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5\nthird-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code sees 35 of the 42 owned skills.\nThe publish step still ships all 42 to the views. **The checker now fails the 7 owned ones** (Gate B B-02).\nResolving them is a roster decision: switch each back on in Claude Code, or retire it from canonical so no\nharness loads it. `library-review` stays in the table above until that is decided.\n\nThe `library-advisor` sentence added during the first run stays: it is accurate, and it matters in Codex and Pi,\nwhere both skills are live.\n\nSide-effect check: no memory file was written by either memory-write run (Claude's subagent had no write tools;\nCodex's sandbox refused the write).\n\n## Gate B (Codex code inspection)\n\nRound 1: skills repo REVISE (1 high, 2 medium), KeystoneOS REVISE (2 medium). All four distinct findings were\naccepted and fixed in `8c6bb7a` (claude-skills) and `e47e3af` (KeystoneOS), except choosing the enabled roster\nfor B-02, which is left to Eric. Dispositions and executed verification:\n`~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-dispositions-r1.md`, summarised in `2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":21,"newStart":3,"newLines":45,"lines":[" Contract: name (== directory name, TitleCase allowed) + description with"," BOTH a positive 'Use when' clause and a negative 'Do not use' clause."," argument-hint and allowed-tools are Claude-only; metadata is Codex-only.","+After Gate B the checker also rejects unloadable plain YAML, compares each","+directory with git's recorded spelling, and fails any owned skill that is","+off in Claude Code's `skillOverrides` but published to Codex and Pi."," ","+Checker output after Gate B round 1 (`e47e3af`):","+"," ```","+FAIL ArXiv","+       - off in Claude Code (settings skillOverrides) but published to the Codex and Pi views - re-enable it or retire it from canonical","+FAIL ISA","+       - (same)","+FAIL Science","+       - (same)","+FAIL capture-insight","+       - (same)","+FAIL library-review","+       - (same)","+FAIL pp-espn","+       - (same)","+FAIL session-miner","+       - (same)"," ","-checked 42 skills, 0 failing, 42 portable","+checked 42 skills, 7 failing, 35 portable"," ```"," ","+**Frontmatter: 0 failures. Parity: 7 failures, pending Eric's roster decision** (see the last section).","+"," ## What changed"," ","-- Baseline: `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`. After: 0 failing.","+- Baseline: `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`. Frontmatter failures after Task 5: 0."," - 33 descriptions rewritten: a `Do not use ... (use <sibling>)` clause added to all 33; 9 also had","   `Triggers on` / `Trigger phrases:` / `Use whenever` / `Use automatically for` turned into a `Use when` clause.","   Every existing trigger phrase was kept. Word-diff against HEAD: only connector words were removed.","-- `Harvest`: `name: harvest` -> `name: Harvest` (contract: name == directory; `CreateSkill` already loads with a TitleCase name).","+- `harvest`: briefly renamed `Harvest` to match the Mac's folder spelling, then **reverted** (Gate B R13-02):","+  git records `harvest/`, so a fresh checkout is lowercase. The local folder case was corrected and the views republished."," - `new-project`: its description was **invalid YAML** before (an unquoted `: `). Now a `>-` block; all 42 parse with a real YAML loader."," - `library-advisor` (already passing) got one extra `Do not use` sentence pointing gap reviews to `library-review` (see the extra row below for why).","+- `claude-stack-doctor`, `memory-write`, `library-advisor` trimmed to 564 / 573 / 529 chars after Gate B, to stay under the","+  ~650-char listing budget. Triggers kept."," - Bodies: byte-identical to HEAD in every file. `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn` carry CRLF line endings; a first pass normalised them and was reverted to the original bytes."," "," ## Live trigger test (Step 5)"]},{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":24,"newStart":54,"newLines":34,"lines":[" | memory-write | note that the skill portability trigger test ran on 2026-09-12 | FIRED | FIRED |"," | pp-zotero-research-library | search my Zotero library for papers about acute chronic workload ratio | FIRED | FIRED |"," | meeting-prep | verify we're up to speed before the meeting about KeystoneOS | FIRED | FIRED (run stopped after the skill loaded) |","+| **library-review** (open acceptance case) | review my library - what's missing from my sport-science advisor? | **NOT FIRED** — off in `skillOverrides` | FIRED |"," ","-### Extra row — `library-review`, and a harness-parity gap it exposed","+`memory-write` and `library-advisor` were trimmed after these runs; their trigger phrases are unchanged."," ","-Prompt: `review my library - what's missing from my sport-science advisor?`. Codex: **FIRED**. Claude Code: first run loaded `library-advisor` instead;","-a re-run loaded no skill (NOT-FIRED).","+### `library-review`, and the harness-parity gap it exposed"," ","+Claude Code's first run loaded `library-advisor` instead; a re-run loaded no skill.","+"," Cause, verified: `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` sets `library-review` to `\"off\"`, so it is absent from"," Claude Code's startup skill list (121 entries). This predates Task 5 — it also hides `ArXiv`, `ISA` and `Science`,","-which Task 5 never edited. Codex does not read `skillOverrides`, so it loaded the skill. It is therefore","-replaced by `meeting-prep` in the table above.","+which Task 5 never edited. Codex does not read `skillOverrides`, so it loaded the skill."," ","-**Parity gap for `aios-audit`:** 12 skills in the canonical repo are off in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi —","+12 skills in the canonical repo are off in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi —"," 7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`, `capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5"," third-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code sees 35 of the 42 owned skills.","-The publish step still ships all 42 to the views. Decide per skill: switch it back on, or retire it from canonical.","+The publish step still ships all 42 to the views. **The checker now fails the 7 owned ones** (Gate B B-02).","+Resolving them is a roster decision: switch each back on in Claude Code, or retire it from canonical so no","+harness loads it. `library-review` stays in the table above until that is decided."," "," The `library-advisor` sentence added during the first run stays: it is accurate, and it matters in Codex and Pi,"," where both skills are live."," "," Side-effect check: no memory file was written by either memory-write run (Claude's subagent had no write tools;"," Codex's sandbox refused the write).","+","+## Gate B (Codex code inspection)","+","+Round 1: skills repo REVISE (1 high, 2 medium), KeystoneOS REVISE (2 medium). All four distinct findings were","+accepted and fixed in `8c6bb7a` (claude-skills) and `e47e3af` (KeystoneOS), except choosing the enabled roster","+for B-02, which is left to Eric. Dispositions and executed verification:","+`~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-dispositions-r1.md`, summarised in `2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`."]}],"originalFile":"# Skill portability normalization - 2026-09-12\n\nContract: name (== directory name, TitleCase allowed) + description with\nBOTH a positive 'Use when' clause and a negative 'Do not use' clause.\nargument-hint and allowed-tools are Claude-only; metadata is Codex-only.\n\n```\n\nchecked 42 skills, 0 failing, 42 portable\n```\n\n## What changed\n\n- Baseline: `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`. After: 0 failing.\n- 33 descriptions rewritten: a `Do not use ... (use <sibling>)` clause added to all 33; 9 also had\n  `Triggers on` / `Trigger phrases:` / `Use whenever` / `Use automatically for` turned into a `Use when` clause.\n  Every existing trigger phrase was kept. Word-diff against HEAD: only connector words were removed.\n- `Harvest`: `name: harvest` -> `name: Harvest` (contract: name == directory; `CreateSkill` already loads with a TitleCase name).\n- `new-project`: its description was **invalid YAML** before (an unquoted `: `). Now a `>-` block; all 42 parse with a real YAML loader.\n- `library-advisor` (already passing) got one extra `Do not use` sentence pointing gap reviews to `library-review` (see the extra row below for why).\n- Bodies: byte-identical to HEAD in every file. `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn` carry CRLF line endings; a first pass normalised them and was reverted to the original bytes.\n\n## Live trigger test (Step 5)\n\nHeadless runs, not interactive sessions: `claude -p` (stream-json, 3-turn cap, Bash/Write/Edit denied) and\n`codex exec -s read-only`. FIRED = the harness loaded that skill's SKILL.md. Exit 1 on Claude rows is the turn cap, not a failure.\n\n| skill | prompt | Claude Code | Codex |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| memory-write | note that the skill portability trigger test ran on 2026-09-12 | FIRED | FIRED |\n| pp-zotero-research-library | search my Zotero library for papers about acute chronic workload ratio | FIRED | FIRED |\n| meeting-prep | verify we're up to speed before the meeting about KeystoneOS | FIRED | FIRED (run stopped after the skill loaded) |\n\n### Extra row — `library-review`, and a harness-parity gap it exposed\n\nPrompt: `review my library - what's missing from my sport-science advisor?`. Codex: **FIRED**. Claude Code: first run loaded `library-advisor` instead;\na re-run loaded no skill (NOT-FIRED).\n\nCause, verified: `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` sets `library-review` to `\"off\"`, so it is absent from\nClaude Code's startup skill list (121 entries). This predates Task 5 — it also hides `ArXiv`, `ISA` and `Science`,\nwhich Task 5 never edited. Codex does not read `skillOverrides`, so it loaded the skill. It is therefore\nreplaced by `meeting-prep` in the table above.\n\n**Parity gap for `aios-audit`:** 12 skills in the canonical repo are off in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi —\n7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`, `capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5\nthird-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code sees 35 of the 42 owned skills.\nThe publish step still ships all 42 to the views. Decide per skill: switch it back on, or retire it from canonical.\n\nThe `library-advisor` sentence added during the first run stays: it is accurate, and it matters in Codex and Pi,\nwhere both skills are live.\n\nSide-effect check: no memory file was written by either memory-write run (Claude's subagent had no write tools;\nCodex's sandbox refused the write).\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c8b50efc-dedd-48d7-8bf6-3cd5f644be3a","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"2237524f-c218-4b9b-82e6-e5da111925e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezNcxq6dzLiLCEjKdi3z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017dtRuyq91FRR7aVghvH8CZ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","old_string":"**Risk recorded:** a concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted in\nany repo it sweeps. Long plan executions should commit at each verified step,\nnot batch the commit to the end of a task.","new_string":"**Risk recorded:** a concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted in\nany repo it sweeps. Long plan executions should commit at each verified step,\nnot batch the commit to the end of a task.\n\n| 7 | Daily backup reloaded: skills tree clean first; plist has no `RunAtLoad` (09:00 only); `launchctl list` shows `com.keystone.dailybackup`. |\n\n## Gate B — round 1\n\nTwo fresh Codex inspections (`runner.py inspect --host claude --builder claude`),\none per repo: claude-skills from `3ab4467`, KeystoneOS from `8c4c028`.\n\n| Repo | Verdict | Findings |\n|---|---|---|\n| claude-skills | REVISE | R13-01 high (a view root aliasing canonical makes the publish loop delete the canonical skill), R13-02 medium (git records `harvest/`; `name: Harvest` breaks a fresh checkout), R13-03 medium (checker accepts unloadable YAML) |\n| KeystoneOS | REVISE | B-01 medium (= R13-03), B-02 medium (`skillOverrides` parity gap not enforced) |\n\nAll accepted. Fixed in `8c6bb7a` (claude-skills) and `e47e3af` (KeystoneOS):\n\n- **R13-01:** both twins resolve all three roots through every link in the path and its ancestors and refuse (exit 2, no changes) on same-or-nested roots. Bash: 9 scratch-HOME cases pass, canonical intact in all. PowerShell: parses; resolver tested on real symlinks under pwsh 7 (7 cases pass); Windows PowerShell 5.1 not exercised.\n- **R13-02:** `name: harvest` restored; local folder case fixed; real sync retired the `Harvest` view links (archived) and published `harvest`. Metrics after: drift 0/0, dangling 0/0, tracked links 0.\n- **R13-03 / B-01:** plain scalars with `: ` or ` #` fail. 6 new fixtures behave as expected; PyYAML cross-check over 48 files: 0 disagreements.\n- **B-02, in part:** owned skills `\"off\"` in Claude Code but published now fail the checker — **7 today**. Choosing the enabled roster is left to Eric (the overrides were set on purpose in the 2026-09-12 skill audit).\n- Not a finding: three descriptions trimmed under 650 chars.\n\nConsequence for the numbers: `portability_failures` is now **7**, not 0, until the roster decision is made."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7291,"cache_read_input_tokens":353339,"output_tokens":4018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":647},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7291,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4018,"cache_read_input_tokens":353339,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7291},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezNcwXiHv9KkNSpeeG6b","attributionSkill":"CreateSkill","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b8267b5-e784-458b-839d-2339cec6a302","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:59:01.682Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.