{"parentUuid":"acb6c2b7-d2f9-48a3-a995-d9f1f95d4845","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KBBsAKrtEjBvEiM9HvkDAx","type":"tool_result","content":"Command running in background with ID: bcfhhuuxd. Output is being written to: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649/tasks/bcfhhuuxd.output. You will be notified when it completes. To check interim output, use Read on that file path.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7905ebd8-d926-4816-b6b9-4ef9d6e44b06","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:59:36.369Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"backgroundTaskId":"bcfhhuuxd"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"acb6c2b7-d2f9-48a3-a995-d9f1f95d4845","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"8a2bbf8c-2a65-4606-bf82-cffaa418fdca","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0172TEBjU1jBizqDidoMaCJ9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: skill-bloat-and-promotion\n3\tdescription: \"Measured skill bloat in this setup, the project-until-promoted rule that fixes it, and the command that re-measures usage from .jsonl session logs\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d\n8\t  modified: 2026-09-12T17:43:28.514Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tMeasured 2026-09-12 from a gap analysis of a Nate Herk / **Mark Kashef** video\n12\t(\"How to Actually Choose the Right AI Agent\", 2026-09-11). Full note:\n13\t`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`.\n14\tSame shape as the earlier audit in [[brain-audit-loop]] — that one scored the\n15\t**vault**, this one scores the **skill layer**.\n16\t\n17\t## The measurement\n18\t\n19\t| Metric | Count |\n20\t|---|---|\n21\t| Global skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | 160 (→ **117** after the Tier 1 archive, 2026-09-12) |\n22\t| Plugin skills exposed per session | ~37 (6 enabled, 18 disabled) |\n23\t| SKILL.md files in plugin cache | 606 — disabled plugins + old versions, NOT the load |\n24\t| Project-level skills anywhere in `~/DEV` | **0** |\n25\t| `.jsonl` sessions scanned | 414 |\n26\t| Distinct real skills **ever** invoked | **58** |\n27\t| Used 3+ times | 30 |\n28\t| Used exactly once | 19 |\n29\t\n30\tEverything is global. That is the anti-pattern, not the achievement.\n31\t\n32\t## The rule that fixes it — promotion\n33\t\n34\t**Everything stays project-level until it earns global.** A skill lives in\n35\t`<project>/.claude/skills/` until it proves itself across 2+ projects, then it\n36\tgets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/`. Keeps the global load small and the blast\n37\tradius tight — so when something underperforms you can tell a *model* problem\n38\tfrom a *harness* problem from an *organisation* problem.\n39\t\n40\t## The audit question\n41\t\n42\tNot \"how often did I run this skill?\" but **\"would the model do this fine without\n43\tthe skill now?\"** A skill is a crutch; as the brain gets smarter the crutch starts\n44\tto *limit* it. Seasonal skills (`forecast-capture`) and occasional ones\n45\t(`ingest-book`) are low-count by design — low usage alone is not a delete signal.\n46\t\n47\t## Re-measure (BUILTIN filter is the whole trick)\n48\t\n49\tWithout the `BUILTIN` set you also count `/exit`, `/clear`, `/compact` and friends,\n50\twhich inflates the total to 74 and buries the real skills.\n51\t\n52\t```bash\n53\tpython3 - <<'EOF'\n54\timport glob,re,collections\n55\tBUILTIN={'exit','clear','compact','rename','color','login','logout','plugin','doctor',\n56\t'help','model','config','resume','cost','status','init','agents','mcp','hooks','memory',\n57\t'review','vim','terminal-setup','install-github-app','add-dir','bug','release-notes',\n58\t'pr-comments','ide','permissions','statusline','output-style','todos','export',\n59\t'privacy-settings','upgrade','fast','artifacts','tasks','loop','context','usage','rewind',\n60\t'sandbox','feedback','worktrees','skills','reload-skills','reload-plugins','bashes',\n61\t'keybindings','theme'}\n62\tc=collections.Counter()\n63\tfor f in glob.glob('/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl',recursive=True):\n64\t    try:\n65\t        for line in open(f,encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore'):\n66\t            if 'Skill' not in line and 'command-name' not in line: continue\n67\t            for m in re.finditer(r'\"name\"\\s*:\\s*\"Skill\"\\s*,\\s*\"input\"\\s*:\\s*\\{[^}]*?\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"([^\"]+)\"', line):\n68\t                c[m.group(1)]+=1\n69\t            for m in re.finditer(r'<command-name>/([a-zA-Z0-9:_-]+)</command-name>', line):\n70\t                c[m.group(1)]+=1\n71\t    except Exception: pass\n72\treal={k:v for k,v in c.items() if k.split(':')[-1] not in BUILTIN and k not in BUILTIN}\n73\tprint(\"distinct real skills ever invoked:\",len(real))\n74\tprint(\"used >=3 times:\",len([k for k,v in real.items() if v>=3]))\n75\tprint(\"used exactly once:\",len([k for k,v in real.items() if v==1]))\n76\tfor k,v in sorted(real.items(),key=lambda x:-x[1]): print(f\"{v:5d}  {k}\")\n77\tEOF\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t## Decision, 2026-09-12\n81\t\n82\t**Do the skill audit BEFORE adopting Pi** (`pi.dev`) as an alternative harness.\n83\tRationale: the leverage is the bloat, not the harness. Auditing first means any\n84\tfuture harness move ports ~30 good skills instead of ~200 mixed ones.\n85\t\n86\tPi facts, verified from `pi.dev/docs/latest` 2026-09-12 — full note at\n87\t`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-pi-harness-research.md`:\n88\t\n89\t1. **No sandbox, no approval flows.** \"Pi does not include a built-in sandbox.\"\n90\t   Project trust only guards resource *loading*, not what the agent then does.\n91\t   Never run Pi in `~/DEV` or near `DexaProject`. Trial it in `~/pi-trial` or a\n92\t   container (`sbx` keeps the credential off the container).\n93\t2. **Skills port for one line.** Pi implements the Agent Skills standard and already\n94\t   auto-discovers `~/.agents/skills/` — where 45 of the skills live. Add the rest with\n95\t   `{\"skills\": [\"~/.claude/skills\"]}` in `~/.pi/agent/settings.json`. It loads\n96\t   `AGENTS.md` **or** `CLAUDE.md` directly.\n97\t3. **Hooks → TypeScript extensions is a bounded port, not a rewrite** (earlier note\n98\t   said \"weeks\", that was wrong). Hooks here are already `.ts`; Pi's `tool_call` event\n99\t   returns `{block, reason}` — the same shape as the dcg guard.\n100\t4. **Claude subscription through Pi bills per token as \"extra usage\", NOT against plan\n101\t   limits.** Changes the economics of brain-swapping.\n102\t\n103\tConfig lives in `~/.pi/agent/` and survives npm uninstall.\n104\tSee also [[hook-two-copies-trap]] and [[dcg-guard-blocks]].\n105\t\n106\t## Audit outcome, 2026-09-12\n107\t\n108\t**Both tiers executed.** 99 skills archived, global **160 → 61**, roster cost\n109\t**19,158 → 6,428 tokens/session (a 66% cut)**. Zero regressions: none of the 99\n110\thad ever been invoked in 414 sessions.\n111\t\n112\tDecision 2026-09-12: keep the `mattpocock-skills` and `superpowers` **plugins** and\n113\tarchive the local bare-name duplicates. The plugin (v1.2.3, 35 skills) ships every\n114\tduplicate removed and is newer than the July symlinks. Rule that follows: when a\n115\tplugin and a local skill share a name, **the plugin wins** — delete the local copy.\n116\t\n117\tScript: `~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh` (archives, never deletes — undo with\n118\t`mv ~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/* ~/.claude/skills/`).\n119\tReport: `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-skill-audit.md`.\n120\t\n121\tTraps found while doing it:\n122\t1. **CORRECTED 2026-09-12 — `~/.claude/skills/` IS version-controlled.** It is its own\n123\t   git repo, remote `https://github.com/erash11/claude-skills.git`, and the audit was\n124\t   committed as `3ab4467 chore: apply global skill audit` and pushed. The earlier note\n125\t   that it is \"gitignored, archive is the only undo\" was true only of the *`dotclaude`*\n126\t   repo, which ignores this path — a different thing. **Git IS the safety net here, and\n127\t   it is also how the cut reaches Windows.** Undo with\n128\t   `git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <sha> && git push`, not the archive folder\n129\t   (`skills-archive/` is not in the repo and never reaches the other machine).\n130\t2. **A cut in `~/.claude/skills/` does NOT reach `~/.agents/skills/`.** After the audit,\n131\t   98 of the 99 archived skills were still live in the pool (306 entries there vs 61\n132\t   canonical). Claude Code stopped seeing them; **Pi auto-discovers that folder**, so\n133\t   installing Pi would have re-exposed all of them. Always cut both.\n134\t3. **Skills live in three places and it is easy to edit the wrong copy.**\n135\t   `~/.claude/skills/` (19 entries were symlinks pointing *out* to the pool),\n136\t   `~/.agents/skills/` (Pi, Cowork), `~/.codex/skills/` (Codex, 27 symlinks + 5 real\n137\t   dirs). Count with `find -L`; plain `find` undercounts.\n138\t4. **`sync-to-codex.sh` did `rm -rf \"$dst/$s\"; cp -R \"$SRC/$s\"`** over a 7-name\n139\t   allowlist. If `$SRC/$s` ever became a symlink into `$dst`, that deletes the real\n140\t   data. `dev-sync` tells you to run it after every pull. A `.ps1` twin has the same\n141\t   shape — patch both.\n142\t5. **`~/.claude/skills/_shared/`** holds `config.json` + `Inference/` and is resolved by\n143\t   10+ skills via `parents[2]/_shared/config.json`. It has **no SKILL.md**. Never treat\n144\t   \"no SKILL.md\" as \"orphan, delete\".\n145\t6. **\"606 plugin skills\" is cache, not load.** Only 6 of 24 plugins are enabled\n146\t   (~37 skills exposed). The rest are disabled plugins and old cached versions.\n147\t\n148\t## Architecture decided 2026-09-12 (plan approved, not yet executed)\n149\t\n150\t**Canonical = `~/.claude/skills/`** (the git repo, real directories only, **never commit\n151\ta symlink** — Windows pulls this repo). `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are\n152\t**generated views**, rebuilt by `sync-to-codex.sh` from a complete manifest of every\n153\tcanonical dir holding a SKILL.md, recorded in a `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` ownership\n154\tfile so an audit can tell a generated entry from a third-party `npx skills add` install.\n155\tSymlink on Mac, copy on Windows.\n156\t\n157\tPortable frontmatter contract (fires in Claude Code *and* Codex): `name` must equal the\n158\tdirectory name (TitleCase is legal), and `description` needs **both** a positive\n159\t\"Use when …\" clause with literal trigger phrases *and* a negative \"Do not use …\" clause.\n160\tCodex reads only `name` + `description` (+ optional `metadata.short-description`) and\n161\tignores `argument-hint` / `allowed-tools`. Codex over-fires without the negative clause;\n162\tClaude will not trigger without the literal phrases.\n163\t\n164\tPlan (Codex-approved after 6 review rounds, 10→0 findings):\n165\t`~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`.\n166\tSee [[dev-layout-and-discovery]], [[hook-two-copies-trap]], [[vendored-skill-install]].\n167\t"}]},"uuid":"04c93b21-a04d-450d-808d-8f482e204afc","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:59:36.510Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md","content":"---\nname: skill-bloat-and-promotion\ndescription: \"Measured skill bloat in this setup, the project-until-promoted rule that fixes it, and the command that re-measures usage from .jsonl session logs\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d\n  modified: 2026-09-12T17:43:28.514Z\n---\n\nMeasured 2026-09-12 from a gap analysis of a Nate Herk / **Mark Kashef** video\n(\"How to Actually Choose the Right AI Agent\", 2026-09-11). Full note:\n`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`.\nSame shape as the earlier audit in [[brain-audit-loop]] — that one scored the\n**vault**, this one scores the **skill layer**.\n\n## The measurement\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Global skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | 160 (→ **117** after the Tier 1 archive, 2026-09-12) |\n| Plugin skills exposed per session | ~37 (6 enabled, 18 disabled) |\n| SKILL.md files in plugin cache | 606 — disabled plugins + old versions, NOT the load |\n| Project-level skills anywhere in `~/DEV` | **0** |\n| `.jsonl` sessions scanned | 414 |\n| Distinct real skills **ever** invoked | **58** |\n| Used 3+ times | 30 |\n| Used exactly once | 19 |\n\nEverything is global. That is the anti-pattern, not the achievement.\n\n## The rule that fixes it — promotion\n\n**Everything stays project-level until it earns global.** A skill lives in\n`<project>/.claude/skills/` until it proves itself across 2+ projects, then it\ngets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/`. Keeps the global load small and the blast\nradius tight — so when something underperforms you can tell a *model* problem\nfrom a *harness* problem from an *organisation* problem.\n\n## The audit question\n\nNot \"how often did I run this skill?\" but **\"would the model do this fine without\nthe skill now?\"** A skill is a crutch; as the brain gets smarter the crutch starts\nto *limit* it. Seasonal skills (`forecast-capture`) and occasional ones\n(`ingest-book`) are low-count by design — low usage alone is not a delete signal.\n\n## Re-measure (BUILTIN filter is the whole trick)\n\nWithout the `BUILTIN` set you also count `/exit`, `/clear`, `/compact` and friends,\nwhich inflates the total to 74 and buries the real skills.\n\n```bash\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport glob,re,collections\nBUILTIN={'exit','clear','compact','rename','color','login','logout','plugin','doctor',\n'help','model','config','resume','cost','status','init','agents','mcp','hooks','memory',\n'review','vim','terminal-setup','install-github-app','add-dir','bug','release-notes',\n'pr-comments','ide','permissions','statusline','output-style','todos','export',\n'privacy-settings','upgrade','fast','artifacts','tasks','loop','context','usage','rewind',\n'sandbox','feedback','worktrees','skills','reload-skills','reload-plugins','bashes',\n'keybindings','theme'}\nc=collections.Counter()\nfor f in glob.glob('/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl',recursive=True):\n    try:\n        for line in open(f,encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore'):\n            if 'Skill' not in line and 'command-name' not in line: continue\n            for m in re.finditer(r'\"name\"\\s*:\\s*\"Skill\"\\s*,\\s*\"input\"\\s*:\\s*\\{[^}]*?\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"([^\"]+)\"', line):\n                c[m.group(1)]+=1\n            for m in re.finditer(r'<command-name>/([a-zA-Z0-9:_-]+)</command-name>', line):\n                c[m.group(1)]+=1\n    except Exception: pass\nreal={k:v for k,v in c.items() if k.split(':')[-1] not in BUILTIN and k not in BUILTIN}\nprint(\"distinct real skills ever invoked:\",len(real))\nprint(\"used >=3 times:\",len([k for k,v in real.items() if v>=3]))\nprint(\"used exactly once:\",len([k for k,v in real.items() if v==1]))\nfor k,v in sorted(real.items(),key=lambda x:-x[1]): print(f\"{v:5d}  {k}\")\nEOF\n```\n\n## Decision, 2026-09-12\n\n**Do the skill audit BEFORE adopting Pi** (`pi.dev`) as an alternative harness.\nRationale: the leverage is the bloat, not the harness. Auditing first means any\nfuture harness move ports ~30 good skills instead of ~200 mixed ones.\n\nPi facts, verified from `pi.dev/docs/latest` 2026-09-12 — full note at\n`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-pi-harness-research.md`:\n\n1. **No sandbox, no approval flows.** \"Pi does not include a built-in sandbox.\"\n   Project trust only guards resource *loading*, not what the agent then does.\n   Never run Pi in `~/DEV` or near `DexaProject`. Trial it in `~/pi-trial` or a\n   container (`sbx` keeps the credential off the container).\n2. **Skills port for one line.** Pi implements the Agent Skills standard and already\n   auto-discovers `~/.agents/skills/` — where 45 of the skills live. Add the rest with\n   `{\"skills\": [\"~/.claude/skills\"]}` in `~/.pi/agent/settings.json`. It loads\n   `AGENTS.md` **or** `CLAUDE.md` directly.\n3. **Hooks → TypeScript extensions is a bounded port, not a rewrite** (earlier note\n   said \"weeks\", that was wrong). Hooks here are already `.ts`; Pi's `tool_call` event\n   returns `{block, reason}` — the same shape as the dcg guard.\n4. **Claude subscription through Pi bills per token as \"extra usage\", NOT against plan\n   limits.** Changes the economics of brain-swapping.\n\nConfig lives in `~/.pi/agent/` and survives npm uninstall.\nSee also [[hook-two-copies-trap]] and [[dcg-guard-blocks]].\n\n## Audit outcome, 2026-09-12\n\n**Both tiers executed.** 99 skills archived, global **160 → 61**, roster cost\n**19,158 → 6,428 tokens/session (a 66% cut)**. Zero regressions: none of the 99\nhad ever been invoked in 414 sessions.\n\nDecision 2026-09-12: keep the `mattpocock-skills` and `superpowers` **plugins** and\narchive the local bare-name duplicates. The plugin (v1.2.3, 35 skills) ships every\nduplicate removed and is newer than the July symlinks. Rule that follows: when a\nplugin and a local skill share a name, **the plugin wins** — delete the local copy.\n\nScript: `~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh` (archives, never deletes — undo with\n`mv ~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/* ~/.claude/skills/`).\nReport: `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-skill-audit.md`.\n\nTraps found while doing it:\n1. **CORRECTED 2026-09-12 — `~/.claude/skills/` IS version-controlled.** It is its own\n   git repo, remote `https://github.com/erash11/claude-skills.git`, and the audit was\n   committed as `3ab4467 chore: apply global skill audit` and pushed. The earlier note\n   that it is \"gitignored, archive is the only undo\" was true only of the *`dotclaude`*\n   repo, which ignores this path — a different thing. **Git IS the safety net here, and\n   it is also how the cut reaches Windows.** Undo with\n   `git -C ~/.claude/skills revert <sha> && git push`, not the archive folder\n   (`skills-archive/` is not in the repo and never reaches the other machine).\n2. **A cut in `~/.claude/skills/` does NOT reach `~/.agents/skills/`.** After the audit,\n   98 of the 99 archived skills were still live in the pool (306 entries there vs 61\n   canonical). Claude Code stopped seeing them; **Pi auto-discovers that folder**, so\n   installing Pi would have re-exposed all of them. Always cut both.\n3. **Skills live in three places and it is easy to edit the wrong copy.**\n   `~/.claude/skills/` (19 entries were symlinks pointing *out* to the pool),\n   `~/.agents/skills/` (Pi, Cowork), `~/.codex/skills/` (Codex, 27 symlinks + 5 real\n   dirs). Count with `find -L`; plain `find` undercounts.\n4. **`sync-to-codex.sh` did `rm -rf \"$dst/$s\"; cp -R \"$SRC/$s\"`** over a 7-name\n   allowlist. If `$SRC/$s` ever became a symlink into `$dst`, that deletes the real\n   data. `dev-sync` tells you to run it after every pull. A `.ps1` twin has the same\n   shape — patch both.\n5. **`~/.claude/skills/_shared/`** holds `config.json` + `Inference/` and is resolved by\n   10+ skills via `parents[2]/_shared/config.json`. It has **no SKILL.md**. Never treat\n   \"no SKILL.md\" as \"orphan, delete\".\n6. **\"606 plugin skills\" is cache, not load.** Only 6 of 24 plugins are enabled\n   (~37 skills exposed). The rest are disabled plugins and old cached versions.\n\n## Architecture decided 2026-09-12 (plan approved, not yet executed)\n\n**Canonical = `~/.claude/skills/`** (the git repo, real directories only, **never commit\na symlink** — Windows pulls this repo). `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are\n**generated views**, rebuilt by `sync-to-codex.sh` from a complete manifest of every\ncanonical dir holding a SKILL.md, recorded in a `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` ownership\nfile so an audit can tell a generated entry from a third-party `npx skills add` install.\nSymlink on Mac, copy on Windows.\n\nPortable frontmatter contract (fires in Claude Code *and* Codex): `name` must equal the\ndirectory name (TitleCase is legal), and `description` needs **both** a positive\n\"Use when …\" clause with literal trigger phrases *and* a negative \"Do not use …\" clause.\nCodex reads only `name` + `description` (+ optional `metadata.short-description`) and\nignores `argument-hint` / `allowed-tools`. Codex over-fires without the negative clause;\nClaude will not trigger without the literal phrases.\n\nPlan (Codex-approved after 6 review rounds, 10→0 findings):\n`~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`.\nSee [[dev-layout-and-discovery]], [[hook-two-copies-trap]], [[vendored-skill-install]].\n","numLines":167,"startLine":1,"totalLines":167}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a2bbf8c-2a65-4606-bf82-cffaa418fdca","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
