{"parentUuid":"35befe3a-3c24-4f63-a5b7-fc9a8060db1c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6232cf53-7ac0-4333-99ca-e5a272e4bab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AuhayFgAAaetZzG65d3KeH","type":"tool_result","content":"}\nstatus: completed | VERDICT: REVISE\nsummary: The root-overlap guards address R13-01, but manifest writes can still overwrite canonical files through a symlink. The seven acknowledged roster-parity failures also remain unresolved.\n\n[B2-01] high /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh:315\n  evidence: Both manifest redirects follow symlinks; the PowerShell twin similarly uses Set-Content at line 254. On a prepared machine, a view's .generated-by-sync-to-codex symlink pointing to canonical library-review/SKILL.md passes the root-overlap checks. Its contents are read as manifest entries, then the final write replaces that canonical skill with the manifest. Plain-basename validation protects retirement paths, not this write.\n  fix: Reject linked/reparse-point manifests before any mutation in both twins. Write each manifest to a newly created regular temporary file in the view and atomically replace the manifest directory entry without following its target.\n\n[B2-02] medium /Users/kristinarash/.claude/settings.json:140\n  evidence: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn and session-miner remain explicitly off in Claude settings while published in the generated pool. Disk inspection confirms these links exist. The new checker detects the mismatch, but detection does not satisfy Task 5's zero-failure parity requirement. The host explicitly leaves the roster decision unresolved.\n  fix: Resolve the intended enabled roster with Eric, then consistently enable or retire these skills across harnesses. Keep Gate B unresolved until configuration and publication agree.\n\nlimitations: ['No files edited, tests executed or work delegated. Host-reported test results were not independently reproduced.', 'Bulk reads of complete skill bodies and research notes were truncated; full unchanged-body coverage is not claimed.', 'Windows filesystem behavior, PowerShell 5.1, live harness triggering and Pi isolation were not exercised.', 'Manifest redirection is a static failure scenario; no destructive reproduction was performed.']\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"27943335-fe9a-4a95-af51-dc4a61809b67","timestamp":"2026-09-12T23:00:58.792Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"}\nstatus: completed | VERDICT: REVISE\nsummary: The root-overlap guards address R13-01, but manifest writes can still overwrite canonical files through a symlink. The seven acknowledged roster-parity failures also remain unresolved.\n\n[B2-01] high /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/sync-to-codex.sh:315\n  evidence: Both manifest redirects follow symlinks; the PowerShell twin similarly uses Set-Content at line 254. On a prepared machine, a view's .generated-by-sync-to-codex symlink pointing to canonical library-review/SKILL.md passes the root-overlap checks. Its contents are read as manifest entries, then the final write replaces that canonical skill with the manifest. Plain-basename validation protects retirement paths, not this write.\n  fix: Reject linked/reparse-point manifests before any mutation in both twins. Write each manifest to a newly created regular temporary file in the view and atomically replace the manifest directory entry without following its target.\n\n[B2-02] medium /Users/kristinarash/.claude/settings.json:140\n  evidence: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn and session-miner remain explicitly off in Claude settings while published in the generated pool. Disk inspection confirms these links exist. The new checker detects the mismatch, but detection does not satisfy Task 5's zero-failure parity requirement. The host explicitly leaves the roster decision unresolved.\n  fix: Resolve the intended enabled roster with Eric, then consistently enable or retire these skills across harnesses. Keep Gate B unresolved until configuration and publication agree.\n\nlimitations: ['No files edited, tests executed or work delegated. Host-reported test results were not independently reproduced.', 'Bulk reads of complete skill bodies and research notes were truncated; full unchanged-body coverage is not claimed.', 'Windows filesystem behavior, PowerShell 5.1, live harness triggering and Pi isolation were not exercised.', 'Manifest redirection is a static failure scenario; no destructive reproduction was performed.']","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"35befe3a-3c24-4f63-a5b7-fc9a8060db1c","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
