{"parentUuid":"3345c90e-f74f-4367-af4a-9ca141da0e6c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b5056620-885f-4cb3-99cc-a7cb889b9006","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012iR2sahbvahFXYp5pFxPbU","type":"tool_result","content":" M scripts/skill-portability-check.py\ncommit exit=0\n602f3a8 fix: Gate B r2 - checker validates quoted/nested YAML and fails closed\n602f3a8dcb25cc2c7b99cd871de553720ce9b313\n602f3a8dcb25cc2c7b99cd871de553720ce9b313\nstatus lines:        0","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ff72b78a-e8e6-44c4-9549-fcbfea47ac1f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T23:09:59.124Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":" M scripts/skill-portability-check.py\ncommit exit=0\n602f3a8 fix: Gate B r2 - checker validates quoted/nested YAML and fails closed\n602f3a8dcb25cc2c7b99cd871de553720ce9b313\n602f3a8dcb25cc2c7b99cd871de553720ce9b313\nstatus lines:        0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierMetaLines":"{\"meta\":{\"repoVisibility\":{\"remote\":\"erash11/DEV\",\"branch\":\"main\",\"visibility\":\"private\"}}}\n","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3345c90e-f74f-4367-af4a-9ca141da0e6c","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"ff72b78a-e8e6-44c4-9549-fcbfea47ac1f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezPVMLqBt5rj4xbYCqfz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019EvxwTLefmcFcK1JzQir63","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-dispositions-r2.md","content":"# Gate B round 2 dispositions\n\nTwo fresh Codex inspections with the round-1 dispositions as feedback.\nBoth REVISE. Round 2 is the last inspection the claudex-loop budget allows\n(MAX_INSPECTION_ROUNDS = 2), so the fixes below are host-verified but NOT\nindependently re-inspected. A third round needs Eric's go-ahead.\n\nIDs: S2-* = claude-skills inspection, K2-* = KeystoneOS inspection\n(Codex labelled both sets B2-*).\n\n| ID | Sev | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| S2-01 | high | ACCEPTED | Both twins refuse (exit 2, before any mutation, dry runs included) when a view's manifest is a link or not a regular file. The manifest write now goes to a new regular file (bash `mktemp`; PowerShell GUID name), removes the old entry (which deletes a link, never its target), and moves the new file into place. Commit `7459560`. |\n| K2-01 | medium | ACCEPTED | Checker validates the supported YAML subset line by line, nested and list-item lines included: quoted scalars need valid escapes and a closing quote on the same line; only `[a, b]` flow sequences of plain scalars are allowed; flow mappings, anchors, aliases, tags, tab indentation and malformed block headers are rejected. Found and fixed during testing: any empty-valued key (`metadata:`) made every nested line skip validation (`\"\" in \"|>\"` is True), and a list item's sibling key was misread as a continuation. |\n| K2-03 | medium | ACCEPTED | Evidence failures exit 2: settings file present but unreadable or malformed, `skillOverrides` not an object, git probe failing in a repo. Absent settings still mean \"no overrides\". The staged `aios-metrics.py` reports `error_rc<N>` unless the checker exits 0 or 1. |\n| S2-02 / K2-02 | medium | OPEN — Eric's decision | 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in Claude Code and published to Codex and Pi. The checker fails them. Resolving needs a roster choice (re-enable, or retire from canonical). |\n\n## Executed verification\n\n- Sync, bash 3.2, 13 scratch-HOME cases: all 9 round-1 cases still pass; pool manifest linked to\n  canonical `SKILL.md` → exit 2; codex manifest linked, `DRY_RUN=1` → exit 2; manifest is a\n  directory → exit 2; second normal run → manifests regular files, no temp files left.\n  Canonical `SKILL.md` intact in all 13.\n- PowerShell twin: 0 parse errors; preflight logic refuses a linked manifest; the write logic run\n  against a real symlink leaves the canonical file untouched, leaves a regular manifest with the\n  right content, and no temp file. Windows PowerShell 5.1 not exercised.\n- Real layout: sync exit 0; both manifests regular files, 43 lines, 0 temp files; drift 0/0,\n  dangling 0/0, tracked links 0.\n- Checker: 16/16 fixtures as expected; syntax check agrees with PyYAML on all 42 real skills;\n  real roster 7 failing, all override-only; fail-closed 4/4 exit 2; control exit 0; older\n  fixtures unchanged.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400422,"cache_read_input_tokens":37767,"output_tokens":2752,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":49},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":400422,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2752,"cache_read_input_tokens":37767,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":400422},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transfor