key was misread as a continuation. |\n| K2-03 | medium | ACCEPTED | Evidence failures exit 2: settings file present but unreadable or malformed, `skillOverrides` not an object, git probe failing in a repo. Absent settings still mean \"no overrides\". The staged `aios-metrics.py` reports `error_rc<N>` unless the checker exits 0 or 1. |\n| S2-02 / K2-02 | medium | OPEN — Eric's decision | 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in Claude Code and published to Codex and Pi. The checker fails them. Resolving needs a roster choice (re-enable, or retire from canonical). |\n\n## Executed verification\n\n- Sync, bash 3.2, 13 scratch-HOME cases: all 9 round-1 cases still pass; pool manifest linked to\n  canonical `SKILL.md` → exit 2; codex manifest linked, `DRY_RUN=1` → exit 2; manifest is a\n  directory → exit 2; second normal run → manifests regular files, no temp files left.\n  Canonical `SKILL.md` intact in all 13.\n- PowerShell twin: 0 parse errors; preflight logic refuses a linked manifest; the write logic run\n  against a real symlink leaves the canonical file untouched, leaves a regular manifest with the\n  right content, and no temp file. Windows PowerShell 5.1 not exercised.\n- Real layout: sync exit 0; both manifests regular files, 43 lines, 0 temp files; drift 0/0,\n  dangling 0/0, tracked links 0.\n- Checker: 16/16 fixtures as expected; syntax check agrees with PyYAML on all 42 real skills;\n  real roster 7 failing, all override-only; fail-closed 4/4 exit 2; control exit 0; older\n  fixtures unchanged.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"631f01f3-5532-4e53-bc87-290571aa56cb","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
