{"parentUuid":"26652092-44f8-4f05-94b2-7a6aa8c4fe0c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezPjs3eN54f72ZzYvgXL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013gGnFPaFaNTNnvw24hZfLu","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t8-pi-trial.md","content":"# Pi trial - 2026-09-12\n\nBoundary: separate macOS user `piuser`, no read access to the operator home.\n`cd` into a directory is NOT a boundary and was not treated as one (R5).\n\n**Verdict: BLOCKED at Step 1.** Creating `piuser` needs `sudo`, and this plan ran as a\nnon-interactive background session: `sudo -n true` → \"a password is required\". The plan's\nstop condition applies (\"If the user cannot be created ... stop and write up what failed\").\nNothing was installed and no Pi process was run. Eric's own `/opt/homebrew/bin/pi` was left\nuntouched on purpose: it auto-discovers Eric's real pool, so it is not the trial binary.\n\n| Question | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| pi version | not reached (Step 1) — the trial installs its own copy under `/Users/piuser/.npm-global` |\n| piuser blocked from ~/DEV and ~/SecondBrain? | not reached (Step 1). Pre-check: `ls -ld ~` = `drwxr-x---+ kristinarash staff`, so a `piuser` in group `staff` WOULD read `~` through the group bits — the plan's own-group step (GID 4242, confirmed unused) is required, not optional |\n| skills auto-discovered | not reached (Step 1). Expected value to compare against: `pool_skills=210` (Task 4 Step 6) |\n| skills needing edits to fire in Pi | not reached (Step 1) |\n| extension contract matched the research note? | not reached (Step 1). Guard staged byte-for-byte from the plan (factory + `pi.on('tool_call')` + `event.input`) |\n| minutes to port the dcg guard | not reached (Step 1) |\n| hooks still to port | not reached (Step 1); inventory today: 61 in `~/.claude/hooks`, 59 in `~/.codex/hooks` (the two copies differ by 2) |\n| verdict | BLOCKED |\n\n## What the guard proved\n\nNothing yet — the guard needs the boundary user first. Probes A/B/C in plan Step 6 are unchanged.\n\n## To unblock (Eric, in a terminal — about 2 minutes)\n\nRun plan Task 8 Step 1 exactly. It prompts for your password:\n\n```bash\nsudo sysadminctl -addUser piuser -fullName \"Pi Trial\" -password - -home /Users/piuser\nsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial\nsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial PrimaryGroupID 4242\nsudo dscl . -create /Users/piuser PrimaryGroupID 4242\nid piuser\ndseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff\nsudo -u piuser ls ~/DEV          2>&1 | tail -2\nsudo -u piuser ls ~/SecondBrain  2>&1 | tail -2\n```\n\nBoth `ls` lines must print **Permission denied**; `id piuser` must not list `staff(20)`.\nThen a session can run Steps 2-8 (Steps 2, 3, 6 and 8 also use `sudo`, so they need an\ninteractive session or a sudo-capable one).\n\n## What a real adoption would still need\n\nNot in scope here. At minimum: a boundary design that is not a second user\naccount, an approval-prompt layer, and a port of the remaining hooks.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2534,"cache_read_input_tokens":917203,"output_tokens":3393,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":698},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1085,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":26,"cache_read_input_tokens":458059,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1085},"type":"message"},{"input_tokens":378073,"output_tokens":9783,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"advisor_message","model":"cla