-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
{"parentUuid":"c0a2e033-2722-4f62-8aa1-c0a7aa1806c0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b5056620-885f-4cb3-99cc-a7cb889b9006","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LE57nWXzkrdbCjNGfjU4oB","type":"tool_result","content":"================ gateC-keystone\n}\nstatus: completed | error: None | VERDICT: REVISE\nsummary: Three concrete Gate C defects remain: the scheduled entry point loses executability in Git, stale-lock recovery permits concurrent writers, and Claude-only usage counts are presented as cross-harness non-use.\n\n[C-01] medium scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh\n  evidence: Git records this script as mode 100644, although the working copy is executable. The installed launchd plist runs `/bin/bash -lc '$HOME/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh'`, which executes the script directly. A fresh checkout therefore fails with permission denied; the current host's successful run depends on an unversioned permission change.\n  fix: Commit executable mode 100755, or change the plist to pass the script as an explicit argument to /bin/bash.\n\n[C-02] medium scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh:21\n  evidence: Stale-lock reclamation is not atomic. Two invocations can both read the same dead owner. After the first removes and recreates the lock, the second executes its already-decided `rm -rf`, deleting the first invocation's live lock, then acquires its own. Both append trend rows, and either EXIT trap can remove the other's lock. The supplied sequential live/stale checks do not cover this interleaving.\n  fix: Serialize reclamation with a separate atomic recovery lock, recheck ownership while holding it, and release locks only when their ownership token still belongs to the releasing process.\n\n[C-03] medium scripts/aios-metrics.py:46\n  evidence: `usage()` reads only ~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl, silently ignores read failures, and `never_used` subtracts those results from the entire owned roster. The audit then treats these as skills never invoked 'across all sessions' and uses them for DELETE recommendations. A skill used exclusively in Codex or Pi—or whose Claude transcript is unreadable—is incorrectly classified as never used.\n  fix: Label this metric explicitly as observed Claude usage, report unavailable transcript evidence, and prohibit cross-harness non-use conclusions from it. Alternatively, incorporate supported Codex/Pi usage evidence before computing the combined metric.\n\nlimitations: ['Static, read-only review; no tests, scheduled jobs, edits, or delegation performed.', 'Host-reported verification was treated as evidence, not independently reproduced.', 'Windows filesystem behavior and Pi runtime behavior were not exercised.', 'The known seven-skill roster decision remains a separate unresolved Gate B item; this review does not approve overall harness parity.']\n================ gateB3-skills\n}\nstatus: failed | error: codex exited 1; inspect stdout.txt and stderr.txt. | VERDICT: None\nsummary: None\n\nlimitations: None\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"68e550b5-2f4b-48a7-bfb5-32a9fbd1943d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T23:16:04.410Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"================ gateC-keystone\n}\nstatus: completed | error: None | VERDICT: REVISE\nsummary: Three concrete Gate C defects remain: the scheduled entry point loses executability in Git, stale-lock recovery permits concurrent writers, and Claude-only usage counts are presented as cross-harness non-use.\n\n[C-01] medium scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh\n  evidence: Git records this script as mode 100644, although the working copy is executable. The installed launchd plist runs `/bin/bash -lc '$HOME/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh'`, which executes the script directly. A fresh checkout therefore fails with permission denied; the current host's successful run depends on an unversioned permission change.\n  fix: Commit executable mode 100755, or change the plist to pass the script as an explicit argument to /bin/bash.\n\n[C-02] medium scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh:21\n  evidence: Stale-lock reclamation is not atomic. Two invocations can both read the same dead owner. After the first removes and recreates the lock, the second executes its already-decided `rm -rf`, deleting the first invocation's live lock, then acquires its own. Both append trend rows, and either EXIT trap can remove the other's lock. The supplied sequential live/stale checks do not cover this interleaving.\n  fix: Serialize reclamation with a separate atomic recovery lock, recheck ownership while holding it, and release locks only when their ownership token still belongs to the releasing process.\n\n[C-03] medium scripts/aios-metrics.py:46\n  evidence: `usage()` reads only ~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl, silently ignores read failures, and `never_used` subtracts those results from the entire owned roster. The audit then treats these as skills never invoked 'across all sessions' and uses them for DELETE recommendations. A skill used exclusively in Codex or Pi—or whose Claude transcript is unreadable—is incorrectly classified as never used.\n  fix: Label this metric explicitly as observed Claude usage, report unavailable transcript evidence, and prohibit cross-harness non-use conclusions from it. Alternatively, incorporate supported Codex/Pi usage evidence before computing the combined metric.\n\nlimitations: ['Static, read-only review; no tests, scheduled jobs, edits, or delegation performed.', 'Host-reported verification was treated as evidence, not independently reproduced.', 'Windows filesystem behavior and Pi runtime behavior were not exercised.', 'The known seven-skill roster decision remains a separate unresolved Gate B item; this review does not approve overall harness parity.']\n================ gateB3-skills\n}\nstatus: failed | error: codex exited 1; inspect stdout.txt and stderr.txt. | VERDICT: None\nsummary: None\n\nlimitations: None","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c0a2e033-2722-4f62-8aa1-c0a7aa1806c0","session_id":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"c59d1788-5ebe-4b20-81a1-9007c16d8649","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-greeting-planet"}
